E["item:amethyst-phial"] = {t="item",n="Amethyst Phial",z="teldrassil",s="Corithras Moonrage entrusts the Amethyst Phial to travelers in Dolanaar. They carry it to the Oracle Glade to gather water from the moonwell beneath the Oracle Tree.",h="Corithras Moonrage entrusts the Amethyst Phial to travelers in Dolanaar.",sec={{t="Vessel of Sacred Waters",b="Corithras Moonrage entrusts the Amethyst Phial to travelers on Teldrassil. It is the final vessel used in the Crown of the Earth pilgrimage. They carry it to the far northwest of the boughs, to the Oracle Glade. Beneath the ancient canopy of the Oracle Tree lies the island’s first and most potent moonwell. The phial is dipped into its radiant waters to gather the essence of Elune’s grace. Druids and priestesses study and tend to the World Tree’s unpredictable growth with that water.",sp=0},{t="A Burden of Unblessed Growth",b="Teldrassil was raised under the guidance of Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm, without the blessings of the Dragon Aspects. They refused to endorse what they considered an act of arrogance. As a consequence, the boughs suffer from unsettling corruption, and the kaldorei remain mortal. Filling the Amethyst Phial is both a spiritual rite and an ongoing survey. Researchers in Dolanaar scrutinize the purity of Teldrassil’s sacred waters.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Amethyst Phial used for?",a="Corithras Moonrage gives the phial to travelers to gather water from Teldrassil’s first and most potent moonwell, beneath the Oracle Tree in the Oracle Glade.",al={"amethyst phial purpose","what do i do with amethyst phial","amethyst phial use"},it="purpose"},{q="Where do I fill the Amethyst Phial?",a="Fill it in the moonwell far northwest of Dolanaar, north of the entrance to Darnassus, in the Oracle Glade.",al={"where to fill amethyst phial","amethyst phial location","oracle glade moonwell"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Why is the water from the Oracle Glade so important?",a="The moonwell beneath the Oracle Tree is considered the first and most potent well on the World Tree. Its waters carry the essence of Elune and help researchers monitor Teldrassil’s spiritual and physical health.",al={"why oracle glade water","oracle tree moonwell power","significance of oracle well"},it="motive"},{q="Who sends you to use this phial?",a="Corithras Moonrage, a night elf druid in Dolanaar, gives you the phial for a ritual meant to understand Teldrassil’s troubled growth.",al={"who gives amethyst phial","corithras moonrage phial","who wants the amethyst phial"},it="why_me"},{q="What is the Amethyst Phial?",a="The Amethyst Phial is an empty ceremonial vessel given to travelers in Teldrassil. Crafted specifically to hold pure, enchanted liquid, its purpose is to draw and safeguard water from the moonwell resting beneath the ancient Oracle Tree.",al={"amethyst phial","what is this phial","amethyst vial"},it="identity",add="f821d918"},{q="Why does Corithras Moonrage want the Amethyst Phial filled?",a="Corithras Moonrage seeks water from the premier moonwell at the Oracle Glade to study the strange state of Teldrassil. Because the great World Tree lacks the blessings of the dragon aspects, its growth remains flawed and unpredictable, prompting the druids to scrutinize its most sacred waters.",al={"why fill the amethyst phial","why corithras wants phial","purpose of amethyst phial"},it="why_wanted",add="af37ef60"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a kaldorei, you take on a solemn duty when you fill the phial, confronting the flaws in Teldrassil’s unblessed creation.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you use the phial to monitor the World Tree’s vital energies and creeping corruption."},kw={"amethyst phial","corithras moonrage","crown of the earth","dolanaar","moonwell","oracle glade","oracle tree","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:corithras-moonrage","item:filled-amethyst-phial","quest:921","subzone:oracle-glade","subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","topic:elune","topic:druid"},src={"Amethyst Phial","Crown of the Earth (5)","Teldrassil: The Burden of the Kaldorei"}}
E["item:black-feather-quill"] = {t="item",n="Black Feather Quill",z="teldrassil",s="The Black Feather Quill lies in Ban'ethil Barrow Den, needed to wake the Druids of the Talon.",h="The Black Feather Quill lies in Ban'ethil Barrow Den, needed to wake the Druids of the Talon.",sec={{t="A Vessel of Wakening",b="The Black Feather Quill is one of four sacred focuses used to wake the Druids of the Talon from hibernation. The others are the Raven Claw Talisman, the Sapphire of Sky, and the Rune of Nesting. The rite calls slumbering druids back from the Emerald Dream. Without these items, a druid may remain trapped in the Dream and unable to return to their waking body.",sp=0},{t="The Threat in Ban'ethil",b="Corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs overran Ban'ethil Barrow Den, putting the chests that held the relics in danger. Athridas Bearmantle in Dolanaar ordered their swift recovery, before the captive druids were lost to the Dream.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Black Feather Quill used for?",a="The Black Feather Quill is one of four Relics of Wakening used to wake the Druids of the Talon from ritual hibernation in the Emerald Dream.",al={"black feather quill purpose","why need black feather quill","what does the quill do"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is the Black Feather Quill kept?",a="The Black Feather Quill is kept in the Chest of the Black Feather, deep inside Ban'ethil Barrow Den in central Teldrassil.",al={"black feather quill location","where is chest of black feather","quill location"},it="place"},{q="Why can't the druids wake up without the quill and other relics?",a="Druidic hibernation sends the druids into the Emerald Dream under delicate enchantments. Without the sacred focuses, their slumbering spirits cannot find their way back to their bodies.",al={"why do druids need relics to wake","can druids wake up on their own"},it="power"},{q="Who asks for the Black Feather Quill?",a="Athridas Bearmantle in Dolanaar directs adventurers to recover the Black Feather Quill and the other Relics of Wakening to rescue the imperiled druids.",al={"who needs the quill","black feather quill quest giver"},it="target"},{q="What is the Black Feather Quill?",a="The Black Feather Quill is one of four sacred Relics of Wakening preserved by the night elf Druids of the Talon within Teldrassil's Ban'ethil Barrow Den. Stored within a dedicated chest, it is an essential ceremonial component used to peacefully wake slumbering druids from the Emerald Dream.",al={"what is black feather quill","black feather quill item","black feather quill lore"},it="identity",add="8b872c36"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you know the quill as one of the sacred tools that tether the Druids of the Talon to the waking world while their spirits commune with the Emerald Dream.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know the defilement of Ban'ethil's relic chests by Gnarlpine furbolgs as another painful reminder of Teldrassil's encroaching corruption."},kw={"athridas bearmantle","ban'ethil barrow den","black feather quill","chest of the black feather","dolanaar","druids of the talon","relics of wakening"},rel={"quest:483","subzone:ban-ethil-barrow-den","item:raven-claw-talisman","item:sapphire-of-sky","item:rune-of-nesting","npc:athridas-bearmantle","topic:emerald-dream","zone:teldrassil"},src={"Black Feather Quill","The Relics of Wakening"}}
E["item:bloodfeather-belt"] = {t="item",n="Bloodfeather Belt",z="teldrassil",s="In northern Teldrassil, Bloodfeather harpies wear crude leather belts as they crowd the Oracle Glade. Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak collects them as proof that the nearby nests have been cleared.",h="In northern Teldrassil, Bloodfeather harpies wear crude leather belts as they crowd the Oracle Glade.",sec={{t="Trophies from the Nests",b="Bloodfeather harpies have built aggressive nests in the boughs around the Oracle Glade. Their presence threatens the ancient Oracle Tree and blocks travel through northern Teldrassil. After the flock ambushed and killed a runner carrying reports to Darnassus, Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak called on travelers to strike at the nests. The belts taken from fallen harpies show that their numbers are being culled and the paths are being secured, so messages can reach the capital again.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak want these belts?",a="Arynia Cloudsbreak and her small detachment of Sentinels guard the sacred Oracle Tree against the nearby Bloodfeather nests. After the harpies killed a messenger bound for Darnassus, Arynia asks travelers to bring back belts as proof that they are clearing the nests and thinning the flock.",al={"why arynia wants belts","bloodfeather belt purpose","why collect belts"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where do Bloodfeather Belts come from?",a="Bloodfeather harpies in the trees and crags around the Oracle Glade in northern Teldrassil carry these belts. Every kind in the flock carries one, including wind witches, sorceresses, rogues, and furies.",al={"who drops bloodfeather belt","where to get belts","bloodfeather belt location"},it="origin"},{q="Why are harpies a problem in the Oracle Glade?",a="The harpies have nested close to the Oracle Tree, an ancient tree that watches over the health of the World Tree. Their aggression isolates the Sentinels guarding the glade and violently disrupts messages bound for Darnassus.",al={"oracle glade harpies","why are harpies in teldrassil","harpy threat oracle tree"},it="conflict"},{q="What is a Bloodfeather Belt?",a="A Bloodfeather Belt is a personal ornament worn by the Bloodfeather harpies infesting the Oracle Glade in northern Teldrassil. To the night elves stationed at the glade, these crude belts serve as trophies and tangible proof that another vicious harpy has been culled from the sacred boughs.",al={"bloodfeather belt info","what are bloodfeather belts","bloodfeather belt lore"},it="identity",add="40b720b3"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The Bloodfeather coven has defiled Teldrassil’s natural canopy. Reclaiming the Oracle Glade from their nests is a duty for any protector of the Kaldorei homeland.",["faction:Alliance"]="Helping Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak lets vital reports from Teldrassil’s ancient trees reach Darnassus’s leaders without interruption."},kw={"arynia cloudsbreak","bloodfeather","bloodfeather belt","harpy","oracle glade","teldrassil","the enchanted glade"},rel={"quest:937","npc:sentinel-arynia-cloudsbreak","subzone:oracle-glade","topic:harpy","zone:teldrassil","topic:sentinels","quest:940","zone:darnassus"},src={"Bloodfeather Belt","The Enchanted Glade (Classic)"}}
E["item:crystal-phial"] = {t="item",n="Crystal Phial",z="teldrassil",s="In Shadowglen, Tenaron Stormgrip entrusts young night elves with a Crystal Phial. They carry it to a nearby moonwell to draw sacred water for rites honoring and nourishing Teldrassil.",h="In Shadowglen, Tenaron Stormgrip entrusts young night elves with a Crystal Phial.",sec={{t="A Vessel for Sacred Waters",b="Young night elves receive a Crystal Phial atop Aldrassil. Tenaron Stormgrip sends them to the moonwell just north of the bough to gather its glowing waters. The delicate vessel holds water touched by the sacred legacy of the Well of Eternity. Returning with a Filled Crystal Phial begins the Crown of the Earth pilgrimage, teaching the young kaldorei about the balance of magic, history, and nature in their new island home.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Crystal Phial used for?",a="The Crystal Phial gathers blessed water from the moonwell just north of Aldrassil in Shadowglen. You return the filled phial to Tenaron Stormgrip for the Crown of the Earth pilgrimage.",al={"crystal phial purpose","use of crystal phial","what do i do with the phial"},it="purpose"},{q="Who gives you the Crystal Phial?",a="Druid Tenaron Stormgrip gives you the empty Crystal Phial atop Aldrassil.",al={"who gives crystal phial","where to get crystal phial"}},{q="Why is gathering moonwell water significant?",a="Moonwell water is tied to the Well of Eternity and the grace of Elune. Gathering it helps you learn about the aftermath of the Third War and take part in rites to nourish Teldrassil.",al={"why moonwell water","significance of moonwell water","moonwell purpose"}},{q="What happens after the phial is filled?",a="Once filled, the vessel becomes a Filled Crystal Phial. You return it to Tenaron Stormgrip, completing your first trial and opening further lessons about creating and caring for the World Tree across Teldrassil.",al={"after filling phial","filled crystal phial use"},it="next_step"},{q="What is the Crystal Phial?",a="The Crystal Phial is a delicate, specially crafted vessel provided by Tenaron Stormgrip atop Aldrassil in Shadowglen. Designed to safely transport sacred liquids, its pure crystal construction ensures that the delicate magical energies of moonwell water remain uncorrupted as you carry it back from the forest's holy shrines.",al={"what is crystal phial","crystal phial item"},it="identity",add="d56aa813"},{q="Why does Tenaron Stormgrip want the Crystal Phial filled?",a="Tenaron Stormgrip asks you to fill the Crystal Phial as the first step of your initiation into night elf society and the broader world. Moonwells contain waters blessed with the legacy of the Well of Eternity, revered by Sentinels as shrines to Elune and tended by druids. Gathering its water teaches you about the sacrifices made at Mount Hyjal and tests your readiness to understand the fragile state of Teldrassil.",al={"why fill crystal phial","why does tenaron want moonwell water","tenaron crystal phial why"},it="why_wanted",add="819f868c"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a young kaldorei, filling this phial is a first rite of passage beyond Aldrassil. It connects you to the waters of Elune and your people's recovery after the Third War.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you hold moonwells in deep reverence. Their serene waters help you channel natural energies and nurture new growth without giving in to arcane sorcery."},kw={"aldrassil","crown of the earth","crystal phial","moonwell","shadowglen","teldrassil","tenaron stormgrip"},rel={"quest:921","item:filled-crystal-phial","npc:tenaron-stormgrip","subzone:aldrassil","subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil","topic:elune","topic:nordrassil"},src={"Crystal Phial","Crown of the Earth"}}
E["item:dolanaar-delivery"] = {t="item",n="Dolanaar Delivery",z="teldrassil",s="In Shadowglen, young travelers carry harvested herbs south to Dolanaar. Porthannius entrusts them with the bundle for Innkeeper Keldamyr.",h="In Shadowglen, young travelers carry harvested herbs south to Dolanaar.",sec={{t="A Bundle from Shadowglen",b="Fresh herbs from Aldrassil are bound for Dolanaar. Porthannius is occupied with matters among the druids of Shadowglen, so he entrusts the bundle to young travelers heading south along the road. They carry it to Innkeeper Keldamyr.",sp=0},{t="Welcome to the Hearth",b="The parcel brings you to Dolanaar's inn, where Keldamyr receives it with gratitude. The inn offers weary travelers rest, peace of mind, and sanctuary before they venture deeper into Teldrassil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside the Dolanaar Delivery?",a="The package holds fresh herbs gathered in Shadowglen for Innkeeper Keldamyr and the patrons of Dolanaar's inn.",al={"what herbs are inside","contents of dolanaar delivery","whats in the package"},it="item"},{q="Who sends this delivery?",a="Porthannius, an elf tending to business with the druids in Shadowglen, prepares the bundle but cannot spare time to travel south himself.",al={"who gives the delivery","who sent the herbs","porthannius delivery"},it="origin"},{q="Who receives the package in Dolanaar?",a="Innkeeper Keldamyr receives the package at the communal inn in the heart of Dolanaar.",al={"who do i bring the herbs to","dolanaar delivery recipient","keldamyr herbs"},it="target"},{q="Why couldn't Porthannius deliver the parcel himself?",a="Porthannius has urgent, unfinished business with the druids around Aldrassil, so he seeks a traveler heading south along the forest road.",al={"why porthannius stay","why did porthannius send me"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Dolanaar Delivery?",a="The Dolanaar Delivery is a package of fresh herbs gathered in Shadowglen and bound for the settlement of Dolanaar to the south. Entrusted to you by Porthannius, it represents routine trade and provisions passing from the sheltered groves of Shadowglen down to the larger night elf community.",al={"what is dolanaar delivery","dolanaar parcel","shadowglen package"},it="identity",add="432231a6"},{q="Why does Innkeeper Keldamyr want the Dolanaar Delivery?",a="Innkeeper Keldamyr relies on these fresh herbs from Shadowglen to maintain supplies at the Dolanaar inn. Herbs are essential for brewing draughts, cooking restorative meals, and tending to tired travelers and defenders who seek rest and healing on Teldrassil.",al={"why does keldamyr need herbs","dolanaar herbs purpose","why want dolanaar delivery"},it="why_wanted",add="7521a0db"}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Herbs gathered around Aldrassil meet steady demand as Teldrassil's outlying settlements stock their supplies.",["race:NightElf"]="As a young kaldorei, carrying the package marks a rite of passage beyond Shadowglen's protective boughs and into the wider realm."},kw={"aldrassil","delivery","dolanaar","herbs","keldamyr","porthannius","shadowglen"},rel={"quest:2159","npc:innkeeper-keldamyr","subzone:dolanaar","subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil","topic:druid"},src={"Dolanaar Delivery","Dolanaar Delivery (quest)"}}
E["item:emerald-dreamcatcher"] = {t="item",n="Emerald Dreamcatcher",z="teldrassil",s="In Starbreeze Village, the Emerald Dreamcatcher lies forgotten after the Gnarlpine furbolgs drove out its people. Druids of Ban’ethil Barrow Den gave it to Tallonkai Swiftroot, hoping it would draw vigor from the Emerald Dream.",h="In Starbreeze Village, the Emerald Dreamcatcher lies forgotten after the Gnarlpine furbolgs drove out its...",sec={{t="A Gift from Ban'ethil",b="Gaerolas Talvethren, the druidic warden of Ban’ethil Barrow Den, oversaw the making of the Emerald Dreamcatcher. The druids gave the enchanted amulet to only a chosen few. It draws ambient energy from the Emerald Dream, bringing fortune and protection to whoever carries it. When the maddened Gnarlpine furbolgs overran Starbreeze Village, the amulet remained inside a dresser, stranded in hostile, corrupted territory.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does the Emerald Dreamcatcher do?",a="Tallonkai Swiftroot says the amulet draws raw energy from the Emerald Dream, bringing luck and vitality to whoever possesses it. The Cenarion druids regard it as a rare token of favor.",al={"emerald dreamcatcher powers","what is the dreamcatcher for","dreamcatcher lore"},it="power"},{q="Who made the Emerald Dreamcatcher?",a="Gaerolas Talvethren, the druid warden watching over the sleeping Cenarion circle in Ban’ethil Barrow Den, gave the Emerald Dreamcatcher to Tallonkai.",al={"who crafted the dreamcatcher","who gave tallonkai the dreamcatcher"},it="origin"},{q="Why was the dreamcatcher left behind in Starbreeze Village?",a="Tallonkai kept the amulet in his dresser in Starbreeze Village. When corruption consumed the local Gnarlpine furbolgs and turned them violent, the settlement had to be abandoned before he could retrieve it.",al={"why did tallonkai leave it","where was the dreamcatcher lost"},it="history"},{q="Why are the furbolgs in Starbreeze Village hostile?",a="The Gnarlpine tribe across Teldrassil has fallen to a dark, spreading corruption that drives its members into an aggressive frenzy. Night elves have been forced to flee outlying settlements such as Starbreeze.",al={"why did star breeze fall","starbreeze village furbolgs"},it="hostile"},{q="What is the Emerald Dreamcatcher?",a="The Emerald Dreamcatcher is a rare and potent enchanted amulet crafted by the druids of Teldrassil. Capable of drawing power directly from the Emerald Dream, it channels soothing nature magic to grant fortune and clarity to whoever bears it. Tallonkai Swiftroot of Dolanaar considers it a prized personal gift, one bestowed only upon a favored few.",al={"what is emerald dreamcatcher","emerald dreamcatcher item","what kind of item is dreamcatcher"},it="identity",add="a335891d"},{q="Why does Tallonkai Swiftroot want the Emerald Dreamcatcher back?",a="Tallonkai Swiftroot was forced to leave the amulet behind in his dresser when the Gnarlpine furbolgs fell to corruption and overran Starbreeze Village. Beyond its spiritual power to draw fortune from the Emerald Dream, the talisman holds great personal significance to him as a rare gift from Gaerolas Talvethren, warden of the Ban'ethil Barrow Den.",al={"why does tallonkai want dreamcatcher","why retrieve dreamcatcher","why is dreamcatcher important"},it="why_wanted",add="54ca5db1"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can see how the amulet links the sleeping druids of Ban’ethil Barrow Den to the settlements of the Kaldorei below, carrying aid through their communion with the Emerald Dream.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, recovering the relic is a small victory against the spreading sickness taking Starbreeze Village and the surrounding boughs of Teldrassil."},kw={"ban'ethil barrow den","dolanaar","emerald dreamcatcher","furbolg","gaerolas talvethren","starbreeze village","tallonkai swiftroot","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:2438","npc:tallonkai-swiftroot","subzone:starbreeze-village","npc:gaerolas-talvethren","subzone:ban-ethil-barrow-den","quest:2459","subzone:dolanaar","topic:emerald-dream"},src={"Emerald Dreamcatcher","The Emerald Dreamcatcher (quest)"}}
E["item:encrypted-sigil"] = {t="item",n="Encrypted Sigil",z="teldrassil",s="In Shadowglen, the Encrypted Sigil carries a summons to newly awakened night elf rogues. Frahun Shadewhisper calls them to begin training as dangers gather around Teldrassil.",h="In Shadowglen, the Encrypted Sigil carries a summons to newly awakened night elf rogues.",sec={{t="A Hidden Summons",b="New night elf scouts and infiltrators in Shadowglen receive the Encrypted Sigil through discreet means. A quiet messenger delivers it on behalf of Frahun Shadewhisper. Its contents are hidden instructions that tell the initiate to report to Frahun near Aldrassil. Reading and delivering the token shows Frahun that an initiate can follow subtle directions and handle covert messages.",sp=0},{t="Eyes in the Shadows",b="Frahun uses the summons to explain why rogues matter in an unsettled world. Tensions simmer between the night elves and the distant Horde, but open warfare is not the only danger facing their people. Rogues must gather intelligence across Teldrassil as the Kaldorei’s unseen eyes and blades, and learn to strike before threats take root in the World Tree’s boughs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Encrypted Sigil?",a="The Encrypted Sigil summons novice night elf rogues to begin training. Its hidden instructions direct you to report to Frahun Shadewhisper near Aldrassil.",al={"what does the sigil do","what is encrypted sigil for","why do i have encrypted sigil"},it="purpose"},{q="Who sends the Encrypted Sigil?",a="Frahun Shadewhisper sends the Encrypted Sigil. He is the rogue trainer in Shadowglen beneath Aldrassil’s boughs.",al={"who wrote this sigil","who sent encrypted sigil","who is the sigil from"},it="origin"},{q="What does Frahun Shadewhisper want with me?",a="Frahun wants to judge your readiness, teach you about dangers facing the night elves, including possible discord stirred by the Horde, and give you basic combat instruction.",al={"why does frahun want me","frahun quest","why talk to frahun"},it="wants"},{q="Where should I take the sigil once I read it?",a="Take the sigil to Frahun Shadewhisper near Aldrassil in Shadowglen.",al={"where to bring encrypted sigil","frahun location","where is frahun"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What is the Encrypted Sigil?",a="The Encrypted Sigil is a coded missive delivered to promising night elf rogues beginning their journey in Shadowglen. Marked with concealed script to safeguard sensitive matters from prying eyes, it serves as an official summons from the local rogue trainer, Frahun Shadewhisper, who seeks to evaluate and mentor fresh talent for the shadowy challenges facing their people.",al={"what is encrypted sigil","encrypted sigil lore","what does the sigil do"},it="identity",rc="Night Elf",add="f0a92b78"},{q="Why does Frahun Shadewhisper want the Encrypted Sigil returned?",a="Frahun Shadewhisper asks you to bring the sigil back to him after deciphering it to verify that you received the summons and can follow tradecraft discreetly. Presenting the token confirms your identity and readiness to begin your formal training in stealth, information gathering, and weaponry.",al={"why does frahun want the sigil","why return encrypted sigil","who wants encrypted sigil"},it="why_wanted",rc="Night Elf",add="66ac44ca"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you begin your path by following the sigil’s hidden instructions and making contact with your mentor.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know covert operatives gather vital intelligence while the Kaldorei face new encroachment from the Horde. This is a fragile era."},kw={"aldrassil","encrypted sigil","frahun shadewhisper","kaldorei rogue","rogue trainer","shadowglen","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:3118","npc:frahun-shadewhisper","subzone:shadowglen","subzone:aldrassil","zone:teldrassil","topic:rogue","topic:horde"},src={"Encrypted Sigil","Encrypted Sigil (Classic)"}}
E["item:etched-sigil"] = {t="item",n="Etched Sigil",z="teldrassil",s="In Shadowglen, the Etched Sigil calls new night elf hunters to their trainer.",h="In Shadowglen, the Etched Sigil calls new night elf hunters to their trainer.",sec={{t="Summons of the Wilds",b="Newly awakened night elf hunters receive the Etched Sigil as they enter Shadowglen. Its carved marks of the hunt carry a welcome and summons from Ayanna Everstride, the hunter trainer who lives high in Aldrassil’s hollowed boughs. The token sends each novice to seek her out and begin instruction in archery, wilderness tracking, and the night elf bond between stalker and beast.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Etched Sigil?",a="The Etched Sigil summons a novice night elf hunter to seek Ayanna Everstride in Aldrassil and begin instruction in survival, tracking, and archery.",al={"what does etched sigil do","etched sigil use","why do i have this sigil"},it="purpose"},{q="Who sends the Etched Sigil?",a="Ayanna Everstride, the hunter trainer in Shadowglen, sends the Etched Sigil.",al={"who sent etched sigil","where did etched sigil come from"},it="origin"},{q="Where should the sigil be taken?",a="Bring the sigil to Ayanna Everstride atop Aldrassil in Shadowglen.",al={"where do i bring etched sigil","who do i give etched sigil to"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why do night elf hunters receive a sigil rather than a paper letter?",a="The entry gives no reason for using a carved token instead of a paper letter.",al={"why a sigil instead of letter","what is the sigil made of"}},{q="What is the Etched Sigil?",a="The Etched Sigil is a token inscribed with a summons meant for aspiring night elf hunters within Shadowglen. Carried by a courier and placed in your hands upon your arrival in Teldrassil, it serves as an official introduction to Ayanna Everstride, inviting you to begin your formal discipline in marksmanship and beast training beneath Aldrassil's boughs.",al={"what is etched sigil","etched sigil item","about etched sigil"},it="identity",rc="Night Elf",add="fbac1def"},{q="Why does Ayanna Everstride want you to bring her the Etched Sigil?",a="Ayanna Everstride sends the sigil to ensure you know where to find guidance in Shadowglen. Returning it to her at the top of Aldrassil proves you received her message and are ready to commence your training, learning to wield bows with unerring precision and respect the wild creatures of Kalimdor.",al={"why bring etched sigil","why does ayanna want the sigil","who wants the etched sigil"},it="why_wanted",rc="Night Elf",add="e2d33d60"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, the Etched Sigil marks the start of your training in the bow and the ways of beasts under Ayanna Everstride.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you receive the sigil in Shadowglen, among the canopy traditions of night elven foresters who safeguard Teldrassil."},kw={"aldrassil","ayanna everstride","etched sigil","hunter","shadowglen","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:3117","npc:ayanna-everstride","subzone:aldrassil","subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil","topic:hunter","topic:elune"},src={"Etched Sigil","Etched Sigil (Classic)"}}
E["item:fel-cone"] = {t="item",n="Fel Cone",z="teldrassil",s="Beneath Teldrassil's boughs, Fel Cones carry corruption into the forest. Night elf defenders put the pods to use against nearby tricksters.",h="Beneath Teldrassil's boughs, Fel Cones carry corruption into the forest.",sec={{t="Blight in the Canopy",b="Beneath Teldrassil's boughs, Fel Cones show that corruption has reached the young tree. Gnarled and fallen, the pine cones billow foul green smoke. They lie scattered just east of Dolanaar. Tainted magic has warped the surrounding flora, and the pods are dangerous to touch or eat without caution.",sp=0},{t="A Bitter Medicine",b="Zenn Foulhoof is a satyr who tricks passersby into doing his bidding. When travelers fall for his wiles, Syral Bladeleaf and the Sentinels direct them to gather Fel Cones and offer them to Foulhoof as an innocent snack. The corruption in a cone briefly transforms the satyr into a harmless frog.",sp=1,bt={"q488.2"}}},faq={{q="What is a Fel Cone?",a="A Fel Cone is a corrupted pine cone that falls from Teldrassil's boughs. Tainted by unnatural magic, it gives off eerie green smoke and holds volatile, transformative power.",al={"what are fel cones","fel cone lore","what is fel cone"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Fel Cones be found?",a="Fel Cones lie on the forest floor beneath the trees just east of Dolanaar, in Teldrassil.",al={"where are fel cones","fel cone location","how to find fel cones"},gp=true},{q="Why does the Council of the Forest want them collected?",a="If you helped Zenn Foulhoof harm nature's creatures without knowing it, the Council of the Forest gives you a chance to make amends. They tell you to gather Fel Cones and trick Zenn into eating them as a lesson.",al={"seek redemption cones","why collect fel cones","who wants fel cones"},sp=1,it="why_wanted",bt={"q488.2"}},{q="What happens when someone eats a Fel Cone?",a="The Council of the Forest means the cones to teach Zenn Foulhoof a lesson. He is expected to mistake one for a harmless snack.",al={"what does fel cone do","eating fel cone","zenn foulhoof frog"},sp=1},{q="Where do Fel Cones come from, and who made them?",a="Fel Cones are not crafted by mortal hands; they are corrupted seed cones that naturally fall from the boughs of Teldrassil's trees. A foul, billowing green smoke rises from them, showing that the dark corruption plaguing the great world tree has seeped deep into its very seeds and soil.",al={"where do fel cones come from","who made fel cones","fel cone origin"},it="origin",add="5dfa7f39"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know Fel Cones signal sickness deep within Teldrassil's roots. Even the young World Tree is not safe from demonic corruption.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you see wholesome woodland seed pods become smoking fel remnants. Their corruption shows how fragile Teldrassil's balance is."},kw={"dolanaar","fel cone","satyr","seek redemption","syral bladeleaf","teldrassil","zenn foulhoof"},rel={"quest:489","npc:zenn-foulhoof","npc:syral-bladeleaf","subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","topic:satyr","topic:night-elf"},src={"Fel Cone","Seek Redemption!"}}
E["item:fel-moss"] = {t="item",n="Fel Moss",z="teldrassil",s="Fel Moss spreads through Teldrassil’s forests, its insidious corruptive energies carried by hostile grell and grellkin. The taint threatens the World Tree’s wildlife and native furbolg tribes.",h="Fel Moss spreads through Teldrassil’s forests, its insidious corruptive energies carried by hostile grell and...",sec={{t="Blight on the World Tree",b="Corruption has reached Teldrassil’s boughs, though the World Tree was planted to restore the night elves’ immortality and heal the natural world. Fel Moss is one clear sign of that decay. Impish grell and grellkin infest Shadowglen, with the unnatural, wicked magic of the moss clinging to them and radiating from their growth. The dryad Tarindrella gathers samples to measure how deeply the rot has entered the sacred woodland canopy.",sp=0},{t="Seeds of Madness",b="The furbolgs native to Teldrassil’s heights have succumbed to Fel Moss’s touch. Once peaceful, they abandoned their traditional dwellings and banded together as the hostile Gnarlpine tribe. The moss’s evil power drives them mad under leaders such as Ursal the Mauler, revealing a sickness taking root within the great tree.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Fel Moss?",a="Fel Moss is corrupted plant matter found in Teldrassil. Its insidious, foul energies cling to grell and grellkin and threaten the surrounding wildlife and native furbolgs.",al={"fel moss lore","what is fel moss","what does fel moss do"},it="identity"},{q="Where does Fel Moss come from?",a="Around Shadowglen, grell and grellkin carry clumps of Fel Moss through Teldrassil’s hills. The moss bears corruptive energies spreading through the World Tree’s forests.",al={"where do you get fel moss","fel moss drop","source of fel moss"},it="origin"},{q="How does Fel Moss affect the furbolgs?",a="Fel Moss’s evil power has touched the furbolgs native to Teldrassil. They abandoned their traditional dwellings and formed the hostile, xenophobic Gnarlpine tribe, driven mad under leaders like Ursal the Mauler.",al={"furbolg corruption","why are gnarlpine mad","gnarlpine fel moss"},it="power"},{q="Who is trying to stop the spread of Fel Moss?",a="In Shadowglen, the dryad Tarindrella gathers Fel Moss samples from grellkin to measure how deeply corruption has spread through the woodland. She directs concerned protectors to druids such as Athridas Bearmantle in Dolanaar.",al={"who studies fel moss","who wants fel moss","tarindrella quest"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Tarindrella want Fel Moss?",a="Tarindrella seeks samples of Fel Moss to confirm whether the aggressive grell and grellkin infesting Shadowglen are acting under its wicked enchantment. By securing this tainted growth, she hopes to gauge how far the corruption has spread and understand the threat facing the nearby Gnarlpine furbolgs.",al={"why collect fel moss","tarindrella fel moss","why do they want fel moss"},it="why_wanted",add="464589e1"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid of the Cenarion Circle, you see Fel Moss as a cancer spreading through Teldrassil. Its demonic blight shows how vulnerable the newborn World Tree is.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you venerate Teldrassil as your new homeland. Fel Moss is a distressing omen that peace remains elusive among its sacred boughs."},kw={"fel moss","gnarlpine","grell","grellkin","shadowglen","tarindrella","teldrassil","ursal the mauler"},rel={"npc:tarindrella","quest:458","subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil","topic:furbolg","quest:476","quest:486","npc:athridas-bearmantle"},src={"Fel Moss","The Woodland Protector (2)"}}
E["item:filled-amethyst-phial"] = {t="item",n="Filled Amethyst Phial",z="teldrassil",s="In Teldrassil, water from the Oracle Tree's moonwell fills an amethyst phial. Corithras Moonrage receives it for the Cenarion druids to study the World Tree's troubled growth.",h="In Teldrassil, water from the Oracle Tree's moonwell fills an amethyst phial.",sec={{t="Water of the Oracle Tree",b="The Oracle Glade lies in northwest Teldrassil, where the oldest and most potent moonwell rests beneath the Oracle Tree. Other moonwells across the boughs meet the night elves' daily needs, but the water here carries the raw essence of Elune's grace. Druids who watch over the World Tree's health collect it in amethyst phials, preserving it for testing and ritual cleansing.",sp=0},{t="A Flawed Renewal",b="Corithras Moonrage receives the sample as the druids watch over Teldrassil's troubled growth. Archdruid Fandral Staghelm raised the tree to replace fallen Nordrassil, but the Dragon Aspects refused to sanctify it. Without Nozdormu's blessing to restore night elven immortality or Alexstrasza's protection for its life force, Teldrassil remains stunted and afflicted by corruption. Even the sacred waters of the glade reveal the malaise taking root in the World Tree.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does the water in this phial come from?",a="The water comes from the moonwell in the Oracle Glade, beneath the Oracle Tree in northwest Teldrassil.",al={"where do i fill it","moonwell location","oracle tree well"},it="origin"},{q="Why is the moonwell in Oracle Glade special?",a="The Oracle Glade moonwell is the first and most powerful moonwell created on Teldrassil. It holds the concentrated essence of Elune's power, beneath the ancient Oracle Tree.",al={"why oracle glade","oracle moonwell importance"}},{q="Who asks you to gather this water?",a="Corithras Moonrage, a night elf druid stationed in Dolanaar, asks you to gather the water for the Crown of the Earth rituals.",al={"who wants the phial","corithras quest"}},{q="Why are the druids testing Teldrassil's moonwells?",a="The druids test Teldrassil's moonwells because the tree was raised without the Dragon Aspects' blessings and remains vulnerable. The samples help them watch for its troubling corruption and stunted growth.",al={"why test the water","teldrassil sickness"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is the Filled Amethyst Phial?",a="The Filled Amethyst Phial is a vessel containing sacred water drawn from the moonwell nestled beneath the Oracle Tree in the Oracle Glade. Known as the first and most powerful of Teldrassil's moonwells, its shimmering waters hold the concentrated essence of Elune's grace, making this sample crucial for the kaldorei examining the island's health.",al={"what is filled amethyst phial","filled amethyst phial item","amethyst phial purpose"},it="identity",add="d7e170ec"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a kaldorei, you fill this phial knowing the Dragon Aspects rejected your new home and your lost immortality has not returned.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you know Cenarion druids revere moonwells as sources of nature and astral energy. They use purified vessels like this phial to study Teldrassil's blighted ecology."},kw={"amethyst phial","corithras moonrage","crown of the earth","filled amethyst phial","moonwell","oracle glade","oracle tree","teldrassil"},rel={"item:amethyst-phial","npc:corithras-moonrage","subzone:oracle-glade","quest:921","zone:teldrassil","topic:nordrassil","topic:elune","subzone:dolanaar"},src={"Filled Amethyst Phial","Crown of the Earth (5)","Teldrassil: The Burden of the Kaldorei"}}
E["item:filled-crystal-phial"] = {t="item",n="Filled Crystal Phial",z="teldrassil",s="In Shadowglen, the Filled Crystal Phial holds water drawn from the moonwell north of Aldrassil. Tenaron Stormgrip asks young night elves to gather it as a first lesson in Teldrassil’s sacred power.",h="In Shadowglen, the Filled Crystal Phial holds water drawn from the moonwell north of Aldrassil.",sec={{t="Waters of the Moonwell",b="Tenaron Stormgrip sends young night elves to gather moonwell water before they venture into the wider world. The moonwell lies in Shadowglen, and its waters hold more than spring water: they carry energies traced to the ancient Well of Eternity. Sentinels honor moonwells as shrines of Elune, while druids use their restorative power to tend nature. The arcane sorcery of old remains forbidden. Gathering the water begins a lesson in the sacrifice at Mount Hyjal and the care needed to nurture Teldrassil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside the Filled Crystal Phial?",a="The phial holds water drawn from the moonwell north of Aldrassil in Shadowglen. The waters carry remnants of the ancient Well of Eternity, blessed by Elune’s light and nurtured by druidic care.",al={"what water is in the phial","phial contents","what is in crystal phial"},it="item"},{q="Who asks you to fill the phial?",a="Tenaron Stormgrip, stationed atop the boughs of Aldrassil, asks fledgling adventurers to draw the water as a rite of passage and a lesson in history.",al={"who wants the phial","who gives crystal phial quest","tenaron stormgrip quest"},gp=true},{q="Why does Tenaron Stormgrip want this water?",a="Tenaron uses the gathering as an opening lesson in night elf history after the Third War. Young adventurers learn of Nordrassil’s sacrifice, the power of moonwells, and the ongoing care of Teldrassil.",al={"why fill crystal phial","crown of the earth purpose"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Are the waters dangerous?",a="The waters carry potent magic rooted in the ancient Well of Eternity. Druids and priestesses safely use them for blessings and healing, but reckless arcane manipulation brought catastrophe in ancient times and remains forbidden.",al={"is moonwell water dangerous","is the water magic"},it="danger"},{q="What is the Filled Crystal Phial?",a="The Filled Crystal Phial is a delicate crystal vessel containing water gathered from the moonwell in Shadowglen. It holds the pure, sacred liquid infused with the ancient power of the Well of Eternity, meant to serve both as a sacred offering and a practical lesson in your people's ongoing spiritual stewardship.",al={"what is filled crystal phial","filled crystal phial","filled crystal phial item"},it="identity",add="e7bb2009"},{q="Where does the Filled Crystal Phial come from?",a="It is created when you take an empty crystal phial provided by Tenaron Stormgrip and immerse it directly into the waters of the sacred moonwell situated just north of Aldrassil in Shadowglen.",al={"filled crystal phial origin","where did the filled crystal phial come from","how to get filled crystal phial"},it="origin",add="e140e7c7"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a young kaldorei beginning training beneath Aldrassil, you fill this phial and reflect on the sacrifice at Mount Hyjal and your sacred duty to protect nature.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you hold moonwell water in deep reverence and use its revitalizing energy to tend corrupted flora and sustain the great trees."},kw={"aldrassil","crown of the earth","crystal phial","filled crystal phial","moonwell","shadowglen","tenaron stormgrip","well of eternity"},rel={"quest:921","item:crystal-phial","npc:tenaron-stormgrip","subzone:aldrassil","subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil","topic:elune","topic:nordrassil"},src={"Filled Crystal Phial","Crown of the Earth"}}
E["item:filled-jade-phial"] = {t="item",n="Filled Jade Phial",z="teldrassil",s="In Dolanaar, the Filled Jade Phial is carried back with sacred water from Starbreeze Village. The water helps replenish the central wells while young night elves learn their people's history.",h="In Dolanaar, the Filled Jade Phial is carried back with sacred water from Starbreeze Village.",sec={{t="Waters of Starbreeze",b="Druids in Darnassus draw sacred moonwell water from across Teldrassil to replenish their central wells. Corithras Moonrage entrusts young travelers in Dolanaar with a jade phial made to hold the pure water safely. The moonwell outside Starbreeze Village lies east of Dolanaar. Initiates collect its water as they tend the World Tree.",sp=0},{t="A Lesson in History",b="When you bring the Filled Jade Phial back to Dolanaar, Corithras Moonrage shares another chapter of kaldorei history. He tells of the years after the Third War, when Nordrassil burned, night elves lost their immortality, the Betrayer was released, and Shan'do Malfurion Stormrage disappeared.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Jade Phial filled?",a="Fill the Jade Phial at the sacred moonwell just outside Starbreeze Village, east of Dolanaar on Teldrassil.",al={"where do i fill the jade phial","how to get filled jade phial","starbreeze moonwell location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who requires the Filled Jade Phial?",a="Corithras Moonrage, an elder night elf in Dolanaar, asks travelers to fetch the water for the Crown of the Earth ritual.",al={"who wants the filled jade phial","corithras moonrage quest item"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Why are moonwell waters collected in phials like this?",a="Druids in Darnassus use specially crafted vessels like the Jade Phial to carry pure water from Teldrassil's outlying wells and replenish their primary moonwells.",al={"why collect moonwell water","what is the jade phial for"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What history does Corithras share when turning this in?",a="When Corithras Moonrage receives the filled phial, he tells of the aftermath of the Battle of Mount Hyjal: the loss of night elf immortality, the release of Illidan Stormrage, and the unexplained disappearance of Shan'do Malfurion Stormrage.",al={"what does corithras tell you","crown of the earth lore"},it="history"},{q="What is the Filled Jade Phial?",a="The Filled Jade Phial is a specially crafted jade vessel holding sacred water drawn directly from the moonwell near Starbreeze Village. Infused with lunar energy and nature's grace, such consecrated water is vital to the night elves for sustaining the life of Teldrassil and carrying out their spiritual rites.",al={"what is filled jade phial","filled jade phial lore","filled jade phial"},it="identity",add="10c296e8"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a young kaldorei, fetching the water honors your sacred duty to Teldrassil. Corithras also teaches you about the loss of night elf immortality after Mount Hyjal.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, tending the moonwells connects you to the restorative magic that sustains Darnassus and the Cenarion Circle's work to nurture the young World Tree."},kw={"corithras moonrage","crown of the earth","dolanaar","filled jade phial","jade phial","moonwell","starbreeze village","teldrassil"},rel={"item:jade-phial","npc:corithras-moonrage","subzone:starbreeze-village","subzone:dolanaar","quest:921","zone:teldrassil","zone:darnassus","topic:shan-do"},src={"Filled Jade Phial","Crown of the Earth (3)"}}
E["item:filled-tourmaline-phial"] = {t="item",n="Filled Tourmaline Phial",z="teldrassil",s="At the Pools of Arlithrien, the Filled Tourmaline Phial carries moonwell water for Corithras Moonrage. Its waters help him watch the health and balance of the growing World Tree.",h="At the Pools of Arlithrien, the Filled Tourmaline Phial carries moonwell water for Corithras Moonrage.",sec={{t="Waters of Arlithrien",b="The Filled Tourmaline Phial draws water from a moonwell southeast of the road to Darnassus, on the shores of the Pools of Arlithrien. Reaching the shrine has grown dangerous as the Gnarlpine furbolgs, once peaceful neighbors, turn violently mad. Corithras Moonrage asks travelers to brave the hostile groves and bring back the water. He hopes it will help him find the deepening corruption unsettling the land.",sp=0},{t="The Roots of Teldrassil",b="Back in Dolanaar, Corithras Moonrage speaks of how Teldrassil came to be. After Shan'do Malfurion Stormrage disappeared, Archdruid Fandral Staghelm rallied the Circle of Ancients across the sea in Darkshore to plant the tree and seek the return of their lost immortality. The water in the phial reflects the state of that sacred undertaking. An unexplained sickness now spreads among the beasts and furbolgs.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Filled Tourmaline Phial used for?",a="Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar asks for the Filled Tourmaline Phial, which carries enchanted moonwell water. He gathers water from moonwells across Teldrassil to study the spread of corruption and explain the World Tree's history to newly arrived defenders.",al={"filled tourmaline phial use","tourmaline phial purpose","why fill the phial"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Where is the moonwell for the Tourmaline Phial located?",a="The moonwell lies southeast of Darnassus's main gate, along the shores of the Pools of Arlithrien in southwestern Teldrassil. Enraged Gnarlpine furbolgs contest the area.",al={"where do i fill tourmaline phial","pools of arlithrien moonwell","arlithrien well location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are the furbolgs near the moonwell attacking?",a="The Gnarlpine furbolgs once lived peacefully alongside the night elves, but a creeping corruption afflicts them. Their sudden violence is one of several signs of sickness in the young World Tree.",al={"why are gnarlpine mad","furbolg hostility arlithrien","crazed gnarlpine"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Corithras Moonrage?",a="Corithras Moonrage is a night elf scholar and caretaker in Dolanaar. He guides young adventurers through the rite known as the Crown of the Earth, teaching the history of the night elves, the planting of Teldrassil, and Malfurion Stormrage's disappearance.",al={"corithras role","corithras dolanaar"},it="identity"},{q="What is the Filled Tourmaline Phial?",a="It is an empty tourmaline phial filled with the sacred, luminescent waters of the moonwell near the Pools of Arlithrien in Teldrassil. Night elf druids use phials carved from distinct minerals to harvest pure moonwell water throughout the island, keeping each sample distinct for their sacred rites and the cleansing of the land.",al={"what is filled tourmaline phial","filled tourmaline phial item"},it="identity",add="360c6167"},{q="Where does the Filled Tourmaline Phial come from?",a="The vessel itself is provided by Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar. You create the filled phial by taking it southeast of Darnassus to the moonwell resting along the shores of the Pools of Arlithrien and drawing water directly from the basin amidst the prowling, agitated Gnarlpine furbolgs.",al={"filled tourmaline phial origin","where did the filled tourmaline phial come from"},it="origin",add="b07aae52"},{q="Why does Corithras Moonrage want the Filled Tourmaline Phial?",a="Corithras Moonrage collects the waters from Teldrassil's various moonwells to assess and preserve the spiritual vitality of the young World Tree. As corruption creeps into the boughs and maddens the native Gnarlpine furbolgs, collecting and examining water from across the boughs helps the druids maintain their sacred balance and understand what plagues their home.",al={"why does corithras want the phial","filled tourmaline phial purpose","why gather moonwell water"},it="why_wanted",add="c83d83e7"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you carry a phial tied to Archdruid Fandral Staghelm's controversial legacy. He pushed to plant Teldrassil during Shan'do Stormrage's unexplained absence.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know moonwell waters are a spiritual lifeline for the kaldorei. Corruption in the Gnarlpine groves surrounding this moonwell is an unsettling omen for your new home."},kw={"corithras moonrage","crown of the earth","filled tourmaline phial","gnarlpine","moonwell","pools of arlithrien","teldrassil","tourmaline phial"},rel={"item:tourmaline-phial","quest:921","npc:corithras-moonrage","subzone:pools-of-arlithrien","subzone:dolanaar","npc:fandral-staghelm","topic:furbolg","zone:teldrassil"},src={"Filled Tourmaline Phial","Crown of the Earth (4)"}}
E["item:filled-vessel"] = {t="item",n="Filled Vessel",z="teldrassil",s="At Dolanaar, Corithras Moonrage gathers sacred waters for Fandral Staghelm in Darnassus. The Filled Vessel carries samples from Teldrassil’s moonwells to aid his study of the World Tree’s ailments.",h="At Dolanaar, Corithras Moonrage gathers sacred waters for Fandral Staghelm in Darnassus.",sec={{t="A Confluence of Sacred Waters",b="Night elf acolytes gather water from moonwells across Teldrassil. The tree was planted without the blessings of the Great Aspects, Alexstrasza and Nozdormu, leaving its boughs open to corruption, strange beasts, and crazed furbolg tribes. Corithras Moonrage gathers the phials in Dolanaar and pours them into the Filled Vessel for the journey to the capital. Together, the waters offer a vital sample of Teldrassil’s vitality. Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm studies them in the Cenarion Enclave, seeking a remedy for the Great Tree’s flaws.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside the Filled Vessel?",a="The Filled Vessel holds water gathered from several moonwells across Teldrassil. Corithras Moonrage combines the phials in Dolanaar.",al={"vessel contents","what water is this","what is in the vessel"},it="identity"},{q="Who needs the Filled Vessel?",a="Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm needs the Filled Vessel. He resides atop the Cenarion Enclave in Darnassus.",al={"who do I give the filled vessel to","where does the vessel go","filled vessel hand in"},it="target"},{q="Why does Fandral Staghelm need these water samples?",a="Teldrassil’s afflictions stem from its lack of the Great Aspects’ blessings. Strange corruption, aggressive wildlife, and mad furbolgs plague its branches, and Staghelm studies the mingled waters to understand the tree’s flaws and seek a remedy.",al={"why staghelm wants water","staghelm moonwell water purpose","why collect moonwell water"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who prepared the vessel?",a="Corithras Moonrage prepares the vessel in Dolanaar, pouring in the phials gathered by young adventurers before sending it to Darnassus.",al={"who made the filled vessel","who gives the filled vessel","corithras filled vessel"},it="origin"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid serving the Cenarion cause, delivering this vessel is your first official errand to Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm. It shows you how fragile Teldrassil’s living world remains.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know the moonwell waters as sacred lifelines of your people’s new home. They mingle Elune’s magic with the uncertain growth of the unblessed World Tree."},kw={"cenarion enclave","corithras moonrage","crown of the earth","darnassus","fandral staghelm","filled vessel","moonwell water","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:921","npc:fandral-staghelm","npc:corithras-moonrage","subzone:cenarion-enclave","zone:teldrassil","zone:darnassus","topic:druid","topic:night-elf"},src={"Filled Vessel","Crown of the Earth (6)"}}
E["item:gargantuan-tumor"] = {t="item",n="Gargantuan Tumor",z="teldrassil",s="In Teldrassil, a great growth was torn from Oakenscowl, the corrupted timberling by Lake Al'Ameth. The tumor bears witness to sickness spreading among the creatures there.",h="In Teldrassil, a great growth was torn from Oakenscowl, the corrupted timberling by Lake Al'Ameth.",sec={{t="Blight Upon the Lake",b="Oakenscowl lurks in a cavern near Lake Al'Ameth's southern bank. Once a noble timberling elder, the creature has fallen to a vile affliction. A huge growth poisoned Oakenscowl, warped its behavior, and spread taint through the surrounding wildlife. The tumor was severed to end the beast's rampage and give local researchers a chance to examine the blight. They hope to learn how the malady took root in the boughs of the newly grown World Tree.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the Gargantuan Tumor come from?",a="The Gargantuan Tumor comes from Oakenscowl, a large corrupted timberling in a cave on Lake Al'Ameth's southern shore in Teldrassil.",al={"tumor source","how to get gargantuan tumor","oakenscowl drop"},it="origin"},{q="What is causing the tumor to grow on Oakenscowl?",a="The tumor is a visible sign of the strange corruption poisoning timberlings and wildlife around Lake Al'Ameth. Oakenscowl was once a grand leader of its kind, but the growth overcame it.",al={"why does oakenscowl have a tumor","timberling sickness","lake al'ameth corruption"}},{q="Who wants to study this tumor?",a="Investigators in the area want the tumor to study the strange rot afflicting local timberlings and learn how to treat or halt the blight.",al={"who takes the tumor","turn in gargantuan tumor","oakenscowl quest turn in"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is the Gargantuan Tumor?",a="It is a massive, grotesque growth cut from Oakenscowl, a corrupted timberling elder lurking in a cave along the southern bank of Lake Al'Ameth. The tumor is visibly poisoning the creature and driving it mad, fueling the spread of unnatural rot and affliction across the local waters and nearby wildlife.",al={"what is gargantuan tumor","gargantuan tumor","tumor of oakenscowl"},it="identity",add="b9b4574c"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid tending Teldrassil's young boughs, you can see in the tumor how vulnerable nature there is to corruption.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see a respected elder timberling reduced to a mad, blighted monster, a sign of the troubles facing your new homeland."},kw={"corruption","gargantuan tumor","lake al'ameth","oakenscowl","teldrassil","timberling"},rel={"quest:2499","subzone:lake-al-ameth","zone:teldrassil","quest:940"},src={"Gargantuan Tumor","Oakenscowl (Classic)"}}
E["item:glowing-fruit"] = {t="item",n="Glowing Fruit",z="teldrassil",s="On Teldrassil, a strange fruit glows beneath unusual fronds. Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth studies its strange reaction to the World Tree's soil.",h="On Teldrassil, a strange fruit glows beneath unusual fronds.",sec={{t="A Curious Specimen",b="The Glowing Fruit hangs beneath unusual fronds on Teldrassil, bright and round. Botanist Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth recognizes it as foreign to the World Tree. He thinks its seeds came from distant lands across the sea. Its reaction to Teldrassil's rich, enchanted soil shows how foreign plants can affect the young World Tree.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Glowing Fruit?",a="The Glowing Fruit is a round fruit found beneath unusual fronds on Teldrassil. It shines with its own light and reacts strangely to the local soil.",al={"glowing fruit teldrassil","what is this fruit","strange fruit quest"},it="identity"},{q="Where did this fruit come from?",a="Denalan believes the Glowing Fruit is foreign to Teldrassil. He suspects its seeds came from far across the sea, perhaps from the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"fruit origin","where did the seeds come from","is it native"},it="origin"},{q="Who wants to inspect the Glowing Fruit?",a="Denalan, a night elf researcher at Lake Al'Ameth, wants to study the Glowing Fruit. He studies Teldrassil's boughs and ecosystem, and takes an interest in foreign plants that react with the World Tree's soil.",al={"who needs the fruit","where do i bring glowing fruit","denalan fruit"},it="why_wanted"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid attuned to Teldrassil's balance, you may see foreign plants that react strangely with its soil as a threat to the young World Tree.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As an herbalist, you can see the fruit's strange glow as a sign of an unusual interaction between foreign seeds and enchanted soil."},kw={"botany","denalan","glowing fruit","lake al'ameth","plant","teldrassil","timberlings"},rel={"quest:930","npc:denalan","subzone:lake-al-ameth","zone:teldrassil","quest:940"},src={"Glowing Fruit","The Glowing Fruit"}}
E["item:hallowed-sigil"] = {t="item",n="Hallowed Sigil",z="teldrassil",s="In Shadowglen, the Hallowed Sigil summons young night elf initiates to Aldrassil. Shanda sends it to call them into service to Elune.",h="In Shadowglen, the Hallowed Sigil summons young night elf initiates to Aldrassil.",sec={{t="A Summons to the Priesthood",b="Young night elf priests in Shadowglen receive the Hallowed Sigil from a woodland messenger. Holy markings are engraved on the token, which carries a personal summons from Shanda, the priest trainer at Aldrassil. Read it, then go up to the great hollow of Aldrassil. There, the summons brings the acolyte to the Sisterhood of Elune and begins their service to the Kaldorei as new travelers arrive across Teldrassil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Hallowed Sigil?",a="The Hallowed Sigil is an inscribed holy token given to young night elf priests in Shadowglen. Its summons tells the initiate to seek Shanda, their mentor.",al={"what is hallowed sigil","priest sigil shadowglen"},it="identity"},{q="Who sends the Hallowed Sigil?",a="A woodland messenger carries the Hallowed Sigil on behalf of Shanda, the priest trainer inside Aldrassil.",al={"who sent this sigil","shanda priest token"},it="origin"},{q="Where should I take the sigil?",a="Take the sigil to Shanda inside Aldrassil, at the heart of Shadowglen in Teldrassil. Read it, then present the token to her to make your first introduction to your priesthood mentors.",al={"where do i bring hallowed sigil","hallowed sigil turn in"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Shanda want the Hallowed Sigil returned to her?",a="The sigil serves as a formal summons and an introductory token for novice night elf priests. Priestess Shanda sent it through a messenger to call you to Aldrassil, ensuring you seek out her guidance as the wider world stirs and travelers arrive upon Teldrassil's boughs. Returning with it confirms you received her message and stand ready to begin your sacred training.",al={"why bring hallowed sigil to shanda","why does shanda want the sigil","hallowed sigil purpose"},it="why_wanted",rc="Night Elf",add="71c8963a"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a night elf priest, you receive the Hallowed Sigil as your first summons into formal training under the Sisterhood of Elune.",["race:NightElf"]="As a Kaldorei devotee, the sigil marks the beginning of your service, as Alliance travelers begin arriving on Teldrassil's boughs."},kw={"aldrassil","hallowed sigil","initiate","kaldorei","priest","shadowglen","shanda","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:3119","npc:shanda","subzone:aldrassil","subzone:shadowglen","topic:priest","zone:teldrassil","topic:alliance"},src={"Hallowed Sigil","Hallowed Sigil (Classic)"}}
E["item:hyacinth-mushroom"] = {t="item",n="Hyacinth Mushroom",z="teldrassil",s="In Shadowglen, Hyacinth Mushrooms grow at the roots of trees across Teldrassil. Night elf herbalists use them for medicine, and grell and grellkin forage for them.",h="In Shadowglen, Hyacinth Mushrooms grow at the roots of trees across Teldrassil.",sec={{t="Flora of Shadowglen",b="Hyacinth Mushrooms grow in Shadowglen among the trees and roots of Aldrassil. Forest healers use them in remedies for young night elf sentinels and trainees harmed by venomous creatures. The spiders of Shadowthread Cave are among the dangers they face, and the mushrooms go into soothing draughts and antivenoms. Corrupted grell also hoard them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are Hyacinth Mushrooms used for?",a="Dirania Silvershine uses Hyacinth Mushrooms to make an antidote for Iverron, a young night elf poisoned by venomous spiders while exploring Shadowthread Cave.",al={"hyacinth mushroom use","what does it do","iverron cure"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where do Hyacinth Mushrooms grow?",a="Hyacinth Mushrooms grow on the ground near large tree trunks and roots, and beside boulders in Shadowglen on Teldrassil.",al={"mushroom location","where to find hyacinth mushroom","shadowglen mushrooms"},it="place"},{q="Why do the grell carry Hyacinth Mushrooms?",a="Grell and grellkin in southern Shadowglen forage for Hyacinth Mushrooms and hoard them in their camps.",al={"grell drop mushrooms","why do grell have them","grellkin mushrooms"},it="ties"},{q="Are Hyacinth Mushrooms poisonous themselves?",a="No. Local healers safely use Hyacinth Mushrooms in healing poultices and antivenoms.",al={"is hyacinth mushroom toxic","poisonous mushroom"},it="power"},{q="What is a Hyacinth Mushroom?",a="A Hyacinth Mushroom is a native fungus found throughout the shadowy boughs of Teldrassil, particularly around the bases of trees and mossy stones in Shadowglen. Notable for their medicinal value, these woodland mushrooms possess natural properties capable of counteracting venom when properly brewed alongside other local flora.",al={"what is hyacinth mushroom","hyacinth mushroom info","about hyacinth mushrooms"},it="identity",add="77b7a797"}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Gathering these fungi in Shadowglen takes no formal training. A fledgling herbalist can learn how they help counter forest toxins.",["race:NightElf"]="As a young night elf training in Shadowglen, you can gather wild plants like Hyacinth Mushrooms to help sustain your kin."},kw={"antidote","dirania silvershine","grell","grellkin","hyacinth mushroom","iverron","shadowglen","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:3521","npc:iverron","subzone:shadowglen","item:moonpetal-lily","item:webwood-ichor","zone:teldrassil","subzone:aldrassil","subzone:shadowthread-cave"},src={"Hyacinth Mushroom","Iverron's Antidote (Classic)"}}
E["item:inscribed-bark"] = {t="item",n="Inscribed Bark",z="teldrassil",s="In Teldrassil, Inscribed Bark carries word of the World Tree's state to Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm. The Oracle Tree entrusts it with news of the boughs and the threats troubling the woods.",h="In Teldrassil, Inscribed Bark carries word of the World Tree's state to Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm.",sec={{t="A Message from the Oracle",b="The Oracle Tree sends Inscribed Bark to the Cenarion Circle in Darnassus. After you drive the harpies from their nests, the ancient tree gives you its message, wary of sending ordinary couriers along Teldrassil's tainted paths. The report tells Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm of recent victories and the deeper blight still gripping the woods.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Inscribed Bark?",a="Inscribed Bark carries a report from the Oracle Tree to Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm in Darnassus, telling of the boughs' health and dangers.",al={"what is inscribed bark","oracle tree bark","inscribed bark purpose"},it="identity"},{q="Who sends this message and why?",a="The Oracle Tree gives Inscribed Bark to you after you drive harpies from their nests. Wary of sending ordinary messengers across the endangered forest paths, it entrusts the report to a proven traveler.",al={"who wrote inscribed bark","who gives inscribed bark","oracle tree messenger"},it="origin"},{q="How does Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm react to the message?",a="Fandral acknowledges the respite gained from clearing the harpies, but says deeper problems persist. The report renews his anxiety over whether his work on Teldrassil can restore the night elves' lost immortality.",al={"fandral reaction bark","what does fandral say about bark"},sp=1,it="why_wanted"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a Kaldorei, you know messages carried on ancient bark bind nature to its guardians, linking wild groves with Darnassus's marble terraces.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you recognize Inscribed Bark as an urgent message from an ancient ally, speaking of the delicate balance and afflictions troubling the young World Tree."},kw={"cenarion circle","darnassus","fandral staghelm","inscribed bark","oracle tree","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:940","npc:fandral-staghelm","zone:teldrassil","zone:darnassus","quest:937","quest:952","topic:druid"},src={"Inscribed Bark","Teldrassil (quest)"}}
E["item:iverron-s-antidote-item"] = {t="item",n="Iverron's Antidote (item)",z="teldrassil",s="In Shadowglen, Iverron's Antidote must reach a young night elf before it spoils. Dirania Silvershine brews it to counter the lethal venom of local Webwood spiders, but it lasts only five minutes.",h="In Shadowglen, Iverron's Antidote must reach a young night elf before it spoils.",sec={{t="A Fragile Remedy",b="Dirania Silvershine brews the antidote in Aldrassil for Iverron, a young night elf bitten by Webwood spiders. Its volatile ingredients and herbal catalysts give the draught a shelf life of only five minutes. Couriers must hurry north to the Webwood cave and deliver it before it spoils.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Iverron's Antidote used for?",a="Iverron's Antidote cures Iverron after a toxic bite from Webwood spiders outside their cave in northern Shadowglen.",al={"antidote use","what does iverrons antidote do"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why does the antidote have a time limit?",a="Dirania Silvershine says the fragile draught stays potent for only five minutes after brewing. After that, its medicinal properties break down.",al={"why 5 minutes","antidote timer","why does it expire"},it="power"},{q="Who brews the antidote?",a="Dirania Silvershine, a night elf healer in Aldrassil in Shadowglen, brews the potion from ingredients gathered to save Iverron.",al={"who made antidote","antidote maker"},it="origin"},{q="What happens if the antidote expires?",a="Once the five minutes pass, the draught spoils and no longer works. The courier must return to Dirania Silvershine in Aldrassil for a fresh batch.",al={"antidote expired","timer ran out"},gp=true},{q="What is Iverron's Antidote?",a="It is a freshly brewed medicinal draught concocted specifically to neutralize the deadly venom of the Webwood spiders lurking in the boughs of Teldrassil. Because of its delicate natural mixture, the curative is highly volatile and will quickly spoil if not consumed within minutes of its preparation.",al={"what is iverrons antidote","iverron antidote","iverrons cure"},it="identity",add="59c1ca07"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a young night elf adventurer in Shadowglen, hurrying Iverron this cure shows how the community relies on quick action and herbal knowledge against corruption in Teldrassil's boughs.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As an herbalist, you can see how volatile native Teldrassil reagents make some remedies that must be used at once."},kw={"aldrassil","dirania silvershine","iverron","iverron's antidote","shadowglen","spider poison","teldrassil","webwood venom"},rel={"quest:3521","npc:iverron","zone:teldrassil"},src={"Iverron's Antidote (item)","Iverron's Antidote (2)"}}
E["item:jade-phial"] = {t="item",n="Jade Phial",z="teldrassil",s="In Dolanaar, Corithras Moonrage entrusts the Jade Phial to young initiates. It carries sacred water from Teldrassil’s moonwells to replenish the druids’ central well in Darnassus.",h="In Dolanaar, Corithras Moonrage entrusts the Jade Phial to young initiates.",sec={{t="A Vessel for Sacred Waters",b="The Jade Phial gathers water from a moonwell near Starbreeze Village. Teldrassil’s many moonwells channel lunar and natural energies that matter to night elf society and druidic worship. From time to time, the druids replenish their central moonwell in Darnassus with water from wells across the great bough. Corithras Moonrage entrusts the phial to young initiates, who use it to collect pure water without disturbing the moonwell’s spiritual potency.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Jade Phial used for?",a="The Jade Phial collects sacred water from the moonwell just outside Starbreeze Village. Once it is filled, return it to Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar so the druids can replenish their moonwell in Darnassus.",al={"jade phial purpose","why do i need jade phial","what does jade phial do"},it="purpose"},{q="Who provides the Jade Phial?",a="Corithras Moonrage, a night elf druid in Dolanaar, provides the Jade Phial to adventurers undertaking the rite known as the Crown of the Earth.",al={"who gives jade phial","where to get jade phial","corithras jade phial"},it="origin"},{q="Where does the water from this phial end up?",a="The water gathered in the phial is carried to Darnassus to replenish the central moonwell maintained by the Cenarion druids.",al={"where does moonwell water go","jade phial destination","who uses the water"},it="target"},{q="What is the Jade Phial?",a="The Jade Phial is a specially crafted ritual vessel provided by Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar. It is designed to safely contain and transport the sacred, blessed waters drawn from Teldrassil's moonwells without disturbing or degrading their inherent magical properties.",al={"jade phial","what is the jade phial","what is jade phial"},it="identity",add="8250d8c3"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a young druid, carrying the Jade Phial is an early lesson in caring for Teldrassil’s moonwells, whose vitality calls for constant reverence and care.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know moonwells mark the enduring bond between the kaldorei and Elune. Tending them with vessels like the Jade Phial is a sacred duty."},kw={"corithras moonrage","crown of the earth","dolanaar","jade phial","moonwell","starbreeze village","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:corithras-moonrage","item:filled-jade-phial","quest:921","subzone:starbreeze-village","subzone:dolanaar","zone:darnassus","zone:teldrassil","topic:druid"},src={"Jade Phial","Crown of the Earth (3)"}}
E["item:melenas-head"] = {t="item",n="Melenas' Head",z="teldrassil",s="At Fel Rock, Melenas' Head marks the end of a lingering demonic threat on Teldrassil. Taken as a bounty from Lord Melenas, the satyr commander encamped there, it is proof of his death.",h="At Fel Rock, Melenas' Head marks the end of a lingering demonic threat on Teldrassil.",sec={{t="An Unspoken Disgrace",b="Satyrs on Teldrassil’s new World Tree shame the night elves who guard Shadowglen and the surrounding reaches. Lord Melenas made his lair in Fel Rock’s twisted caverns, just north of the elven settlements, and rallied aggressive grell warriors to his banner. The kaldorei prize discretion when dealing with corruption so close to their heartlands. Melenas' Head is private proof that his schemes have ended before his influence could spread.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Lord Melenas?",a="Lord Melenas was a satyr commander who lurked in Fel Rock on Teldrassil. He gathered grell warriors under his command to plot against nearby kaldorei outposts.",al={"lord melenas lore","who is melenas","melenas story"},it="identity"},{q="Why must his death remain quiet?",a="Satyrs are ancient night elves cursed and twisted by demonic corruption, and their presence so close to Teldrassil’s sacred boughs is a deep embarrassment to kaldorei authorities. Dealing with Melenas swiftly and quietly prevents panic and limits the shame.",al={"why secrecy","twisted hatred secret","why quiet"},it="motive"},{q="Where was Melenas' Head taken from?",a="Melenas' Head was taken deep inside Fel Rock, a corrupted cavern just north of Dolanaar in central Teldrassil.",al={"where to find melenas","fel rock location","melenas location"},it="origin"},{q="What is Melenas' Head?",a="It is the severed head of Lord Melenas, a vile satyr who made his lair within Fel Rock just north of Dolanaar. Melenas rallied aggressive grell to his side and plotted dark deeds uncomfortably close to the night elves' sacred home, making his severed head undeniable proof that his corrupt influence has been extinguished.",al={"what is melenas head","melenas head item","whose head is this"},it="item",add="05bed8f4"},{q="Why does Tallonkai want Melenas' Head?",a="Tallonkai Swiftroot seeks the head as absolute proof of Lord Melenas's demise. The presence of a satyr so close to Shadowglen is considered a dangerous humiliation for the night elves. Delivering his head ensures the foul plotter has been silenced swiftly and quietly before his schemes can spread further across Teldrassil.",al={"why bring melenas head","who wants melenas head","why does tallonkai want the head"},it="why_wanted",add="b9c077d0"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know satyrs are a tragic demonic corruption of your ancient lineage. Lord Melenas’ quiet execution was both necessary and a source of cultural shame.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you know a severed enemy warlord’s head gives unmistakable proof that a dangerous adversary and his grell host have been broken."},kw={"fel rock","grell","lord melenas","melenas' head","satyr","teldrassil","twisted hatred"},rel={"quest:932","subzone:fel-rock","topic:satyr","zone:teldrassil"},src={"Melenas' Head","Twisted Hatred"}}
E["item:moonpetal-lily"] = {t="item",n="Moonpetal Lily",z="teldrassil",s="Moonpetal Lilies are large, luminous flora native to Teldrassil that flourish around freshwater pools. Renowned for their potent restorative qualities, their petals are prized as key ingredients in natural remedies and healing draughts.",h="Moonpetal Lilies are large, luminous flora native to Teldrassil that flourish around freshwater pools.",sec={{t="Flora of the Pools",b="Moonpetal Lilies grow exclusively along the moist banks of freshwater pools and ponds, particularly favored along the northwestern side of Aldrassil in Shadowglen. Like much of the plant life flourishing atop the newly grown World Tree, they absorb the unique essence of Teldrassil's sheltered groves. Their broad petals are gentle and radiant, easily spotted hugging the tranquil water's edge where natural moisture allows them to thrive.",sp=0},{t="Natural Antidotes",b="Night elf healers and herbalists value the Moonpetal Lily for its extraordinary healing properties. When combined with other forest flora, such as Hyacinth Mushrooms, the lily acts as a powerful soothing and stabilizing agent. This restorative quality makes it an essential component when brewing antidotes to counteract lethal toxins, notably the virulent venom produced by the Webwood spiders lurking within Shadowthread Cave.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do Moonpetal Lilies grow?",a="They grow along the banks of the two freshwater ponds situated on the northwestern side of Aldrassil within Shadowglen on Teldrassil.",al={"where to find moonpetal lilies","moonpetal lily location","lily spots"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What are Moonpetal Lilies used for?",a="The lilies possess notable restorative and healing properties. In Shadowglen, Dirania Silvershine uses them alongside Hyacinth Mushrooms and Webwood Ichor to brew a potent antidote for spider venom.",al={"moonpetal lily uses","what does moonpetal lily do"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who needs an antidote made from these lilies?",a="A night elf named Iverron, who fell victim to the poisonous bite of the Webwood spiders near Shadowthread Cave, requires an antidote concocted from Moonpetal Lilies to survive.",al={"who is the antidote for","iverron poison"},it="target"},{q="Can Moonpetal Lilies be gathered outside of Teldrassil?",a="They are tied directly to the secluded pools of Teldrassil and are known locally within the sheltered boughs of Shadowglen.",al={"do lilies grow elsewhere","moonpetal lily other zones"},it="place"},{q="What is a Moonpetal Lily?",a="The Moonpetal Lily is a large, aquatic flower native to the tranquil waters of Teldrassil. Renowned for its potent natural healing properties, it flourishes in damp soil along the edges of shaded woodland pools and ponds, such as those nestled near Aldrassil in Shadowglen.",al={"what is moonpetal lily","moonpetal lily info","about moonpetal lily"},it="identity",add="1aae6896"}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Though collected directly by hand during urgent crises, Moonpetal Lilies serve as a clear demonstration of Teldrassil's rich, restorative botanical potential.",["race:NightElf"]="For young kaldorei training in Shadowglen, learning the restorative properties of native plants like the Moonpetal Lily is a vital early lesson in living harmoniously with nature."},kw={"aldrassil","antidote","dirania silvershine","iverron","moonpetal","moonpetal lily","shadowglen","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:3521","item:hyacinth-mushroom","item:webwood-ichor","npc:iverron","subzone:aldrassil","subzone:shadowglen","subzone:shadowthread-cave","zone:teldrassil"},src={"Moonpetal Lily","Iverron's Antidote (Classic)"}}
E["item:nightsaber-fang"] = {t="item",n="Nightsaber Fang",z="teldrassil",s="In Teldrassil, hunters take fangs from the nightsabers prowling the forest. Woodland residents also seek these teeth as reagents.",h="In Teldrassil, hunters take fangs from the nightsabers prowling the forest.",sec={{t="Trophy of the Hunt",b="Nightsabers hunt beneath Teldrassil’s canopy, among the deadliest natural predators of northern Kalimdor. Night elves revere them for their agility, ferocity, and deep spiritual bond with Elune. A hunter who kills one can take its sharp fangs as proof of skill. Some figures in the forest seek those fangs for darker rites.",sp=0},{t="A Satyr's Reagent",b="Outside Dolanaar, the satyr Zenn Foulhoof preys on eager, inexperienced travelers. He claims to need woodland reagents and persuades newcomers to gather nightsaber fangs, strigid feathers, and spider silk. Giving him these materials aids the trickster, who openly mocks the naive hero when they deliver them.",sp=1,bt={"q488.2"}}},faq={{q="Where do Nightsaber Fangs come from?",a="Nightsaber Fangs come from the predatory nightsabers prowling Teldrassil, especially the forest around Dolanaar.",al={"where to get nightsaber fangs","who drops nightsaber fangs","nightsaber fang source"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Who wants Nightsaber Fangs in Teldrassil?",a="Zenn Foulhoof, a satyr outside Dolanaar, asks wandering adventurers to bring him Nightsaber Fangs.",al={"who needs nightsaber fangs","nightsaber fang turn in","who buys nightsaber fangs"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why does Zenn Foulhoof want Nightsaber Fangs?",a="Zenn claims he needs animal reagents for his work in the forest, but keeps its nature secret and takes delight in duping gullible travelers.",al={"why zenn wants fangs","zenn foulhoof reagent purpose","zenn bidding motive"},sp=1,it="purpose",bt={"q488.2"}},{q="What other reagents does Zenn ask for alongside the fangs?",a="Along with two nightsaber fangs, Zenn asks for two strigid owl feathers and two swatches of webwood spider silk.",al={"what else does zenn need","zenn bidding items","other reagents for zenn"}},{q="What is a Nightsaber Fang?",a="A Nightsaber Fang is a sharp canine tooth taken from the nightsabers prowling the forests of Teldrassil. While simply a natural part of these predatory great cats, such fangs are sought out by practitioners of dark arts who prize them as raw reagents for clandestine rituals and unsanctioned concoctions.",al={"what is nightsaber fang","nightsaber fang lore","about nightsaber fangs"},it="identity",add="bc504af2"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know nightsabers as cherished companions and symbols of Elune. Hunting these sacred predators for a treacherous satyr brings shame.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you prove your skill in the wild by felling a nightsaber and taking its fang. Giving its parts to corrupt woodland spirits twists the spirit of the hunt."},kw={"dolanaar","fang","nightsaber","reagent","satyr","teldrassil","zenn foulhoof"},rel={"npc:zenn-foulhoof","quest:488","zone:teldrassil","subzone:dolanaar","item:strigid-owl-feather","item:webwood-spider-silk","topic:satyr","topic:night-elf"},src={"Nightsaber Fang","Zenn's Bidding"}}
E["item:partially-filled-vessel"] = {t="item",n="Partially Filled Vessel",z="teldrassil",s="Tenaron Stormgrip gives young night elf initiates the Partially Filled Vessel in Aldrassil. It carries blessed moonwell water from Shadowglen toward Dolanaar.",h="Tenaron Stormgrip gives young night elf initiates the Partially Filled Vessel in Aldrassil.",sec={{t="A Sacred Delivery",b="Young kaldorei initiates gather blessed water from Shadowglen’s secluded moonwell. In Aldrassil, Tenaron Stormgrip pours a sample into the vessel for its journey across Teldrassil. More water from the tree’s moonwells must be gathered to tend to the island’s health.",sp=0},{t="Onward to Dolanaar",b="Carry the vessel south through the valley gates, then follow the cobblestone roads west to Dolanaar. The journey takes a young adventurer beyond Shadowglen’s protected nursery and into Teldrassil’s wider wilds. At Dolanaar’s central moonwell, Corithras Moonrage takes the vessel and directs the next part of the ritual.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside the vessel?",a="The vessel holds pure water from Shadowglen’s sacred moonwell, poured in by the druid Tenaron Stormgrip.",al={"what's in the vessel","vessel contents","what water is in it"},it="item"},{q="Why is it only partially filled?",a="Shadowglen’s moonwell supplies only the first sample. Caring for Teldrassil requires water from several moonwells before the vessel is full.",al={"why partly filled","why is it not full"},it="power"},{q="Who do I take this vessel to?",a="Carry the vessel south out of Shadowglen, then follow the cobblestone road west to Dolanaar. Deliver it to Corithras Moonrage, who tends the town’s moonwell.",al={"who gets the vessel","where do i bring it","vessel turn in"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Why is moonwell water being moved around Teldrassil?",a="Druids and priestesses monitor and nourish Teldrassil through its moonwell waters. Moving water between wells helps maintain their blessings across the troubled boughs of the newly grown World Tree.",al={"why transport moonwell water","purpose of the water","why move water"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the Partially Filled Vessel?",a="The Partially Filled Vessel is an enchanted container used by night elf druids to collect and transport the sacred waters of Teldrassil's moonwells. When Tenaron Stormgrip sends you forth from Shadowglen, he combines your gathered phial of blessed moonwell water into this vessel so that the sacred work can continue across the boughs of the World Tree.",al={"partially filled vessel lore","what is this vessel","what is the partially filled vessel"},it="identity",add="5f4a3df1"},{q="Where did the Partially Filled Vessel come from, and who made it?",a="Tenaron Stormgrip, one of the elder druids stationed atop Aldrassil in Shadowglen, provides you with this vessel. After you draw water from Shadowglen's moonwell, Tenaron pours your phial into the container to begin the collection, entrusting you to carry it onward into the wider reaches of Teldrassil.",al={"who made the vessel","where did the vessel come from","vessel origin"},it="origin",add="4f920d4c"},{q="Why does Corithras Moonrage want the Partially Filled Vessel?",a="Corithras Moonrage awaits the vessel at the moonwell in Dolanaar to continue a vital druidic task known as the Crown of the Earth. Gathering the waters of Teldrassil is essential for inspecting and tending to the young World Tree, and Corithras requires the water you carried from Aldrassil before he can direct you toward the next stages of the ritual.",al={"why does corithras want this","why take the vessel to dolanaar","why bring vessel to corithras"},it="why_wanted",add="089d2d88"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a young night elf, carrying this vessel marks a passage from Shadowglen’s sanctuary to the wider work of caring for Teldrassil.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you carry sanctified water in service to the Cenarion Circle’s effort to nurture the World Tree and inspect its health."},kw={"aldrassil","corithras moonrage","crown of the earth","dolanaar","moonwell","partially filled vessel","shadowglen","tenaron stormgrip","vessel"},rel={"quest:921","npc:tenaron-stormgrip","npc:corithras-moonrage","subzone:shadowglen","subzone:dolanaar","subzone:aldrassil","item:filled-vessel","zone:teldrassil"},src={"Partially Filled Vessel","Crown of the Earth (2)"}}
E["item:rare-earth"] = {t="item",n="Rare Earth",z="teldrassil",s="At Dolanaar, Rare Earth waits for delivery to Denalan's camp near Lake Al'Ameth. The mineral-rich soil came from Darnassus for his botanical experiments on Teldrassil.",h="At Dolanaar, Rare Earth waits for delivery to Denalan's camp near Lake Al'Ameth.",sec={{t="Soil of Darnassus",b="Rare Earth is late reaching Dolanaar from Darnassus. Denalan, an eccentric botanist on Lake Al'Ameth's eastern shore, requested the parcel to study plants in Teldrassil's young ecosystem. Herbalist Syral Bladeleaf now entrusts the soil to travelers heading south, hoping it reaches Denalan before its potency fades.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Rare Earth used for?",a="Denalan, an herbalist and botanical researcher at Lake Al'Ameth, will use Rare Earth in his experiments. He cultivates Teldrassil's native plants with mineral compounds and enriched soils from Darnassus.",al={"rare earth use","what does denalan do with rare earth","rare earth purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Who sends the Rare Earth to Denalan?",a="Herbalist Syral Bladeleaf holds the package in Dolanaar. It arrived late from Darnassus, and she asks travelers heading south toward Lake Al'Ameth to carry it to Denalan.",al={"who gives rare earth","where do you get rare earth","syral bladeleaf parcel"},it="origin"},{q="Why was Denalan worried about the delivery?",a="The shipment was delayed on its way to Dolanaar, leaving Denalan waiting by the lake. When it arrives, he worries that the soil may have lost the freshness his experiments need.",al={"is rare earth ruined","denalan fresh earth","why late earth"},it="motive"},{q="What is Rare Earth?",a="Rare Earth is a specially sourced, fertile soil shipment dispatched from Darnassus. It is carefully prepared and packaged for sensitive agricultural and botanical research, retaining specialized nutrients that require it to be delivered fresh to maintain its potency for delicate cultivation experiments.",al={"what is rare earth","rare earth item","rare earth lore"},it="identity",add="e720b4cb"},{q="Why does Denalan want Rare Earth?",a="Denalan is an herbalist researcher stationed on the eastern shores of Lake Al'Ameth, studying and experimenting with the local flora of Teldrassil. He relies on this rare, nutrient-rich soil from Darnassus to nurture his delicate plantings and advance his botanical work on the island.",al={"why does denalan want rare earth","why want rare earth","why rare earth needed"},it="why_wanted",add="5312d2a9"}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Herbalists can look to Syral Bladeleaf and Denalan, who study how specialized earth changes the growth and properties of Teldrassil's saplings.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf tending the young World Tree, you can see how experiments at Lake Al'Ameth reveal the ways life adapts to Teldrassil's untamed boughs."},kw={"darnassus","denalan","dolanaar","herbalism","lake al'ameth","rare earth","syral bladeleaf"},rel={"quest:997","npc:denalan","npc:syral-bladeleaf","subzone:lake-al-ameth","subzone:dolanaar","zone:darnassus","zone:teldrassil","quest:940"},src={"Rare Earth","Denalan's Earth"}}
E["item:raven-claw-talisman"] = {t="item",n="Raven Claw Talisman",z="teldrassil",s="In Ban'ethil Barrow Den, the Raven Claw Talisman is kept among relics needed to awaken sleeping druids. The sacred night elf relic is one of four Relics of Wakening used to guide the Druids of the Talon safely back from the Emerald Dream.",h="In Ban'ethil Barrow Den, the Raven Claw Talisman is kept among relics needed to awaken sleeping druids.",sec={{t="A Key to Awakening",b="The Raven Claw Talisman rests in a designated chest inside Ban'ethil Barrow Den, where Teldrassil's Druids of the Talon entered deep meditative sleep. Their hibernation is a delicate spiritual threshold. Without the proper ceremonial focus, a druid whose link to the waking world is broken may remain stranded in the Emerald Dream. Athridas Bearmantle in Dolanaar needs this talisman, the Black Feather Quill, the Sapphire of Sky, and the Rune of Nesting to perform the awakening ritual and bring the sleepers back safely.",sp=0},{t="The Threat in the Barrow Den",b="Corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs have overrun Ban'ethil Barrow Den, putting its sacred chests and sleeping druids in peril. Their desecration has cut the sanctuary off from outside aid, and the relics may be lost or destroyed. Athridas Bearmantle calls on Teldrassil's defenders to brave the den's winding earthen corridors and secure the Raven Claw Talisman before the displaced druids are lost to the Dream forever.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Raven Claw Talisman used for?",a="The Raven Claw Talisman is one of four sacred Relics of Wakening needed to rouse the Druids of the Talon from deep hibernation in the Emerald Dream.",al={"what does the raven claw talisman do","raven claw talisman purpose","why do i need raven claw talisman"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is the Raven Claw Talisman found?",a="The Raven Claw Talisman rests in the Chest of the Raven Claw, inside the earthen tunnels of Ban'ethil Barrow Den, west of Dolanaar on Teldrassil.",al={"where is raven claw talisman","chest of the raven claw location","how to find raven claw talisman"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who needs the Raven Claw Talisman?",a="Athridas Bearmantle, a night elf druid in Dolanaar, needs the talisman to prepare the wakening rites for his displaced kin.",al={"who wants raven claw talisman","who takes the raven claw talisman","who do i turn this in to"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why can't the druids wake up without it?",a="Druidic hibernation involves a complex, delicate trance in the Emerald Dream. Without the Relics of Wakening to anchor the awakening ritual, a sleeper's spirit risks remaining lost there indefinitely.",al={"why do druids need relics to wake up","why relics of wakening","can druids wake up without relics"},it="power"},{q="What is the Raven Claw Talisman?",a="The Raven Claw Talisman is one of the four sacred Relics of Wakening kept by the Druids of the Talon. Stored within a dedicated chest inside the Ban'ethil Barrow Den, it is an essential component of the delicate ritual required to safely call slumbering druids back from their hibernation in the Emerald Dream.",al={"what is raven claw talisman","raven claw talisman info","relic raven claw talisman"},it="identity",add="33636b37"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can see how the Raven Claw Talisman reflects the Druids of the Talon's use of ritual foci to safeguard a spirit wandering the Emerald Dream.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you protect an ancient tradition and your sleeping kin by recovering this relic from the Gnarlpine furbolgs."},kw={"athridas bearmantle","ban'ethil","barrow den","dolanaar","druids of the talon","raven claw talisman","relics of wakening","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:483","subzone:ban-ethil-barrow-den","npc:athridas-bearmantle","item:black-feather-quill","item:sapphire-of-sky","item:rune-of-nesting","topic:emerald-dream","subzone:dolanaar"},src={"Raven Claw Talisman","The Relics of Wakening"}}
E["item:rune-of-nesting"] = {t="item",n="Rune of Nesting",z="teldrassil",s="At Ban'ethil Barrow Den, the Rune of Nesting lies among four sacred relics. It helps Athridas Bearmantle prepare the ritual that safely awakens the Druids of the Talon from the Emerald Dream.",h="At Ban'ethil Barrow Den, the Rune of Nesting lies among four sacred relics.",sec={{t="A Sacred Focus for Awakening",b="The Rune of Nesting lies in the Chest of Nesting, deep in the winding chambers of Ban'ethil Barrow Den. Night elf druids hibernate in underground barrow dens to commune with nature through the Emerald Dream. To return safely, the Druids of the Talon need a precise awakening ritual guided by sacred relics. The rune is one of four: the Raven Claw Talisman, the Black Feather Quill, the Sapphire of Sky, and the Rune of Nesting. Together, the relics help call the sleeping druids back to the waking world.",sp=0},{t="Crisis in Ban'ethil",b="Corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs have overrun Ban'ethil Barrow Den, putting its sleeping defenders in peril. Without the relics, the druids risk remaining trapped in the Emerald Dream while invaders desecrate their sanctuary. Recovering the Rune of Nesting and its companion artifacts allows Athridas Bearmantle in Dolanaar to prepare the ritual that can safely awaken them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Rune of Nesting used for?",a="Athridas Bearmantle requires the Rune of Nesting to conduct the ritual that safely rouses the Druids of the Talon from their deep slumber in the Emerald Dream. It is one of the four Relics of Wakening used in that ritual.",al={"what does rune of nesting do","rune of nesting purpose"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is the Rune of Nesting found?",a="The Rune of Nesting is stored in the Chest of Nesting, in the subterranean tunnels of Ban'ethil Barrow Den, west of Dolanaar on Teldrassil.",al={"where is rune of nesting","chest of nesting location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why can't the sleeping druids simply wake up on their own?",a="The druids enter a delicate, trance-like state when they hibernate in the Emerald Dream. Without sacred relics and an awakening ritual, they may be unable to return, leaving their minds adrift and their bodies exposed to danger.",al={"why do druids need waking ritual","why can't druids wake up"}},{q="What other relics are needed alongside the Rune of Nesting?",a="The ritual requires four Relics of Wakening: the Rune of Nesting, the Raven Claw Talisman, the Black Feather Quill, and the Sapphire of Sky.",al={"other relics of wakening","relics of wakening items"},it="item"},{q="What is the Rune of Nesting?",a="The Rune of Nesting is one of the four sacred Relics of Wakening kept by the Druids of the Talon in Teldrassil. Stored within a dedicated chest inside the Ban'ethil Barrow Den, it carries the specialized enchantments required to properly perform the awakening ritual for druids resting in deep communion with the Emerald Dream.",al={"rune of nesting","what is rune of nesting","rune of nesting lore"},it="identity",add="375c0565"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, the Rune of Nesting speaks to the sacred rituals of the Cenarion Circle and the danger sleeping brethren face when their sanctuaries are breached.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, the loss of wakening relics and the desecration of barrow dens reflect the growing corruption among Teldrassil's wildlife and furbolgs."},kw={"athridas bearmantle","ban'ethil barrow den","chest of nesting","druids of the talon","emerald dream","relics of wakening","rune of nesting"},rel={"quest:483","subzone:ban-ethil-barrow-den","npc:athridas-bearmantle","item:raven-claw-talisman","item:black-feather-quill","item:sapphire-of-sky","topic:druid","topic:emerald-dream"},src={"Rune of Nesting","The Relics of Wakening"}}
E["item:sapphire-of-sky"] = {t="item",n="Sapphire of Sky",z="teldrassil",s="In Ban'ethil Barrow Den, Sapphire of Sky helps call sleeping Druids of the Talon back from the Emerald Dream. It is one of four sacred Relics of Wakening kept by the night elves.",h="In Ban'ethil Barrow Den, Sapphire of Sky helps call sleeping Druids of the Talon back from the Emerald Dream.",sec={{t="The Wakening Ritual",b="Druids of the Talon sleep in hibernation within Ban'ethil Barrow Den, deep among Teldrassil's roots, while they commune with the wilds. Waking from that deep trance is perilous. Four sacred relics protect the passage: the Black Feather Quill, the Raven Claw Talisman, the Rune of Nesting, and the Sapphire of Sky. The gem completes the harmony needed to call the sleeping spirits back from the Emerald Dream. Without it, they risk being trapped there forever.",sp=0},{t="The Threat in Ban'ethil",b="Corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs have overrun Ban'ethil Barrow Den, leaving the sacred relics in their repositories. The Sapphire of Sky is secured inside the Chest of the Sky, along the winding underground corridors. The druids still sleep as the furbolgs rampage around them. Athridas Bearmantle in Dolanaar needs the sapphire and its companion relics to wake the sleepers before they are lost forever.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Sapphire of Sky?",a="Sapphire of Sky is a sacred gemstone and one of four Relics of Wakening kept in Ban'ethil Barrow Den. It works with three avian talismans to guide Druids of the Talon safely out of the Emerald Dream.",al={"sapphire of sky lore","what is this gem","sky sapphire"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the Sapphire of Sky kept?",a="The Sapphire of Sky is kept inside the Chest of the Sky, in the underground labyrinth of Ban'ethil Barrow Den in central Teldrassil.",al={"where to find sapphire of sky","chest of the sky location","sapphire location"},it="place"},{q="Why is the sapphire needed right now?",a="Corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs have invaded Ban'ethil Barrow Den and put the sleeping druids in grave danger. Deep in trance, the druids cannot simply wake on their own. Athridas Bearmantle needs the sapphire and the other relics for the delicate wakening ritual before the sleepers are lost forever.",al={"why get the sapphire","relics of wakening purpose"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who uses this artifact?",a="The Druids of the Talon and ritual keepers such as Athridas Bearmantle use the sapphire to wake their sleeping brothers from deep communion with nature.",al={"who uses sapphire of sky","druid ritual gem"},it="purpose"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can see why sacred anchors matter when your spirit enters the Emerald Dream. Without them, communion can turn fatal.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know that protecting the sacred relics in Ban'ethil Barrow Den helps preserve Teldrassil's fragile order amid growing corruption."},kw={"athridas bearmantle","ban'ethil barrow den","chest of the sky","druid of the talon","emerald dream","relics of wakening","sapphire of sky"},rel={"quest:483","subzone:ban-ethil-barrow-den","npc:athridas-bearmantle","item:raven-claw-talisman","item:black-feather-quill","item:rune-of-nesting","topic:emerald-dream","zone:teldrassil"},src={"Sapphire of Sky","The Relics of Wakening"}}
E["item:shaman-voodoo-charm"] = {t="item",n="Shaman Voodoo Charm",z="teldrassil",s="In Ban'ethil Barrow Den, Gnarlpine shamans wield the Shaman Voodoo Charm. Its vile magic can sever a sleeping druid's spirit from the body.",h="In Ban'ethil Barrow Den, Gnarlpine shamans wield the Shaman Voodoo Charm.",sec={{t="A Perverted Magic",b="The Gnarlpine tribe has fallen into madness and corruption on Teldrassil. Within Ban'ethil Barrow Den, its shamans wield magic beyond ordinary wilderness sorcery. Their voodoo charms let them tear a sleeping druid's consciousness from the mortal realm and trap it in the Emerald Dream. The furbolgs then animate the empty body. Night elf protectors become mindless guardians, killing anyone who enters the barrows.",sp=0},{t="Unraveling the Curse",b="Oben Rageclaw fell victim to the ritual. His spirit is trapped in the Emerald Dream while his animated body terrorizes the deep barrows. Reaching through the veil, Oben asked adventurers to slay the Gnarlpine shamans and bring back one of their charms. He hoped to study its vile enchantment, understand the furbolgs' twisted craft, and find a way to free his stolen flesh.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Shaman Voodoo Charm used for?",a="Gnarlpine shamans use the charm to sever a sleeping druid's spirit from the body and trap it in the Emerald Dream. The charm's magic animates the empty flesh to attack intruders.",al={"voodoo charm purpose","what does the charm do","shaman charm use"},it="purpose"},{q="Who carries these charms?",a="Gnarlpine shamans in the depths of Ban'ethil Barrow Den in Teldrassil carry these charms.",al={"who drops the charm","where to find shaman voodoo charm","gnarlpine shaman charm"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Oben Rageclaw need one?",a="Oben Rageclaw is trapped in the Emerald Dream while his animated body runs amok. He needs to study the charm's vile aura and magic to find a way to break the furbolgs' enchantment.",al={"why does oben want it","oben rageclaw charm","the sleeping druid item"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why do furbolgs have voodoo magic?",a="Corruption has driven the Gnarlpine shamans on Teldrassil to practice dark magic. Their charms carry a vile, unnatural aura, unlike traditional furbolg reverence for nature spirits and the elements.",al={"why do furbolgs use voodoo","furbolg voodoo lore"}},{q="What is the Shaman Voodoo Charm?",a="It is an enchanted furbolg talisman wielded by corrupted Gnarlpine shamans inside the Ban'ethil Barrow Den. Emanating a vile magical aura, the charm harnesses dark rituals capable of severing a sleeping night elf druid's spirit from their physical form, leaving the spirit helpless while the furbolgs animate and control the slumbering body.",al={"what is shaman voodoo charm","voodoo charm lore","what are these charms"},it="identity",add="6bf5e1a6"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you see the charm as a horrifying perversion of sacred slumber. Its dark magic traps the dreamer in the Emerald Dream and turns the body into a puppet.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know the charms in Ban'ethil Barrow Den reveal how deeply the Gnarlpine have desecrated one of the kaldorei's holiest communal resting places."},kw={"ban'ethil barrow den","emerald dream","furbolg","gnarlpine","oben rageclaw","shaman voodoo charm","sleeping druid","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:2541","npc:oben-rageclaw","subzone:ban-ethil-barrow-den","topic:furbolg","topic:druid","topic:emerald-dream","zone:teldrassil"},src={"Shaman Voodoo Charm","The Sleeping Druid"}}
E["item:shimmering-frond"] = {t="item",n="Shimmering Frond",z="teldrassil",s="In the Oracle Glade, a strange plant casts a twisting, shimmering aura. Its fronds come from a species native to the Swamp of Sorrows, far across the Great Sea.",h="In the Oracle Glade, a strange plant casts a twisting, shimmering aura.",sec={{t="A Specimen from Afar",b="A radiant plant grows among the trees near the Oracle Glade. Its aura pulses, and its fronds shimmer in the woodland light. Denalan, who tends planters beside Lake Al'Ameth, recognizes the leaves as belonging to a species from the Swamp of Sorrows in the Eastern Kingdoms. How seeds from that distant marsh crossed the Great Sea and took root on Teldrassil remains a mystery. Denalan is growing specimens in his own soil to study them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the Shimmering Frond come from?",a="You can gather the frond from a strange plant in the Oracle Glade on Teldrassil. Its leaves shimmer with a twisting, pulsing radiance in the forest light.",al={"where do i get shimmering frond","shimmering frond location","strange fronded plant"},it="origin"},{q="Who is interested in the Shimmering Frond?",a="Denalan, a night elf naturalist conducting botanical research beside Lake Al'Ameth, wants to inspect the frond. He is interested in strange plants taking root across Teldrassil.",al={"who wants shimmering frond","who to give shimmering frond","denalan shimmering frond"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What makes this plant so unusual on Teldrassil?",a="The plant comes from the Swamp of Sorrows in the Eastern Kingdoms, far across the Great Sea. Its presence on Teldrassil is unexpected because it is not native to Kalimdor or the World Tree.",al={"why is shimmering frond special","plant origin","swamp of sorrows plant"}},{q="What happens after giving the frond to Denalan?",a="Denalan plants the specimen in his planters beside Lake Al'Ameth. He tests its rapid growth and exotic properties.",al={"what does denalan do with it","sprouted fronds lore"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What is the Shimmering Frond?",a="It is a leaf taken from an unusual, overgrown flora known as the Strange Fronded Plant found in the Oracle Glade. The frond constantly glimmers under the forest canopy, radiating a twisting, pulsing aura uncommon to the boughs of Teldrassil.",al={"what is shimmering frond","shimmering frond item","what is this frond"},it="identity",add="7be1ca60"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you may find an invasive marsh plant thriving on Teldrassil's newly raised branches a curious anomaly.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As an herbalist, you can appreciate the rare resilience it took for a Swamp of Sorrows plant to cross the ocean and thrive in foreign soil."},kw={"botany","denalan","lake al'ameth","oracle glade","shimmering frond","strange fronded plant","swamp of sorrows","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:931","npc:denalan","subzone:oracle-glade","subzone:lake-al-ameth","zone:swampofsorrows","quest:2399","zone:teldrassil"},src={"Shimmering Frond","The Shimmering Frond"}}
E["item:simple-sigil"] = {t="item",n="Simple Sigil",z="teldrassil",s="In Shadowglen, a Simple Sigil calls novice night elf warriors to training with Alyissia. It marks their first step into Teldrassil’s defense.",h="In Shadowglen, a Simple Sigil calls novice night elf warriors to training with Alyissia.",sec={{t="A Summons to Arms",b="In Shadowglen, Conservator Ilthalaine guides young night elves as they seek their calling. A runner brings a Simple Sigil from the warrior trainer Alyissia, and Ilthalaine gives it to fledgling warriors. Its inscription tells each recruit to report for instruction. The token marks the start of their martial training as troubling times come to the World Tree.",sp=0},{t="The Burden of Defense",b="Alyissia uses the sigil to speak with recruits about the kaldorei’s pressing needs. Teldrassil’s recent growth, corruption spreading among forest beasts, and the rediscovery of distant lands such as Feralas have stretched night elven protectors thin. The sigil holds no power. It welcomes a recruit among the guardians charged with shielding their people from emerging threats.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Simple Sigil?",a="The Simple Sigil is an inscribed token for novice night elf warriors in Shadowglen. Conservator Ilthalaine gives it to them, and its inscription directs them to report to Alyissia for training.",al={"simple sigil item","what does simple sigil do","what is this sigil"},it="identity"},{q="Who sends the Simple Sigil?",a="A runner carries the Simple Sigil from Alyissia, the warrior trainer in Shadowglen, to Conservator Ilthalaine, who gives it to novice warriors.",al={"who made the sigil","who sent simple sigil"},it="origin"},{q="What should I do with it?",a="Read the inscription and take the Simple Sigil to Alyissia near the base of Aldrassil in Shadowglen to begin your warrior training.",al={"where to turn in simple sigil","who takes simple sigil"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Does the sigil grant any special abilities?",a="No. The Simple Sigil is a written notice that introduces aspiring warriors to their mentor.",al={"sigil powers","simple sigil stats"},it="power",gp=true}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a kaldorei warrior, the Simple Sigil is your first credential in the martial traditions used to safeguard Teldrassil.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see the urgency facing the kaldorei: Alyissia and other trainers recruit capable hands to fight the growing corruption in the boughs of the World Tree."},kw={"alyissia","ilthalaine","kaldorei warrior","shadowglen","simple sigil","teldrassil","warrior training"},rel={"quest:3116","npc:alyissia","npc:ilthalaine","subzone:shadowglen","topic:warrior","topic:night-elf","zone:teldrassil","zone:feralas"},src={"Simple Sigil","Simple Sigil (Classic)"}}
E["item:strigid-owl-feather"] = {t="item",n="Strigid Owl Feather",z="teldrassil",s="Strigid Owl Feathers are gathered from the owls in Teldrassil's boughs. Zenn Foulhoof seeks them for his covert dealings.",h="Strigid Owl Feathers are gathered from the owls in Teldrassil's boughs.",sec={{t="Forest Plumage and Dark Dealings",b="Strigid owls and screechers hunt through the Crown of the Earth. Their feathers and down lie across the forest floor. Outside Dolanaar, the renegade satyr Zenn Foulhoof sends inexperienced travelers down the road from Shadowglen to gather strigid feathers, spider silk, and nightsaber fangs for his shady business.",sp=1,bt={"q488.2"}}},faq={{q="Where can I find Strigid Owl Feathers?",a="Strigid owls and strigid screechers live in the woodlands around Dolanaar and across Teldrassil, where you can gather their feathers.",al={"feather location","where do strigid owl feathers drop","owl feather farm"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants Strigid Owl Feathers?",a="Zenn Foulhoof, a satyr along the trail into Dolanaar, asks you to gather the feathers with webwood silk and nightsaber fangs.",al={"who needs owl feathers","owl feather turn in","zenn owl feather"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What does Zenn Foulhoof use the feathers for?",a="Zenn says the feathers are reagents for his secret business in the forest. He also takes pleasure in tricking unsuspecting recruits into doing his dirty work.",al={"why does zenn want feathers","zenn reagent purpose"},sp=1,it="purpose",bt={"q488.2"}},{q="What is a Strigid Owl Feather?",a="A Strigid Owl Feather is a plumage plume gathered from the predatory strigid owls native to the boughs of Teldrassil. While simple bird feathers on their surface, they serve as potent natural reagents for those dabbling in craft, alchemy, or darker woodland rites.",al={"strigid owl feather","what is strigid owl feather","owl feather teldrassil"},it="identity",add="c56fcaa2"},{q="Where does a Strigid Owl Feather come from?",a="These feathers are harvested directly from strigid owls and strigid screechers nesting throughout the forests of Teldrassil, particularly around Dolanaar. As natural biological materials shed or taken from the forest's avian predators, they are grown by nature rather than crafted by any mortal hands.",al={"where do strigid owl feathers come from","strigid owl feather source","who made strigid owl feather"},it="origin",add="91562481"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know Teldrassil's owls are creatures of Elune. Zenn Foulhoof's exploitation of them insults the sacred wood.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you hold Teldrassil's avian hunters in high regard. Seeing their feathers gathered under false pretenses for suspicious reagents can unsettle you."},kw={"dolanaar","reagents","strigid owl","strigid owl feather","strigid screecher","teldrassil","zenn foulhoof"},rel={"quest:488","npc:zenn-foulhoof","item:nightsaber-fang","item:webwood-spider-silk","subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","topic:satyr","topic:night-elf"},src={"Strigid Owl Feather","Zenn's Bidding"}}
E["item:tainted-heart"] = {t="item",n="Tainted Heart",z="teldrassil",s="In Teldrassil, Denalan gives adventurers a heart still troubled by corruption. Though its outer foul moss is gone, lingering energies remain, and he seeks to cleanse them with rich soil.",h="In Teldrassil, Denalan gives adventurers a heart still troubled by corruption.",sec={{t="A Corrupted Core",b="Teldrassil's natural balance is troubled by a malady that warps its plants and beasts. After foul moss is stripped from a blighted growth, Denalan gives adventurers the Tainted Heart within. Darkness still clings to its tissue. Denalan hopes specially prepared, nutrient-rich earth can counter the taint and restore what was corrupted.",sp=0},{t="Denalan's Remedy",b="The Tainted Heart shows a strange vitality when placed in Denalan's enchanted planter. It burrows into the rich soil and absorbs its curative nutrients. The earth burns away the corruption, and the heart emerges alive, pulsing with clean energy and eager to defend those who healed it.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Tainted Heart?",a="The Tainted Heart is the inner core of a corrupted plant found on Teldrassil. Botanist Denalan stripped away the foul moss, but the heart remains corrupted until purified.",al={"what is tainted heart","tainted heart item"},it="identity"},{q="Who cleanses the Tainted Heart?",a="Denalan directs adventurers to plant the Tainted Heart in his specially prepared planter at Lake Al'Ameth. The nutritive soil purifies it and clears away its unnatural corruption.",al={"who cleanses it","how to clean tainted heart"}},{q="What happens after it is planted?",a="The heart burrows into the planter's soil. Moments later, it emerges cleansed and pulsing with vitality, ready to bond with whoever restored it.",al={"what happens to the heart","planted heart result"},sp=1},{q="Why is the heart corrupted in the first place?",a="A strange blight is spreading across the World Tree Teldrassil, corrupting native flora, timberlings, and wildlife throughout its boughs.",al={"why corrupted","teldrassil corruption heart"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Denalan want you to plant the Tainted Heart?",a="Denalan has managed to strip away the foul moss clinging to the heart, but its inner core remains deeply tainted. He hopes the rich, nutritive soil in his specially prepared planter will heal the affliction, drawing out the corruption and restoring the living seed to vitality.",al={"why plant the tainted heart","tainted heart purpose","why does denalan want the tainted heart"},it="why_wanted",add="ae8829e0"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a Cenarion druid, cleansing the Tainted Heart offers direct insight into the creeping corruption threatening the young World Tree's health.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As an herbalist, you can appreciate Denalan's craft in mixing enriched soils that draw unnatural rot from living plant matter."},kw={"cleansing","corruption","denalan","lake al'ameth","planter","tainted heart","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:941","npc:denalan","zone:teldrassil"},src={"Tainted Heart","Planting the Heart"}}
E["item:tallonkai-s-jewel"] = {t="item",n="Tallonkai's Jewel",z="teldrassil",s="On Teldrassil, Tallonkai's Jewel is lost from its druidic talisman. Ferocitas the Dream Eater prizes the emerald, which is needed to mend the Emerald Dreamcatcher.",h="On Teldrassil, Tallonkai's Jewel is lost from its druidic talisman.",sec={{t="A Stolen Core",b="Tallonkai Swiftroot received the Emerald Dreamcatcher from Gaerolas Talvethen, warden of the druids in the Ban'ethil Barrow Den. The talisman is a powerful focus that draws energy from the Emerald Dream. When it was damaged, someone pried its radiant central emerald free and carried it into eastern Teldrassil. Ferocitas the Dream Eater, a corrupted Gnarlpine leader, took the jewel and made it into a necklace. Its green light glimmered in the forest gloom, but its harmony with the Emerald Dream meant nothing to the furbolg. To Ferocitas, it was only a trophy until it could be recovered.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Tallonkai's Jewel?",a="Tallonkai's Jewel is an enchanted emerald and the centerpiece of the Emerald Dreamcatcher, a druidic focus Gaerolas Talvethen gave to Tallonkai Swiftroot of Dolanaar.",al={"what is the jewel","tallonkai jewel lore"},it="identity"},{q="Who stole Tallonkai's Jewel?",a="Ferocitas the Dream Eater stole the jewel. He leads the corrupted Gnarlpine mystics living north of Starbreeze Village.",al={"who has the jewel","who stole it","who took tallonkais jewel"}},{q="Can the Gnarlpine furbolgs use the jewel's power?",a="No. Ferocitas wore the emerald as a glowing necklace, but its druidic power was useless to the corrupted furbolg.",al={"can ferocitas use it","gnarlpine emerald power"},it="power"},{q="Where does the jewel go after it is recovered?",a="The jewel goes back to Tallonkai Swiftroot on Dolanaar's upper tier, where he uses it to mend and fully restore the Emerald Dreamcatcher.",al={"what happens to the jewel","repairing dreamcatcher"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does anyone want Tallonkai's Jewel?",a="Tallonkai Swiftroot desperately needs this glowing emerald returned so he can repair his damaged Emerald Dreamcatcher. The corrupted Gnarlpine furbolg mystic, Ferocitas the Dream Eater, took it to wear as a shining necklace, drawn to its magical glow without understanding that its dream-attuned power is utterly useless in his hands.",al={"why is tallonkai's jewel wanted","why does tallonkai want the jewel","why steal tallonkai's jewel"},it="why_wanted",add="4dd99e12"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you know the emerald is attuned to the Emerald Dream. Its misuse by corrupted furbolgs affronts the balance.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you help restore order to Teldrassil by taking sacred craftwork from the encroaching Gnarlpine."},kw={"dolanaar","emerald dreamcatcher","ferocitas the dream eater","gnarlpine mystics","starbreeze village","tallonkai swiftroot","tallonkai's jewel"},rel={"quest:2459","item:emerald-dreamcatcher","npc:tallonkai-swiftroot","quest:2438","subzone:dolanaar","subzone:starbreeze-village","zone:teldrassil"},src={"Tallonkai's Jewel","Ferocitas the Dream Eater (quest)"}}
E["item:timberling-seed"] = {t="item",n="Timberling Seed",z="teldrassil",s="Across Teldrassil, Timberling Seeds are gathered from plant spirits that have grown hostile. Naturalists and druids study them to learn why the forest's plant life has turned aggressive.",h="Across Teldrassil, Timberling Seeds are gathered from plant spirits that have grown hostile.",sec={{t="Seeds of a Restless Forest",b="Timberlings are nature elementals of Teldrassil, and their temper reflects the World Tree's balance. Lately they have grown hostile and angry, troubling the night elves who tend the boughs. Herbalists such as Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth suspect trouble in the soil. They gather seeds from wild timberlings, hoping that purified, carefully tended soil might let docile offspring sprout.",sp=0},{t="A Rooted Corruption",b="Seeds from wild timberlings carry the taint of their corrupted parents. Cenarion scholars such as Rellian Greenspyre in Darnassus find that the trouble runs deeper than poor growth. Corruption has taken hold among Teldrassil's plant spirits and throughout the great tree's ecosystem.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is a timberling seed?",a="A timberling seed is the reproductive kernel of a timberling, a plant-like nature elemental found across Teldrassil. Naturalists gather the seeds to study timberling growth and ecology.",al={"timberling seeds","what are timberling seeds","seeds of timberling"},it="identity"},{q="Where are these seeds gathered?",a="Wild timberlings and bog beasts along the shores and shallows of Lake Al'Ameth yield these seeds.",al={"where to get seeds","timberling seed drop","who drops timberling seed"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Denalan want timberling seeds?",a="Denalan suspects poor soil is driving the timberlings to rage. He hopes specially prepared soil will let wild seeds sprout into docile, uncorrupted timberlings.",al={"denalan purpose","why collect seeds","denalan's plan"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What does Rellian Greenspyre discover about the seeds?",a="Rellian finds that the seeds carry the taint of their corrupted parents. The corruption is beyond his ability to mend, leaving hope with Denalan's horticultural experiments.",al={"rellian seed study","what did rellian find","are seeds tainted"},sp=1,it="threat"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can read the tainted seeds as an early warning of unnatural corruption among Teldrassil's plant elementals, a grave concern for the Cenarion Enclave's protectors.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As an herbalist, you can study the seeds to see how soil conditions and ambient corruption affect wild flora."},kw={"corruption","darnassus","denalan","lake al'ameth","rellian greenspyre","teldrassil","timberling","timberling seed"},rel={"npc:denalan","quest:918","quest:922","subzone:lake-al-ameth","zone:darnassus","zone:teldrassil","topic:druid"},src={"Timberling Seed","Timberling Seeds (Classic)","Rellian Greenspyre (Classic)"}}
E["item:timberling-sprout"] = {t="item",n="Timberling Sprout",z="teldrassil",s="Along Lake Al'Ameth, Timberling Sprouts take root already touched by corruption. Night elf wardens pull them before they grow into aggressive timberlings.",h="Along Lake Al'Ameth, Timberling Sprouts take root already touched by corruption.",sec={{t="Blighted Seedlings",b="Timberlings are plant spirits bound to Teldrassil's natural vitality. Along Lake Al'Ameth, the night elves find seedlings that sprout tainted and aggressive instead of healthy and in harmony with the wild. The young sprouts seem beyond cleansing or natural healing, so the caretakers gather and destroy them. They hope to stop hostile timberlings from spreading across the fragile boughs of the newly planted World Tree.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are Timberling Sprouts found?",a="Timberling Sprouts grow near the water's edge along Lake Al'Ameth, south of Dolanaar in Teldrassil.",al={"sprout location","where are timberling sprouts","find sprouts"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are night elves pulling Timberling Sprouts from the ground?",a="The sprouts emerge tainted. Left alone, they grow into violent timberlings that threaten Teldrassil's safety and balance. The caretakers consider them beyond help and remove them while they are still small.",al={"why kill sprouts","timberling sprout purpose","why destroy sprouts"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is causing the sprouts to become tainted?",a="A mysterious sickness is affecting Teldrassil's wildlife and plant elementals. Botanist Denalan does not know its source, but it taints young timberlings from the moment they take root.",al={"why are timberlings corrupted","what is tainting them","sprout sickness"},it="threat"},{q="Who asks for Timberling Sprouts to be collected?",a="Denalan, the botanist tending Lake Al'Ameth, asks adventurers to gather the sprouts and clear them from the lakeside to keep the land pure.",al={"who wants sprouts","sprout questgiver","timberling sprouts turn in"},it="target",gp=true},{q="What is a Timberling Sprout?",a="A Timberling Sprout is the juvenile form of a timberling, a small plant-like elemental being that takes root along the moist shores of Lake Al'Ameth. Left undisturbed, these shoots will eventually grow into full-sized timberlings. Unfortunately, the sprouts springing up around the lake are tainted and aggressive, prompting the botanist Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth to have them plucked from the soil before they mature into dangerous threats.",al={"what is timberling sprout","timberling sprouts what are they","timberling sprout info"},it="identity",add="f13cc7b7"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid attuned to Kalimdor's plant life and elementals, you may see woodland spirits emerging corrupted as a grim omen for Teldrassil's future.",["race:NightElf"]="As a young night elf training in Shadowglen, you are tasked with clearing the sprouts to safeguard your new woodland home."},kw={"aldrassil","corruption","lake al'ameth","shadowglen","teldrassil","timberling","timberling sprout"},rel={"quest:919","subzone:lake-al-ameth","zone:teldrassil","quest:940"},src={"Timberling Sprout","Timberling Sprouts"}}
E["item:tourmaline-phial"] = {t="item",n="Tourmaline Phial",z="teldrassil",s="At the Pools of Arlithrien, the Tourmaline Phial gathers blessed moonwell water for Teldrassil's rituals.",h="At the Pools of Arlithrien, the Tourmaline Phial gathers blessed moonwell water for Teldrassil's rituals.",sec={{t="Vessel of Arlithrien",b="Corithras Moonrage gives the Tourmaline Phial to travelers for rituals that tend the World Tree. Druids in Dolanaar use gemstone vials to collect pure moonwell water across Teldrassil. This phial is meant for the moonwell beside the Pools of Arlithrien, southeast of the road to Darnassus, where hostile Gnarlpine furbolgs are growing more troublesome.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Tourmaline Phial used for?",a="The Tourmaline Phial collects sacred water from the moonwell at the Pools of Arlithrien. Once filled, you return it to Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar for the Crown of the Earth rituals.",al={"what does tourmaline phial do","tourmaline phial purpose","use tourmaline phial"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Who provides the Tourmaline Phial?",a="Corithras Moonrage, a night elf druid in Dolanaar, gives travelers the empty phial.",al={"who gives tourmaline phial","where do i get tourmaline phial"},it="origin"},{q="Where is the moonwell for this phial?",a="The moonwell lies beside the Pools of Arlithrien, southeast of the main gateway to Darnassus.",al={"pools of arlithrien moonwell","where to fill tourmaline phial"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Tourmaline Phial?",a="The Tourmaline Phial is an empty ceremonial vessel crafted to draw and transport sacred waters from the moonwells across Teldrassil. Entrusted to you by Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar, it is specially designated to collect water from the secluded moonwell resting near the Pools of Arlithrien.",al={"what is tourmaline phial","tourmaline phial lore","tourmaline vial"},it="identity",add="6b01991a"},{q="Why does Corithras Moonrage want the Tourmaline Phial filled?",a="Corithras Moonrage requires water from each of Teldrassil's moonwells to study and assess the health of the World Tree and its sanctuaries. Drawing from the moonwell by the Pools of Arlithrien has become perilous due to violent Gnarlpine furbolg activity, prompting him to rely on capable travelers to safely retrieve a sample.",al={"why fill tourmaline phial","tourmaline phial purpose","why corithras wants phial"},it="why_wanted",add="001b9aba"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you carry a gemstone phial to gather moonwell water, a ceremonial duty as you learn to tend Teldrassil's fragile ecosystem.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know moonwell water reflects your people's reliance on Elune's grace and druidic vigilance as Teldrassil struggles against corruption."},kw={"corithras moonrage","crown of the earth","dolanaar","moonwell","pools of arlithrien","teldrassil","tourmaline phial"},rel={"npc:corithras-moonrage","item:filled-tourmaline-phial","quest:921","subzone:pools-of-arlithrien","subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","topic:furbolg"},src={"Tourmaline Phial","Crown of the Earth (4)"}}
E["item:verdant-sigil"] = {t="item",n="Verdant Sigil",z="teldrassil",s="In Shadowglen, Conservator Ilthalaine gives young night elf druids the Verdant Sigil as a summons to begin training.",h="In Shadowglen, Conservator Ilthalaine gives young night elf druids the Verdant Sigil as a summons to begin...",sec={{t="A Summons to the Path",b="Young night elves in Shadowglen who feel the call of the wild receive the Verdant Sigil from Conservator Ilthalaine. A messenger brings it from Mardant Strongoak, the druid trainer, and it directs novices to climb into Aldrassil's boughs. The token invites them to leave basic chores behind and begin serious study of communion with nature spirits and the mysteries of the Emerald Dream.",sp=0},{t="The First Step Into the Dream",b="Presenting the Verdant Sigil to Mardant Strongoak begins a young druid's lifelong craft. Novices are not yet ready to walk the sleeping trance of the Emerald Dream, but the token marks the start of their mentorship. Under Mardant's instruction, they learn to read the wilderness's whispers and practice early shapeshifting and healing arts in service of Teldrassil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Verdant Sigil?",a="The Verdant Sigil summons novice night elf druids in Shadowglen to seek out Mardant Strongoak in Aldrassil and begin formal training.",al={"what does verdant sigil do","why do i have verdant sigil","verdant sigil use"},it="purpose"},{q="Who hands out the Verdant Sigil?",a="Conservator Ilthalaine gives budding druids the Verdant Sigil in Shadowglen, carrying a message from Mardant Strongoak.",al={"who gives verdant sigil","where do i get verdant sigil"},gp=true},{q="Where do I take the sigil once I receive it?",a="You bring the Verdant Sigil to Mardant Strongoak, the druid trainer in Aldrassil's central chambers at the heart of Shadowglen.",al={"where do i bring verdant sigil","who takes verdant sigil","verdant sigil turn in"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What happens after presenting the sigil to Mardant Strongoak?",a="Mardant accepts the Verdant Sigil and welcomes you as his student. He guides you in communion with nature and prepares you for the mysteries of the Emerald Dream as your strength grows.",al={"what does mardant do with sigil","after verdant sigil"}},{q="What is the Verdant Sigil?",a="The Verdant Sigil is an inscribed token sent by the druid mentor Mardant Strongoak to young night elf initiates in Shadowglen. Carried by a messenger to Conservator Ilthalaine, it serves as a formal summons and introductory token, calling promising novices to climb the boughs of Aldrassil and begin their instruction in the ways of nature and the Emerald Dream.",al={"what is verdant sigil","verdant sigil item","verdant sigil lore"},it="identity",rc="Night Elf",add="e7925638"},{q="Where does the Verdant Sigil come from, and who made it?",a="The sigil originates with Mardant Strongoak, the druid trainer stationed within the great boughs of Aldrassil in Shadowglen. Seeking out novices ready to attune themselves to nature, Mardant dispatched the token via a courier to Conservator Ilthalaine, ensuring it would reach promising young druids taking their first steps in Teldrassil.",al={"who made verdant sigil","where did verdant sigil come from","origin of verdant sigil"},it="origin",rc="Night Elf",add="1efc6d6b"},{q="Why does anyone want the Verdant Sigil?",a="Mardant Strongoak asks you to bring the sigil to him as proof of your readiness and willingness to learn. By accepting the summons and returning it to the mentor, you establish your formal bond with him, demonstrating that you are prepared to study the spirits, master shapeshifting, and explore the mysteries of the Emerald Dream.",al={"why is verdant sigil wanted","why does mardant want verdant sigil","who wants the verdant sigil"},it="why_wanted",rc="Night Elf",add="fa84d5c5"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a young night elf druid, receiving the Verdant Sigil marks your first rite of passage from basic forest tending to disciplined Cenarion teaching.",["race:NightElf"]="Under Aldrassil's canopy, the sigil reflects the kaldorei tradition of attuning your spirit to the natural world and Teldrassil's guardians."},kw={"aldrassil","druid","emerald dream","ilthalaine","mardant strongoak","shadowglen","teldrassil","verdant sigil"},rel={"quest:3120","npc:mardant-strongoak","npc:ilthalaine","subzone:aldrassil","subzone:shadowglen","topic:druid","topic:emerald-dream","zone:teldrassil"},src={"Verdant Sigil","Verdant Sigil (Classic)"}}
E["item:voodoo-charm"] = {t="item",n="Voodoo Charm",z="teldrassil",s="In Teldrassil’s barrows, the Voodoo Charm can break the Gnarlpine enchantment holding Oben Rageclaw’s body.",h="In Teldrassil’s barrows, the Voodoo Charm can break the Gnarlpine enchantment holding Oben Rageclaw’s body.",sec={{t="A Severing of Dark Bonds",b="The spirit of Oben Rageclaw is separated from his flesh in the Gnarlpine barrow dens of Teldrassil. The furbolgs used foul magic to control the sleeping forms of sacred kaldorei protectors, and Oben’s body remains under their sorcery. He examines the charm and sees that its dark tether cannot be dispelled through traditional prayers. Once his soulless body is struck down, the charm must be channeled over the fallen form to purge the furbolg hold. Then Oben’s wandering spirit can depart for the Emerald Dream forever.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Voodoo Charm?",a="The Voodoo Charm breaks the Gnarlpine furbolgs’ magical control over Oben Rageclaw. After his soulless, enthralled body is struck down, the charm must be used on his remains to sever the enchantment and free his soul.",al={"what does voodoo charm do","voodoo charm use","how to use voodoo charm"},it="purpose"},{q="Who gives you the Voodoo Charm?",a="The spirit of Oben Rageclaw gives you the Voodoo Charm during Druid of the Claw. After examining it, he explains how it can free him from the Gnarlpine tribe’s sorcery.",al={"where do i get voodoo charm","who gives the charm","oben charm"}},{q="Why is it called a Voodoo Charm in night elf lands?",a="The name reflects the foreign or distorted occult magic of the Gnarlpine furbolgs, who have succumbed to corruption and bizarre tribal magic as it seeped into the Great Tree. The charm represents the magic used to ensnare and puppeteer the bodies of resting druids.",al={"why voodoo in teldrassil","is it troll voodoo"},it="origin"},{q="What happens after the charm is used?",a="Once the charm breaks the enchantment on Oben Rageclaw’s body, he is freed from the Gnarlpine tribe’s grip. His physical vessel is laid to rest, and his spirit departs Teldrassil for the Emerald Dream.",al={"what happens to oben","does oben survive"},sp=1},{q="What is the Voodoo Charm?",a="The Voodoo Charm is a magical talisman tied to the corrupted magic gripping Teldrassil's Gnarlpine furbolgs. The spirit of Oben Rageclaw inspects it to uncover how the furbolgs ensnared his physical form, realizing that only through the charm can the foul enchantment binding his soulless body be broken once and for all.",al={"what is voodoo charm","voodoo charm teldrassil","oben voodoo charm"},it="identity",add="b324ca48"},{q="Why does Oben Rageclaw want the Voodoo Charm used?",a="Oben Rageclaw requires the charm to sever the Gnarlpine furbolgs' hold over him. After his soulless body is defeated in battle, using the talisman over his fallen remains dispels the dark enchantment, releasing his trapped spirit so he can finally rest peacefully within the Emerald Dream.",al={"why use voodoo charm","why does oben want the charm","voodoo charm purpose"},it="why_wanted",add="75919bea"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For young druids training in Teldrassil, using the charm to mercy-kill and release a brother Druid of the Claw shows the tragic vulnerability of leaving one’s physical shell behind while traveling through the Emerald Dream.",["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, the charm reveals how deeply the Gnarlpine furbolgs have degenerated, turning sacred kaldorei barrow dens into places of grotesque spiritual imprisonment."},kw={"druid of the claw","gnarlpine","oben rageclaw","teldrassil","the sleeping druid","voodoo charm"},rel={"quest:2561","quest:2541","npc:oben-rageclaw","topic:druid","topic:emerald-dream","zone:teldrassil"},src={"Voodoo Charm","Druid of the Claw (quest)"}}
E["item:webwood-egg"] = {t="item",n="Webwood Egg",z="teldrassil",s="In Shadowthread Cave, Webwood Eggs lie in brooding nests in Shadowglen. Naturalists seek viable eggs to study the young spiders in secure laboratory conditions.",h="In Shadowthread Cave, Webwood Eggs lie in brooding nests in Shadowglen.",sec={{t="A Contained Specimen",b="Researchers cannot safely tame or subdue a fully grown, venomous Webwood spider alone. Scholars like Gilshalan Windwalker instead collect unhatched eggs from clutches hidden in Shadowthread Cave. An egg can be carried safely, and the spiderlings contained when they hatch, giving naturalists live subjects to study without facing adult spiders’ deadly fangs.",sp=0},{t="Destined for Darnassus",b="Teldrassil’s native wildlife has grown unnaturally aggressive and corrupted, alarming scholars across the boughs. Eggs and gathered venoms secured at Aldrassil are bound for Darnassus. Researchers hope that raising and examining the spiders in controlled settings will reveal more about the dark affliction spreading through the World Tree’s boughs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are Webwood Eggs found?",a="Webwood Eggs are found in clutches deep in the tunnels of Shadowthread Cave, in northwestern Shadowglen.",al={"webwood egg location","where is webwood egg","find webwood egg"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants the Webwood Egg?",a="Gilshalan Windwalker, a researcher at Aldrassil, wants the egg for his study of the aggressive arachnids troubling Shadowglen.",al={"who needs webwood egg","egg turn in","gilshalan egg"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why collect an egg instead of capturing a spider?",a="A mature Webwood spider is dangerous and too massive to capture and contain easily. An unhatched egg can be transported safely and placed in a secure enclosure before it hatches.",al={"why an egg","why not capture live spider"},it="motive"},{q="What happens to the egg after it is collected?",a="Gilshalan arranges for the egg and extracted spider venoms to be delivered to Darnassus, where scholars can study the creatures away from the dangers of the wild.",al={"where does the egg go","egg destination"},it="next_step"},{q="What is a Webwood Egg?",a="A Webwood Egg is an unhatched spider egg laid by the giant Webwood spiders nesting within Shadowglen. It holds live spider specimens before they emerge, allowing researchers to study the aggressive arachnids without risking immediate harm.",al={"what is webwood egg","webwood egg lore"},it="identity",add="0a629fbc"},{q="Where does the Webwood Egg come from?",a="These eggs are produced naturally by the giant Webwood spiders infesting Shadowthread Cave in northwestern Shadowglen. Within the dark, web-draped recesses of the cave, the spiders maintain nesting clutches where their broods incubate before hatching.",al={"webwood egg origin","where do webwood eggs come from","who made webwood egg"},it="origin",add="fd568742"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a young kaldorei defending Teldrassil’s sacred boughs, securing these eggs helps scholars investigate the unnatural taint spreading through the World Tree’s native wildlife.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, understanding how tainted Webwood spiders reproduce and behave offers clues to healing Teldrassil’s disrupted natural balance."},kw={"aldrassil","gilshalan","shadowglen","shadowthread cave","spider egg","teldrassil","webwood egg"},rel={"quest:917","subzone:shadowthread-cave","subzone:shadowglen","subzone:aldrassil","zone:darnassus","zone:teldrassil"},src={"Webwood Egg","Webwood Egg (quest)"}}
E["item:webwood-ichor"] = {t="item",n="Webwood Ichor",z="teldrassil",s="In Shadowglen, Webwood spiders carry venom that has left Iverron gravely ill. Dirania Silvershine needs their ichor, hyacinth mushrooms, and moonpetal lilies to brew an antidote.",h="In Shadowglen, Webwood spiders carry venom that has left Iverron gravely ill.",sec={{t="A Toxic Cure",b="Webwood spiders in Shadowglen carry venom that has left Iverron gravely ill. Dirania Silvershine asks for their ichor, hyacinth mushrooms, and moonpetal lilies to prepare an antidote.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Webwood Ichor used for?",a="Dirania Silvershine in Shadowglen needs Webwood Ichor, hyacinth mushrooms, and moonpetal lilies to prepare an antidote for Iverron, the poisoned night elf.",al={"webwood ichor use","what does webwood ichor do","why get ichor"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does Webwood Ichor come from?",a="Webwood Ichor comes from Webwood Spiders in northwestern Shadowglen, especially those around and inside Shadowthread Cave.",al={"where to find webwood ichor","how to get webwood ichor","webwood ichor drop"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Why use spider fluid to cure a spider bite?",a="Dirania requests Webwood Ichor as one ingredient for Iverron's antidote. She does not explain how the ichor works in the mixture.",al={"spider poison cure","why venom for antidote"}},{q="What is Webwood Ichor?",a="Webwood Ichor is fluid gathered from the Webwood spiders in Shadowglen. Dirania Silvershine requests it as one of the ingredients for an antidote to help Iverron.",al={"webwood ichor","what is webwood ichor","spider ichor"},it="identity",add="dbd415b9"},{q="Where does Webwood Ichor come from, and who made it?",a="It is not crafted or manufactured, but harvested directly from the Webwood spiders that infest the northwestern reaches of Shadowglen around Shadowthread Cave. The spiders produce the fluid naturally as part of their biology.",al={"webwood ichor source","where does webwood ichor come from","who made webwood ichor"},it="origin",add="789dead2"},{q="Why does anyone want Webwood Ichor?",a="Dirania Silvershine requires Webwood Ichor to concoct an urgent antidote for Iverron, who has fallen severely ill from spider poison. Combined with local Hyacinth Mushrooms and Moonpetal Lilies, the ichor is crucial to counteracting the venom that afflicted him.",al={"why gather webwood ichor","why do they need webwood ichor","who needs webwood ichor"},it="why_wanted",add="15a9db63"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a young night elf defending Aldrassil, gathering Webwood ichor teaches you that Teldrassil's deadliest poisons can harbor their own cures."},kw={"antidote","dirania silveshine","iverron","shadowglen","shadowthread cave","teldrassil","webwood ichor","webwood spider"},rel={"quest:3521","npc:iverron","subzone:shadowthread-cave","subzone:shadowglen","item:moonpetal-lily","item:hyacinth-mushroom","subzone:aldrassil","zone:teldrassil"},src={"Webwood Ichor","Iverron's Antidote (Classic)"}}
E["item:webwood-spider-silk"] = {t="item",n="Webwood Spider Silk",z="teldrassil",s="Webwood Spider Silk is gathered from Webwood Lurkers in the woods of Teldrassil. Crafters use spider silk in many ways, but these swatches draw the interest of suspicious figures among the World Tree’s boughs.",h="Webwood Spider Silk is gathered from Webwood Lurkers in the woods of Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Dubious Reagent",b="Webwood Lurkers around Dolanaar spin a fine, strong thread that is dangerous to gather. Zenn Foulhoof, a satyr along the forest road, asks young adventurers to collect the silk with nightsaber fangs and strigid owl feathers. He says these rare reagents are needed for his forest business, and newcomers gather them without asking about his corrupt nature or true motives.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can Webwood Spider Silk be found?",a="Webwood Spider Silk comes from Webwood Lurkers and related spiders in Teldrassil’s wilds, especially around Dolanaar.",al={"webwood silk location","who drops webwood spider silk","where to get webwood spider silk"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants this silk?",a="Zenn Foulhoof wants the silk. The satyr conceals his dealings just north of the path between Shadowglen and Dolanaar, and asks for it alongside owl feathers and predator fangs.",al={"who needs webwood silk","webwood silk quest giver","zenn foulhoof silk"},it="target"},{q="Why does Zenn Foulhoof want Webwood Spider Silk?",a="Zenn says he needs the silk as a reagent for his forest business, but keeps its details to himself.",al={"zenn foulhoof motive","why does zenn want silk"},sp=1,it="why_wanted"},{q="Can players use Webwood Spider Silk for tailoring?",a="No. Though it is genuine spider silk, this harvested thread is a reagent for a task, not ordinary tailoring cloth.",al={"is webwood silk tailoring mat","crafting webwood silk"},gp=true},{q="What is Webwood Spider Silk?",a="Webwood Spider Silk is raw, spun thread gathered from the giant arachnids that haunt the forests of Teldrassil. Fine yet resilient, swatches of this natural silk are prized by various practitioners across the boughs, though gathering it requires facing the venomous Webwood spiders directly in their shaded dens.",al={"what is webwood spider silk","webwood silk","spider silk teldrassil"},it="identity",add="9ba9fe8b",nx={6}},{q="Where does Webwood Spider Silk come from?",a="The silk is produced naturally by Webwood spiders, such as the Webwood Lurkers that lurk in the tangled thickets around Dolanaar. These aggressive arachnids spin thick webs among the great roots and hollows of Teldrassil, crafting durable threads that adventurers must harvest directly from the beasts themselves.",al={"webwood silk origin","who produces webwood silk","where does webwood silk come from"},it="origin",add="9736af76"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a young night elf leaving Shadowglen, take care with the creatures you hunt, especially when a solitary satyr near your heartland presses you to gather them.",["profession:Tailoring"]="As a tailor, you may seek arachnid thread, but these swatches are bound up in dark bargains with a satyr rather than ordinary loom work."},kw={"dolanaar","spider silk","teldrassil","webwood lurker","webwood spider silk","zenn foulhoof","zenn's bidding"},rel={"npc:zenn-foulhoof","quest:488","item:nightsaber-fang","item:strigid-owl-feather","subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","topic:satyr","topic:night-elf"},src={"Webwood Spider Silk","Zenn's Bidding"}}
E["item:webwood-venom-sac"] = {t="item",n="Webwood Venom Sac",z="teldrassil",s="In Shadowglen, Webwood Venom Sacs draw the attention of naturalists studying Teldrassil's growth. The sacs come from overgrown spiders, and their venom may show how the new World Tree has changed local wildlife.",h="In Shadowglen, Webwood Venom Sacs draw the attention of naturalists studying Teldrassil's growth.",sec={{t="A Symptom of Teldrassil's Growth",b="Webwood spiders live around and within Shadowthread Cave, and they are cousins to a much smaller breed found elsewhere. Their sudden growth and predatory aggression worry night elf researchers. Naturalists such as Gilshalan Windwalker study the venom in their sacs, examining its strength and composition. They hope to learn how Teldrassil's rapid, unblessed growth is changing the creatures that live on its boughs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are Webwood Venom Sacs found?",a="Webwood Venom Sacs come from spiders in northern Shadowglen, especially around and within Shadowthread Cave.",al={"where do these drop","webwood venom sac location","spider venom location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants these venom sacs?",a="Gilshalan Windwalker, a night elf researcher at Aldrassil in Shadowglen, collects the sacs to study the spiders' biology before returning to Darnassus.",al={"who needs venom sacs","gilshalan windwalker quest"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why are the webwood spiders so large?",a="Researchers believe Teldrassil's emergence and rapid growth have changed local wildlife, turning ordinary spiders into massive, aggressive predators.",al={"why are spiders big","webwood spider size"}},{q="Is this venom used to make an antidote?",a="Gilshalan collects the sacs for comparison and study. Spider venom in the region is dangerous, and remedies such as Iverron's antidote are needed to save those bitten in the woods.",al={"is this for a cure","antidote ingredient"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What is a Webwood Venom Sac?",a="A Webwood Venom Sac is an intact gland harvested from the webwood spiders nesting in and around Shadowthread Cave. These unnatural arachnids produce potent venom that researchers are keen to analyze, especially given how drastically the spiders have mutated compared to their smaller kin.",al={"what is webwood venom sac","webwood venom sac item","venom sac"},it="identity",add="bab81581"},{q="Where does a Webwood Venom Sac come from?",a="These sacs are harvested directly from the bodies of the webwood spiders that infest northern Shadowglen. They are biological organs produced naturally by the arachnids, whose alarming growth and venomous potency are believed to be influenced by the presence of Teldrassil itself.",al={"where do webwood venom sacs come from","origin of webwood venom sac","who made webwood venom sac"},it="origin",add="64d32b3b"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For a druid attuned to nature's balance, the potency of these venom sacs is troubling evidence that something is wrong among Teldrassil's boughs.",["race:NightElf"]="As a young night elf adventurer in Shadowglen, you gather these specimens to help scholars understand the strange ecology of your homeland in the boughs."},kw={"aldrassil","gilshalan windwalker","shadowglen","shadowthread cave","teldrassil","venom","webwood spider","webwood venom sac"},rel={"quest:916","npc:gilshalan-windwalker","subzone:shadowthread-cave","subzone:shadowglen","subzone:aldrassil","zone:teldrassil","quest:3521","zone:darnassus"},src={"Webwood Venom Sac","Webwood Venom"}}
E["npc:alyissia"] = {t="npc",n="Alyissia",z="teldrassil",s="In Aldrassil, Alyissia trains young night elves to fight with strength and discipline. She teaches warriors how to defend the young world tree.",h="In Aldrassil, Alyissia trains young night elves to fight with strength and discipline.",sec={{t="Martial Mentor of Shadowglen",b="Alyissia trains young night elves inside Aldrassil, where they learn to fight with steel and shield instead of nature magic or the priesthood. Kaldorei forces are known for their Sentinels and stealthy archers, but danger across Kalimdor also calls for fighters who can hold the front line. Alyissia teaches the first techniques: how to direct battle fury, master a stance, and withstand the wild creatures and corrupted grells that press into Shadowglen.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Alyissia?",a="Alyissia trains new night elf warriors in Aldrassil, the heart of Shadowglen. She gives them their first lessons and simple martial exercises as they begin training in Teldrassil.",al={"who is alyissia","alyissia npc","what does alyissia do"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Alyissia?",a="Alyissia is on the ground level inside Aldrassil's great hollow trunk, at the heart of Shadowglen in Teldrassil.",al={"alyissia location","where is alyissia","find alyissia"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What quests does Alyissia offer?",a="Alyissia receives the Simple Sigil carried by new night elf warriors. It introduces them to their warrior trainer in Aldrassil.",al={"alyissia quests","quests from alyissia"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Alyissia on?",a="Alyissia stands firmly with the night elves of Darnassus and the wider Alliance. Stationed in Aldrassil at the heart of Shadowglen, she serves her people by schooling promising young night elf warriors in the fundamentals of combat and duty, helping protect Teldrassil from surrounding threats.",al={"alyissia faction","who does alyissia serve","alyissia alliance"},it="side",add="ce80cb6f"},{q="Why is Alyissia here?",a="Alyissia is stationed in Aldrassil to guide newly awakened and aspiring night elf warriors taking their first steps in Shadowglen. She ensures that those who take up arms possess the discipline, combat techniques, and resolve needed to defend their secluded woodland sanctuary.",al={"why is alyissia in aldrassil","alyissia purpose shadowglen","what does alyissia do here"},it="why_here",add="6cc138aa"},{q="What does Alyissia want?",a="Alyissia seeks capable recruits who can learn the arts of martial combat and prove their valor. She wants incoming warriors to hone their discipline and martial skills so they can safeguard their woodland home and aid their kin across Teldrassil.",al={"what are alyissia goals","what does alyissia need","alyissia motive"},it="wants",add="8fbe341c"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a night elf warrior, Alyissia is your first mentor. She teaches early stances and martial discipline before you venture farther into Teldrassil's wilds.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you can learn the kaldorei's front-line martial discipline from Alyissia, preparing to defend Aldrassil's roots from corruption."},kw={"aldrassil","alyissia","night elf","shadowglen","teldrassil","warrior trainer"},rel={"subzone:aldrassil","quest:3116","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf"},src={"Alyissia"}}
E["npc:athridas-bearmantle"] = {t="npc",n="Athridas Bearmantle",z="teldrassil",s="In Dolanaar, Athridas Bearmantle works to protect the settlement and its wilds. The night elf druid sends young adventurers to investigate corruption among local wildlife and the nearby Gnarlpine furbolgs.",h="In Dolanaar, Athridas Bearmantle works to protect the settlement and its wilds.",sec={{t="Guardian of Dolanaar",b="In Dolanaar, Athridas Bearmantle helps defend night elves arriving from Shadowglen. Teldrassil, the newly grown world tree, shows unnatural signs of decay and unrest. Athridas organizes local scouting and guards the township against threats from the surrounding wilds.",sp=0},{t="The Furbolg Affliction",b="Athridas worries over the nearby Gnarlpine furbolgs. Once peaceful neighbors, the tribe has fallen to spreading madness and corruption that poisons its shamans and chieftains, driving them to violence against the Kaldorei. Athridas calls on willing champions to contain the danger and investigate the deeper taint taking root in the wilderness.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Athridas Bearmantle?",a="Athridas Bearmantle is a night elf in Dolanaar on Teldrassil. He organizes the settlement's defense and calls on adventurers to confront threats moving through the World Tree's boughs.",al={"who is athridas","athridas bearmantle lore","athridas dolanaar"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Athridas Bearmantle?",a="Find Athridas in Dolanaar, the first major town night elf adventurers reach after leaving Shadowglen in Teldrassil.",al={"athridas location","where is athridas","find athridas bearmantle"},gp=true},{q="What threats does Athridas focus on?",a="Athridas focuses on the aggressive Gnarlpine furbolgs, whose corruption has driven them to attack. He directs travelers to quell their assaults, investigate their madness, and recover vital relics.",al={"athridas quests","what does athridas want","athridas bearmantle tasks"},it="threat"},{q="Why are the Gnarlpine furbolgs attacking Dolanaar?",a="The Gnarlpine tribe has fallen to an unnatural corruption spreading through Teldrassil. It has driven their shamans and warriors mad with hostility toward the night elves.",al={"why are gnarlpine mad","gnarlpine corruption","furbolg hostility teldrassil"}},{q="What role does Athridas play in securing Teldrassil?",a="Athridas organizes an early defense against corruption among Teldrassil's beasts and furbolgs, working to keep the danger from overrunning Dolanaar.",al={"athridas role","athridas importance"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Athridas Bearmantle on?",a="Athridas stands firmly with the night elves of Darnassus and the Alliance. Stationed in Dolanaar, he devotes his efforts to protecting his kin and maintaining order across Teldrassil against encroaching corruption.",al={"athridas faction","who does athridas serve","athridas bearmantle allegiance"},it="side",add="04c7b610"},{q="What does Athridas Bearmantle want?",a="Athridas seeks to cleanse the sudden blight poisoning Teldrassil's wildlife and to quell the frenzy overtaking the local Gnarlpine furbolgs. He enlists capable travelers to investigate the corruption, recover sacred relics, and neutralize dangerous rogue furbolgs threatening Dolanaar.",al={"athridas goal","what is athridas trying to do","athridas bearmantle motivation"},it="wants",add="aae97259"},{q="Why is Athridas Bearmantle here in Dolanaar?",a="Dolanaar serves as the first major settlement travelers reach beyond Shadowglen, making it ground zero for managing local crises. Athridas remains stationed here to coordinate defensive efforts, monitor the troubled forests, and direct adventurers against escalating woodland threats.",al={"why is athridas in dolanaar","athridas post","reason athridas is here"},it="why_here",add="7a39a622"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For young Kaldorei leaving Shadowglen, Athridas shows the struggles of their new home, already threatened from within.",["class:Druid"]="Athridas's efforts against the corrupted Gnarlpine and his concern for ancient relics touch on the balance of nature druids are sworn to restore."},kw={"athridas","bearmantle","dolanaar","furbolg","gnarlpine","kaldorei","night elf","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","quest:476","quest:475","quest:483","quest:486","topic:night-elf"},src={"Athridas Bearmantle"}}
E["npc:ayanna-everstride"] = {t="npc",n="Ayanna Everstride",z="teldrassil",s="In Shadowglen, Ayanna Everstride trains young kaldorei in the hunter’s way. Stationed in Aldrassil, she teaches marksmanship, tracking, and survival beneath the World Tree.",h="In Shadowglen, Ayanna Everstride trains young kaldorei in the hunter’s way.",sec={{t="A Mentor in Shadowglen",b="Ayanna Everstride trains newly awakened kaldorei hunters inside Aldrassil, in the heart of Shadowglen. To the night elves, hunters are indispensable guardians of the sacred forests, not merely trappers or sharpshooters. Ayanna teaches novices early martial skills, ranged combat, and how to survive Teldrassil’s perilous woods.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ayanna Everstride?",a="Ayanna Everstride trains novice night elf hunters in Aldrassil, within Shadowglen on Teldrassil. She teaches basic combat and outdoor survival skills.",al={"ayanna everstride","who is ayanna","aldrassil hunter trainer"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Ayanna Everstride?",a="You can find Ayanna Everstride inside Aldrassil, the massive hollowed tree settlement in Shadowglen, at the heart of Teldrassil.",al={"ayanna location","where is ayanna","find ayanna everstride"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What quests involve Ayanna Everstride?",a="Early training sends new night elf hunters to Ayanna. Their first instructors may give them an Etched Sigil, and Ayanna then provides introductory training for aspiring woodland rangers.",al={"ayanna quests","etched sigil quest","ayanna quest giver"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Ayanna Everstride on?",a="Ayanna stands firmly with the night elves of Darnassus and the Alliance. Stationed at Shadowglen within Aldrassil, she guides newly awakened night elves in communion with the wilds, offering her loyalty to her kin and the defense of Teldrassil.",al={"ayanna everstride faction","who does ayanna everstride serve","ayanna everstride alliance"},it="side",add="881ffa5e"},{q="What does Ayanna Everstride want?",a="Ayanna is dedicated to guiding novice hunters. She wants to ensure that young night elves learn the ways of tracking, marksmanship, and surviving in harmony with nature before venturing deeper into the world.",al={"ayanna everstride goal","what does ayanna want","ayanna everstride purpose"},it="wants",add="e6b7d676"},{q="Why is Ayanna Everstride here in Shadowglen?",a="Ayanna resides in Aldrassil to serve as a hunter trainer. As young night elves awaken within the sheltered grove of Shadowglen, she prepares those drawn to the path of the hunter with essential skills, weapons, and instruction.",al={"why is ayanna in aldrassil","why is ayanna everstride here","ayanna everstride shadowglen role"},it="why_here",add="bbb0d24a"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter starting in Shadowglen, you can look to Ayanna Everstride for your first guidance in weapon handling, tracking, and wilderness survival.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you find Ayanna within Aldrassil’s sacred hollows. She prepares raw recruits to defend the surrounding forest from encroaching corruption and help safeguard the young World Tree."},kw={"aldrassil","ayanna","everstride","hunter trainer","night elf","shadowglen","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:aldrassil","quest:3117","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf"},src={"Ayanna Everstride"}}
E["npc:corithras-moonrage"] = {t="npc",n="Corithras Moonrage",z="teldrassil",s="Corithras Moonrage is a night elf scholar and quest giver stationed in the village of Dolanaar on Teldrassil. He guides newly arrived adventurers in understanding the nature of the great World Tree and tasks them with maintaining its sacred moonwells. Through his lessons, he reveals both the spiritual importance of Teldrassil and the growing burdens carried by the kaldorei.",h="Corithras Moonrage is a night elf scholar and quest giver stationed in the village of Dolanaar on Teldrassil.",sec={{t="Scholar of Dolanaar",b="Residing in the shaded settlement of Dolanaar, Corithras Moonrage serves as an instructor to travelers leaving the sheltered bounds of Shadowglen. As young kaldorei venture into the wider boughs of Teldrassil, Corithras ensures they understand the history of their new home. He teaches that survival in this changing era requires vigilance and reverence for the natural order.",sp=0},{t="Crown of the Earth",b="Much of Corithras's duty revolves around collecting moonwell water for the druids in Darnassus. He directs adventurers to collect pure waters from moonwells across Teldrassil in specially crafted phials for delivery to Fandral Staghelm. Through these trials, he monitors the health of the World Tree and seeks to maintain the delicate balance of the wilderness against creeping corruption.",sp=0},{t="The Burden of the Kaldorei",b="Beneath Corithras's guidance lies an uneasy truth regarding Teldrassil's creation. Unlike the ancient Nordrassil, this new World Tree was raised without the blessings of the Dragon Aspects, who refused Fandral Staghelm's ambitious creation. Corithras reflects on the loss of night elven immortality and the fragile, uncertain future the kaldorei now face under the boughs of an unblessed bough.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Corithras Moonrage?",a="Corithras Moonrage is a night elf scholar located in Dolanaar. He introduces adventurers to the history of Teldrassil and tasks them with tending to the sacred moonwells and testing the waters of the World Tree.",al={"corithras moonrage role","who is corithras","dolanaar quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Corithras Moonrage be found?",a="He can be found standing outdoors in Dolanaar, the central crossroads village situated in the southern reaches of Teldrassil.",al={"corithras location","where is corithras","find corithras"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Crown of the Earth questline about?",a="The Crown of the Earth quests involve drawing water from moonwells across Teldrassil. Corithras combines the collected water for delivery to Fandral Staghelm in Darnassus, where the druids need to replenish their moonwell.",al={"crown of the earth meaning","corithras quests","moonwell quests"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is Corithras concerned about Teldrassil's origins?",a="Corithras shares the history of how Teldrassil was planted after the Third War to restore night elven immortality. Because the Dragon Aspects refused to bless the tree, Corithras remains acutely aware that the tree lacks divine protection and that his people remain mortal.",al={"why burden of kaldorei","aspects refusal","why no immortality"},it="motive"},{q="What does Corithras teach new adventurers?",a="He imparts lessons on the recent sacrifices of the Third War, the founding of Teldrassil, and the responsibility each kaldorei bears to defend their new woodland home.",al={"corithras lore","dolanaar history","what does corithras tell you"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Is Corithras aligned with the Cenarion Circle or Darnassus?",a="He serves as a loyal citizen and scholar of Darnassus in Dolanaar, working closely with druids and priests alike to monitor the well-being of the forest and its waters.",al={"corithras faction","is corithras a druid"},it="side"},{q="What does Corithras Moonrage want?",a="Corithras seeks to tend and understand the health of the young World Tree. Through the ritual known as the Crown of the Earth, he tasks travelers with gathering vital waters from sacred moonwells across Teldrassil to bless the great boughs, striving to nurture the land and unravel the burdens weighing upon the kaldorei.",al={"what does corithras want","corithras moonrage goals","corithras objective"},it="wants",add="a5e544f2"},{q="Why is Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar?",a="Stationed in the bustling settlement of Dolanaar, Corithras acts as a guide to newly arrived night elf adventurers venturing out from Shadowglen. Positioned at the heart of Teldrassil, he enlists able hands to carry out essential rituals and investigate the growing ecological and spiritual troubles surrounding the World Tree.",al={"why is corithras here","why is corithras in dolanaar","corithras moonrage dolanaar purpose"},it="why_here",add="35aa58f2"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, speaking with Corithras is a foundational lesson in the post-Third War reality, confronting the loss of ancient immortality and the disputed creation of Teldrassil.",["class:Druid"]="Druids will find Corithras's tasks deeply connected to their calling, as his moonwell rites directly track the health and creeping ailments of the World Tree.",["class:Priest"]="Priests of Elune assist Corithras in carrying the blessed waters of the moonwells, maintaining the spiritual and physical harmony of Dolanaar's surrounding wilds."},kw={"corithras moonrage","crown of the earth","dolanaar","fandral staghelm","kaldorei","moonwell","night elf","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","quest:929","quest:940","topic:night-elf"},src={"Corithras Moonrage"}}
E["npc:dazalar"] = {t="npc",n="Dazalar",z="teldrassil",s="In Dolanaar, Dazalar trains young night elf hunters for the wilds of Teldrassil. He teaches them to aim true and form bonds with the beasts of the great boughs.",h="In Dolanaar, Dazalar trains young night elf hunters for the wilds of Teldrassil.",sec={{t="The Dolanaar Encampment",b="Dazalar trains young hunters in Dolanaar before they venture beyond Shadowglen. Night elf rangers and sentinels patrol the wilderness, and he teaches newcomers the patience and discipline needed to protect Teldrassil's fragile ecosystem.",sp=0},{t="Bonding with the Wild",b="Dazalar teaches hunters to tame and care for beasts. The Kaldorei seek a pact with forest predators such as nightsabers, owls, and strigid hunters, training them to fight beside their companions with respect rather than force.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Dazalar?",a="Dazalar trains night elf hunters in Dolanaar, teaching them combat skills and how to tame wild beasts.",al={"who is dazalar","dazalar lore","dazalar identity"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Dazalar?",a="You can find Dazalar outdoors in Dolanaar, Teldrassil's central hub, shortly after leaving Shadowglen.",al={"dazalar location","where is dazalar","dolanaar hunter trainer"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What training does Dazalar provide?",a="Dazalar teaches ranged attacks, traps, and survival skills. He also guides novice hunters through trials to master taming wilderness animals.",al={"what does dazalar teach","dazalar skills","hunter training dazalar"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Does Dazalar offer any special quests?",a="Yes. Dazalar offers hunter training that includes The Hunter's Path, the multi-part trial Taming the Beast, and Training the Beast. These teach young hunters to bond with and care for animal companions.",al={"dazalar quests","hunter quests dolanaar","taming the beast quest"},gp=true},{q="Why do night elves rely so heavily on hunters?",a="Night elves have lived in harmony with Kalimdor's ancient forests for millennia. Archers and scouts form the backbone of the Sentinel army, using stealth, marksmanship, and animal allies to protect their lands without disrupting nature.",al={"night elf hunters lore","why sentinels use hunters","kaldorei hunters"},it="history"},{q="What kind of beasts does Dazalar send hunters to tame?",a="Dazalar directs hunters to find native Teldrassil beasts, including local spiders, nightsabers, and birds of prey. The trials test their ability to approach and calm wild predators.",al={"what beasts to tame","dolanaar taming trial","tame beasts teldrassil"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Dazalar on?",a="Dazalar is loyal to the night elves of Darnassus and serves as part of the Alliance. Stationed in Dolanaar, he devotes his craft to guiding young kaldorei hunters in communion with the wilds of Teldrassil, ensuring they can defend their people and preserve the balance of their new woodland home.",al={"dazalar faction","is dazalar alliance","who does dazalar serve"},it="side",add="0fd37214"},{q="What does Dazalar want?",a="Dazalar aims to train aspiring hunters in the foundational disciplines of tracking, marksmanship, and wilderness survival. Beyond standard combat prowess, he seeks to ensure every kaldorei hunter masters the art of bonding with, taming, and training the diverse beasts native to the boughs of Teldrassil.",al={"what is dazalar's goal","dazalar purpose","why does dazalar train hunters"},it="wants",add="5be2ad1d"},{q="Why is Dazalar here?",a="Dazalar makes his home in Dolanaar because the settlement is the first major haven young night elves visit after leaving the Shadowglen. Positioned right along the forest trails, he can instruct fledgling scouts, sentinels, and rangers before they venture deeper into the untamed reaches of Teldrassil.",al={"why is dazalar in dolanaar","dazalar teldrassil role","dazalar location reason"},it="why_here",add="6e364749"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, Dazalar guides you through the first trials of beast mastery and caring for an animal companion.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you learn the traditions of the Kaldorei sentinels and scouts, and how to live in balance with nature's fierce predators."},kw={"dazalar","dolanaar","hunter","night elf","taming the beast","teldrassil","the hunter's path","trainer"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","quest:6061","quest:6065","quest:6081","topic:night-elf","quest:940"},src={"Dazalar"}}
E["npc:denalan"] = {t="npc",n="Denalan",z="teldrassil",s="At Lake Al'Ameth, Denalan studies Teldrassil's unusual plants and seeks remedies for its corruption. He tends a small lakeside plot and asks young adventurers to gather samples, examine timberlings, and test enchanted soil.",h="At Lake Al'Ameth, Denalan studies Teldrassil's unusual plants and seeks remedies for its corruption.",sec={{t="A Botanist at Lake Al'Ameth",b="Denalan studies plants on Lake Al'Ameth's eastern shore. He works beneath a cloth awning, with field tools and rows of planter boxes close at hand. While many kaldorei focus on martial vigilance or high druidic rites, he gives his days to herbalism. He chooses this plot over Darnassus's grand barrows, so he can examine the unusual flora that has grown since the new World Tree was planted.",sp=0},{t="Investigating Teldrassil's Blemishes",b="Denalan investigates the growing unrest among Teldrassil's native wildlife. Timberlings, usually docile woodland beings of wood and sprout, have grown increasingly aggressive. He enchants soil to nurture wild seeds in captivity and study how corruption seeps into root systems. Shimmering fronds, glowing fruit, and moss-twined growths are among the specimens he examines as he seeks the taint troubling the forest boughs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Denalan?",a="Find Denalan on Lake Al'Ameth's eastern bank in southern Teldrassil, south of Dolanaar. His small camp, with an awning and cultivated planting beds, lies near the water's edge.",al={"denalan location","where is denalan","denalan map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Denalan researching at his campsite?",a="Denalan studies Teldrassil's unusual flora and the aggressive behavior of local woodland spirits. He uses enchanted planter boxes to grow timberling seeds and examine curious specimens as he seeks ways to cleanse corruption from the new World Tree's ecosystem.",al={"what does denalan do","denalan purpose","why is denalan at the lake"},it="purpose"},{q="Why are the timberlings attacking people?",a="Timberlings are plant-like nature spirits native to Teldrassil's boughs. Usually peaceful, they have grown violent and erratic as unnatural corruption spreads through the World Tree's soil and roots. Researchers like Denalan study their seeds to understand the change.",al={"why are timberlings aggressive","timberling lore","corrupted timberlings"},it="threat"},{q="What are Denalan's planter boxes used for?",a="Denalan uses specially prepared beds filled with enchanted earth to cultivate wild seeds and strange botanical cuttings. They let him observe how forest plants react to purified soil away from wild contaminants.",al={"denalan planter","denalans earth","denalan dirt boxes"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Who does Denalan work with?",a="Denalan works with Rellian Greenspyre, a druid in Darnassus who shares his interest in timberlings. A colleague in Dolanaar also sends him rare earth from Darnassus.",al={"denalan allies","who does denalan report to"},it="ties"},{q="What is the Moss-twined Heart that Denalan examines?",a="The Moss-twined Heart is a blighted botanical core recovered from Blackmoss the Fetid, a corrupted timberling in Teldrassil. Denalan studies it in enchanted soil to understand the unnatural sickness twisting the island's plant life.",al={"moss twined heart","moss-twined heart quest","blackmoss heart"},it="origin"},{q="Who is Denalan?",a="Denalan is a renowned night elf herbalist and researcher residing along the shores of Lake Al'Ameth. Known for his deep understanding of Kalimdor's plant life, he dedicates his craft to studying the flora of Teldrassil and finding natural remedies for the ecological distress troubling the World Tree.",al={"who is denalan","denalan lore","about denalan"},it="identity",add="6481fcca"},{q="Whose side is Denalan on?",a="Denalan is loyal to the night elves of Darnassus and allied with the Alliance. He works openly with his fellow Kaldorei herbalists and druids, aiding any travelers who wish to protect Teldrassil from corruption and harm.",al={"denalan faction","is denalan alliance","who does denalan serve"},it="side",add="6f0f42ae"},{q="What does Denalan want?",a="Denalan seeks to cleanse Teldrassil of the spreading corruption tainting its soils and wildlife. He collects seeds and rare plant specimens from the surrounding forest, using specially enchanted earth to nurture healthy growth and find a remedy for the maddened timberlings.",al={"what does denalan want","denalan goal","denalan objective"},it="wants",add="11aaa3f4"},{q="Why is Denalan here at Lake Al'Ameth?",a="Denalan established his campsite by the lake to study Teldrassil's native vegetation up close. The shores provide an ideal outdoor laboratory for his planter boxes and enchanted soil, placing him near the epicenter of the agitated timberling population he aims to understand.",al={"why is denalan here","why lake alameth denalan","denalan campsite purpose"},it="why_here",add="38f45ee1"},{q="Why is Denalan famous?",a="Denalan is widely respected as a famed herbalist among the night elves. His lifelong study of Kalimdor's botany and expertise in purifying tainted seeds and soil have earned him a reputation as one of the realm's foremost authorities on plant lore.",al={"why is denalan famous","denalan herbalist fame","is denalan well known"},it="fame",add="3bcd2be5"}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="As an herbalist, you follow the kaldorei tradition of botanical study. Gathering and cultivating wild plants can help reveal deeper ailments in the natural world.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you may find common cause with Denalan's lakeside experiments. His work helps the Cenarion Circle trace and purge the taint spreading through Teldrassil's roots.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you share the early kaldorei effort to understand the unexpected flaws and growing pains of your new home, Teldrassil."},kw={"blackmoss","botany","denalan","herbalist","kaldorei","lake al'ameth","oakenscowl","planter","teldrassil","timberlings"},rel={"subzone:lake-al-ameth","zone:teldrassil","quest:997","quest:918","quest:919","quest:927","quest:941","quest:922"},src={"Denalan"}}
E["npc:dirania-silvershine"] = {t="npc",n="Dirania Silvershine",z="teldrassil",s="Dirania Silvershine is a night elf resident of Shadowglen in Teldrassil. Deeply loyal and observant, she watches over the tranquil grove and looks out for her companion Iverron when his reckless ventures land him in peril.",h="Dirania Silvershine is a night elf resident of Shadowglen in Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Watcher in Shadowglen",b="Dirania stands among the tranquil boughs of Shadowglen, the secluded vale where young night elves begin their service to Kalimdor and the Alliance. While many in the barrow mounds and sanctuaries look to broad spiritual duties, Dirania stays mindful of those nearest to her, attentive to the quiet dangers that stir even in the heart of Teldrassil.",sp=0},{t="A Friend's Peril",b="Dirania's immediate concern is her companion Iverron. Overeager and careless around the poisonous woodland creatures creeping across the glen, Iverron frequently gets into trouble. When he succumbs to a venomous bite from the local webwood spiders, Dirania takes it upon herself to seek out willing hands to gather ingredients and prepare a remedy before the venom takes a permanent toll.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Dirania Silvershine?",a="Dirania Silvershine is a night elf found in Shadowglen on Teldrassil. She acts as a quest giver, primarily concerned with rescuing and curing her friend Iverron after he runs afoul of local poisonous wildlife.",al={"dirania","who is dirania","dirania silvershine lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Dirania Silvershine?",a="Dirania is located within Shadowglen, the starter vale inside Teldrassil, not far from the central path near Aldrassil.",al={"dirania location","where is dirania","find dirania silvershine"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Dirania's relationship to Iverron?",a="Dirania and Iverron are close friends. Dirania is the more sensible and watchful of the pair, stepping in to arrange an antidote whenever Iverron acts foolishly and suffers a poisonous bite from the local fauna.",al={"is dirania related to iverron","iverron and dirania","dirania's friend"},it="ties"},{q="What quests does Dirania offer?",a="She offers quests centered on helping her companion, notably 'A Friend in Need' and 'Iverron's Antidote', tasking adventurers with securing ingredients to brew a cure for Iverron's spider venom.",al={"dirania quests","quests from dirania silvershine","iverron quest"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Why is Dirania worried about spiders in Shadowglen?",a="The webwood spiders dwelling in the boughs of Shadowglen carry a potent venom. While experienced sentinels can handle them, novice elves like Iverron frequently underestimate the danger and risk succumbing to their bites.",al={"shadowglen spiders","why spiders in teldrassil","webwood danger"},it="threat"},{q="Does Dirania belong to any formal order or faction?",a="Dirania is an Alliance night elf living peacefully in Teldrassil. She is not depicted as an active member of the Sisterhood of Elune or the Cenarion Circle, but rather a caring civilian looking out for her fellow kin.",al={"dirania faction","is dirania a druid","is dirania a sentinel"},it="side"},{q="What does Dirania Silvershine want?",a="Dirania is desperately seeking help for her close friend Iverron. He ventured out into Shadowglen and was severely poisoned by the native webwood spiders, leaving him incapacitated. She needs someone to quickly gather the necessary ingredients across the glade so that an antidote can be brewed to save his life.",al={"dirania silvershine goal","what does dirania need","dirania silvershine wants"},it="wants",add="f156932e"},{q="Why is Dirania Silvershine here?",a="Dirania resides in Shadowglen, making her home within the sheltered boughs of Aldrassil alongside her fellow night elves. She remains stationed here in distress after her friend Iverron fell victim to spider venom nearby, waiting for capable travelers to come to his aid.",al={"why is dirania in shadowglen","dirania silvershine location reason","why dirania here"},it="why_here",add="e30a1bf8"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For young night elves stepping into Shadowglen, Dirania serves as an early reminder of the bonds of friendship and the creeping dangers threatening even the newest sanctuaries of the World Tree."},kw={"antidote","dirania","iverron","shadowglen","silvershine","teldrassil","webwood"},rel={"npc:iverron","subzone:shadowglen","quest:3519","quest:3521","quest:4495","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf"},src={"Dirania Silvershine"}}
E["npc:fandral-staghelm"] = {t="npc",n="Fandral Staghelm",z="teldrassil",s="Archdruid Fandral Staghelm leads the druids of the Cenarion Circle from the Cenarion Enclave in Darnassus. Stepping into power after Malfurion Stormrage vanished into the Emerald Dream, he championed the planting of the new World Tree, Teldrassil. Proud, abrasive, and relentlessly ambitious, Fandral advocates for an aggressive Kaldorei resurgence that frequently pits him against High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind.",h="Archdruid Fandral Staghelm leads the druids of the Cenarion Circle from the Cenarion Enclave in Darnassus.",sec={{t="Architect of Teldrassil",b="Following the Third War and the sacrifice of Nordrassil atop Mount Hyjal, the night elves lost their immortality and their sacred sanctuary. When Malfurion Stormrage vanished, Fandral took up leadership of the druids and convinced the Circle of Ancients that it was time for their people to rebuild and regain their immortality. With the Circle's approval, he led the druids in raising Teldrassil off the coast of Kalimdor. He envisioned the colossal bough as a monument to Kaldorei endurance and a vessel to restore their lost supremacy, even though the Dragon Aspects pointedly withheld their blessings from the unapproved endeavor.",sp=0},{t="Tragedy in the Shifting Sands",b="A millennium before the First War, Fandral served as the Kaldorei field commander in Silithus during the War of the Shifting Sands. Renowned among the insectoid qiraji as 'Kar'sis'—the Hand of Earth—he held the front lines alongside his beloved only son, Valstann. Exploiting Fandral's devotion, the qiraji General Rajaxx engineered a feint against Southwind Village and captured Valstann, ruthlessly executing him directly in front of the horrified Archdruid. The loss shattered Fandral's spirit, precipitating a devastating retreat and cementing an abiding, bitter hatred for the swarm that remains etched into his haughty demeanor.",sp=0},{t="Rivalry and Hubris",b="Within the marble boughs of Darnassus, Fandral governs Kaldorei affairs with a haughty, unyielding hand. Unlike High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind, who favors spiritual preservation and cautious diplomacy, Fandral views military expansion and decisive strength as paramount to the survival of their people.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Fandral Staghelm?",a="Fandral Staghelm is the acting Archdruid of the Cenarion Circle in Darnassus, presiding over Kaldorei druids in Malfurion Stormrage's absence. Known for his fiery temperament and imperial ambitions, he is the primary visionary behind the creation of Teldrassil.",al={"fandral lore","who is the archdruid","archdruid of darnassus"},it="identity"},{q="Why doesn't Fandral get along with Tyrande?",a="Fandral advocates for Kaldorei military resurgence, aggressive expansion, and reclaiming lost immortality. Tyrande Whisperwind pursues cautious spiritual guidance through Elune. Their competing visions for the night elves' post-Hyjal future spark fierce political friction within Darnassus.",al={"fandral and tyrande","why do druids and priestesses disagree","staghelm vs whisperwind"},it="conflict"},{q="Why was Teldrassil planted?",a="After the Battle of Mount Hyjal, Nordrassil was scarred and the night elves had lost their immortality. With Malfurion missing, Fandral convinced the Circle of Ancients that it was time for their people to rebuild and regain their immortality, and with the Circle's approval he and the most powerful druids grew Teldrassil.",al={"who created teldrassil","why did fandral plant teldrassil","origin of teldrassil"},it="origin"},{q="What happened to Fandral's son?",a="During the War of the Shifting Sands in Silithus, Fandral's son Valstann was lured into an ambush at Southwind Village. The qiraji General Rajaxx captured Valstann and slaughtered him in front of Fandral, leaving the Archdruid grief-stricken and permanently embittered.",al={"fandral son","who was valstann","valstann staghelm"},it="history"},{q="Where can Fandral Staghelm be found?",a="Fandral stands atop the Cenarion Enclave in Darnassus, surrounded by his loyal druids and overseeable business of the Kaldorei capital.",al={"where is fandral","fandral location","cenarion enclave leader"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Fandral Staghelm on?",a="Fandral stands as the Archdruid of Darnassus and a leader within the Cenarion Circle, championing the Kaldorei and the Alliance. However, his loyalties are fiercely nationalistic. Rather than submitting meekly to the traditional caution of the Cenarion elders or the priesthood of Elune, Fandral acts strictly in what he perceives to be the bold, militaristic interest of the night elven people.",al={"fandral staghelm faction","who does fandral serve","fandral allegiance"},it="side",add="d5bab569"},{q="What does Fandral Staghelm want?",a="Fandral desires the restoration of night elven power, immortality, and territorial dominance. Frustrated by centuries of passive isolation, he pushed to plant the World Tree Teldrassil to replace Nordrassil. He envisions an aggressive Kaldorei nation ready to conquer its borders, expand boldly across Kalimdor, and reclaim the lost glory and vigor of its ancient past.",al={"what is fandral staghelm's goal","fandral ambitions","what does archdruid staghelm want"},it="wants",add="adee2909"},{q="Why is Fandral Staghelm in Darnassus?",a="With Malfurion Stormrage trapped and incapacitated in the Emerald Dream, Fandral stepped into the void as Archdruid. He governs the druids of the Cenarion Circle from the heights of the Cenarion Enclave in Darnassus, ruling alongside High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind and actively steering the political and magical future of Teldrassil.",al={"why is fandral in darnassus","fandral staghelm location why","why is fandral here"},it="why_here",add="6d220bca"},{q="Why is Fandral Staghelm famous?",a="Long before he led the planting of Teldrassil, Fandral served as a brilliant Kaldorei field commander during the War of the Shifting Sands in Silithus. His devastating tactical command against the insectoid swarm earned him the title Kar'sis—the Hand of Earth—among the qiraji, who feared his battlefield fury until they orchestrated the tragic execution of his son.",al={"fandral famous","why is fandral feared","hand of earth fandral"},it="fame",add="53c16312"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Staghelm commands the Darnassian druids, pushing the Cenarion Circle toward direct worldly authority while clashing with the traditional teachings of the sleeping Malfurion Stormrage.",["race:NightElf"]="As one of Darnassus's primary leaders, Fandral embodies Kaldorei pride and fury, driving the settlement of Teldrassil even as ordinary citizens feel the rift between his enclave and the Temple of the Moon.",["faction:Alliance"]="Though Teldrassil serves as an Alliance bastion in northern Kalimdor, Staghelm views the younger races with thinly veiled disdain, tolerating their presence only as political expediency demands."},kw={"cenarion circle","darnassus","fandral","malfurion","rajaxx","shifting sands","staghelm","teldrassil","valstann"},rel={"zone:teldrassil","zone:darnassus","topic:cenarion-circle","npc:malfurion-stormrage","npc:tyrande-whisperwind","subzone:southwind-village","zone:silithus","topic:nordrassil"},src={"Fandral Staghelm"}}
E["npc:frahun-shadewhisper"] = {t="npc",n="Frahun Shadewhisper",z="teldrassil",s="At Aldrassil in Shadowglen, Frahun Shadewhisper trains night elf rogues. He teaches new scouts and rogues stealth, agility, and covert strikes. Erion Shadewhisper, another rogue trainer in Darnassus, shares his family name.",h="At Aldrassil in Shadowglen, Frahun Shadewhisper trains night elf rogues.",sec={{t="A Mentor in the Shadows",b="At Aldrassil in Teldrassil, Frahun Shadewhisper teaches new rogues concealment and bladecraft. Night elf society honors priests, sentinels, and druids, yet scouts and infiltrators also help safeguard the World Tree's boughs. Recruits bring Frahun an encrypted sigil. He weighs their potential and guides their first steps in the craft.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Frahun Shadewhisper?",a="Frahun Shadewhisper trains night elf rogues at Aldrassil in Teldrassil. He teaches new rogues stealth, precise combat, and covert tactics.",al={"frahun lore","who is frahun","frahun shadewhisper role"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Frahun Shadewhisper be found?",a="Frahun Shadewhisper can be found in Aldrassil, Shadowglen's central stronghold on Teldrassil.",al={"frahun location","where is frahun","find frahun shadewhisper"},gp=true},{q="Is Frahun related to Erion Shadewhisper?",a="Frahun Shadewhisper is believed to be kin to Erion Shadewhisper, who trains rogues in Darnassus. Their shared surname and work training rogues support that belief.",al={"erion shadewhisper brother","frahun erion related","shadewhisper family"},it="ties"},{q="What role does the Encrypted Sigil play with him?",a="New night elf rogues carry an encrypted sigil to Frahun Shadewhisper. It marks them as ready for formal instruction in the rogue's craft.",al={"encrypted sigil turn in","frahun sigil","rogue starting quest"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Frahun Shadewhisper on?",a="Frahun stands firmly with Darnassus and the Alliance. Stationed among the ancient boughs of Aldrassil in the Shadowglen, he serves his fellow kaldorei by ensuring that those with an aptitude for stealth and subterfuge can hone their crafts to protect night elf lands.",al={"frahun faction","frahun allegiance","is frahun alliance"},it="side",add="a27f02ba"},{q="What does Frahun Shadewhisper want?",a="Frahun seeks to instruct aspiring night elf rogues in the arts of shadows, lockpicking, and stealthy combat. He ensures new scouts and operatives understand their discipline thoroughly before venturing beyond the protected borders of the Shadowglen into greater Teldrassil.",al={"frahun motive","frahun goal","what does frahun do"},it="wants",add="025c0171"},{q="Why is Frahun Shadewhisper here in Aldrassil?",a="Frahun is stationed at Aldrassil to guide newly awakened or novice night elves who walk the path of the rogue. In the safe haven of Shadowglen, he provides foundational training to ensure fledgling practitioners do not succumb to the dangers lurking in the woods.",al={"why is frahun in aldrassil","frahun shadowglen why","frahun location purpose"},it="why_here",add="72dec556"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, Frahun Shadewhisper gives you your first lessons in stealth, ambush tactics, and weapon finesse.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see how your people's nocturnal affinity and elusiveness become practical combat skills for protecting Teldrassil."},kw={"aldrassil","encrypted sigil","erion","frahun","rogue trainer","shadewhisper","shadowglen","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:aldrassil","zone:teldrassil","quest:3118","quest:2259","topic:night-elf"},src={"Frahun Shadewhisper"}}
E["npc:gaerolas-talvethren"] = {t="npc",n="Gaerolas Talvethren",z="teldrassil",s="At Starbreeze Village, Gaerolas Talvethren guards the Sleeping druids in troubled Teldrassil. He seeks aid against aggressive furbolgs and corruption spreading through the boughs.",h="At Starbreeze Village, Gaerolas Talvethren guards the Sleeping druids in troubled Teldrassil.",sec={{t="Guardian of the Sleeping",b="Gaerolas Talvethren guards the Sleeping druids at Starbreeze Village. They slumber in communion with the Emerald Dream, and his watch has grown uneasy as unnatural corruption spreads through the forest and unsettles Teldrassil.",sp=0},{t="The Gnarlpine Menace",b="Gaerolas calls on travelers to push back the Gnarlpine furbolgs, whose minds have turned to madness and savagery. He hopes to uncover the taint spreading from their shamans and the roots of their distress, preserving what sanctity remains in eastern Teldrassil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gaerolas Talvethren?",a="Gaerolas Talvethren is a night elf defender at Starbreeze Village, charged with guarding the Sleeping druids and investigating the strange corruption afflicting the area.",al={"gaerolas","who is gaerolas","gaerolas role"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Gaerolas Talvethren?",a="You can find Gaerolas Talvethren in Starbreeze Village, in eastern Teldrassil, east of Dolanaar.",al={"gaerolas location","where is gaerolas talvethren","find gaerolas"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who are 'the Sleeping' that Gaerolas protects?",a="The Sleeping are night elf druids who entered long slumbers in barrows and sanctuaries to traverse the Emerald Dream, leaving their physical forms vulnerable to harm.",al={"the sleeping","who are the sleeping","sleeping druids"},it="people"},{q="What threats is Gaerolas concerned about?",a="Gaerolas is troubled by corruption afflicting local wildlife and the Gnarlpine furbolgs' sudden, maddened hostility.",al={"starbreeze threats","gaerolas quests","gnarlpine trouble"},it="threat"},{q="Whose side is Gaerolas Talvethren on?",a="Gaerolas stands firmly with the night elves of Darnassus and the Alliance. As the sworn guardian of the slumbering druids resting in Starbreeze Village, his loyalties lie with the Cenarion Circle, his kin, and the defense of Teldrassil.",al={"gaerolas faction","who does gaerolas serve","gaerolas allegiance"},it="side",add="52ffd6bd"},{q="What does Gaerolas Talvethren want?",a="Gaerolas wants to safeguard the slumbering druids from the corrupting forces encroaching on Starbreeze Village. He seeks your aid in investigating the troubling blight spreading through the area and rooting out the aggression of the corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs.",al={"gaerolas goal","what is gaerolas trying to do","gaerolas purpose"},it="wants",add="436c9e7a"},{q="Why is Gaerolas Talvethren here?",a="Gaerolas remains stationed in Starbreeze Village because he is the designated protector of the Sleeping. While the druids commune in the Emerald Dream, they are completely vulnerable to physical danger, leaving Gaerolas to stand watch against any outside menace.",al={"why is gaerolas in starbreeze village","gaerolas reason for being here","why is gaerolas talvethren here"},it="why_here",add="9c3b08f8"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a young night elf leaving Dolanaar, helping Gaerolas shows how deeply the taint has spread through Teldrassil's sacred boughs.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, Gaerolas's duty to guard the slumbering druids makes helping him a personal matter: you protect fellow practitioners of the Cenarion Circle."},kw={"a troubling breeze","gaerolas talvethren","gnarlpine corruption","starbreeze village","teldrassil","the sleeping"},rel={"subzone:starbreeze-village","quest:475","quest:476","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf"},src={"Gaerolas Talvethren"}}
E["npc:gilshalan-windwalker"] = {t="npc",n="Gilshalan Windwalker",z="teldrassil",s="At Aldrassil's roots in Shadowglen, Gilshalan Windwalker studies the corruption spreading through Teldrassil. His work begins with the Webwood spiders and their growing aggression.",h="At Aldrassil's roots in Shadowglen, Gilshalan Windwalker studies the corruption spreading through Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Scholar at the Roots",b="Gilshalan Windwalker watches Shadowglen from the stone steps at Aldrassil's entrance. Teldrassil was planted to restore the night elves' lost sanctuary and their harmony with nature, yet signs of spiritual malaise appeared almost at once. Gilshalan studies how the corruption affects the local beasts, beginning with the venomous spiders weaving webs nearby.",sp=0},{t="The Webwood Menace",b="Gilshalan studies the Webwood spiders in Shadowthread Cave, north of Shadowglen. Once part of the forest's balance, the spiders have grown hostile and tainted. He sends young novices to gather venom sacs and intact eggs. By studying them, he hopes to learn how the venom has changed and whether the corruption passes through generations or spreads from Teldrassil's soil.",sp=0},{t="Word to the Archdruid",b="Gilshalan believes the spiders' venom may bear signs of the new World Tree's recent growth. He arranges to send the venom and an egg to Darnassus, where he will continue his studies. He also tells promising protectors that Tenaron Stormgrip seeks them in Aldrassil's highest room, where the druidic leadership watches over the young World Tree.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Gilshalan Windwalker?",a="Gilshalan Windwalker studies the wildlife at Aldrassil in Shadowglen. The night elf scholar investigates the corruption affecting Teldrassil's creatures.",al={"gilshalan","who is gilshalan","windwalker night elf"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Gilshalan want Webwood venom?",a="Gilshalan wants Webwood venom to study how it has changed and why the spiders have grown so aggressive and tainted.",al={"why webwood venom","webwood venom quest","spider venom gilshalan"},it="wants"},{q="What does he do with the Webwood egg?",a="Gilshalan sends the Webwood egg to Darnassus with the venom so he can study the specimens there. An unhatched egg is easier to transport than a grown giant spider, which is too dangerous to capture.",al={"webwood egg quest","why spider eggs","egg of webwood"},it="motive"},{q="Where does Gilshalan send adventurers next?",a="Gilshalan tells adventurers that Tenaron Stormgrip seeks them in Aldrassil's highest room, and sends them there.",al={"tenaron summons","who do i see after gilshalan","after webwood egg"},it="next_step"},{q="Where is Gilshalan Windwalker located?",a="Gilshalan sits on the stone pathway at Aldrassil's northern base, outside the hollow entrance to the central tree in Shadowglen.",al={"gilshalan location","where is windwalker","find gilshalan"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is the wildlife in Teldrassil aggressive?",a="The cause of Teldrassil's aggressive wildlife is unknown. A blight seeping through the tree's roots and soil corrupts the creatures' minds and nature, drawing concern from residents like Gilshalan.",al={"why are spiders mad","teldrassil corruption","corrupted beasts shadowglen"},it="threat"},{q="Whose side is Gilshalan Windwalker on?",a="Gilshalan stands firmly with his fellow night elves and the Alliance. Stationed at the roots of Aldrassil within the Shadowglen, he assists young adventurers in understanding and combating the strange, corrupting forces afflicting the local wildlife of Teldrassil.",al={"gilshalan faction","who does gilshalan serve","gilshalan windwalker alliance"},it="side",add="4b23360a"},{q="Why is Gilshalan Windwalker here?",a="He sits at the base of Aldrassil to monitor the emerging taint in Shadowglen. By studying venom samples and unhatched eggs from the agitated Webwood spiders, Gilshalan seeks to uncover what is poisoning the natural harmony of the great world tree.",al={"why is gilshalan in shadowglen","gilshalan windwalker aldrassil purpose"},it="why_here",add="61ec761c"},{q="Who is Gilshalan Windwalker tied to?",a="Gilshalan answers to Tenaron Stormgrip, one of the elder druids stationed high above in the boughs of Aldrassil. Once his initial investigations into the Webwood spiders are concluded, he directs promising recruits up to Tenaron to continue aiding Teldrassil's defense.",al={"who does gilshalan report to","gilshalan tenaron","gilshalan connections"},it="ties",add="ba2e5485"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see Gilshalan's early effort to understand why the young World Tree already bears violent, afflicted wildlife.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you see how Gilshalan's research aids the Cenarion Circle's effort to diagnose the ecological imbalance in Shadowglen's boughs."},kw={"aldrassil","gilshalan","shadowglen","spider","tenaron","venom","webwood","windwalker"},rel={"subzone:aldrassil","quest:916","quest:917","quest:920","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf","quest:940"},src={"Gilshalan Windwalker"}}
E["npc:ilthalaine"] = {t="npc",n="Ilthalaine",z="teldrassil",s="In Shadowglen, Ilthalaine keeps watch over the sacred glade and guides young night elves as they begin their lives in Teldrassil. He teaches them to defend their home and tend its balance.",h="In Shadowglen, Ilthalaine keeps watch over the sacred glade and guides young night elves as they begin their...",sec={{t="Guardian of the Glen",b="Ilthalaine watches the woodland paths just outside Shadowglen's heart. He sees changes in the forest that ordinary eyes miss. When young night elves awaken to their duties, he welcomes them and grounds them in Kaldorei traditions. His guidance prepares them to care for Teldrassil and shoulder the responsibilities of its defenders.",sp=0},{t="The Balance of Nature",b="Heavy spring rains have brought more nightsabers and thistle boars to Shadowglen than the glade can feed. Ilthalaine asks young defenders to thin their numbers, leaving room for the woodland's other creatures to flourish and restoring nature's balance.",sp=0},{t="A Guide to Discipline",b="Ilthalaine tests young elves against local wildlife and points them toward their chosen callings. He gives each traveler a class sigil and directs them to their mentors in the Aldrassil sanctuary. Warriors, druids, rogues, priests, and hunters all find where their service to the Kaldorei begins.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ilthalaine?",a="Ilthalaine watches over Shadowglen, the sheltered glade in Teldrassil. He introduces newly arrived night elves to their duties and the state of the forest.",al={"ilthalaine lore","who is this night elf","shadowglen quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="What is Ilthalaine's role in Shadowglen?",a="Ilthalaine watches Shadowglen's wildlife and teaches young night elves to preserve nature's balance. He sends them to hunt and points them to their class mentors inside Aldrassil.",al={"what does ilthalaine do","why is he here","ilthalaine purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Ilthalaine want the young nightsabers and boars culled?",a="Heavy spring rains have increased the nightsaber and thistle boar populations beyond what Shadowglen can support. Ilthalaine asks for their numbers to be thinned so nature's balance can be preserved.",al={"balance of nature quest","why kill nightsabers","why kill boars"},it="wants"},{q="What are the sigils he gives out?",a="Ilthalaine gives novices class sigils and directs them to their mentors within Aldrassil, including priestesses, druids, warriors, and rogues.",al={"etched sigil","simple sigil","verdant sigil","encrypted sigil","hallowed sigil"},it="item"},{q="Where can Ilthalaine be found?",a="Ilthalaine stands on Shadowglen's central path, just south of Aldrassil's great hollow bough in Teldrassil.",al={"ilthalaine location","where is ilthalaine","ilthalaine coords"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Is Ilthalaine affiliated with the druids or the sentinels?",a="Ilthalaine guides novices of every discipline in Shadowglen. He is attuned to nature's harmony and represents the Kaldorei there.",al={"is he a druid","what faction is ilthalaine"},it="side"},{q="Why is Ilthalaine in Shadowglen?",a="Ilthalaine stands watch in Shadowglen to welcome nascent night elf defenders and preserve the delicate equilibrium of Teldrassil's sacred nursery. As local wildlife grows restless and signs of corruption seep into the boughs, he remains stationed near Aldrassil to guide new arrivals and direct early efforts toward healing and protecting the Great Tree.",al={"why is ilthalaine here","ilthalaine shadowglen purpose","why is ilthalaine in teldrassil"},it="why_here",add="e95b9493"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a young night elf, you meet Ilthalaine first. He teaches you to care for your home on Teldrassil and preserve its sacred balance.",["class:Druid"]="As a budding druid, you find your first practical lessons in Cenarion principles in Ilthalaine's teachings on culling and nature's balance.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion, you meet Ilthalaine's calm Kaldorei vigilance as he welcomes new champions into the service of Darnassus and the Alliance."},kw={"aldrassil","balance of nature","ilthalaine","kaldorei","quest giver","shadowglen","sigil","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil","quest:456","topic:night-elf","quest:3116","quest:3117","quest:3118","quest:3120"},src={"Ilthalaine"}}
E["npc:innkeeper-keldamyr"] = {t="npc",n="Innkeeper Keldamyr",z="teldrassil",s="In Dolanaar, Innkeeper Keldamyr offers food, drink, and a place to rest. Young night elves leaving Shadowglen can find shelter at his inn beneath the boughs of the World Tree.",h="In Dolanaar, Innkeeper Keldamyr offers food, drink, and a place to rest.",sec={{t="Hearth of Dolanaar",b="Dolanaar is the first village many newcomers reach after leaving the sheltered glade of Aldrassil. At the village's central inn, Innkeeper Keldamyr offers bread, spring water, and soft beds beneath Teldrassil's canopy. Travelers, sentinels, and young novices bound for Darnassus pause at his counter to rest, bind their Hearthstones, and gather rations for the journey through the boughs.",sp=0},{t="Town Deliveries",b="An inn high among the branches depends on steady supplies from nearby settlements and tradesfolk. Couriers bringing goods are often sent to Keldamyr's desk, tying his inn to the daily trade that keeps Dolanaar running.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Innkeeper Keldamyr?",a="You can find Keldamyr inside the main inn at the heart of Dolanaar, the first major settlement south of Shadowglen on Teldrassil's boughs.",al={"keldamyr location","where is keldamyr","dolanaar innkeeper location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What services does Innkeeper Keldamyr offer?",a="Keldamyr offers food, drink, and a place to rest. You can bind your Hearthstone at his hearth, buy water, milk, juice, and bread, or log out rested beneath his roof.",al={"keldamyr wares","what does keldamyr sell","dolanaar inn food"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What quests involve Innkeeper Keldamyr?",a="Keldamyr receives parcels for the inn through the local courier task called 'Dolanaar Delivery.'",al={"keldamyr quests","dolanaar delivery turn in"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Who is Innkeeper Keldamyr?",a="Innkeeper Keldamyr is a night elf host who manages the inn in Dolanaar. As travelers journey between the shaded glades of Shadowglen and the wider reaches of Teldrassil, Keldamyr provides a quiet hearth, refreshing drink, and provisions for weary adventurers venturing through the great boughs.",al={"who is keldamyr","innkeeper keldamyr lore"},it="identity",add="cc228f0e"},{q="Whose side is Innkeeper Keldamyr on?",a="Innkeeper Keldamyr is loyal to Darnassus and the Alliance. He serves the night elven community of Dolanaar, opening his doors to fellow elves and visiting Alliance allies seeking rest beneath Teldrassil's canopy.",al={"keldamyr faction","is keldamyr alliance"},it="side",add="1430db47"},{q="What does Innkeeper Keldamyr want?",a="Keldamyr aims to keep Dolanaar's inn well-stocked and welcoming. He attends to incoming supplies, coordinates local deliveries, and ensures every passing traveler has food, water, and a safe place to bind their hearthstone before setting out into the wilds.",al={"keldamyr goals","what does keldamyr want"},it="wants",add="ff7bce47"},{q="Why is Innkeeper Keldamyr here in Dolanaar?",a="Dolanaar is the primary crossroads and settlement for young night elves leaving their training in Shadowglen. Keldamyr maintains the village inn right along the road to offer shelter and sustenance at this crucial juncture on Teldrassil.",al={"why is keldamyr here","keldamyr dolanaar"},it="why_here",add="dbe1a8c8"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf leaving Shadowglen's training grounds, you can make Keldamyr's inn your first home away from home and bind your Hearthstone there."},kw={"dolanaar","hearthstone","inn","innkeeper","keldamyr","night elf","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","quest:2159","topic:night-elf"},src={"Innkeeper Keldamyr"}}
E["npc:iverron"] = {t="npc",n="Iverron",z="teldrassil",s="In Shadowglen, Iverron lies stricken by spider venom. His plight warns of growing corruption within Teldrassil.",h="In Shadowglen, Iverron lies stricken by spider venom.",sec={{t="A Bitter Bite",b="Iverron wandered beneath Shadowglen’s quiet canopies when webwood spiders bit him. Their venom left the young night elf unable to return to safety on his own. The spiders once shared the glade in peace, but now they grow increasingly aggressive.",sp=0},{t="Desperate Remedies",b="Iverron’s companions and local healers seek a cure using hyacinth mushrooms, moonpetal lilies, and webwood ichor. Together, these woodland ingredients make an antidote. His survival depends on their swift work.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Iverron?",a="Iverron is a young night elf in Shadowglen, within Teldrassil. Poisonous creatures bit him as he wandered the woodland, and he needs urgent aid to survive.",al={"iverron lore","who is iverron","iverron night elf"},it="identity"},{q="What poisoned Iverron?",a="Aggressive webwood spiders in Shadowglen bit Iverron and poisoned him with debilitating venom.",al={"why is iverron sick","what bit iverron","iverron poison"},it="threat"},{q="How is Iverron cured?",a="Iverron is cured with an antidote made from hyacinth mushrooms, moonpetal lilies, and webwood ichor from the spiders.",al={"cure iverron","iverron antidote","saving iverron"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Where can Iverron be found?",a="You can find Iverron in Shadowglen, a secluded glade in Teldrassil where young night elves begin their training.",al={"iverron location","where is iverron","find iverron"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is helping Iverron?",a="Iverron’s friend Dirania Silvershine asks for help gathering antidote ingredients, then asks that the antidote be brought back to him before it loses its potency.",al={"who saves iverron","iverron friends","dentaria silverglade iverron"},it="allies"},{q="Why are the spiders in Shadowglen so hostile?",a="Shadowglen’s spiders have grown hostile as part of an unnatural malady spreading through Teldrassil. It warps normally reclusive beasts into violent predators.",al={"why spiders attack","teldrassil spider corruption"},it="conflict"},{q="Whose side is Iverron on?",a="Iverron is an ordinary night elf loyal to his people and the Alliance. He lives peacefully within the sheltered boughs of Shadowglen on Teldrassil, relying on the aid of fellow kaldorei like his close friend Dirania Silvershine to look after him when misadventure strikes.",al={"iverron faction","is iverron alliance","who does iverron serve"},it="side",add="7be6aac6"},{q="What does Iverron want?",a="Right now, Iverron simply wants to survive. Struck down by deadly spider venom while venturing through Shadowglen, he is incapacitated and desperately needs a potent counter-venom before the poison claims his life.",al={"iverron goal","what does iverron need","iverron motive"},it="wants",add="9c5ce7fc"},{q="Why is Iverron in Shadowglen?",a="Iverron resides in Shadowglen, the sheltered starting vale of Teldrassil. He ventured into the surrounding woods, only to run afoul of the grove's aggressive webwood spiders. Overcome by their venom, he collapsed and now lies stricken on the forest floor.",al={"why is iverron here","iverron shadowglen reason","what happened to iverron"},it="why_here",add="b06694b4"},{q="Who is Iverron tied to?",a="Iverron is close friends with Dirania Silvershine, who lives in Shadowglen. When he failed to visit her as usual, she sent a passing adventurer to look for him, and after learning he had been poisoned she gathered the ingredients for an antidote to save his life.",al={"iverron connections","who are iverrons friends","iverron dirania"},it="ties",add="61549ef7"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf taking your first steps outside Aldrassil, you can see in Iverron’s misfortune how quickly Teldrassil’s wilds are falling out of balance.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid studying in Shadowglen, you can see Iverron’s poisoning as a symptom of a deeper affliction gripping nature. The remedy draws on the glade’s flora and fauna.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As an herbalist, you can help preserve life by gathering Shadowglen’s plants quickly; Iverron’s survival depends on it."},kw={"antidote","dentaria","iverron","kaldorei","shadowglen","spider","teldrassil","venom"},rel={"quest:3521","quest:3519","quest:4495","subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf","npc:tarindrella"},src={"Iverron"}}
E["npc:jannok-breezesong"] = {t="npc",n="Jannok Breezesong",z="teldrassil",s="In Dolanaar, Jannok Breezesong trains young night elf rogues. He teaches stealth, cunning, and bladecraft to kaldorei setting out beneath the World Tree's boughs.",h="In Dolanaar, Jannok Breezesong trains young night elf rogues.",sec={{t="A Guide in the Shadows",b="Beneath Dolanaar's boughs, Jannok Breezesong teaches novice night elf rogues. He trains those who work quietly beyond the ranks of Teldrassil's sentinels and druids. His lessons teach them to stalk through shadows, strike from behind, and survive unseen among the boughs. When rogues finish their first lessons in Dolanaar, Jannok sends them to more experienced trainers in Darnassus.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Jannok Breezesong?",a="Jannok Breezesong trains young night elf rogues in Dolanaar on Teldrassil. He teaches them foundational rogue skills and techniques.",al={"who is jannok","jannok breezesong role","dolanaar rogue trainer"},it="identity"},{q="Where does Jannok send advancing rogues?",a="After their early training in Dolanaar, rogues can travel to Darnassus for further instruction from Erion Shadewhisper, a senior rogue trainer in the city's Cenarion Enclave.",al={"jannok quest","erion shadewhisper quest","dolanaar rogue next step"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Where can I find Jannok in Dolanaar?",a="Jannok is among Dolanaar's trainer pavilions, in the central settlement of Teldrassil outside Shadowglen.",al={"jannok location","where is jannok","find jannok breezesong"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Jannok Breezesong on?",a="Jannok serves Darnassus and the Alliance. As a night elf rogue trainer stationed within the village of Dolanaar, his loyalty lies with the kaldorei nation and the defense of Teldrassil.",al={"jannok breezesong faction","who does jannok serve","jannok allegiance"},it="side",add="f606b9db"},{q="Why is Jannok Breezesong here?",a="Jannok is stationed in Dolanaar to instruct novice night elf rogues emerging from Shadowglen. He provides training in stealth and cunning, eventually directing promising scouts onward to mentors like Erion Shadewhisper in Darnassus.",al={"why is jannok in dolanaar","jannok breezesong purpose","why is jannok here"},it="why_here",add="b07dd258"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a young night elf rogue starting out on Teldrassil, you can learn from Jannok in Dolanaar before heading to the capital.",["race:NightElf"]="As a kaldorei, you may follow the path of stealth, poisons, and daggers, alongside the traditions of sentinels and druids."},kw={"breezesong","dolanaar","erion shadewhisper","jannok","night elf","rogue trainer","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","quest:2259","quest:940","topic:night-elf"},src={"Jannok Breezesong"}}
E["npc:jocaste"] = {t="npc",n="Jocaste",z="teldrassil",s="In Darnassus, Jocaste trains night elf hunters arriving from the wilds of Teldrassil.",h="In Darnassus, Jocaste trains night elf hunters arriving from the wilds of Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Mentor in the Enclave",b="Jocaste trains night elf hunters in Darnassus's Cenarion Enclave. Young trackers come to her after their first training in Shadowglen, ready to take up the hunt in the capital. She teaches marksmanship and survival in the wild, along with the bond between a hunter and the beasts of Kalimdor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Jocaste?",a="Jocaste trains night elf hunters in the Cenarion Enclave of Darnassus.",al={"jocaste lore","who is jocaste","jocaste darnassus"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Jocaste?",a="Find Jocaste in the Cenarion Enclave, in northwest Darnassus on the boughs of Teldrassil.",al={"jocaste location","where is jocaste","jocaste spot"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role does she play for young hunters?",a="Young hunters come to Jocaste in Darnassus to advance their discipline through The Hunter's Path and learn to train and master wild beasts.",al={"jocaste quests","the hunter's path jocaste","training the beast"},it="purpose"},{q="Is Jocaste affiliated with the Cenarion Circle?",a="Yes. Jocaste trains hunters in the Cenarion Enclave and welcomes visiting hunters into the presence of the Cenarion Circle.",al={"is jocaste cenarion circle","jocaste faction"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Jocaste on?",a="Jocaste stands firmly with Darnassus, the Night Elves, and the wider Alliance. Stationed among the Cenarion Circle in their enclave, she shares their dedication to safeguarding nature and guiding those who live in harmony with the wild.",al={"jocaste faction","who does jocaste serve","jocaste allegiance"},it="side",add="42c501de"},{q="What does Jocaste want?",a="Jocaste is dedicated to passing on the traditions of the hunt. She seeks to nurture aspiring hunters in Darnassus, ensuring they learn the discipline, marksmanship, and spiritual bond required to tame and command beasts in service to nature and their people.",al={"jocaste motive","what is jocastes goal","jocaste purpose"},it="wants",add="05567dfb"},{q="Why is Jocaste here in Darnassus?",a="Jocaste resides in the Cenarion Enclave to offer her wisdom and training to hunters visiting the capital. Amid the ancient trees of Teldrassil, she provides vital instruction to both novice scouts and seasoned wilderness stalkers.",al={"why is jocaste in darnassus","why is jocaste in cenarion enclave"},it="why_here",add="1febd3fe"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a night elf hunter arriving in Darnassus, Jocaste can refine your combat skills and help strengthen your bond with your animal companion.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you can see in Jocaste the harmony between your people, Teldrassil's wild beasts, and the teachings of the Cenarion Circle."},kw={"cenarion enclave","darnassus","hunter trainer","jocaste","night elf hunter","teldrassil"},rel={"zone:darnassus","subzone:cenarion-enclave","topic:cenarion-circle","topic:night-elf","zone:teldrassil","quest:6065","quest:6081"},src={"Jocaste"}}
E["npc:laurna-morninglight"] = {t="npc",n="Laurna Morninglight",z="teldrassil",s="In Dolanaar, Laurna Morninglight teaches young night elf priests the rites of Elune. Devoted to the Sisterhood of Elune, she guides acolytes from Shadowglen in healing and spiritual practice as threats gather in Teldrassil.",h="In Dolanaar, Laurna Morninglight teaches young night elf priests the rites of Elune.",sec={{t="A Guide in Dolanaar",b="In Dolanaar, Laurna Morninglight guides young priests from Shadowglen. As new initiates travel farther into Teldrassil, she teaches them to deepen their bond with Elune. Her lessons join healing with defensive rites, skills needed in an increasingly hostile wild.",sp=0},{t="Devotion to the Moon Goddess",b="Among the kaldorei, priestcraft follows Elune, not the Holy Light revered by humans and dwarves. Laurna sends her students to receive sacred robes and heal a wounded Sentinel. Through these rites, acolytes learn that the Mother Moon grants their power to preserve and mend the kaldorei people.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Laurna Morninglight?",a="Find Laurna Morninglight in Dolanaar, in central Teldrassil, just down the road from Shadowglen.",al={"laurna location","where is laurna","dolanaar priest trainer"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Laurna Morninglight do?",a="Laurna Morninglight trains night elf priests. She teaches new spells, improves familiar abilities, and guides them through early class rites.",al={"what does she do","laurna role","laurna priest trainer"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What kind of quests does she offer?",a="Laurna Morninglight sends fledgling priests to aid wounded allies and seek Elune's favor through ceremonial vestments and prayers.",al={"laurna quests","priest quests dolanaar"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Does she train other races?",a="Laurna Morninglight is rooted in the Sisterhood of Elune, and Alliance priest trainers instruct any allied priest who seeks spiritual discipline.",al={"can humans train here","priest trainer any race"},gp=true},{q="Is she affiliated with the Temple of the Moon?",a="Yes. Laurna Morninglight's vows and magic are dedicated to Elune and the traditions overseen by the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus.",al={"is she sisterhood of elune","laurna temple of the moon"},it="ties"},{q="Does she share a family name with other night elves?",a="No relatives of Laurna Morninglight are known among the kaldorei of Teldrassil.",al={"morninglight family","laurna relatives"},it="ties"},{q="Who is Laurna Morninglight?",a="Laurna Morninglight is a night elf priestess and mentor residing in the village of Dolanaar. Devoted to the worship of Elune, she guides young acolytes and initiates stepping out into Teldrassil, teaching them to channel the goddess's soothing radiance and call upon divine protection.",al={"who is laurna morninglight","who is laurna","laurna morninglight lore"},it="identity",add="3c87933c"},{q="Whose side is Laurna Morninglight on?",a="She is steadfastly loyal to the night elves of Darnassus, the Sisterhood of Elune, and the Alliance. As an acolyte of the moon goddess, her heart lies with protecting her people and guiding the spiritual well-being of the Kaldorei upon Teldrassil.",al={"laurna morninglight faction","who does laurna morninglight serve","laurna morninglight alliance"},it="side",add="5c82db11"},{q="What does Laurna Morninglight want?",a="Her primary devotion is to nurture novice priests in the ways of Elune. She wants promising acolytes to cultivate their divine connection, master healing prayers, and wield sacred garments to aid their kin across the boughs of Teldrassil.",al={"laurna morninglight motive","what does laurna morninglight do"},it="wants",add="6a7a4981"},{q="Why is Laurna Morninglight here in Dolanaar?",a="Dolanaar is the primary crossroads and gathering point for young adventurers leaving the secluded glades of Shadowglen. Laurna is stationed here to ensure that developing priests receive proper guidance, instruction, and sacred rites as they take on greater duties in Teldrassil.",al={"why is laurna in dolanaar","why is laurna morninglight here"},it="why_here",add="65cf8731"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a night elf priest arriving from Shadowglen, you can turn to Laurna Morninglight for foundational spells and guidance in devotion to Elune.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you follow the kaldorei devotion to the Moon Goddess. In Teldrassil, priestcraft draws on Elune rather than the Holy Light."},kw={"dolanaar","elune","kaldorei","laurna","morninglight","priest trainer","sisterhood of elune","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","topic:elune","topic:night-elf","quest:5621","quest:5622","quest:5634","quest:5628"},src={"Laurna Morninglight"}}
E["npc:mardant-strongoak"] = {t="npc",n="Mardant Strongoak",z="teldrassil",s="Mardant Strongoak is a night elf druid trainer residing in Aldrassil in the heart of Teldrassil. He guides fledgling druids in communing with the spirits of nature and introduces them to the mysteries of the Emerald Dream.",h="Mardant Strongoak is a night elf druid trainer residing in Aldrassil in the heart of Teldrassil.",sec={{t="Instructor of the Wilds",b="Within the boughs of Aldrassil, young night elves who feel the call of the wild turn to Mardant Strongoak. His primary task is teaching novitiates how to open their senses to nature spirits, interpret their murmurs, and channel rejuvenating magics. For those taking their initial steps as protectors of the wild, he is often the first master to unveil the vast complexities and ancient perils of the Emerald Dream.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Mardant Strongoak?",a="Mardant Strongoak is a night elf druid trainer stationed in Shadowglen within Aldrassil. He mentors newly awakened druids on Teldrassil in the basic arts of communion and spellcraft.",al={"mardant strongoak lore","who is mardant","mardant aldrassil"},it="identity"},{q="What does he teach new druids?",a="He teaches novitiates how to decipher the messages of wild spirits, cast rudimentary spells like Moonfire and healing arts, and grasp the nature of the Emerald Dream.",al={"what does mardant teach","mardant abilities","druid trainer shadowglen"},it="purpose"},{q="Where can I find Mardant Strongoak?",a="He is located inside or near Aldrassil in Shadowglen, the starting vale for night elf adventurers on Teldrassil.",al={"mardant location","where is mardant strongoak"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Verdant Sigil?",a="The Verdant Sigil is an instructional token presented to fledgling night elf druids in Shadowglen, directing them to seek out Mardant Strongoak for their early training.",al={"verdant sigil quest","sigil for mardant"},it="item"},{q="Whose side is Mardant Strongoak on?",a="Mardant Strongoak is devoted to the night elves, the Alliance, and the sacred tenets of the Cenarion Circle. He stands firmly within Shadowglen to safeguard the fledgling World Tree and ensure the traditions of the kaldorei druids endure in these uncertain times.",al={"mardant strongoak faction","who does mardant serve","is mardant alliance"},it="side",add="a3bbc1b2"},{q="What does Mardant Strongoak want?",a="Mardant wants young night elf initiates to deepen their communion with nature. He seeks to guide new druids through their initial trials, helping them decipher the whisperings of the spirits and navigate the profound mysteries and perils of the Emerald Dream.",al={"what does mardant want","mardant strongoak goals","what is mardant's goal"},it="wants",add="ff8559f4"},{q="Why is Mardant Strongoak here?",a="Stationed within the hollow boughs of Aldrassil, Mardant serves as a mentor for newly awakened druids taking their first steps in Teldrassil. He remains in Shadowglen to watch over novices, instruct them in their innate powers, and direct them toward those in need of aid across the glade.",al={"why is mardant in aldrassil","why is mardant strongoak here","mardant strongoak location reason"},it="why_here",add="b78651d9"},{q="Who is Mardant Strongoak tied to?",a="Mardant is closely tied to the Cenarion Circle and his fellow teachers in Aldrassil, such as the priestesses of Elune and the sentinels guarding the sanctuary. Together, they guide and nurture the young defenders of the night elves.",al={"mardant strongoak allies","who is mardant affiliated with","mardant connections"},it="ties",add="dec3bef7"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For young night elf druids, Mardant Strongoak is the first bridge between mundane existence and the sacred duties of the Cenarion circle.",["race:NightElf"]="Stationed at the core of Aldrassil, Mardant exemplifies the kaldorei devotion to harmonizing with Teldrassil's burgeoning ecosystem."},kw={"aldrassil","druid","emerald dream","mardant","shadowglen","strongoak","teldrassil","trainer"},rel={"subzone:aldrassil","zone:teldrassil","topic:druid","topic:emerald-dream","topic:night-elf","quest:3120"},src={"Mardant Strongoak"}}
E["npc:melithar-staghelm"] = {t="npc",n="Melithar Staghelm",z="teldrassil",s="Outside Aldrassil in Shadowglen, Melithar Staghelm guides young night elves. He sends them to learn why the dryad Tarindrella has returned to the glade. His Staghelm name links him to Archdruid Fandral Staghelm, though their connection is unknown.",h="Outside Aldrassil in Shadowglen, Melithar Staghelm guides young night elves.",sec={{t="A Guide at Aldrassil",b="Melithar Staghelm waits outside Aldrassil, where night elves first step into the world. A druid who listens to the forest spirits, he has learned that Tarindrella, a woodland protector, has returned to Shadowglen after years away. Sensing trouble, Melithar sends newcomers southwest of Aldrassil to find the dryad and learn why she has come back to the grove.",sp=0},{t="The Staghelm Name",b="The Staghelm name draws notice because Archdruid Fandral Staghelm leads the Cenarion Circle in Darnassus, after Malfurion Stormrage disappeared into the Emerald Dream. Melithar makes no claim to a grand heritage and says nothing of his lineage. Whether he belongs to the Archdruid's family or shares an ancient Kaldorei name remains unknown. For now, Melithar tends to his humble duties at the roots of Aldrassil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Melithar Staghelm?",a="Melithar Staghelm is a night elf who guides newcomers outside Aldrassil in Shadowglen. He sends them to find the dryad Tarindrella.",al={"melithar","who is melithar","melithar shadowglen"},it="identity"},{q="Is Melithar related to Archdruid Fandral Staghelm?",a="Their exact kinship is unknown. Melithar never says whether he is related to Archdruid Fandral Staghelm or Fandral's late son Valstann. He may be a distant relative, or they may simply share a Kaldorei surname.",al={"fandral relative","fandral brother","staghelm family"},it="ties"},{q="What role does Melithar play for new adventurers?",a="Melithar sends newcomers southwest of Aldrassil to find Tarindrella, a woodland protector who has returned to Shadowglen after years away. The forest spirits have told him of her return, and he wants them to learn why she has come to the grove.",al={"melithar quests","what does melithar do"},it="purpose"},{q="Where can I find Melithar Staghelm?",a="Melithar Staghelm stands on the wooden ramp outside Aldrassil's entrance, in the center of Shadowglen on Teldrassil.",al={"melithar location","where is melithar","find melithar staghelm"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Melithar Staghelm on?",a="Melithar stands with the night elves of Darnassus and the Alliance. Stationed at Shadowglen right outside Aldrassil, he assists young night elf defenders and recruits as they take their first steps in safeguarding the World Tree.",al={"melithar faction","who does melithar serve","melithar allegiance"},it="side",add="de95e555"},{q="What does Melithar Staghelm want?",a="Melithar works to protect Shadowglen and cleanse Teldrassil of burgeoning threats. Troubled by word from the forest spirits that the dryad Tarindrella has returned to the glade after years away, he asks incoming adventurers to seek her out and learn what is amiss.",al={"melithar goal","what is melithar doing","melithar purpose"},it="wants",add="67f605fc"},{q="Why is Melithar Staghelm here?",a="Melithar is stationed just outside Aldrassil in Shadowglen to watch over the bough and direct nascent night elf adventurers. He provides early guidance, tasking new defenders with curbing local corruption and maintaining harmony in Teldrassil's sacred nursery.",al={"why is melithar in shadowglen","melithar location reason"},it="why_here",add="f95cde78"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf setting out in Shadowglen, you meet Melithar soon after leaving Aldrassil's shelter."},kw={"aldrassil","melithar","shadowglen","staghelm","teldrassil","trainer"},rel={"subzone:aldrassil","npc:fandral-staghelm","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf","quest:458"},src={"Melithar Staghelm"}}
E["npc:moon-priestess-amara"] = {t="npc",n="Moon Priestess Amara",z="teldrassil",s="West of Dolanaar, Moon Priestess Amara watches Teldrassil’s road to Darnassus. Two huntresses guard her as she keeps watch over the woodland paths.",h="West of Dolanaar, Moon Priestess Amara watches Teldrassil’s road to Darnassus.",sec={{t="Guardian of the Boughways",b="Moon Priestess Amara watches the road west of Dolanaar with two huntress companions, Nhemai and Yaeliura. As a priestess of the Sisterhood of Elune, she brings spiritual guidance to her post, while her watch helps keep Teldrassil’s roads secure. Travelers heading west can seek her direction toward Darnassus. Those burdened in spirit can also seek a path of redemption from her.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Moon Priestess Amara?",a="Moon Priestess Amara, also known as Amara Nightwalker, is a priestess of the Sisterhood of Elune. She watches the road between Dolanaar and Darnassus in Teldrassil, tending to travelers’ safety and spiritual well-being.",al={"who is amara","priestess amara","sentinel amara nightwalker"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Moon Priestess Amara?",a="You can find her along the paved road just west of Dolanaar in Teldrassil, with two sentinel huntresses at her side.",al={"where is amara","amara location","priestess amara map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who are the huntresses standing with her?",a="Huntress Nhemai and Huntress Yaeliura accompany and guard Amara. The two night elf sentinels help protect the road from beasts and hostile corruption.",al={"amara companions","nhemai and yaeliura","amara guards"},it="allies"},{q="Whose side is Moon Priestess Amara on?",a="Moon Priestess Amara serves the Priesthood of Elune and the Alliance, watching over the sacred boughs of Teldrassil. Alongside her Sentinel companions, she stands dedicated to guiding travelers and defending the kaldorei heartland from the corruption that threatens its tranquil forests.",al={"amara faction","amara allegiance","who does amara serve"},it="side",add="3d569ab2"},{q="Why is Moon Priestess Amara stationed here?",a="Amara is stationed along the main road west of Dolanaar to safeguard travelers making the journey toward Darnassus. Teldrassil's pathways are increasingly besieged by corrupted beasts and lurking timberlings, making her presence vital in keeping the woodland paths secure.",al={"why is amara here","amara location purpose","why is moon priestess amara on the road"},it="why_here",add="75dde252"},{q="What does Moon Priestess Amara want?",a="She seeks capable adventurers to help secure the road to the capital city of Darnassus. Amara tasks travelers with dispatching the foul gnarlpine furbolgs and vicious forest creatures that harass those who journey westward beneath the boughs of the World Tree.",al={"what does amara need","amara quest motive","why does amara send you on quests"},it="wants",add="74974fcb"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest of the Sisterhood of Elune, you share Priestess Amara’s devotion to the Moon Goddess. She guides young acolytes setting out from Shadowglen.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you meet Amara on your journey west from Dolanaar. Her guidance and tasks lead toward Darnassus."},kw={"amara nightwalker","dolanaar","elanaria","moon priestess amara","nhemai","teldrassil","the road to darnassus","yaeliura"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","zone:darnassus","zone:teldrassil","npc:elanaria","quest:487","quest:489","topic:night-elf"},src={"Moon Priestess Amara"}}
E["npc:oben-rageclaw"] = {t="npc",n="Oben Rageclaw",z="teldrassil",s="In Ban'ethil Barrow Den, Oben Rageclaw's spirit wanders, unable to wake or pass on. His sleeping body remains under the Gnarlpine furbolgs' control.",h="In Ban'ethil Barrow Den, Oben Rageclaw's spirit wanders, unable to wake or pass on.",sec={{t="A Slumber Desecrated",b="Oben Rageclaw entered Ban'ethil Barrow Den to commune with nature and wander the Emerald Dream, as many Druids of the Claw do. When the Gnarlpine furbolgs fell to corruption and overran the barrows, Oben lay defenseless in his trance. A corrupted Gnarlpine shaman used dark rituals to take control of his comatose body. His spirit was left behind as an anguished ghost, unable to wake or pass on.",sp=0},{t="Severing the Vessel",b="Oben Rageclaw cannot reclaim his body from the shaman's control. Travelers moving through the dangerous tunnels can end his torment by finding and destroying the body the shaman commands. When that vessel falls, Oben's tortured ghost is released from the underground gloom and finds rest in the Emerald Dream.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Oben Rageclaw?",a="Oben Rageclaw is a night elf Druid of the Claw whose ghost wanders Ban'ethil Barrow Den in Teldrassil, separated from his body by corrupted furbolgs.",al={"who is oben","oben rageclaw lore","spirit in barrow den"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Oben Rageclaw a ghost?",a="Oben Rageclaw became a ghost while he slept in a druidic trance, communing with the Emerald Dream. Gnarlpine furbolg shamans entered the den, used foul magic to control his body, and trapped his spirit outside it.",al={"why is oben dead","how did oben die","why is oben a ghost"},it="why_here"},{q="Where is Oben's physical body?",a="Oben's body lies deeper in Ban'ethil Barrow Den's winding corridors, under the control of the Gnarlpine shamans who corrupted the den.",al={"find oben body","where is oben body","sleeping druid location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after Oben's body is destroyed?",a="When Oben's body is destroyed, the Gnarlpine shamans' hold over him is broken. His spirit can leave Teldrassil and find rest in the Emerald Dream.",al={"oben fate","what happens to oben spirit","saving oben"},sp=1,it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Oben Rageclaw on?",a="Oben Rageclaw is aligned with the night elves and the Cenarion Circle. Though a corrupted Gnarlpine shaman currently manipulates his slumbering physical form deep within the barrows, Oben's true spirit remains faithful to his people and seeks aid from passing adventurers to end his torment.",al={"is oben rageclaw friendly","oben rageclaw faction","who does oben serve"},it="side",add="9c749c17"},{q="What does Oben Rageclaw want?",a="Oben desires release from the unnatural hold binding his spirit to Ban'ethil Barrow Den. Because foul Gnarlpine magic has seized control of his physical body, he asks you to destroy his corrupted form so that his restless spirit may finally find peace in the Emerald Dream.",al={"what does oben want","oben rageclaw goal","oben rageclaw motive"},it="wants",add="98315864"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, Oben's fate shows how vulnerable druids are while communing with the Emerald Dream in a trance, when sacred barrow dens are undefended.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see how deeply the Gnarlpine furbolgs' corruption has touched Teldrassil's native denizens and sacred sanctuaries."},kw={"ban'ethil barrow den","druid of the claw","emerald dream","gnarlpine","oben rageclaw","teldrassil","the sleeping druid"},rel={"subzone:ban-ethil-barrow-den","quest:2541","quest:2561","zone:teldrassil","topic:druid","topic:emerald-dream","topic:night-elf"},src={"Oben Rageclaw"}}
E["npc:orenthil-whisperwind"] = {t="npc",n="Orenthil Whisperwind",z="teldrassil",s="Beneath Teldrassil’s boughs, Orenthil Whisperwind lives among the night elves of Shadowglen.",h="Beneath Teldrassil’s boughs, Orenthil Whisperwind lives among the night elves of Shadowglen.",sec={{t="A Friendly Face in Teldrassil",b="Orenthil Whisperwind lives among the night elves beneath Teldrassil’s canopy in Shadowglen. Little is known of his personal history.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Orenthil Whisperwind?",a="Orenthil Whisperwind is a night elf found in Shadowglen on Teldrassil. He welcomes adventurers setting out into the boughs of the World Tree.",al={"orenthil","orenthil whisperwind info","who is this elf"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Orenthil Whisperwind?",a="You can find Orenthil Whisperwind in Shadowglen, the night elf starting settlement within Teldrassil.",al={"orenthil location","where is orenthil","orenthil map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Orenthil Whisperwind on?",a="Orenthil stands firmly with the night elves of Darnassus and the greater Alliance. Found dwelling among his kin on the boughs of Teldrassil, he greets new travelers arriving to assist his people.",al={"orenthil whisperwind faction","is orenthil alliance","who does orenthil serve"},it="side",add="38b36176"},{q="Why is Orenthil Whisperwind here?",a="Orenthil resides in Shadowglen on Teldrassil. His personal reasons for settling there are not recorded.",al={"orenthil whisperwind purpose","why is orenthil in dolanaar","what is orenthil doing"},it="why_here",add="71428597"}},kw={"orenthil","shadowglen","teldrassil","whisperwind"},rel={"zone:teldrassil","subzone:shadowglen","topic:night-elf"},src={"Orenthil Whisperwind"}}
E["npc:sentinel-arynia-cloudsbreak"] = {t="npc",n="Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak",z="teldrassil",s="At Oracle Glade on Teldrassil, Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak watches over the northern groves. She guards the enchanted waters and woodland wildlife.",h="At Oracle Glade on Teldrassil, Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak watches over the northern groves.",sec={{t="Watcher of the Oracle Glade",b="Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak keeps watch in Oracle Glade, one of Teldrassil's most secluded reaches. Far from Darnassus, she serves the Sentinel army among ancient trees and ethereal springs, guarding the wilderness from disturbance.",sp=0},{t="Trouble in the Glade",b="Disharmony stirs among Teldrassil's creatures despite the tree's sacred birth. Arynia asks passing adventurers and young night elves to look into local troubles, from strange wildlife to mystical signs around the enchanted springs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak?",a="Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak is a night elf Sentinel guarding Oracle Glade in northern Teldrassil. She watches over the glade and asks travelers to help preserve its natural harmony.",al={"arynia cloudsbreak","who is arynia","sentinel arynia"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Arynia Cloudsbreak be found?",a="Arynia Cloudsbreak keeps watch in the open at Oracle Glade, in northwestern Teldrassil, north of Dolanaar.",al={"arynia location","where is arynia","arynia cloudsbreak map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What duties does she perform in the Sentinels?",a="Arynia patrols the outlying forest boughs and watches local spirits, wildlife, and natural phenomena for signs of corruption or imbalance.",al={"arynia role","what does arynia do"},it="purpose"},{q="Is she related to anyone else on Teldrassil?",a="Arynia Cloudsbreak shares her surname with Mavoris Cloudsbreak, suggesting a family bond among the night elves who dwell on the world tree.",al={"arynia family","mavoris cloudsbreak"},it="ties"},{q="What tasks does she give to adventurers?",a="Arynia asks travelers to investigate the enchanted glade, tend to mysterious disturbances and wandering beasts nearby, and aid creatures in distress.",al={"arynia quests","oracle glade quests"},it="wants"},{q="Why is the Oracle Glade significant to the night elves?",a="Night elves revere Oracle Glade as a sacred sanctuary in Teldrassil, known for tranquil pools. Druids and Sentinels watch over it, seeking nature's guidance and omens.",al={"why oracle glade","oracle glade lore"},it="place"},{q="Whose side is Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak on?",a="Arynia serves the Sentinels, the renowned martial arm of the night elf people, and is steadfastly loyal to the Darnassus leadership and the greater Alliance. Stationed among the peaceful groves of Teldrassil, her duty is to protect her homeland and ensure the spiritual sanctuaries of the Kaldorei remain undisturbed by corruption or outside threats.",al={"arynia cloudsbreak faction","arynia cloudsbreak alliance","who does arynia serve"},it="side",add="8186bb8d"},{q="Why is Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak in the Oracle Glade?",a="Arynia is stationed at the Oracle Glade to watch over the tranquil northern reaches of Teldrassil. The glade holds sacred significance for the night elves, and as a Sentinel, she remains on guard to look after local wildlife and attend to any disturbances that threaten the sanctity of the enchanted woods.",al={"why is arynia cloudsbreak here","arynia cloudsbreak oracle glade","why is sentinel arynia in oracle glade"},it="why_here",add="d0964425"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a young night elf coming of age on Teldrassil, helping Sentinel Cloudsbreak gives you practical experience protecting your new homeland's wild balance.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see Arynia uphold the Kaldorei Sentinels' watch over the Alliance's vital woodland stronghold in Kalimdor."},kw={"arynia cloudsbreak","enchanted glade","kaldorei","mist","night elf","oracle glade","sentinel","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:oracle-glade","zone:teldrassil","quest:937","quest:938","quest:940","topic:night-elf"},src={"Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak"}}
E["npc:shanda"] = {t="npc",n="Shanda",z="teldrassil",s="In Aldrassil, Shanda guides young night elf priests in the ways of Elune. She serves the Sisterhood of Elune in Shadowglen, teaching prayers, wards, and rites as her students prepare to defend Teldrassil.",h="In Aldrassil, Shanda guides young night elf priests in the ways of Elune.",sec={{t="Acolyte of the Moon Mother",b="Shanda guides young night elves devoted to Elune from within Aldrassil. While druids tend Teldrassil's roots and boughs, priestesses keep the Kaldorei close to the White Lady. Shanda teaches new initiates to call on lunar grace for healing and protective wards, preparing them to face the corruption creeping into the World Tree's boughs.",sp=0},{t="Guiding New Initiates",b="Young priests who awaken to their calling in Shadowglen come to Shanda to prove their devotion and learn their first prayers. Through rites such as In Favor of Elune, she tests their resolve, gives them blessed regalia, and teaches basic incantations. Her students learn to tend the wounded with a gentle hand and stand firm against the shadows.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Shanda?",a="Shanda trains night elf priests inside Aldrassil, the central hollow tree settlement of Shadowglen in Teldrassil. She teaches newly awakened priests the ways of the Sisterhood of Elune.",al={"who is this npc","shanda lore","priest trainer aldrassil"},it="identity"},{q="What role does Shanda play for new priests?",a="Shanda teaches novice priests basic prayers, curative spells, and protective magic gifted by Elune. New priests bring her their Hallowed Sigil, and she sends them on to the next stage of training through In Favor of Elune.",al={"priest trainer role","what does shanda teach","what does shanda do"},it="purpose"},{q="Where can I find Shanda?",a="Shanda is on the ground level inside Aldrassil's hollow trunk in Shadowglen, Teldrassil.",al={"where is shanda","shanda location","how to find shanda"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What organization does Shanda belong to?",a="Shanda belongs to the Sisterhood of Elune, the ancient order of night elf priestesses that has guided Kaldorei spiritual and cultural life for thousands of years.",al={"shanda faction","sisterhood of elune","is shanda a priestess of the moon"},it="side"},{q="What does Shanda want?",a="Shanda is dedicated to preparing the next generation of night elf priests to serve the Moon Goddess and protect their people. She seeks to guide young novices in channeling the divine grace of Elune, teaching them how to mend injuries, shield their allies, and smite the growing corruption creeping into the Shadowglen.",al={"what are shanda's goals","shanda motive","what does priest trainer shanda want"},it="wants",add="35bebf44"},{q="Why is Shanda in Aldrassil?",a="As newly awakened defenders gather within the sacred haven of Aldrassil, seasoned mentors are needed to hone their raw talents. Shanda remains stationed at the foot of the great bough in the Shadowglen to watch over emerging priest novices, ensuring they learn the rites and powers of Elune before venturing deeper into Teldrassil.",al={"why is shanda here","why is shanda in shadowglen","shanda location reason"},it="why_here",add="44a52b27"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a night elf priest beginning in Shadowglen, you can turn to Shanda for sacred words and guidance in Elune's grace.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you inherit the Sisterhood of Elune's tradition. Shanda tends to the spiritual well-being of Kaldorei youth taking their first steps on Teldrassil."},kw={"aldrassil","elune","night elf","priest trainer","shadowglen","shanda","sisterhood of elune","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:aldrassil","zone:teldrassil","topic:elune","topic:night-elf","quest:5622","quest:940"},src={"Shanda"}}
E["npc:syral-bladeleaf"] = {t="npc",n="Syral Bladeleaf",z="teldrassil",s="In Dolanaar, Syral Bladeleaf guides night elves arriving from Shadowglen. As a resident of Teldrassil, she speaks for the Council of the Forest and directs them to local caretakers, herbalists, and elders who watch over the crown's boughs.",h="In Dolanaar, Syral Bladeleaf guides night elves arriving from Shadowglen.",sec={{t="A Voice in Dolanaar",b="Syral Bladeleaf helps direct new arrivals through Dolanaar beneath Teldrassil's canopy. She speaks for the Council of the Forest, sending night elves to community leaders and herbalists in the village and nearby wilderness. Her guidance leads travelers to Denalan, a botanist at Lake Al'Ameth, and helps them replenish supplies for the village elders.",sp=0},{t="Ties to the Village",b="In Dolanaar, Syral carries out the Council of the Forest's work for the village. She helps see that medicinal elixirs reach those in need and that disruptions to the local ecosystem receive swift attention.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Syral Bladeleaf?",a="Syral Bladeleaf is a night elf in Dolanaar who conveys the Council of the Forest's directives and helps newcomers assist woodland communities.",al={"who is syral","syral bladeleaf lore","syral dolanaar"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Syral Bladeleaf be found?",a="Syral Bladeleaf can be found in Dolanaar, Teldrassil's central settlement, just southwest of Shadowglen along the main road.",al={"syral bladeleaf location","where is syral","syral map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What tasks does she assign to adventurers?",a="Syral sends travelers to help Denalan, the botanist at Lake Al'Ameth, arrange herbal elixirs for the elders, and aid Teldrassil's natural balance.",al={"syral bladeleaf quests","what does syral want","syral tasks"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Syral Bladeleaf on?",a="Syral serves Darnassus and the Alliance. Stationed in Dolanaar, she acts directly on behalf of the Council of the Forest, helping ensure that the local wilderness and its caretakers remain safeguarded against Teldrassil's creeping troubles.",al={"syral bladeleaf faction","who does syral bladeleaf serve","syral bladeleaf allegiance"},it="side",add="39456ef3"},{q="What does Syral Bladeleaf want?",a="Syral wants to see the will of the Council of the Forest carried out. She relays their directives to capable adventurers, seeking aid for nearby allies like Denalan and working to keep the growing corruption in Teldrassil under control.",al={"what does syral bladeleaf want","syral bladeleaf goals","syral bladeleaf motives"},it="wants",add="47edbb6a"},{q="Why is Syral Bladeleaf in Dolanaar?",a="Syral is stationed in Dolanaar to serve as a vital liaison for the Council of the Forest. From this central settlement, she can easily recruit passing travelers and young night elves to tend to the needs of the boughs and support local caretakers.",al={"why is syral bladeleaf here","syral bladeleaf dolanaar reason","why is syral in dolanaar"},it="why_here",add="7fd35b53"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a young night elf leaving Shadowglen's secluded barrows, you meet one of Dolanaar's first voices of civic and natural leadership in Syral Bladeleaf.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As an herbalist, you can help Syral direct travelers to Denalan's botanical research at Lake Al'Ameth and see that fresh elixirs reach the elders."},kw={"bladeleaf","council of the forest","denalan","dolanaar","elder bladeleaf","syral","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","npc:denalan","quest:997","quest:1581","quest:489","topic:night-elf"},src={"Syral Bladeleaf"}}
E["npc:tallonkai-swiftroot"] = {t="npc",n="Tallonkai Swiftroot",z="teldrassil",s="In Dolanaar, Tallonkai Swiftroot watches the woods as corruption spreads beneath Teldrassil’s boughs. He sends young adventurers to recover enchanted relics and check the foul forces troubling the forest.",h="In Dolanaar, Tallonkai Swiftroot watches the woods as corruption spreads beneath Teldrassil’s boughs.",sec={{t="A Sentinel of Dolanaar",b="Tallonkai Swiftroot watches the woods from Dolanaar, the settlement in Teldrassil’s canopy. Like many night elves beneath the newly grown World Tree, he is alarmed by wildlife acting in unnatural ways and shadows gathering at the edges of their homes.",sp=0},{t="Threats in the Canopy",b="Tallonkai sends adventurers against the foul beings disturbing Teldrassil’s peace. Corrupted dream catchers threaten the sleep of druids, while gnarlpine furbolgs have grown vicious under a dark malaise. Ferocitas the Dream Eater leads corrupted Gnarlpine mystics. Tallonkai seeks to cleanse these threats and defend the Kaldorei’s fragile home.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tallonkai Swiftroot?",a="Tallonkai Swiftroot watches over Dolanaar and works to protect it from nearby threats. He is a night elf who lives in the settlement on Teldrassil’s boughs.",al={"who is tallonkai","tallonkai swiftroot","dolanaar questgiver"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Tallonkai Swiftroot?",a="Tallonkai Swiftroot is in Dolanaar, the central night elf village just outside Shadowglen in Teldrassil.",al={"tallonkai location","where is tallonkai","find tallonkai swiftroot"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What tasks does Tallonkai give?",a="Tallonkai asks travelers to retrieve the Emerald Dreamcatcher from the gnarlpine furbolgs, defeat Ferocitas the Dream Eater, and slay Lord Melenas in his cave at Fel Rock in Twisted Hatred.",al={"tallonkai quests","what does tallonkai want"},gp=true},{q="Why is he concerned about the dreamcatchers?",a="Dreamcatchers are sacred night elf talismans tied to the Emerald Dream. They ward against nightmares and dark visions, so their theft and corruption endanger the local druids and other residents of Teldrassil.",al={"emerald dreamcatcher lore","why dreamcatchers"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Ferocitas the Dream Eater?",a="Ferocitas the Dream Eater leads corrupted Gnarlpine mystics north of Starbreeze. He stole the emerald from Tallonkai’s dreamcatcher and wears it on a necklace that glows green at night.",al={"who is ferocitas","ferocitas lore"},it="target"},{q="What is causing the unrest Tallonkai fights against?",a="A growing sickness and unnatural corruption have spread through Teldrassil. They drive once peaceful creatures, including the gnarlpine furbolgs, into violent madness.",al={"why are furbolgs mad","twisted hatred lore"},it="threat"},{q="Whose side is Tallonkai Swiftroot on?",a="Tallonkai stands firmly with the night elves of Darnassus and the Alliance. Stationed in Dolanaar, he works to protect Teldrassil's burgeoning settlements from corruption and the wild beasts disturbed across the boughs.",al={"tallonkai swiftroot faction","who does tallonkai serve","tallonkai swiftroot allegiance"},it="side",add="cb092b62"},{q="What does Tallonkai Swiftroot want?",a="Tallonkai wants to safeguard Dolanaar and soothe the corrupted wildlife of Teldrassil. He seeks the recovery of sacred Emerald Dreamcatchers stolen by tainted gnarlpine furbolgs, and demands the eradication of foul threats like Ferocitas the Dream Eater and the corrupted satyrs whose hatred poisons the woods.",al={"what does tallonkai want","tallonkai goal","tallonkai motives"},it="wants",add="ea33b78b"},{q="Why is Tallonkai Swiftroot in Dolanaar?",a="Tallonkai is stationed in Dolanaar to monitor rising disturbances in the surrounding wilderness. As corrupted furbolgs and vile beasts threaten the road and settlements of Teldrassil, he remains in town to recruit capable adventurers to strike back at the woodland's blights.",al={"why is tallonkai here","why is tallonkai swiftroot in dolanaar","what brings tallonkai to dolanaar"},it="why_here",add="bffc0ef8"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you can help protect Teldrassil while corruption takes root in your new home.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you know the spiritual importance of relics that keep minds safely tied to the Emerald Dream."},kw={"dolanaar","dreamcatcher","ferocitas","tallonkai swiftroot","teldrassil","twisted hatred"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","quest:2438","quest:2459","quest:932","topic:night-elf"},src={"Tallonkai Swiftroot"}}
E["npc:tarindrella"] = {t="npc",n="Tarindrella",z="teldrassil",s="In Shadowglen, Tarindrella watches over Teldrassil's sheltered woods. The dryad works with night elf protectors to investigate corruption among the World Tree's wildlife.",h="In Shadowglen, Tarindrella watches over Teldrassil's sheltered woods.",sec={{t="A Daughter of Cenarius in Shadowglen",b="Tarindrella dwells in Shadowglen, a protected glade atop Teldrassil. Dryads are fierce caretakers of nature, born of the demigod Cenarius. Many live deep in ancient Kalimdor forests such as Ashenvale, but Tarindrella watches over this young grove. She bridges the wild spirits and young night elf defenders taking their first steps beyond Aldrassil. Her chief concern is a taint creeping through the forest. She sends reliable adventurers to drive back local pests and gather clues to its source.",sp=0},{t="Investigating Teldrassil's Affliction",b="Teldrassil is the new crown of the night elf people, yet sickness has reached its groves. Furbolgs once lived peacefully in their homes; now they have gathered as the Gnarlpine tribe. Grells and grellkin tainted by wicked Fel Moss infest the hills around Shadowglen. Tarindrella suspects the moss is behind these changes. She directs initiates to confront the grells and bring back samples, hoping to halt the corruption before it overtakes the young grove.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tarindrella?",a="In Shadowglen atop Teldrassil, Tarindrella aids night elves in watching the wilderness. The dryad directs young defenders against a strange sickness threatening the World Tree's boughs.",al={"tarindrella lore","who is tarindrella","dryad shadowglen"},it="identity"},{q="What is a dryad?",a="Dryads are woodland beings born of the demigod Cenarius. With the upper body of a night elf and the lower body of a fawn, they guard Kalimdor's sacred groves and their balance.",al={"dryad lore","what are dryads","daughters of cenarius"},it="people"},{q="Why is Tarindrella concerned about Shadowglen?",a="Unnatural corruption is twisting creatures around Shadowglen. Furbolgs have gathered as the hostile Gnarlpine tribe, and Fel Moss-tainted grells fill the hills. Tarindrella seeks to cleanse the taint and protect the young grove.",al={"shadowglen corruption","tarindrella quests","what is wrong with shadowglen"},it="why_here"},{q="What threats does she send adventurers to face?",a="Tarindrella sends adventurers to confront grells and grellkin in Shadowglen and gather the wicked Fel Moss they carry. She hopes to learn whether it lies behind the corruption.",al={"tarindrella spiders","shadowthread cave quests"},it="threat"},{q="Whose side is Tarindrella on?",a="Tarindrella is aligned with the kaldorei and the Cenarion Circle, standing as a protector of nature alongside the night elves. As a daughter of Cenarius, she serves the natural balance and aids young night elf adventurers who set out to defend Teldrassil from harm.",al={"tarindrella faction","who does tarindrella serve","tarindrella alliance or horde"},it="side",add="af6c0001"},{q="What does Tarindrella want?",a="Tarindrella seeks to root out and cleanse the unnatural corruption afflicting the boughs of Teldrassil. She enlists you to investigate the tainted wildlife of Shadowglen and combat the dark blight spreading through the glade's woods and dens.",al={"what does tarindrella want","tarindrella goal","tarindrella purpose"},it="wants",add="d6824959"},{q="Who is Tarindrella tied to?",a="As a dryad, Tarindrella is a daughter of the demigod Cenarius, sharing kinship with the keepers of the grove and other woodland spirits of Kalimdor. Her bonds tie her deeply to the night elves and the druids who revere her father's teachings.",al={"tarindrella family","tarindrella ties","who is tarindrella related to"},it="ties",add="05d535f9"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a young night elf in Shadowglen, you may meet Tarindrella, a dryad who embodies the ancient covenant between the Kaldorei and the children of Cenarius.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you regard dryads as kindred spirits of the wild. Tarindrella's guidance on Teldrassil's sickness calls you to help keep the balance."},kw={"aldrassil","dryad","shadowglen","shadowthread","tarindrella","teldrassil","webwood"},rel={"subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil","subzone:shadowthread-cave","quest:458","quest:940","topic:elune"},src={"Tarindrella"}}
E["npc:tenaron-stormgrip"] = {t="npc",n="Tenaron Stormgrip",z="teldrassil",s="High in Aldrassil, Tenaron Stormgrip guides young night elves through their people's recent history. He also asks them to gather water from a moonwell.",h="High in Aldrassil, Tenaron Stormgrip guides young night elves through their people's recent history.",sec={{t="Watcher of Aldrassil",b="Tenaron Stormgrip guides young night elves on Aldrassil's winding wooden platforms. From high in Shadowglen's central tree, he watches the local woods and their moonwells. He teaches novices about their spiritual bond with the World Tree.",sp=0},{t="Crown of the Earth",b="Tenaron sends initiates to gather a phial of water from the moonwell north of Aldrassil. Along the way, he teaches them what followed the Battle of Mount Hyjal. Their journey carries on through Teldrassil and into Darnassus.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Tenaron Stormgrip located?",a="Tenaron Stormgrip stands on the wooden platforms high in Aldrassil, the central tree of Shadowglen in Teldrassil.",al={"tenaron location","where is tenaron","tenaron stormgrip spot"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Tenaron Stormgrip's role in Shadowglen?",a="Tenaron Stormgrip guides young night elves in Shadowglen and teaches them about the aftermath of the Battle of Mount Hyjal.",al={"what does tenaron do","tenaron stormgrip purpose","who is tenaron"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the Crown of the Earth quest?",a="Tenaron asks initiates to gather moonwell water in a phial. The journey teaches them recent night elf history and continues across Teldrassil.",al={"crown of the earth lore","why carry moonwell water"}},{q="Why is Tenaron concerned about Teldrassil's waters?",a="Tenaron watches Teldrassil's waters because its moonwells are vessels of Elune's grace and natural purity. Since Teldrassil is young and lacks the full blessing of the Aspects, caretakers monitor its water sources for corruption or taint.",al={"why precious waters","teldrassil water issues"},it="motive"},{q="Does Tenaron send adventurers beyond Shadowglen?",a="Yes. Tenaron sends initiates beyond Shadowglen to Dolanaar, where they can continue serving the kaldorei.",al={"tenaron next quest","where does tenaron send you"},it="next_step"},{q="Is Tenaron a druid or a priest?",a="Tenaron's class is not established. He teaches recent night elf history and explains the significance of moonwells.",al={"tenaron stormgrip class","is tenaron druid"},it="identity"},{q="Whose side is Tenaron Stormgrip on?",a="Tenaron is devoted entirely to the night elves of Darnassus and the well-being of Teldrassil. He works alongside the druids and priests tending the Great Tree, guiding fledgling defenders who step forth from Aldrassil to protect their homeland and serve the Alliance.",al={"tenaron faction","is tenaron alliance","who does tenaron serve"},it="side",add="594d14e3"},{q="What does Tenaron Stormgrip want?",a="Tenaron seeks to nurture and protect Teldrassil from the corruption creeping into its boughs. He watches over the waters of Shadowglen and tasks promising adventurers with gathering moonwell water while learning the recent history of their people to ensure the Great Tree flourishes.",al={"what does tenaron want","tenaron goal","tenaron stormgrip mission"},it="wants",add="4431413b"},{q="Why is Tenaron Stormgrip here?",a="Stationed high within the great tree Aldrassil, Tenaron oversees the heart of Shadowglen. He remains here to evaluate new night elven initiates, monitor the sacred waters that feed the boughs, and coordinate the first steps in preserving Teldrassil's burgeoning growth.",al={"why is tenaron in aldrassil","why is tenaron here","tenaron shadowglen role"},it="why_here",add="62d582e4"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For young night elves, Tenaron Stormgrip offers an early lesson in the communal and spiritual duties of keeping Teldrassil alive and pure.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can see in Tenaron's tasks the care needed to watch over Teldrassil's rapid growth and guard against subtle corruption."},kw={"aldrassil","cenarion circle","crown of the earth","moonwell","shadowglen","stormgrip","teldrassil","tenaron"},rel={"subzone:aldrassil","zone:teldrassil","quest:929","quest:940","topic:night-elf"},src={"Tenaron Stormgrip"}}
E["npc:vesprystus"] = {t="npc",n="Vesprystus",z="teldrassil",s="At Rut'theran Village, Vesprystus sends travelers between Teldrassil and mainland Kalimdor. He tends the hippogryph roost at the great World Tree's base.",h="At Rut'theran Village, Vesprystus sends travelers between Teldrassil and mainland Kalimdor.",sec={{t="Keeper of the Rut'theran Roost",b="At Teldrassil's southern base, Vesprystus tends the Rut'theran roost. Trained hippogryphs carry travelers from the isolated elven boughs toward Darkshore and the mainland. A magical portal also links Rut'theran to Darnassus in the canopy above. Across the strait, Vesprystus works with the flight master at Auberdine to carry sentinels, emissaries, and adventurers into Kalimdor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does Vesprystus fly travelers?",a="Vesprystus flies travelers from Rut'theran Village across the water to Auberdine, on the coast of Darkshore. From there, connecting hippogryph routes lead south toward Ashenvale and other night elf enclaves across Kalimdor.",al={"where can he take me","vesprystus flight paths","rut'theran flight route"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What creatures does Vesprystus tend?",a="Vesprystus tends a roost of loyal night elf hippogryphs, ancient winged beasts native to northern Kalimdor. Night elves have raised and bonded with them for generations to travel forest canopies and rugged coastlines.",al={"what mounts does he have","vesprystus animals","what does he fly"},gp=true},{q="How do you reach Darnassus from where Vesprystus stands?",a="You can reach Darnassus from Rut'theran Village without a flight. A shimmering pink-tinted portal just up the path from Vesprystus's roost carries travelers to the city canopy.",al={"how to get to darnassus from vesprystus","vesprystus to darnassus","path to darnassus"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Vesprystus?",a="Vesprystus is a night elf hippogryph master stationed at Rut'theran Village at the base of Teldrassil. He is responsible for managing the roosts and providing reliable aerial transport for travelers moving between the great boughs of Darnassus above and the coastal settlements of northern Kalimdor.",al={"who is vesprystus","vesprystus night elf","vesprystus lore"},it="identity",add="e8883b50"},{q="Whose side is Vesprystus on?",a="He is loyal to Darnassus and the Alliance. His roosts serve night elf sentinels, druids, and visiting allies who need safe, swift passage into and out of Teldrassil.",al={"vesprystus alliance","vesprystus faction","who does vesprystus serve"},it="side",add="f70b999e"},{q="Why is Vesprystus here?",a="Rut'theran Village serves as the vital harbor and arrival point for Teldrassil. Because the World Tree rises steeply from the ocean, overland travel is impossible. Vesprystus stays here to keep the roosts supplied and ensure hippogryphs are always ready to ferry messengers, provisions, and travelers across the water to the mainland.",al={"why is vesprystus at rut'theran","vesprystus purpose here","why is vesprystus in ruttheran"},it="why_here",add="433ae265"},{q="What does Vesprystus want?",a="He wants to ensure his hippogryphs are well cared for and that flight routes connecting Teldrassil to neighboring outposts remain open and secure. He aids travelers and couriers carrying essential deliveries across the sea.",al={"what does vesprystus need","vesprystus goals","vesprystus motivation"},it="wants",add="5aeefd6f"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a young night elf leaving Teldrassil for the first time, you may find Vesprystus ready to send you toward your first glimpse of mainland Kalimdor.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler arriving at Teldrassil's docks, you can turn to Vesprystus for swift passage to coastal Darkshore."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","flight master","hippogryph master","rut'theran village","teldrassil","vesprystus"},rel={"subzone:rut-theran-village","quest:6342","quest:6341","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","zone:darnassus","quest:940","topic:night-elf"},src={"Vesprystus"}}
E["npc:zarrin"] = {t="npc",n="Zarrin",z="teldrassil",s="Behind Dolanaar's inn, Zarrin teaches the ways of Kaldorei cooking. He tends an open hearth on Teldrassil, where young night elves and visitors learn to prepare meals from the tree's native flora and fauna.",h="Behind Dolanaar's inn, Zarrin teaches the ways of Kaldorei cooking.",sec={{t="Hearthkeeper of Dolanaar",b="Behind Dolanaar's inn, Zarrin tends an open cooking fire and teaches Kaldorei culinary arts. Teldrassil's native plants and animals provide food for those who live here. Zarrin shows visitors how to forage and prepare meals at home.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Zarrin?",a="Find Zarrin behind the inn in Dolanaar, at a cooking fire in the open yard across from the road.",al={"zarrin location","where is zarrin","dolanaar cooking trainer"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Zarrin teach?",a="Zarrin teaches the basics of cooking and traditional night elf recipes to novices.",al={"zarrin trainer","what does zarrin teach"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What tasks does Zarrin offer?",a="Zarrin asks travelers to help prepare traditional dishes through Recipe of the Kaldorei, teaching newcomers local cooking practices.",al={"zarrin quest","recipe of the kaldorei quest"},gp=true},{q="Who is Zarrin?",a="Zarrin is a night elf culinary mentor tending his hearth in Dolanaar. Stationed just behind the village inn, he spends his days by the open fire instructing young travelers and local sentinels in the traditional culinary arts of the kaldorei.",al={"who is zarrin","zarrin lore","zarrin identity"},it="identity",add="43472bbf"},{q="Whose side is Zarrin on?",a="Zarrin stands loyally with Darnassus and the greater Alliance. He resides peacefully within Teldrassil's borders, offering his hearth and culinary knowledge to any friendly travelers who visit the settlement of Dolanaar.",al={"zarrin faction","zarrin alliance","who does zarrin serve"},it="side",add="9b474307"},{q="What does Zarrin want?",a="Zarrin is dedicated to preserving and passing along the traditional culinary heritage of the kaldorei. He seeks to instruct emerging adventurers on how to prepare wholesome meals from the bounteous wildlife and flora of Teldrassil.",al={"what does zarrin want","zarrin goals","zarrin purpose"},it="wants",add="08ffbf8a"},{q="Why is Zarrin in Dolanaar?",a="Dolanaar is the primary crossroads for young night elves venturing forth from Shadowglen. Zarrin keeps his spit and cookfire behind the local inn so he can readily supply novice wanderers with vital survival recipes before they brave deeper perils.",al={"why is zarrin in dolanaar","why is zarrin here","zarrin location why"},it="why_here",add="351be696"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As you begin your journey in Teldrassil, Zarrin can teach you to prepare nourishing meals from wild beast meat and foraged goods.",["race:NightElf"]="Zarrin keeps everyday Kaldorei foodways alive, passing traditional tastes and methods on beneath the World Tree's canopy."},kw={"cooking","dolanaar","kaldorei","teldrassil","trainer","zarrin"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","quest:4161","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf"},src={"Zarrin"}}
E["npc:zenn-foulhoof"] = {t="npc",n="Zenn Foulhoof",z="teldrassil",s="East of Dolanaar, Zenn Foulhoof asks travelers for forest reagents. The night elves watch him closely.",h="East of Dolanaar, Zenn Foulhoof asks travelers for forest reagents.",sec={{t="A Schemer in the Woods",b="Zenn Foulhoof keeps a place just outside Dolanaar, where the night elves tolerate him under watch. Most satyrs serve demonic masters and attack openly, but Zenn offers a friendly face. He says he has changed, or asks to trade for nightsaber fangs, strigid owl feathers, and webwood spider silk. Gullible youths gather the ingredients he needs for foul rituals. Dolanaar's council will not let him act unchecked. They order travelers to feed him corrupted forest fruit, humiliating him by turning the scheming satyr into a harmless frog for a time.",sp=1,bt={"q488.2"}}},faq={{q="Why isn't Zenn Foulhoof immediately attacked by the night elves?",a="Zenn Foulhoof keeps a friendly face and has not openly committed atrocities on the World Tree. Dolanaar's council watches him and chooses public humiliation over an immediate death sentence.",al={"why is zenn friendly","why don't night elves kill zenn","is zenn foulhoof evil"},it="why_here"},{q="What happens when you feed Zenn the corrupted cones and berries?",a="Dolanaar's elders order the corrupted fruit as penance for Zenn's misdeeds. The punishment's result appears when he eats it.",al={"zenn redemption quest","seek redemption quest","zenn frog"},sp=1},{q="What is a satyr?",a="Satyrs were night elves who became horned, cloven-hoofed fiends during the War of the Ancients after pledging service to the Burning Legion. Most are deeply corrupted and violently hostile to their uncorrupted kin.",al={"what are satyrs","satyr lore"},it="origin"},{q="Who is Zenn Foulhoof?",a="Zenn Foulhoof is a solitary satyr found lurking just east of Dolanaar in Teldrassil. While satyrs are demonic beings and ancient enemies of the night elves, Zenn claims to seek a peaceful existence, living quietly among the boughs of the World Tree rather than openly attacking the local denizens.",al={"who is zenn","zenn foulhoof lore","who is foulhoof"},it="identity",add="1240b4a1"},{q="Whose side is Zenn Foulhoof on?",a="Zenn is ultimately on his own side, cloaking sinister intentions beneath a harmless, cooperative facade. Though he presents himself peacefully to young adventurers and interacts without overt hostility, he is up to no good, manipulating outsiders into aiding his corrupt schemes while walking a fine line under the watchful eyes of Dolanaar's council.",al={"is zenn evil","zenn foulhoof faction","is zenn friendly"},sp=1,it="side",add="8f35fa9f"},{q="What does Zenn Foulhoof want?",a="Zenn asks passing adventurers to gather nightsaber fangs, strigid owl feathers, and webwood spider silk as reagents for his secret business in the forest.",al={"what does zenn want","zenn foulhoof motives","zenn bidding goal"},sp=1,it="wants",add="7266a9e7"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, seeing a satyr lounging on Teldrassil's sacred boughs insults Elune and the spirits of the wild. Satyrs have betrayed kaldorei heritage.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you may see Zenn's tampering with wild reagents and spreading corrupting taints as an offense against Cenarion teachings, which seek to keep Teldrassil pristine."},kw={"corrupted cone","dolanaar","satyr","seek redemption","teldrassil","zenn foulhoof"},rel={"topic:satyr","subzone:dolanaar","quest:488","quest:489","zone:teldrassil"},src={"Zenn Foulhoof"}}
E["quest:1581"] = {t="quest",n="Elixirs for the Bladeleafs",z="teldrassil",s="Syral Bladeleaf seeks help keeping her family’s busy trade supplied in Dolanaar. Her husband spends nearly all his time brewing, and fresh elixirs could ease his workload while earning the brewer uncommon herbs.",h="Syral Bladeleaf seeks help keeping her family’s busy trade supplied in Dolanaar.",sec={{t="A Burden of Prosperity",b="Dolanaar draws travelers, sentinels, and druids moving through Teldrassil. Syral Bladeleaf and her husband have built a flourishing herb and alchemy trade to serve them. Demand keeps her husband bent over vials and cauldrons for nearly all his hours, leaving the couple little time together.",sp=0},{t="A Trader's Exchange",b="Syral turns to passing herbalists and brewers to ease her husband’s workload. She asks for Elixirs of Lion's Strength and Minor Defense, offering freshly gathered, uncommon herbs in exchange. For a fledgling alchemist practicing beneath the Great Tree, the exchange brings a bundle of herbs and a chance to turn common forest flora into coveted regional flora.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Syral Bladeleaf need these potions?",a="Syral Bladeleaf’s family shop in Dolanaar has grown busy, and her husband spends nearly all his time brewing to meet demand. Having someone else prepare the elixirs gives him a much-needed break.",al={"why need elixirs","syral bladeleaf motive","bladeleaf shop problem"},it="motive"},{q="What potions are required for the task?",a="Syral asks for six Elixirs of Lion's Strength and two Elixirs of Minor Defense. Adventurers and local sentinels in Teldrassil often buy both kinds.",al={"which elixirs","what do i need to brew","potions needed"},gp=true},{q="What herbs are needed to brew the required elixirs?",a="The batch calls for Silverleaf, Earthroot, and standard Crystal Vials. Silverleaf and Earthroot grow across Teldrassil’s forest floor.",al={"ingredients needed","mats for elixirs","what herbs do i pick"},gp=true},{q="Who can undertake this request?",a="This request is offered to alchemists with basic competence in the craft. Syral wants dependable, well-mixed remedies for her shop.",al={"level requirement","profession requirement","can anyone do this quest"},gp=true},{q="What does Syral offer in exchange for the elixirs?",a="Syral offers a bundle of freshly gathered, uncommon herbs, difficult to find casually along Teldrassil’s woodland trails.",al={"reward lore","what does syral give","bladeleaf trade reward"},gp=true},{q="Where is Syral Bladeleaf located?",a="Syral Bladeleaf is outside the northern building in Dolanaar, near the central road through the forest village.",al={"where is syral","bladeleaf location","where do i turn this in"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Elixir of Lion's Strength for?",a="The Elixir of Lion's Strength is a staple draught among frontline warriors and alchemists, brewed to temporarily bolster the physical might of anyone who drinks it. Syral Bladeleaf stocks it in Dolanaar to meet the constant demands of hunters, sentinels, and travelers preparing to face the dangerous wildlands of Teldrassil.",al={"elixir of lions strength use","why lion strength elixir","elixir of lion's strength purpose"},it="item",add="c3ad307f"},{q="What is the Elixir of Minor Defense for?",a="The Elixir of Minor Defense is an alchemical concoction designed to harden the skin and fortify natural armor against physical strikes. Syral Bladeleaf keeps it on hand to sell in her shop, catering to protectors and adventurers who need reliable, basic safeguarding while patrolling the boughs of the great tree.",al={"elixir of minor defense use","why minor defense elixir","elixir of minor defense purpose"},it="item",add="34301f2f"}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Teldrassil’s rich soil holds Silverleaf and Earthroot, so you can forage the raw herbs for Syral’s shop order.",["race:NightElf"]="As a Night Elf, you know the Bladeleafs’ trade is part of Dolanaar’s life beneath Teldrassil’s canopy.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can help keep Dolanaar supplied with restorative and defensive draughts for defenders and traveling allies facing woodland threats."},kw={"alchemy","dolanaar","earthroot","elixir of lion's strength","elixir of minor defense","elixirs for the bladeleafs","silverleaf","syral bladeleaf","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:syral-bladeleaf","subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf","topic:alliance"},m={start="Syral Bladeleaf",faction="Alliance",id=1581,ri={"Elixir of Lion's Strength","Elixir of Minor Defense"}},src={"Elixirs for the Bladeleafs"}}
E["quest:2159"] = {t="quest",n="Dolanaar Delivery",z="teldrassil",s="Travelers leave Shadowglen with a parcel of herbs bound for Dolanaar. Porthannius, occupied with the druids, asks them to carry it south, marking their first venture beyond the sheltered glade.",h="Travelers leave Shadowglen with a parcel of herbs bound for Dolanaar.",sec={{t="A Messenger for Shadowglen",b="Porthannius asks travelers heading south from Shadowglen to carry a bundle of freshly harvested herbs along the forest path. He is occupied with pressing business alongside the druids tending the glade, and cannot leave to handle the errand himself. The bundle goes south as young adventurers prepare to leave the training grounds for the wider reaches of Teldrassil.",sp=0},{t="The Road to Dolanaar",b="The southern road from Shadowglen leads to Dolanaar, a foremost night elf settlement on Teldrassil's great boughs. Innkeeper Keldamyr oversees hospitality, rest, and supplies for wanderers, sentinels, and druids. When he receives the herbs on Porthannius's behalf, he urges young adventurers to rest their minds and spirits before facing the corruption spreading across the world tree.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Porthannius?",a="Porthannius is a night elf who lives in Shadowglen, Teldrassil's starting glade. He works with the local druids and asks travelers leaving the glade to carry supplies south for him.",al={"porthannius","who gives dolanaar delivery","quest giver porthannius"},it="identity"},{q="Why can't Porthannius deliver the herbs himself?",a="Urgent business with Shadowglen's druids keeps Porthannius occupied in the sheltered vale, so he relies on passing adventurers to carry the herbs south.",al={"why does porthannius need help","why cant porthannius go"},it="why_me"},{q="What is inside the package?",a="The package holds herbs gathered in Shadowglen for use at the inn in Dolanaar.",al={"dolanaar delivery package contents","what are the herbs"},it="item"},{q="Who is Innkeeper Keldamyr?",a="Innkeeper Keldamyr manages Dolanaar's inn, offering travelers hospitality, lodging, and hearthstones. He also coordinates trade and supply exchanges with other settlements across Teldrassil.",al={"keldamyr","dolanaar innkeeper","who receives the herbs"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Dolanaar located?",a="Dolanaar lies south of Shadowglen. The primary road from the glade's exit leads travelers directly to the town center.",al={"where is dolanaar","dolanaar location","directions to dolanaar"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is this delivery important for young adventurers?",a="The delivery introduces young adventurers to the world beyond Shadowglen and encourages them to venture out and discover Dolanaar's inn, trainers, and service providers.",al={"significance of delivery","why deliver herbs"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Porthannius need this package delivered to Dolanaar?",a="Porthannius has prepared a vital bundle of fresh herbs gathered in Shadowglen that Innkeeper Keldamyr is awaiting down in Dolanaar. However, urgent duties keep Porthannius occupied with the local druids, preventing him from making the journey down the road himself. To ensure the innkeeper receives these necessary supplies without delay, he relies on a passing traveler heading out into Teldrassil.",al={"porthannius delivery motive","why send herbs to dolanaar","dolanaar delivery purpose"},it="motive",add="e1815add"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, this delivery marks your departure from Aldrassil's protected cradle and the beginning of broader responsibilities in safeguarding Teldrassil.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As a herbalist, you know how raw herbs from Shadowglen's soil matter to Dolanaar's healers, cooks, and caretakers.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you know that Porthannius is occupied with Shadowglen's druids and the spiritual duties and natural imbalances that concern the Cenarion Circle among Teldrassil's boughs."},kw={"delivery","dolanaar","dolanaar delivery","herbs","innkeeper keldamyr","night elf","porthannius","shadowglen","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","subzone:shadowglen","npc:innkeeper-keldamyr","zone:teldrassil","topic:druid"},m={start="Porthannius",["end"]="Innkeeper Keldamyr",faction="Alliance",id=2159},src={"Dolanaar Delivery (quest)"}}
E["quest:2399"] = {t="quest",n="The Sprouted Fronds",z="teldrassil",s="At Denalan's garden by Lake Al'Ameth, the planted frond has taken root and sprouted. Travelers can see the new growth among the garden beds.",h="At Denalan's garden by Lake Al'Ameth, the planted frond has taken root and sprouted.",sec={{t="A Garden by Lake Al'Ameth",b="You find Denalan's garden near Lake Al'Ameth, where the botanist studies Teldrassil's peculiar plants. After a shimmering frond is planted, new fronds rise from the soil in his planter, ready to be gathered and examined.",sp=0},{t="The Strange Flora of the World Tree",b="Teldrassil is young and vast, and its plant life grows quickly. Night elf herbalists find that growth fascinating and troubling. The shimmering fronds and their offshoots show how quickly life takes hold on the World Tree's boughs, though its vitality can be hard to predict.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are the sprouted fronds?",a="They are the plants that sprouted after Denalan planted a shimmering frond at his camp by Lake Al'Ameth. The peculiar fronds grow from it and tremble when they are ready to be gathered.",al={"sprouted fronds","what are these plants","denalans fronds"},it="item"},{q="Where is Denalan's garden located?",a="Denalan keeps his garden and research camp along the eastern edge of Lake Al'Ameth, southeast of Dolanaar in Teldrassil.",al={"denalan location","where is denalan","wellspring lake garden"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Denalan plant these fronds?",a="Denalan studies the curious, rapid growth of Teldrassil's plants. He plants seeds in prepared soil to learn about them and test for useful restorative or herbal properties.",al={"why plant fronds","denalan experiment","purpose of fronds"},it="purpose"},{q="Are the sprouted fronds dangerous?",a="No. These sprouted fronds are harmless plants waiting to be picked, unlike some corrupted or hostile plants elsewhere on Teldrassil's boughs.",al={"are fronds dangerous","do fronds attack","is the plant harmful"},it="danger"},{q="What comes before this quest?",a="Adventurers first find a shimmering frond in Teldrassil's wilds and bring it to Denalan. He plants it in his garden planter, hoping it will take root.",al={"prereq for sprouted fronds","what quest comes first"},it="history",gp=true},{q="Why do the fronds tremble?",a="The fronds tremble as they await picking. What causes the movement is unknown.",al={"trembling fronds","why do they shake"}}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Denalan's research shows the practical work of gathering and studying Teldrassil's plants, and how quickly local seeds adapt to tended soil.",["race:NightElf"]="As a kaldorei, you help watch over and nurture the life taking root across your young World Tree.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can see life flourish under attentive care in Denalan's planter, even as Teldrassil faces growing perils."},kw={"denalan","herbalism","planter","seeds","shimmering frond","sprouted fronds","teldrassil","wellspring lake"},rel={"quest:931","npc:denalan","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Sprouted Frond",faction="Alliance",id=2399},src={"The Sprouted Fronds"}}
E["quest:2438"] = {t="quest",n="The Emerald Dreamcatcher",z="teldrassil",s="In Dolanaar, Tallonkai Swiftroot asks you to recover a cherished heirloom from his abandoned home in Starbreeze Village. Gaerolas Talvethren, the druid warden, gave him the Emerald Dreamcatcher, which he left behind when corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs overran the settlement. Recovering it keeps its gentle nature magic from falling into foul hands.",h="In Dolanaar, Tallonkai Swiftroot asks you to recover a cherished heirloom from his abandoned home in...",sec={{t="A Druidic Talisman",b="Gaerolas Talvethren gave Tallonkai a rare druidic talisman. The warden watches over the sleeping druids within Ban'ethil Barrow Den. Crafted to channel the serene currents of the Emerald Dream, the amulet draws on that pure spiritual energy to bring peace and fortune to its bearer. Such gifts go only to a trusted few whose lives are bound to the forest's care.",sp=0},{t="Fleeing Starbreeze Village",b="Starbreeze Village was peaceful until the Gnarlpine furbolgs succumbed to violent madness. They drove the villagers from their ancestral homes. During the fearful flight, Tallonkai left his most treasured possession hidden inside his dresser in the village's southeastern quarter. He could not reclaim it on his own.",sp=0},{t="The Threat of Corruption",b="Leaving a focus of Emerald Dream magic in an overrun village carries grave risks. The Gnarlpine have fallen under dark influences, and the Dream's power in the amulet could be tainted or turned to harm. Returning the dreamcatcher to Tallonkai keeps its lingering magic from the furbolgs or other foul denizens. It also brings a piece of Starbreeze's heritage back to him.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Emerald Dreamcatcher?",a="The Emerald Dreamcatcher is a rare amulet Gaerolas Talvethren gave to Tallonkai. The warden tends the sleeping druids in Ban'ethil Barrow Den. The dreamcatcher draws energy from the Emerald Dream to bring good fortune and spiritual harmony to its bearer.",al={"what is the dreamcatcher","dreamcatcher lore","emerald dreamcatcher"},it="item"},{q="Why was the dreamcatcher left behind in Starbreeze Village?",a="The local Gnarlpine furbolgs overran Starbreeze Village in a violent, corrupted frenzy. Tallonkai Swiftroot fled for his life to Dolanaar, leaving the heirloom hidden in his bedroom dresser.",al={"why leave it behind","starbreeze village dresser","tallonkai dresser"}},{q="Who is Tallonkai Swiftroot?",a="Tallonkai Swiftroot is a night elf refugee staying in Dolanaar. He escaped the fall of Starbreeze Village and seeks brave travelers to enter the occupied ruins and recover his family heirlooms and druidic relics.",al={"who is tallonkai","tallonkai swiftroot"},it="identity"},{q="Who made the dreamcatcher?",a="Tallonkai says Gaerolas Talvethren gave him the dreamcatcher. Gaerolas watches over the sleeping druids in Ban'ethil Barrow Den, but who made the amulet is never said.",al={"who made it","gaerolas talvethren dreamcatcher","gaerolas"},it="origin"},{q="Where in Starbreeze Village is the dreamcatcher located?",a="The dreamcatcher rests in Tallonkai's dresser, inside the far southeastern house in Starbreeze Village. Hostile Gnarlpine furbolgs now prowl the house heavily.",al={"where is the dresser","starbreeze dresser location","find dreamcatcher"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after the dreamcatcher is returned?",a="After Tallonkai inspects the recovered amulet, he discovers its emerald is missing. Ferocitas the Dream Eater, leader of the Gnarlpine, stole it, setting the hunt for him in motion.",al={"quest continuation","next quest after dreamcatcher"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Tallonkai Swiftroot want the Emerald Dreamcatcher back?",a="The Emerald Dreamcatcher is a rare and deeply personal treasure. It was gifted to Tallonkai by Gaerolas Talvethren, warden of the druids in Ban'ethil Barrow Den, and carries potent magic drawn from the Emerald Dream to bestow luck. When Starbreeze Village fell to the corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs, Tallonkai was forced to leave it behind. He fears the sacred relic will be defiled or destroyed by the rampaging furbolgs if it remains inside his abandoned home.",al={"why does tallonkai want dreamcatcher","tallonkai motive","why recover emerald dreamcatcher"},it="motive",add="1ded4259"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you know Gaerolas Talvethren as the warden tending to your sleeping kin in Ban'ethil Barrow Den. The dreamcatcher he gave Tallonkai makes its recovery a matter of druidic honor.",["race:NightElf"]="Starbreeze was once a tranquil haven for your people. Helping Tallonkai recover his heritage strikes a small blow against the madness seizing Teldrassil's wildlife.",["faction:Alliance"]="By aiding the displaced Kaldorei of Dolanaar, you help secure local stability as corruption spreads among Teldrassil's furbolg tribes."},kw={"ban'ethil barrow den","dolanaar","emerald dream","emerald dreamcatcher","furbolg","gaerolas talvethren","gnarlpine","starbreeze village","tallonkai swiftroot","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:tallonkai-swiftroot","quest:2459","subzone:starbreeze-village","subzone:dolanaar","npc:gaerolas-talvethren","subzone:ban-ethil-barrow-den","topic:emerald-dream","topic:furbolg"},m={start="Tallonkai Swiftroot",faction="Alliance",id=2438,ri={"Emerald Dreamcatcher"}},src={"The Emerald Dreamcatcher (quest)"}}
E["quest:2459"] = {t="quest",n="Ferocitas the Dream Eater",z="teldrassil",s="Tallonkai Swiftroot in Dolanaar sends you after a stolen emerald in northern Teldrassil. The jewel was pried from his damaged heirloom dreamcatcher by Gnarlpine furbolgs north of Starbreeze Village, and now hangs from their leader, Ferocitas the Dream Eater.",h="Tallonkai Swiftroot in Dolanaar sends you after a stolen emerald in northern Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Defiled Heirloom",b="Tallonkai Swiftroot felt relief when the dreamcatcher recovered from the corrupted wilds came back to him, then dismay at its ruined state. The sacred artifact had been vandalized, its emerald centerpiece pried from the woven frame. Night elves spoke of Gnarlpine mystics north of Starbreeze Village, fallen under the influence of a furbolg leader named Ferocitas the Dream Eater. He wore a brilliant green stone around his neck. In Ferocitas's clutches, the sacred gem was useless and perverse, so Tallonkai sent defenders to take it back.",sp=0},{t="Purging the Mystics",b="The Gnarlpine furbolgs in Teldrassil's northern reaches were once peaceful neighbors. Corruption seeping into the World Tree drove them into frenzy and madness. Their mystics once practiced harmonious nature rites, but began drawing on distorted magical energies. Travelers can track down Ferocitas by cutting through the mystics guarding his woodland enclave. The jewel can then be returned to Tallonkai, so his dreamcatcher may be made whole and balance restored to the woods.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do I find Ferocitas the Dream Eater?",a="Ferocitas the Dream Eater is in the forest north of Starbreeze Village on Teldrassil, among corrupted Gnarlpine mystics and other woodland hazards.",al={"ferocitas location","where is ferocitas","find dream eater"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Who is Ferocitas?",a="Ferocitas is a Gnarlpine furbolg leader who commands corrupted mystics north of Starbreeze Village. He took the emerald from Tallonkai Swiftroot's dreamcatcher and made it into a crude necklace.",al={"who is ferocitas","ferocitas lore","what is dream eater"},it="target"},{q="Why does Tallonkai Swiftroot want the jewel back?",a="The emerald is the core power source of Tallonkai's dreamcatcher. Without it, the talisman cannot be repaired or channel the Emerald Dream's protective energies.",al={"why tallonkai wants jewel","tallonkai jewel purpose"},it="motive"},{q="Can the Gnarlpine actually use the emerald's magic?",a="No. Tallonkai Swiftroot says the emerald's magic is useless to Ferocitas and the Gnarlpine mystics, who coveted it only as a glowing bauble.",al={"can gnarlpine use dreamcatcher","does ferocitas use emerald"}},{q="What happens after this quest?",a="This is the final chapter of the two-part chain that began with The Emerald Dreamcatcher. Once you deliver the jewel to Tallonkai in Dolanaar, he can repair his heirloom.",al={"quest after ferocitas","next quest dreamcatcher"},it="next_step"},{q="Why are the Gnarlpine mystics hostile?",a="A strange corruption warping the boughs of the newly planted World Tree has affected much of Teldrassil's wildlife and furbolg tribes. It has twisted the Gnarlpine's minds and made them aggressive.",al={"why are furbolgs mad","gnarlpine corruption"},it="hostile"},{q="What is Tallonkai's Jewel for?",a="The missing emerald is the vital focus of Tallonkai Swiftroot's damaged dreamcatcher. Without it, the talisman cannot function, and he needs the stone returned intact so he can finally repair the sacred ward.",al={"what is tallonkais jewel","tallonkai jewel purpose","missing emerald use"},it="item",add="80c83c66"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf defending Teldrassil, you see a tragedy in the corruption of the Gnarlpine mystics and their theft of sacred talismans. The Gnarlpine were once allies of the Kaldorei.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you know dreamcatchers are potent instruments tied to the Emerald Dream. A corrupted furbolg has defiled one, and nature calls for swift retribution."},kw={"dolanaar","dream eater","emerald dreamcatcher","ferocitas","gnarlpine mystics","starbreeze village","tallonkai swiftroot","tallonkai's jewel","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:2438","npc:tallonkai-swiftroot","subzone:starbreeze-village","subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Tallonkai Swiftroot",faction="Alliance",id=2459,ri={"Tallonkai's Jewel"}},src={"Ferocitas the Dream Eater (quest)"}}
E["quest:2498"] = {t="quest",n="Return to Denalan",z="teldrassil",s="At Lake Al'Ameth, Return to Denalan carries Rellian's alarming news to the botanist studying corruption in Teldrassil. After examining the mossy tumors on timberlings, you head south to help Denalan with his discovery.",h="At Lake Al'Ameth, Return to Denalan carries Rellian's alarming news to the botanist studying corruption in...",sec={{t="A Message Across the Boughs",b="Rellian Greenspyre studies the mossy tumors afflicting Teldrassil's timberlings when urgent word arrives from his colleague Denalan. At his camp beside Lake Al'Ameth, Denalan has finally isolated the cause of these unnatural growths on the forest's nature spirits. Rellian recognizes the gravity of this discovery and sends you south at once to lend a hand.",sp=0},{t="The Threat at the Lake",b="At Lake Al'Ameth, Denalan faces blighted beings poisoning Teldrassil's boughs. His work begins with corrupted plants and diseased timberlings, then brings him into direct conflict with the corrupted timberling Oakenscowl.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Denalan?",a="Denalan is a night elf researcher and naturalist at Lake Al'Ameth in southern Teldrassil. He studies the island's plants, strange seedling mutations, and the unnatural afflictions spreading among local timberlings.",al={"denalan lore","who is denalan","denalan lake al'ameth"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Rellian Greenspyre send you back to Lake Al'Ameth?",a="Rellian receives word that Denalan has found the likely root cause of the tumors corrupting timberlings. The discovery is still unfolding rapidly and poses a growing danger to the forest, so Rellian sends you to help in the field at once.",al={"why go to denalan","rellian greenspyre mission"},it="motive"},{q="What are the tumors afflicting the timberlings?",a="Timberlings are peaceful nature spirits born from the island's plant life, but corruption taking root in Teldrassil makes bizarre mossy growths sprout on them. These tumors leave the creatures hostile and maddened.",al={"timberling tumors","why do timberlings have tumors","mossy tumors"},it="threat"},{q="Where can I find Denalan?",a="Denalan has a camp on the shores of Lake Al'Ameth, just south of Dolanaar in Teldrassil's southern woodlands.",al={"denalan location","where is denalan"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after you reach Denalan?",a="Denalan welcomes your help and says he has discovered something disturbing. He explains what comes next when you reach his camp.",al={"what comes next","oakenscowl follow up"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="How does this errand connect Rellian and Denalan?",a="Rellian Greenspyre studies timberlings in Darnassus, while Denalan works from his camp at Lake Al'Ameth. Rellian's research into the tumors reaches Denalan, whose new discovery concerns their cause.",al={"why does rellian send me to denalan","return to denalan purpose"},gp=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know timberlings as living signs of Teldrassil's vitality. Helping Denalan is part of your duty to heal the corruption threatening your people's new home.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you know that investigating unnatural tumors on woodland spirits serves the Cenarion duty to keep nature in balance and cleanse blights."},kw={"denalan","dolanaar","lake al'ameth","oakenscowl","rellian greenspyre","teldrassil","timberlings","tumors"},rel={"quest:923","quest:2499","npc:denalan","quest:922","subzone:lake-al-ameth","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Rellian Greenspyre",["end"]="Denalan",level="9",faction="Alliance",id=2498},src={"Return to Denalan"}}
E["quest:2499"] = {t="quest",n="Oakenscowl",z="teldrassil",s="Along Lake Al'Ameth, blight spreads from a corrupted timberling called Oakenscowl. Denalan asks you to end the threat. The maddened creature dwells in a cave on the lake's southern bank.",h="Along Lake Al'Ameth, blight spreads from a corrupted timberling called Oakenscowl.",sec={{t="A Fallen Guardian",b="Timberlings tend the boughs of Teldrassil, and Oakenscowl once led them. Now corruption runs through the world tree, reaching humble wildlife and ancient protectors alike. A massive growth swells across Oakenscowl's bark, driving the timberling mad. Where it once guarded the forest, blight now takes hold.",sp=0},{t="Purging Lake Al'Ameth",b="Oakenscowl hides in a cavern on Lake Al'Ameth's southern shore. Its presence poisons the nearby water and woodland beasts. Denalan cannot face the creature alone, so he seeks its destruction to cut off the corruption and study the strange growth afflicting the lake's spirits.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Oakenscowl?",a="Oakenscowl is a massive timberling, a forest spirit tied to Teldrassil's plant life. The timberling once led its kind before a malignant growth took hold.",al={"who is oakenscowl","oakenscowl lore","what kind of creature is oakenscowl"},it="target"},{q="Why must Oakenscowl be destroyed?",a="Oakenscowl's massive growth has twisted its mind and made it violently aggressive. From its cavern by Lake Al'Ameth, it spreads blight to nearby timberlings and beasts.",al={"why kill oakenscowl","oakenscowl hostile"},it="motive"},{q="Where does Oakenscowl reside?",a="Oakenscowl dwells in a cavern on the southern shore of Lake Al'Ameth in southern Teldrassil.",al={"oakenscowl location","where is oakenscowl cave"},it="place"},{q="Who is Denalan and why is he studying the tumor?",a="Denalan is an herbalist and naturalist who lives on Lake Al'Ameth's eastern shore. He studies the world tree's plants and animals, seeking to understand and cure the strange rot infecting local timberlings.",al={"who gives oakenscowl quest","denalan oakenscowl"},it="identity"},{q="What caused the tumor on Oakenscowl?",a="The tumor points to a deeper sickness spreading through Teldrassil's soil and roots, corrupting nature spirits from within.",al={"why do timberlings have tumors","source of corruption"},it="origin"},{q="Is Oakenscowl beyond saving?",a="Oakenscowl's affliction has gone too far by the time adventurers find it. The growth has completely warped the timberling, leaving Denalan to call for a mercy kill.",al={"can oakenscowl be healed","cure oakenscowl"},it="threat"},{q="What does Denalan need the Gargantuan Tumor for?",a="Denalan needs the Gargantuan Tumor to study the unnatural affliction poisoning Teldrassil's timberlings. As a nature researcher living on Lake Al'Ameth, he has watched the creatures fall to madness and corruption. Because Oakenscowl bore the largest growth he has ever seen, examining such an extreme specimen provides Denalan his best chance to understand the disease upsetting the local wildlife.",al={"why gargantuan tumor","purpose of gargantuan tumor","gargantuan tumor use"},it="item",add="a853a20e"},{q="Why does Denalan need your help against Oakenscowl?",a="Denalan is an isolated researcher and herbalist, not a warrior capable of battling a massive, corrupted timberling in its den. He admitted he dared not even get close to the beast when scouting the southern bank. Because you already proved your capability gathering mossy tumors and aiding his work, he entrusts you with removing the threat that endangers his lakeside home.",al={"why me denalan","why send an adventurer oakenscowl","why can't denalan fight oakenscowl"},it="why_me",add="47d0c5c8"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, seeing a guardian timberling warped by strange growths shows how deeply unwell Teldrassil's young ecosystem has become.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, Oakenscowl's fall threatens Lake Al'Ameth, just south of Dolanaar, close to the heart of your people.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As an herbalist, you can see how unseen rot twists plant life into malignant, mossy blights while helping Denalan."},kw={"corruption","denalan","gargantuan tumor","lake al'ameth","mossy tumors","oakenscowl","teldrassil","timberling"},rel={"npc:denalan","subzone:lake-al-ameth","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Denalan",level="9",faction="Alliance",id=2499,ri={"Gargantuan Tumor"}},src={"Oakenscowl (Classic)"}}
E["quest:2541"] = {t="quest",n="The Sleeping Druid",z="teldrassil",s="Oben Rageclaw lies asleep in Ban'ethil Barrow Den, but his spirit is caught in the Emerald Dream. Gnarlpine shamans have drawn it from his body and set his flesh moving through the den.",h="Oben Rageclaw lies asleep in Ban'ethil Barrow Den, but his spirit is caught in the Emerald Dream.",sec={{t="A Slumber Disrupted",b="Night elf druids sleep in barrow dens across Kalimdor while their spirits wander the Emerald Dream. Their bodies rest in stone alcoves, safe through centuries of slumber. Teldrassil's corruption has driven the Gnarlpine furbolgs to desperate savagery. In Ban'ethil Barrow Den, Gnarlpine shamans found a way to breach Oben Rageclaw's sacred rest and draw his living spirit from his sleeping body.",sp=0},{t="Voodoo and Corruption",b="A Shaman Voodoo Charm, a talisman, lets the Gnarlpine shamans animate Oben's empty body. His spirit is trapped in the Emerald Dream, watching as his flesh stalks the den's corridors and blindly attacks anyone who enters. Oben's spirit asks you to retrieve one of the Gnarlpine charms so he can study it and seek a way to undo the enchantment and restore his body.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Oben Rageclaw?",a="Oben Rageclaw is a night elf druid who entered a sacred slumber in Ban'ethil Barrow Den to commune with the Emerald Dream. Hostile Gnarlpine furbolgs took control of his body, leaving his spirit displaced.",al={"oben rageclaw","who is the sleeping druid","sleeping night elf in barrow den"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Oben's body attacking people?",a="Gnarlpine shamans separated Oben's spirit from his flesh and animated his empty body with dark magic. It now guards the depths of Ban'ethil Barrow Den.",al={"why is oben hostile","why is oben attacking","oben rageclaw body attacking"},it="conflict"},{q="What is the Shaman Voodoo Charm?",a="The Shaman Voodoo Charm is an enchanted focus carried by Gnarlpine shamans in Ban'ethil Barrow Den. They use its dark power to pull sleeping druids' spirits from their bodies and animate their physical husks.",al={"shaman charm","voodoo charm teldrassil","what is shaman voodoo charm"},it="item"},{q="Where is Oben's true spirit during the quest?",a="Oben's spirit is trapped in the Emerald Dream, unable to rejoin his body. Near his resting place, he can communicate with the waking world as a shimmering spirit.",al={"where is oben","oben spirit location","emerald dream oben"},it="place"},{q="Why are the furbolgs in Ban'ethil Barrow Den hostile?",a="Teldrassil's rising taint and madness have turned the Gnarlpine tribe against their former night elf allies. The Gnarlpine furbolgs have desecrated sacred druidic sites.",al={"why are gnarlpine mad","furbolg corruption teldrassil","why furbolgs aggressive"},it="hostile"},{q="Can Oben's body be saved without killing it?",a="Studying the Shaman Voodoo Charm is Oben's first hope of breaking the ritual. By examining the enchantments binding his flesh, he hopes to understand the magic and find a way to resolve the crisis.",al={"save oben rageclaw","can oben be saved","cure oben"},gp=true},{q="Why does Oben Rageclaw want the charm?",a="Gnarlpine furbolg shamans have managed to rip Oben Rageclaw's spirit away from his sleeping physical form. His wandering body has been animated by their dark magic to violently attack anyone who enters the Ban'ethil Barrow Den, while his true consciousness remains trapped in the Emerald Dream. Oben wants a charm so he can inspect its foul enchantment and search for a way to break the furbolgs' hold over his body.",al={"oben rageclaw motive","why does oben want the charm","why help oben rageclaw"},it="motive",add="08a1a718"},{q="Why are the Gnarlpine shaman in Ban'ethil Barrow Den?",a="The Gnarlpine tribe has overrun the sacred Ban'ethil Barrow Den, exploiting the vulnerability of slumbering night elf druids. Their shamans have begun practicing vile rituals to separate the druids' spirits from their flesh, seizing control of the physical bodies as violent sentries to guard their newly occupied subterranean domain.",al={"why gnarlpine shamans here","gnarlpine in barrow den","who are gnarlpine shamans"},it="target",add="21a70b6c"},{q="Why does Oben need you to retrieve the charm?",a="Oben is completely helpless to act on his own. His spirit is severed from the waking realm and trapped within the Emerald Dream, while his physical body is an animated puppet controlled by the Gnarlpine shamans. Without physical form or agency, he relies entirely on an outside adventurer to face the furbolgs and bring the charm to his spirit.",al={"why does oben need me","why cant oben get the charm himself","why me oben quest"},it="why_me",add="2131a103"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can see Oben's plight as a waking nightmare: having your body taken while you commune in the Emerald Dream violates the heart of druidic slumber.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know the Gnarlpine furbolgs' desecration of Ban'ethil Barrow Den marks how far they have fallen from their ancient kinship with the Kaldorei."},kw={"ban'ethil barrow den","barrow den","emerald dream","gnarlpine","oben rageclaw","shaman voodoo charm","teldrassil","the sleeping druid"},rel={"npc:oben-rageclaw","subzone:ban-ethil-barrow-den","topic:druid","topic:furbolg","topic:emerald-dream","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Oben Rageclaw",faction="Alliance",id=2541,ri={"Shaman Voodoo Charm"}},src={"The Sleeping Druid"}}
E["quest:2561"] = {t="quest",n="Druid of the Claw",z="teldrassil",s="Oben Rageclaw’s spirit waits in the barrows beneath Teldrassil, unable to rest. The Gnarlpine furbolgs have bound his body with a dark enchantment, and you can break that bond by destroying his soulless shell.",h="Oben Rageclaw’s spirit waits in the barrows beneath Teldrassil, unable to rest.",sec={{t="A Severed Spirit",b="Oben Rageclaw was resting in the barrows beneath Teldrassil when the corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs laid a voodoo enchantment over his sleeping body. The magic tore his spirit from his mortal flesh and trapped it in the Emerald Dream. Now his spirit lingers nearby, unable to rest or reclaim his body.",sp=0},{t="Mercy for the Flesh",b="Oben Rageclaw’s physical shell is under the furbolgs’ control. Enter the nearby chamber and destroy the mindless, hostile husk. Then use the furbolg charm over his remains to shatter the magic binding his soul.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why do I have to kill Oben Rageclaw?",a="The Gnarlpine furbolgs enchanted Oben while he slept, turning his body into a soulless puppet. His flesh remains under their control, so destroying it is the only way to break the enchantment and free his spirit.",al={"why kill oben","kill sleeping druid","oben rageclaw body"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Voodoo Charm used for?",a="The charm breaks the enchantment controlling Oben. After you destroy his soulless body, use the charm over his remains to unravel the magic holding his spirit.",al={"voodoo charm use","how to use voodoo charm","gnarlpine charm oben"},it="item"},{q="Where does Oben go after this quest?",a="Once Oben Rageclaw’s body is destroyed and the enchantment dispelled, his spirit can leave the mortal world and journey into the Emerald Dream to rest.",al={"oben fate","what happens to oben rageclaw","does oben survive"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why are the Gnarlpine using voodoo magic?",a="The Gnarlpine furbolgs have fallen into corruption and madness. They have turned from their ancestral harmony to use foul sorcery and dark magic to subjugate nearby creatures and sleeping druids.",al={"furbolg voodoo","gnarlpine voodoo magic","why do furbolgs have charms"}},{q="Who was Oben Rageclaw?",a="Oben was a night elf Druid of the Claw who entered a sacred slumber in Teldrassil’s barrows to commune with the Emerald Dream. The Gnarlpine furbolgs disturbed his rest and enslaved his body.",al={"who is oben","oben lore","oben rageclaw background"},it="identity"},{q="Is Oben's spirit still talking to me while his body is alive?",a="Yes. The enchantment tore Oben’s spirit from his flesh. His ghost appeared near the chamber entrance, unable to control or re-enter the enchanted, empty shell inside.",al={"oben ghost and body","two obens","why is oben in two places"}},{q="Who is the target I am sent against in Ban'ethil Barrow Den?",a="You are sent to destroy the soulless physical body of Oben Rageclaw himself. While his spirit lingers outside, his sleeping mortal shell has fallen under a powerful enchantment wielded by the Gnarlpine furbolgs inside Ban'ethil Barrow Den. Devoid of his soul, the husk now acts under their corrupt dominion.",al={"who am i killing","oben target","soulless body oben"},it="target",add="bff893ba"},{q="Why does Oben Rageclaw need me instead of doing this himself?",a="Oben is currently an ethereal spirit, entirely severed from his mortal form. Trapped as an apparition outside the barrow chamber, he lacks physical substance to confront his enchanted shell or wield the Voodoo Charm needed to break the magic. Deep within the barrow den, far from the reach of night elf sentinels, you are the only one present capable of intervening.",al={"why does oben need me","why cant oben kill his body","why me oben rageclaw"},it="why_me",add="6e4ee394"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a Druid, you see the danger when corrupted furbolgs desecrate a sleeping Druid of the Claw, leaving the body behind while its spirit communes with the Emerald Dream.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know Teldrassil was meant to be your refuge. The Gnarlpine furbolgs’ corruption now threatens even the sacred barrows."},kw={"ban'ethil","druid of the claw","emerald dream","gnarlpine","oben rageclaw","teldrassil","the sleeping druid","voodoo charm"},rel={"quest:2541","npc:oben-rageclaw","topic:druid","topic:emerald-dream","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Oben Rageclaw",faction="Alliance",id=2561},src={"Druid of the Claw (quest)"}}
E["quest:3116"] = {t="quest",n="Simple Sigil",z="teldrassil",s="In Shadowglen, Alyissia calls young night elf warriors to defend their people. Conservator Ilthalaine carries her summons as the Kaldorei face changes across Teldrassil and beyond.",h="In Shadowglen, Alyissia calls young night elf warriors to defend their people.",sec={{t="A Call to Arms in Shadowglen",b="After you prove your basic survival skills against Shadowglen's restless wildlife, Conservator Ilthalaine gives you an inscribed sigil. The token formally marks your move into combat training. It carries a request from Alyissia, the warrior trainer at Aldrassil, asking you to dedicate your strength to defending your people.",sp=0},{t="A Tumultuous New Era",b="Alyissia sets your training against a time of rapid change and danger. In only a few years, the night elves have raised the World Tree Teldrassil, seen a taint spread through forest beasts near and far, and reconnected with ancient lands once thought lost, including Feralas. The Kaldorei need capable defenders against these perils.",sp=0},{t="Opening the Boughs",b="Alyissia prepares young Kaldorei for more than combat. She urges you not to judge outsiders who arrive on Teldrassil by their race. Some travelers may not act from pure generosity, but allies are vital to the Kaldorei's defense. As you take up the work of protecting your people, she asks you to offer them reasonable trust.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Simple Sigil?",a="The inscribed sigil is sent by Alyissia, the warrior trainer in Shadowglen, and delivered to novice night elf warriors as they begin formal combat instruction.",al={"simple sigil item","what is this sigil","sigil of the warrior"}},{q="Who sends you to find Alyissia?",a="Conservator Ilthalaine delivers the sigil and directs you to Alyissia after you complete your first work maintaining the balance in Shadowglen.",al={"who gives the simple sigil","quest giver simple sigil"}},{q="Where can Alyissia be found?",a="Alyissia trains aspiring night elf warriors near the great trunk of Aldrassil, within Shadowglen's safe haven.",al={"alyissia location","where is alyissia","warrior trainer shadowglen"}},{q="Why does Alyissia say warriors are needed right now?",a="The night elves have raised Teldrassil, corruption has spread through local wildlife, and the Kaldorei have rediscovered ancient lands such as Feralas. Skilled fighters are needed to shield their people from these threats.",al={"why do night elves need warriors","shadowglen warrior lore"}},{q="What does Alyissia say about other races visiting Teldrassil?",a="Alyissia advises you not to judge visitors to Teldrassil by their race. Though not every traveler acts from pure generosity, she urges you to offer some trust so they may help defend the tree.",al={"alyissia on other races","night elves and outsiders","alliance in teldrassil"}},{q="What is the significance of mentioning Feralas?",a="Feralas is an ancient night elf land long cut off or believed lost after the Great Sundering. Its rediscovery shows how the Kaldorei are reconnecting with the wider world after millennia of isolation.",al={"why mention feralas","feralas connection"}}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a Kaldorei warrior, you begin your training with Alyissia as your first mentor in arms.",["race:NightElf"]="The sigil points to the rapid changes around the Kaldorei, from the raising of Teldrassil to opening their secluded home to foreign allies.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alyissia's counsel reflects the night elves' early efforts to welcome other Alliance races to their boughs after centuries of isolation."},kw={"aldrassil","alyissia","feralas","ilthalaine","shadowglen","simple sigil","teldrassil","warrior"},rel={"npc:alyissia","subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil","zone:feralas"},m={start="Conservator Ilthalaine",["end"]="Alyissia",level="1",faction="Alliance",id=3116},src={"Simple Sigil (Classic)"}}
E["quest:3117"] = {t="quest",n="Etched Sigil",z="teldrassil",s="In Shadowglen, the Etched Sigil calls young night elf hunters to Aldrassil. Through Conservator Ilthalaine, Ayanna Everstride summons them to meet their trainer and begin learning archery and beastcraft.",h="In Shadowglen, the Etched Sigil calls young night elf hunters to Aldrassil.",sec={{t="A Summons to the Boughs",b="After young kaldorei hunters help defend Shadowglen, Conservator Ilthalaine gives them an inscribed token. A messenger brought it from their mentor, Ayanna Everstride. The sigil directs each novice up into Aldrassil’s high boughs, where the trainers watch over the canopy.",sp=0},{t="The Path of the Hunter",b="Meeting Ayanna begins a hunter’s training on Teldrassil. She teaches novices marksmanship and how to understand Kalimdor’s wild creatures. A hunter must respect their beast companions and meet the world’s unseen dangers with awareness and humility.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Etched Sigil?",a="The Etched Sigil is Ayanna Everstride’s inscribed message, directing promising night elf novices to her post atop Aldrassil.",al={"etched sigil","what is this sigil","sigil item"}},{q="Where is Ayanna Everstride located?",a="Ayanna Everstride is on Aldrassil’s upper terraces, in the great world-tree hollow at the center of Shadowglen.",al={"where is ayanna","find ayanna everstride","ayanna everstride location"}},{q="Who hands out the Etched Sigil?",a="Conservator Ilthalaine gives the Etched Sigil to night elf hunters as they begin proving themselves by defending the local woodland.",al={"who gives the quest","quest giver","where do i get etched sigil"}},{q="What does Ayanna Everstride teach?",a="Ayanna teaches marksmanship, care for beasts, and wilderness survival. She warns hunters not to underestimate the dangers abroad.",al={"hunter training","what does ayanna teach","why talk to ayanna"}},{q="Why does Ayanna caution hunters about their pets?",a="Ayanna cautions hunters to respect their animal companions. The wilderness holds threats far beyond what novices may expect, so they should never take their companions’ abilities lightly.",al={"beast danger","why respect beasts","pet caution"}},{q="Is this quest available to other classes?",a="No. The Etched Sigil is an introductory summons for night elf hunters alone.",al={"can druids do this","is this hunter only","other classes"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you begin your training in Teldrassil, learning bow craft, tracking, and beast mastery.",["race:NightElf"]="As a kaldorei, you inherit a hunting tradition shaped by harmony with nature and reverence for Elune, not mere sport."},kw={"aldrassil","ayanna everstride","etched sigil","hunter","ilthalaine","shadowglen","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:ayanna-everstride","subzone:aldrassil","subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil","topic:elune"},m={start="Conservator Ilthalaine",["end"]="Ayanna Everstride",level="1",faction="Alliance",id=3117},src={"Etched Sigil (Classic)"}}
E["quest:3118"] = {t="quest",n="Encrypted Sigil",z="teldrassil",s="In Shadowglen, a coded summons calls new night elf rogues to begin their training. Conservator Ilthalaine carries it for Frahun Shadewhisper, who also warns of the fragile peace across Kalimdor.",h="In Shadowglen, a coded summons calls new night elf rogues to begin their training.",sec={{t="A Message in the Shadows",b="While young night elves study nature's balance under Conservator Ilthalaine, those drawn to stealth receive a quieter summons. A runner brings the Encrypted Sigil from Frahun Shadewhisper, Shadowglen's rogue mentor. Its ciphers are meant for initiates of the trade. The bearer is to decipher the message and find Frahun near the roots of Aldrassil to begin instruction.",sp=0},{t="Watching the Horizon",b="Frahun's message also warns of Kalimdor's uncertain peace. The Third War has ended, but the truce between the Alliance and the emerging Horde remains fragile. Rogue scouts and informers in Shadowglen are urged to sharpen their eyes and ears early. They watch for threats and covert provocations that could renew war across the borders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Encrypted Sigil?",a="The Encrypted Sigil is a coded token from rogue mentor Frahun Shadewhisper, directing new rogues in Shadowglen to find him beneath Aldrassil for training.",al={"what is this sigil","encrypted sigil quest","sigil item"}},{q="Who hands the sigil to young night elves?",a="Conservator Ilthalaine delivers the sigil on Frahun's behalf once an initiate has shown basic skill in managing the local wildlife around Shadowglen's boughs.",al={"who gives quest","quest giver","conservator ilthalaine"}},{q="Where can Frahun Shadewhisper be found?",a="Frahun Shadewhisper can be found within the shelter of the Great Tree Aldrassil in Shadowglen, ready to instruct newly arrived night elf rogues.",al={"where is frahun","find frahun shadewhisper","frahun location"}},{q="Why are rogues needed in peaceful Teldrassil?",a="Rogues are needed because the truce with outside factions is fragile. Scouts and informers watch for subterfuge, including Horde movements and threats within the boughs.",al={"why do night elves need rogues","rogues in shadowglen","purpose of rogues"}},{q="What happens after presenting the sigil to Frahun?",a="After you present the sigil, Frahun accepts the cipher and acknowledges your readiness. He invites you to return as you gain experience, so he can teach combat techniques, weapon handling, and stealth.",al={"what comes next","after encrypted sigil","sigil reward lore"}},{q="Does the Horde actively threaten Shadowglen directly?",a="The Horde does not openly assault secluded Teldrassil, but whispers that Horde agents are sowing distrust across Kalimdor keep kaldorei sentries and operatives alert.",al={"is horde in teldrassil","horde threat shadowglen","horde seeds of distrust"}}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you enter the kaldorei network of scouts, assassins, and informers who protect Teldrassil from unseen adversaries.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you share Aldrassil's watch over Kalimdor's shifting borders and defend the newly planted boughs.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you hear Shadowglen's trainers warn that treaties between factions are fragile and intelligence work helps prevent Horde incursions."},kw={"aldrassil","conservator ilthalaine","encrypted sigil","frahun shadewhisper","rogue trainer","shadowglen","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:frahun-shadewhisper","subzone:aldrassil","subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil","topic:horde"},m={start="Conservator Ilthalaine",["end"]="Frahun Shadewhisper",level="1",faction="Alliance",id=3118},src={"Encrypted Sigil (Classic)"}}
E["quest:3119"] = {t="quest",n="Hallowed Sigil",z="teldrassil",s="In Shadowglen, young night elf priests are called to begin their training in Aldrassil. Conservator Ilthalaine passes along Shanda's message as novices learn to wield Elune's grace.",h="In Shadowglen, young night elf priests are called to begin their training in Aldrassil.",sec={{t="A Calling to Service",b="Night elf priests serve Elune as handmaidens and servants of the moon goddess. When a young kaldorei in Shadowglen shows devotion and an affinity for the divine light, Conservator Ilthalaine gives them a hallowed sigil. Shanda, the priest trainer, sent the token by messenger as an invitation to come to Aldrassil and begin spiritual training.",sp=0},{t="A Changing World",b="Shanda tells the young acolyte that unusual change has reached Teldrassil's sheltered sanctuary. Travelers fill the World Tree's boughs, including members of the wider Alliance who have leave to meet with the kaldorei. The wider world calls, but Shanda urges novices to first attend to the troubles facing Shadowglen before turning to conflicts beyond it.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Hallowed Sigil?",a="The Hallowed Sigil is an inscribed token Shanda sent by messenger to Conservator Ilthalaine to summon a novice priest for instruction in Aldrassil.",al={"hallowed sigil item","what is this sigil","sigil of shanda"}},{q="Who is Shanda?",a="Shanda trains priests in Aldrassil, guiding young night elf priests in the rites, disciplines, and prayers of the Sisterhood of Elune.",al={"priest trainer aldrassil","who is shanda"}},{q="Where is Shanda located?",a="Shanda is inside the hollow base of Aldrassil, the great central tree at the heart of Shadowglen in Teldrassil.",al={"find shanda","where to turn in hallowed sigil","shanda location"}},{q="Why are Alliance members visiting Teldrassil?",a="Alliance members are visiting Teldrassil to meet and confer with the kaldorei. The night elves formed ties with the Alliance after the Third War, and travelers from other races are beginning to arrive on the World Tree's boughs as both sides prepare for challenges facing Azeroth.",al={"alliance in teldrassil","why outsiders on world tree"}},{q="What should a priest do after completing this task?",a="Shanda advises priests to help the local defenders and caretakers across Shadowglen. They can return to her to learn new prayers and techniques.",al={"what next after sigil","after hallowed sigil"}},{q="Why does Ilthalaine give this quest?",a="Conservator Ilthalaine oversees the earliest trials of novices in Shadowglen. When Shanda's messenger arrived with the sigil, Ilthalaine kept it until the aspiring priest was ready to take the next steps.",al={"conservator ilthalaine priest","why talk to ilthalaine"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a kaldorei priest, you begin formal training with Shanda in Elune's light and wisdom.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you belong to a people whose culture centers on the priesthood and ancient traditions of devotion to the moon, guiding them for millennia.",["faction:Alliance"]="Shanda's words reflect the new ties between the kaldorei and the Alliance, which bring unfamiliar races and travelers to Teldrassil's boughs."},kw={"aldrassil","conservator ilthalaine","elune","hallowed sigil","priest","shadowglen","shanda","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:shanda","subzone:aldrassil","subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil","topic:alliance"},m={start="Conservator Ilthalaine",["end"]="Shanda",level="1",faction="Alliance",id=3119},src={"Hallowed Sigil (Classic)"}}
E["quest:3120"] = {t="quest",n="Verdant Sigil",z="teldrassil",s="A summons reaches newly awakened night elf druids in Shadowglen. Conservator Ilthalaine passes the Verdant Sigil to fledgling shapeshifters, directing them to Mardant Strongoak within Aldrassil. The token marks the start of their formal training in nature and the Emerald Dream.",h="A summons reaches newly awakened night elf druids in Shadowglen.",sec={{t="A Call to the Boughs",b="When a young night elf shows promise in keeping Shadowglen's balance, the order calls for a formal introduction. A runner brings the Verdant Sigil to Conservator Ilthalaine, who entrusts it to the initiate. The token shows that the circle in Aldrassil has taken notice and invites the young druid to begin formal training.",sp=0},{t="Communion and the Dream",b="Presenting the sigil to Mardant Strongoak inside Aldrassil brings the initiate into the fold. Deeper communion with the Emerald Dream and mastery of animal forms lie ahead. For now, Mardant becomes their first guide, teaching them to read nature's spirits and channel the raw power of the woods.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Verdant Sigil?",a="It is an inscribed summons that Conservator Ilthalaine delivers on Mardant Strongoak's behalf, calling a novice druid to begin formal training inside Aldrassil.",al={"verdant sigil item","what is this sigil","druid sigil"}},{q="Where do I take the Verdant Sigil?",a="Bring it to Mardant Strongoak, the druid trainer within Aldrassil, the great barrow-tree at the heart of Shadowglen.",al={"where is mardant","turn in verdant sigil","where do i go"}},{q="Why does Mardant mention the Emerald Dream?",a="Druids draw power and wisdom from the Emerald Dream through long sleeping trances. A novice is not ready to wander the Dream freely, but Mardant names it as a mystery they will study in time.",al={"why emerald dream","mardant dream dialogue","druid trance"}},{q="Who sends the sigil to Ilthalaine?",a="A messenger sent by Mardant Strongoak brings the sigil to Conservator Ilthalaine, so she can place it in the hands of a promising young druid.",al={"who sent the sigil","sigil messenger"}},{q="What happens after presenting the sigil?",a="Mardant Strongoak becomes your primary mentor in Shadowglen, where you learn your earliest druidic spells and magical techniques as you grow in power.",al={"what do i learn next","after verdant sigil"}},{q="Can non-druids receive this quest?",a="No. The Verdant Sigil is meant only for night elf druids beginning their journey in Shadowglen. Other classes receive their own summons to their trainers.",al={"is this druid only","who gets verdant sigil"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, this marks your formal initiation into the Cenarion circle's teachings under Mardant Strongoak, beginning the long path toward understanding the Emerald Dream.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you enter an ancient tradition: presenting this sigil at Aldrassil is your first step into druidism, deeply woven into your culture."},kw={"aldrassil","druid trainer","emerald dream","ilthalaine","mardant strongoak","shadowglen","verdant sigil"},rel={"npc:mardant-strongoak","subzone:aldrassil","subzone:shadowglen","topic:druid","topic:emerald-dream","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Conservator Ilthalaine",["end"]="Mardant Strongoak",level="1",faction="Alliance",id=3120},src={"Verdant Sigil (Classic)"}}
E["quest:3519"] = {t="quest",n="A Friend in Need",z="teldrassil",s="Iverron lies bitten and in danger in Shadowglen. The young night elf calls for Dirania Silvershine, whose help may save him from Githyiss the Vile's venom.",h="Iverron lies bitten and in danger in Shadowglen.",sec={{t="A Reckless Venture",b="Iverron lies weakened after a bite from Githyiss the Vile. He ignored warnings and went too near the webwood caverns, where the vicious spider struck. Dizziness and failing strength leave him unable to reach safety alone.",sp=0},{t="A Call to Aldrassil",b="Iverron sends passersby toward Aldrassil's central tree to find Dirania Silvershine. She looks out for him and knows the dangers of Shadowglen. His life may depend on her preparing an antidote before the venom proves fatal.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Iverron?",a="Iverron is a young night elf who lives in Shadowglen, within Teldrassil. He often wanders into danger despite his companions' warnings, and Githyiss the Vile has left him near death.",al={"iverron lore","who is the poisoned elf","who gives a friend in need"},it="identity"},{q="What attacked Iverron?",a="Githyiss the Vile bit Iverron. The highly poisonous spider lurks inside a spider cave in Shadowglen.",al={"what bit iverron","who is githyiss","what spider poisoned him"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Dirania Silvershine?",a="Dirania Silvershine is a night elf who lives at Aldrassil in Shadowglen. She is Iverron's close friend and guardian figure, and knows how to treat venomous injuries.",al={"dirania role","who to talk to for iverron"},it="identity"},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="The events take place entirely in Shadowglen, the night elves' sheltered vale high on Teldrassil's crown.",al={"where is a friend in need","iverron location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after reporting Iverron's condition to Dirania?",a="After hearing of Iverron's condition, Dirania begins preparing a remedy. She sends adventurers across the grove to gather rare reagents for an antidote before the poison kills him.",al={"what next after a friend in need","does iverron get saved"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why are there deadly spiders inside Shadowglen?",a="Shadowglen shelters young night elves, but corruption spreading across Teldrassil has stirred wild beasts and vermin, including webwood spiders, into unusually aggressive and venomous predators.",al={"why are there spiders in shadowglen","spider corruption teldrassil"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Iverron want this done?",a="Iverron was bitten by the venomous webwood spider Githyiss the Vile while exploring a nearby cave. The deadly poison is rapidly spreading through his veins, leaving him weak, dizzy, and fearing for his life. Knowing he cannot cure the affliction on his own, he urgently needs Dirania Silvershine to intervene before the venom overcomes him entirely.",al={"why does iverron need help","iverron motive","what happened to iverron"},it="motive",add="c3a2deab"},{q="Why does Iverron need you instead of seeking help himself?",a="The venom from Githyiss the Vile has struck Iverron hard, leaving him severely disoriented and barely able to stand. Stranded alone in the wild, he cannot make the trek back to Aldrassil without collapsing. You are the only capable traveler who found him in time to sprint back and summon Dirania's aid.",al={"why can't iverron go himself","why me a friend in need","why doesn't iverron get guards"},it="why_me",add="b12cb73c"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a young kaldorei beginning your training beneath Aldrassil, you can see that even Shadowglen's sheltered boughs hold corruption and deadly peril.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you learn early that imbalanced wildlife can strike down the unwary, and that understanding and countering nature's venoms matters."},kw={"aldrassil","dirania silvershine","githyiss","iverron","poison","shadowglen","spider","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:iverron","npc:dirania-silvershine","quest:4495","subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Iverron",["end"]="Dirania Silvershine",level="4",faction="Alliance",id=3519},src={"A Friend in Need (Classic)"}}
E["quest:3521"] = {t="quest",n="Iverron's Antidote",z="teldrassil",s="Iverron's Antidote is an urgent task in Shadowglen to save a poisoned night elf scout. By gathering wild mushrooms, lilies, and spider ichor, adventurers help Dirania Silvershine brew a remedy before the venom takes full hold.",h="Iverron's Antidote is an urgent task in Shadowglen to save a poisoned night elf scout.",sec={{t="A Race Against Venom",b="While scouting the boughs of Shadowglen, young Iverron fell victim to the poisonous fangs of the local Webwood spiders. Collapsed and dying, his survival depends entirely on the herbal knowledge of Dirania Silvershine at Aldrassil. With the youth fading fast, she must quickly prepare a specialized concoction to neutralize the aggressive venom coursing through his blood.",sp=0},{t="Reagents of Shadowglen",b="Dirania's recipe relies on the restorative flora of Teldrassil balanced against the venom itself. Hyacinth mushrooms, favored by the thieving grell to the south, provide an earthy base, while delicate Moonpetal lilies gathered from tranquil forest pools offer purifying qualities. To finish the draft, a sample of Webwood ichor must be extracted directly from the spiders prowling near Shadowthread Cave to tailor the cure to their specific poison.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Iverron?",a="Iverron is a young night elf in Shadowglen who ventured too close to the hostile Webwood spiders and was struck down by their lethal venom.",al={"iverron","who is iverron","who poisoned"},it="identity"},{q="Who gives the quest Iverron's Antidote?",a="Dirania Silvershine, an attendant stationed outside the great boughs of Aldrassil in Shadowglen, provides the quest and concocts the remedy.",al={"quest giver","dirania","dirania silvershine"},it="identity"},{q="Why does the antidote need spider ichor?",a="In traditional herbal remedies, introducing a component of the creature's own bodily fluids or venom helps counteract the specific toxins inflicting the victim.",al={"why spider ichor","webwood ichor use","spider venom cure"},it="item"},{q="Where are Hyacinth Mushrooms found?",a="Hyacinth mushrooms grow at the bases of large trees throughout Shadowglen and can also be pried from the clutches of grell who hoard them to the south.",al={"where to find hyacinth mushrooms","hyacinth mushroom location"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Where do Moonpetal Lilies grow?",a="Moonpetal lilies bloom along the edges of the quiet, fresh-water pools tucked away on the northwestern side of Aldrassil.",al={"moonpetal lily location","where are lilies"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Where are the Webwood spiders located?",a="Webwood spiders dwell in the northern woods of Shadowglen, especially around the dark entrance of Shadowthread Cave.",al={"webwood spider location","spider location shadowglen"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Why does Dirania Silvershine want this done?",a="Dirania knows how to brew a remedy that can neutralize the deadly poison coursing through Iverron. Without quick intervention, his condition will deteriorate, and she relies on your speed to gather the necessary forest ingredients before it is too late to save him.",al={"dirania silvershine motive","why help iverron","why make the antidote"},it="motive",add="77bb41e6"},{q="What is the Hyacinth Mushroom used for?",a="Hyacinth mushrooms are native fungi that grow beneath the great boughs of Shadowglen. Dirania uses them as a primary herbal component to brew the antidote, balancing the harsher venoms and neutralizing the toxin invading Iverron's body.",al={"hyacinth mushroom purpose","why hyacinth mushroom","hyacinth mushroom lore"},it="item",add="d7eaa833"},{q="What is the Moonpetal Lily used for?",a="Moonpetal lilies are delicate aquatic blossoms that thrive along the tranquil forest pools of Shadowglen. Dirania blends them into her remedy to harness their soothing natural properties and counter the virulent spider venom.",al={"moonpetal lily purpose","why moonpetal lily","moonpetal lily lore"},it="item",add="ece05283"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Tending to fallen kin is sacred duty in Shadowglen, where every defender is needed to protect the newly budding World Tree.",["class:Druid"]="Crafting remedies from local flora and neutralizing natural poisons reflects the fundamental balance druids strive to maintain within the wild.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Gathering Moonpetal lilies and Hyacinth mushrooms showcases how wild plants of Teldrassil possess potent medicinal properties when handled with care."},kw={"aldrassil","antidote","dirania silvershine","hyacinth mushroom","iverron","moonpetal lily","shadowglen","shadowthread cave","webwood ichor"},rel={"npc:iverron","npc:dirania-silvershine","subzone:shadowglen","subzone:aldrassil","subzone:shadowthread-cave","zone:teldrassil","topic:elune"},m={start="Dirania Silvershine",level="4",faction="Alliance",id=3521,ri={"Hyacinth Mushroom","Moonpetal Lily","Webwood Ichor"}},src={"Iverron's Antidote (Classic)"}}
E["quest:3522"] = {t="quest",n="Iverron's Antidote",z="teldrassil",s="In Shadowglen, Iverron waits for medicine before its strength fades. Poisoned by Webwood spiders, the night elf scout depends on Dirania Silvershine's brew, which must reach him within five minutes.",h="In Shadowglen, Iverron waits for medicine before its strength fades.",sec={{t="A Race Against the Clock",b="Dirania Silvershine brews the cure from fresh venom sacs, lily roots, and hyacinth fungi. The unstable mixture keeps its strength for only five minutes after it is distilled. Whoever carries the vial must sprint straight from the glade toward the northern heights without hesitation.",sp=0},{t="A Habit of Trouble",b="Webwood spiders around Shadowglen's barrows and caves have poisoned Iverron. He admits he has a habit of stumbling into danger and often depends on Dirania's herbal skill to save him. Even after drinking the antidote, his recovery is fragile. The hostile spiders still guard his way home, and he remains wary of them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is there a time limit on delivering the antidote?",a="Dirania Silvershine's antidote loses its healing strength quickly because it is made from fresh natural ingredients and venom. It is useless if Iverron does not drink it within five minutes of leaving her care.",al={"why five minutes","antidote timer","timed quest"},it="item"},{q="Where is Iverron located?",a="Iverron waits against the rocks outside the northern cave in Shadowglen, north of the grove's main path.",al={"where is iverron","iverron location","find iverron"},it="target",gp=true},{q="How was Iverron poisoned?",a="Webwood spiders poisoned Iverron. They live on Shadowglen's northern outskirts, where they have multiplied around Teldrassil's roots and caves.",al={"who poisoned iverron","why is iverron sick","iverron poison"},it="conflict"},{q="What happens after Iverron drinks the antidote?",a="The antidote neutralizes the poison, but Iverron remains too weak and shaken to travel safely alone. He asks for help clearing the nearby Webwood spiders that block his way back to safety.",al={"what next iverron","after iverron antidote","iverron follow up"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What relationship do Dirania and Iverron have?",a="Dirania Silvershine is an herbalist and healer in Shadowglen who often rescues Iverron from trouble. He admits that he keeps getting into danger and that Dirania is always helping him out.",al={"dirania and iverron","who is dirania to iverron","are they friends"},it="ties"},{q="What happens if the antidote expires before reaching him?",a="If the brew spoils before it reaches Iverron, you need a fresh dose from Dirania Silvershine in Shadowglen and must make the run again.",al={"antidote expired","failed timer","lost antidote"},gp=true},{q="Why does Dirania Silvershine want you to deliver the antidote?",a="Iverron has fallen victim to deadly spider venom in the wilds of Shadowglen and will die without immediate intervention. Dirania Silvershine has already prepared the cure, but the mixture is unstable and will spoil quickly if it is not administered without delay. She cares for Iverron and routinely helps bail him out of trouble, making your rapid delivery a matter of life and death.",al={"dirania silvershine motive","why help iverron","why does dirania want this done"},it="motive",add="b60b9a13"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a young night elf training in Shadowglen, you see Iverron's rescue as a sobering reminder of the corruption and aggression stirring among Teldrassil's native wildlife.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As an herbalist, you know raw woodland plants can be difficult to work with. Their concoctions lose vital properties almost at once without proper preservation."},kw={"antidote","dirania silvershine","iverron","shadowglen","teldrassil","venom","webwood spider"},rel={"npc:iverron","npc:dirania-silvershine","quest:3521","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Dirania Silvershine",["end"]="Iverron",level="4",faction="Alliance",id=3522},src={"Iverron's Antidote (2)"}}
E["quest:4161"] = {t="quest",n="Recipe of the Kaldorei",z="teldrassil",s="Zarrin teaches a lesson in balance through the Recipe of the Kaldorei. In Dolanaar, young cooks learn to gather only what they need from Teldrassil's woods.",h="Zarrin teaches a lesson in balance through the Recipe of the Kaldorei.",sec={{t="Children of the Stars",b="Behind the inn in Dolanaar, Zarrin tends a bubbling cauldron and teaches young adventurers the traditions of his people. The night elves once called themselves the kaldorei, or children of the stars. Zarrin begins their understanding of that heritage with the bond between a hunter, their food, and Teldrassil's boughs, rather than the battlefield.",sp=0},{t="Taking Only What Is Needed",b="Zarrin teaches restraint through a simple demand: gather small spider legs from the woodland arachnids outside Shadowglen, but take exactly seven. The kaldorei seek harmony with nature by taking only what they need and showing kindness to the wild. Even in troubled times, that balance matters. A spider kabob becomes a lesson in living with care.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Zarrin?",a="Zarrin is a night elf who tends a cauldron behind the inn in Dolanaar. He teaches young adventurers to cook while honoring kaldorei traditions.",al={"zarrin","who is zarrin","dolanaar cook","cooking trainer dolanaar"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Zarrin insist on collecting exactly seven spider legs?",a="Zarrin asks for exactly seven spider legs to teach that the kaldorei take only what they need and live in harmony with nature. The lesson encourages respect for the living forest and its balance.",al={"why seven legs","why only seven","take no more than seven"},it="motive"},{q="What does the word 'kaldorei' mean?",a="Kaldorei means children of the stars in the Darnassian tongue. It is the ancient name the night elves have used for themselves for thousands of years.",al={"what does kaldorei mean","kaldorei meaning","children of the stars"},it="origin"},{q="Where are the spider legs gathered?",a="Gather the legs from webwood spiders in Teldrassil's forests, outside Shadowglen's sheltered borders.",al={"where do spiders drop legs","spider leg location","which spiders"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What do night elves prepare with spider legs?",a="Zarrin teaches young adventurers to prepare Kaldorei Spider Kabobs, a traditional wilderness dish made from woodland spider meat for a nourishing meal on the road.",al={"what is the recipe","kaldorei spider kabob","spider food"},it="item"},{q="Do all spiders in Teldrassil yield the legs needed?",a="No. Immature spiders in Shadowglen do not yield the proper legs for Zarrin's recipe. Gather them from spiders roaming the wider woods of Teldrassil.",al={"do shadowglen spiders work","shadowglen spider legs"},it="target",gp=true},{q="What spiders are you hunting in Teldrassil?",a="You are sent to hunt the wild webwood spiders roaming the forests outside Shadowglen. While spiders are a natural part of the boughs of Teldrassil, Zarrin asks you to cull only what you need so that you respect the forest's harmony rather than slaughter aimlessly.",al={"what spiders drop legs","which spiders to hunt","teldrassil spiders"},it="target",add="214de26a"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Learning to cook in Teldrassil brings the recipe for Kaldorei Spider Kabobs.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you learn the kaldorei way of keeping harmony with nature through restraint and taking only what you need."},kw={"cooking","dolanaar","kaldorei","recipe of the kaldorei","spider kabob","teldrassil","zarrin"},rel={"npc:zarrin","subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf","subzone:shadowglen","topic:alliance"},m={start="Zarrin",level="7",faction="Alliance",id=4161,ri={"Small Spider Leg"}},src={"Recipe of the Kaldorei"}}
E["quest:4495"] = {t="quest",n="A Good Friend",z="teldrassil",s="At Aldrassil, Dirania Silvershine grows worried when Iverron misses his daily visit. She asks travelers to search the hills near Shadowthread Cave, north of Shadowglen.",h="At Aldrassil, Dirania Silvershine grows worried when Iverron misses his daily visit.",sec={{t="A Missing Visitor",b="Dirania Silvershine waits beneath Aldrassil for Iverron, who visits her every day. Hours pass without him, and she asks travelers heading into Shadowglen to look for her friend.",sp=0},{t="Peril at Shadowthread Cave",b="Iverron often wanders the hills in northern Shadowglen, near the webwood spiders of Shadowthread Cave. The spiders make the surrounding slopes dangerous for travelers. Search west of the cave entrance, where Iverron is hiding and needs help.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Dirania Silvershine?",a="Dirania Silvershine is a night elf who lives beneath Aldrassil in Shadowglen. Iverron visits her every day, so she notices when he fails to arrive.",al={"dirania","dirania silvershine lore","who starts a good friend"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Iverron?",a="Iverron is a night elf who wanders the hills near Shadowthread Cave in Shadowglen. He misses his daily visit to Dirania Silvershine and is found on the cliffs west of the cave entrance.",al={"iverron","where is iverron","who is the missing friend"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Iverron be found?",a="Iverron is hiding on the hillside just west of the entrance to Shadowthread Cave, in northern Shadowglen.",al={"iverron location","finding iverron","shadowthread cave iverron"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is the northern cave considered dangerous?",a="Venomous webwood spiders overrun Shadowthread Cave and its surrounding slopes. The spreading corruption on Teldrassil has agitated them, making the area dangerous for travelers alone.",al={"why is shadowthread cave dangerous","spiders in shadowglen","spider cave teldrassil"},it="danger"},{q="What happens after finding Iverron?",a="After you find Iverron, he tells you that his misadventure near the spider cave has left him in dire straits. A search for treatment begins with A Friend in Need.",al={"quest after a good friend","next step for iverron","a friend in need quest"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why was Dirania so quick to worry about Iverron?",a="Iverron visits Dirania at the same hour every day. When he is several hours late, and she knows he often wanders near the dangerous spider hollows, she fears something has happened to him.",al={"why is dirania worried","iverron routine","why did dirania notice"},it="motive"},{q="Why does Dirania Silvershine need my help specifically?",a="Dirania is not issuing a formal military request or mobilizing the Sentinels—she is simply asking a passing adventurer for a personal favor. Because Iverron is known to frequent the hazardous hills near the northern cave, she hopes that someone capable of handling the local wildlife will keep an eye out while traveling that direction.",al={"why ask me dirania","why cant dirania look for iverron","why not send guards"},it="why_me",add="9ca4ec06"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a young kaldorei beneath Aldrassil, you can answer Dirania's call and see how the glade's growing dangers touch its people.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you may recognize the aggressive webwood spiders near Shadowthread Cave as a sign of the wider corruption afflicting the great bough."},kw={"a good friend","aldrassil","dirania silvershine","iverron","shadowglen","shadowthread cave","spiders","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:iverron","npc:dirania-silvershine","quest:3519","quest:3521","subzone:shadowthread-cave","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Dirania Silvershine",["end"]="Iverron",level="4",faction="Alliance",id=4495},src={"A Good Friend"}}
E["quest:456"] = {t="quest",n="The Balance of Nature",z="teldrassil",s="Conservator Ilthalaine calls newly awakened night elves to tend Shadowglen’s wildlife. Young nightsabers and thistle boars have grown too numerous, and keeping Teldrassil’s natural harmony calls for stewardship and difficult choices.",h="Conservator Ilthalaine calls newly awakened night elves to tend Shadowglen’s wildlife.",sec={{t="A Delicate Harmony",b="In Shadowglen, beneath the Great Tree’s sprawling boughs, heavy spring rains have disrupted Teldrassil’s young, fragile forest cycle. Some wildlife populations have grown beyond what the land can sustain. They threaten to strip the glen of resources and bring famine to the ecosystem. Preserving the forest calls for active care.",sp=0},{t="The Conservator's Call",b="Conservator Ilthalaine watches over Shadowglen’s woods, keeping any one part from overtaking the others. To prevent mass starvation among the animals, he sends young night elves into the grove to thin thistle boars and predatory nightsabers. The work is unglamorous, but vital: kaldorei stewardship means seeking harmony with nature through active balance and difficult decisions.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why do the nightsabers and boars need to be killed?",a="Heavy spring rains caused young nightsabers and thistle boars to flourish. Shadowglen can sustain only so much wildlife, and the overgrown populations risk stripping the grove of food and starving themselves and other creatures.",al={"why kill boars","why kill nightsabers","balance of nature reason"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Conservator Ilthalaine?",a="Conservator Ilthalaine is a kaldorei guardian stationed in Shadowglen. His sworn duty is to watch the grove’s wildlife and vegetation so nature’s harmony remains intact.",al={"who is ilthalaine","quest giver","conservator ilthalaine lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="The task takes place in secluded Shadowglen, a forest enclave among the branches of Teldrassil, the World Tree off the coast of northern Kalimdor.",al={"quest location","where is shadowglen","starting area night elf"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What comes next after completing this task?",a="After this first part of the culling, Ilthalaine sends you to carry out its second part. He also gives you a class-specific sigil that points you to your first trainer in Aldrassil.",al={"follow up quest","next quest in chain"},it="next_step"},{q="What are the beasts you are sent to hunt?",a="You are sent against the young nightsabers and young thistle boars roaming the surrounding woods of Shadowglen. They are native wildlife of the great world tree, Teldrassil. Following unusually heavy spring rains, both populations have exploded in numbers, threatening to strip the glen of food and throw the local woodland into chaos.",al={"what are nightsabers and boars","who are you hunting in shadowglen","young nightsaber young thistle boar"},it="target",add="3ad6c91a"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, this is your first step on the path to becoming an adult protector of the kaldorei. You learn that keeping nature in balance calls for active care and respect.",["class:Druid"]="As a budding druid, you learn the harsh realities of Cenarion stewardship: protecting the wilds can mean shedding blood to save the whole.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you begin learning to track and cull aggressive wildlife, a foundation for communion with the beasts of Kalimdor."},kw={"aldrassil","balance of nature","ilthalaine","kaldorei","nightsaber","shadowglen","teldrassil","thistle boar"},rel={"npc:ilthalaine","subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf","quest:3120","quest:3117","quest:3119","quest:3118"},m={start="Conservator Ilthalaine",level="2",faction="Alliance",id=456},src={"The Balance of Nature (Classic)"}}
E["quest:457"] = {t="quest",n="The Balance of Nature",z="teldrassil",s="Conservator Ilthalaine sends defenders into Shadowglen to thin its growing wildlife. Mature thistle boars and mangy nightsabers threaten the glade's balance.",h="Conservator Ilthalaine sends defenders into Shadowglen to thin its growing wildlife.",sec={{t="A Burden of Stewardship",b="Shadowglen's adult animals now threaten the World Tree's ecosystem. Conservator Ilthalaine sends young defenders deeper into the forest to hunt mature thistle boars and older, mangy nightsabers. Their appetites can exhaust the land's limited plants and game.",sp=0},{t="Predator and Prey",b="North of Aldrassil, younger cubs give way to mottled nightsabers and aggressive boars that root through the soil. For kaldorei, controlled hunting is a grim duty, but it protects the whole forest from collapse.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Conservator Ilthalaine having these beasts culled?",a="Without intervention, growing numbers of thistle boars and nightsabers could strip Shadowglen of vital resources. The land would be left barren and unable to sustain life on Teldrassil's boughs.",al={"why kill boars and sabers","why balance of nature","reason for hunting"},it="motive"},{q="Where are the mangy nightsabers and thistle boars located?",a="The mangy nightsabers and thistle boars roam northern Shadowglen, past Aldrassil's boughs. Look for spotted coats on the nightsabers; younger cubs closer to the sanctuary have stripes.",al={"where are mangy nightsabers","thistle boar location","where to find them"},gp=true},{q="Who is Conservator Ilthalaine?",a="Conservator Ilthalaine cares for Shadowglen and oversees the health of Teldrassil's starting glade. She guides newly awakened night elves in keeping the forest in balance.",al={"who is ilthalaine","conservator ilthalaine lore"},it="identity"},{q="How does this fit into night elf beliefs about nature?",a="Night elves honor nature, and stewardship means managing overgrowth. When one species grows too numerous and starves out others, the whole forest suffers; culling is a sorrowful but vital duty.",al={"night elf nature beliefs","why druids kill animals","kaldorei balance"},it="origin"},{q="Is this the end of the Balance of Nature chain?",a="This is the second and final step in the initial Balance of Nature chain. Other work soon addresses the deeper, more unnatural corruption troubling Teldrassil's wildlife.",al={"does balance of nature continue","what comes after balance of nature"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why are the nightsabers described as mangy?",a="Older, rougher nightsabers roam the glade's fringes, where their numbers strain Shadowglen's food supply. Many grow scruffy and aggressive.",al={"why mangy","what is wrong with the sabers"}},{q="Why are you sent against mangy nightsabers and thistle boars?",a="These nightsabers and thistle boars populate the northern reaches of Shadowglen. Left unchecked, their unchecked numbers threaten to strip the woodland of its limited nourishment. Conservator Ilthalaine directs you to cull them so the local flora and other woodland creatures can endure.",al={"why kill nightsabers and boars","mangy nightsabers thistle boars purpose","target nightsabers and boars"},it="target",add="af153fa8"},{q="Why does Conservator Ilthalaine ask you instead of the Sentinels?",a="Shadowglen is a sanctum for training young night elves in their heritage, duty, and martial ways. Ilthalaine tasks you with managing the local wildlife not only to ease the burden on forest wardens and Sentinels, but to test your dedication to safeguarding the land and its harmony.",al={"why does ilthalaine need me","why not sentinels","why ask adventurer balance of nature"},it="why_me",add="2a769140"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For young night elves, this is an early lesson in the harsh demands of caring for the wilderness on Teldrassil.",["class:Druid"]="Druidic teachings prize harmony over sentiment. Thinning overgrown packs preserves the great web of life.",["class:Hunter"]="Taking down swift sabers and stubborn boars teaches you to track and thin their numbers, skills needed to keep nature in balance."},kw={"aldrassil","balance of nature","culling","ilthalaine","mangy nightsaber","shadowglen","teldrassil","thistle boar"},rel={"quest:456","npc:ilthalaine","subzone:shadowglen","subzone:aldrassil","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Conservator Ilthalaine",level="3",faction="Alliance",id=457},src={"The Balance of Nature (2)"}}
E["quest:458"] = {t="quest",n="The Woodland Protector",z="teldrassil",s="In Shadowglen, Melithar Staghelm hears troubling whispers from the forest spirits. He asks you to find Tarindrella, an elusive dryad whose unexpected return hints at trouble beneath Teldrassil’s canopy.",h="In Shadowglen, Melithar Staghelm hears troubling whispers from the forest spirits.",sec={{t="Whispers in the Glen",b="Melithar Staghelm receives troubling omens from the woodland spirits while training novices beneath Aldrassil’s boughs. Tarindrella, a dryad regarded as a protector of the wild, has returned to Shadowglen after many years away from Kalimdor’s woodlands. Dryads rarely appear without cause, and Melithar fears the natural order is out of balance.",sp=0},{t="Seeking the Dryad",b="A Sentinel scouting report points newly awakened defenders southwest of Aldrassil, into the surrounding woods. There, you can find Tarindrella. Melithar’s instincts prove right: Cenarius’s daughter has returned to address a taint affecting the barrow and nearby glades.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who starts this quest?",a="Melithar Staghelm, a night elf druid on Aldrassil’s lower platforms in Shadowglen, asks newly awakened adventurers for help.",al={"quest giver","who gives quest","melithar quest"},gp=true},{q="Where can I find Tarindrella?",a="Tarindrella stands by the wooded paths of Shadowglen, in the forest southwest of Aldrassil.",al={"tarindrella location","where is tarindrella","find dryad"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Tarindrella?",a="Tarindrella is a dryad, one of Cenarius’s immortal daughters. Dryads are revered as woodland protectors, bound closely to the forest’s health, and rarely intervene directly unless nature faces a significant threat.",al={"who is tarindrella","tarindrella lore","dryad shadowglen"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Melithar concerned about her return?",a="Kalimdor’s forests have not felt Tarindrella’s presence for years. Her sudden return to Teldrassil’s newly grown boughs suggests something has gone wrong in the grove.",al={"why is melithar worried","melithar staghelm concern"},it="motive"},{q="What happens after finding Tarindrella?",a="Speaking with Tarindrella completes the errand and leads directly to her request for aid: she asks you to investigate corrupted plants and animals in Shadowglen.",al={"next quest","what next","tarindrella followup"},it="next_step"},{q="Is Melithar Staghelm related to Archdruid Fandral Staghelm?",a="Melithar shares the Staghelm surname with Archdruid Fandral Staghelm, leader of the night elf druids in Darnassus, but no family tie between them is known. Melithar mentors fledglings in Shadowglen.",al={"melithar fandral relation","is melithar staghelm related"},it="ties"},{q="Why does Melithar Staghelm send an adventurer instead of handling it himself?",a="Melithar Staghelm is tending to Aldrassil and the delicate spirits of Shadowglen, where strange tidings and growing unrest keep the druids and Sentinels watchful. When news arrived that the reclusive dryad Tarindrella had suddenly appeared, Melithar needed a capable, discreet courier to seek her out southwest of the boughs without abandoning his post in the glade.",al={"why send me","why melithar doesn't go","why does melithar need me"},it="why_me",add="47512ade"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a young night elf leaving Aldrassil, you meet one of Cenarius’s daughters and take your first direct duty in preserving harmony in your young World Tree.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you hold dryads in high esteem as kin in nature. Tarindrella’s presence calls you early to heed the balance of the Emerald Dream and the woods."},kw={"aldrassil","dryad","melithar staghelm","shadowglen","tarindrella","teldrassil","woodland protector"},rel={"npc:tarindrella","npc:melithar-staghelm","subzone:shadowglen","subzone:aldrassil","zone:teldrassil","topic:druid","topic:sentinels"},m={start="Melithar Staghelm",["end"]="Tarindrella",level="1",faction="Alliance",id=458},src={"The Woodland Protector (Classic)"}}
E["quest:459"] = {t="quest",n="The Woodland Protector",z="teldrassil",s="In Shadowglen, Tarindrella seeks the cause of the forest’s sudden unrest and the furbolgs’ disappearance. Grells have turned aggressive, and Fel Moss points to dark magic in Teldrassil’s boughs.",h="In Shadowglen, Tarindrella seeks the cause of the forest’s sudden unrest and the furbolgs’ disappearance.",sec={{t="A Blight in the Glade",b="Shadowglen’s quiet woods have grown hostile. The furbolgs have left their ancestral dens and gathered as the Gnarlpine tribe. Feral grells and grellkin now overrun the woodland paths, and Tarindrella has noticed the dark change spreading through Teldrassil.",sp=0},{t="Tainted Growth",b="Tarindrella suspects corruption is stirring the forest’s creatures. You slay the grells and bring her samples of Fel Moss, evidence of dark enchantments clinging to Teldrassil’s boughs. With the corruption confirmed, she sends young defenders to Dolanaar to speak with Druid Athridas Bearmantle.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tarindrella?",a="Tarindrella is a dryad watcher in Shadowglen and a daughter of Cenarius. She guards the glade’s plants and animals and alerts night elf protectors when corruption threatens the balance.",al={"tarindrella","who is the questgiver","shadowglen dryad"},it="identity"},{q="What is Fel Moss?",a="Fel Moss is a tainted growth touched by dark magic that clings to Shadowglen’s wildlife. It enrages creatures such as grells and drives them to unnatural aggression.",al={"fel moss","what is fel moss","moss corruption"},it="item"},{q="What happened to the furbolgs in Shadowglen?",a="Shadowglen’s furbolgs left their peaceful homes and gathered as the hostile Gnarlpine tribe.",al={"furbolg mystery","gnarlpine tribe","where did the furbolgs go"},it="history"},{q="Where does this investigation lead next?",a="Tarindrella sends travelers to Dolanaar, where Druid Athridas Bearmantle investigates corruption across the World Tree.",al={"next quest","where do i go after","athridas bearmantle"},it="next_step"},{q="What are grells and grellkin?",a="Grells and grellkin are small, mischievous woodland spirits native to Teldrassil’s boughs. Though usually unruly pests, they grow violently aggressive when exposed to corruption such as Fel Moss.",al={"grells","grellkin","what are grells"},it="threat"},{q="Why is corruption present on Teldrassil?",a="Teldrassil was grown to restore the night elves’ lost immortality and give them a new sanctuary. Dark energies now seep into its boughs and wildlife, troubling the druids and forest spirits who guard it.",al={"why is teldrassil corrupted","shadowglen corruption"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Tarindrella want you to gather Fel Moss?",a="Tarindrella senses a dark, corrupting influence creeping through Shadowglen. The peaceful furbolgs abandoned their ancestral homes to muster as the hostile Gnarlpine tribe, and grells have surged into the abandoned groves. She needs physical proof that Fel Moss is responsible for driving the local wildlife and spirits mad, allowing her to confirm the source of the taint threatening the World Tree.",al={"why does tarindrella need fel moss","tarindrella motive fel moss","why collect fel moss"},it="motive",add="2b4aa272"},{q="Who are you being sent to fight?",a="You are sent to hunt the grells and grellkin infesting the hills where the furbolgs once lived. These small, mischievous woodland spirits have fallen under a dark enchantment, turning violently aggressive toward the inhabitants of Shadowglen while carrying the tainted Fel Moss that fuels their unnatural malice.",al={"what are we fighting","who has the fel moss","target grells and grellkin"},it="target",add="84e2b96b"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a young Kaldorei setting out from Aldrassil, you learn that corruption can threaten your sacred new home from within.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you share a sacred bond with the forest’s spirits and dryads. Investigating the tainted Fel Moss helps diagnose the spiritual sickness afflicting the World Tree."},kw={"athridas bearmantle","fel moss","gnarlpine","grell","grellkin","shadowglen","tarindrella","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:458","npc:tarindrella","subzone:shadowglen","npc:athridas-bearmantle","subzone:dolanaar","topic:furbolg","topic:druid","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Tarindrella",level="3",faction="Alliance",id=459,ri={"Fel Moss"}},src={"The Woodland Protector (2)"}}
E["quest:475"] = {t="quest",n="A Troubling Breeze",z="teldrassil",s="Athridas Bearmantle waits for word from Starbreeze Village, but the reports have stopped. Great Warden Gaerolas Talvethren watches over the sleeping Druids of the Talon in the Ban'ethil Barrow Den, and his silence points to danger in Teldrassil.",h="Athridas Bearmantle waits for word from Starbreeze Village, but the reports have stopped.",sec={{t="A Silent Watcher",b="Athridas Bearmantle depends on regular word from Gaerolas Talvethren, the Great Warden watching over the Druids of the Talon in the Ban'ethil Barrow Den. The druids sleep there to keep their sacred pact with Ysera in the Emerald Dream. Their sanctuary matters to the spiritual balance of the young World Tree. Now reports from the east have ceased, and unease spreads through the forest.",sp=0},{t="Unease in Starbreeze",b="You are sent east across Teldrassil to Starbreeze Village to find Gaerolas. The silence is no simple oversight: corruption stirs, and wildlife grows agitated in the wilderness. When you reach him, you learn that trouble has come to the village and threatens the nearby barrow dens.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Athridas Bearmantle?",a="Athridas Bearmantle is a prominent night elf overseer in Teldrassil who watches over the forest and keeps the sanctuaries of his sleeping druidic kin undisturbed.",al={"athridas bearmantle","athridas lore","quest giver athridas"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Gaerolas Talvethren?",a="Gaerolas Talvethren is the Great Warden chosen to guard the sleeping Druids of the Talon in the nearby Ban'ethil Barrow Den while their spirits wander the Emerald Dream.",al={"gaerolas talvethren","great warden gaerolas","who is gaerolas"},it="identity"},{q="What is the Ban'ethil Barrow Den?",a="The Ban'ethil Barrow Den is a sacred underground hollow on Teldrassil where night elf druids sleep for long periods to commune with Ysera and honor their pacts in the Emerald Dream.",al={"ban'ethil barrow den","banethil","what is ban'ethil"},it="place"},{q="Why was Gaerolas out of contact?",a="Gaerolas could not send his regular reports because danger and corruption threatened Starbreeze Village and the surrounding forest, leaving him struggling to keep control.",al={"why was gaerolas silent","what happened to gaerolas","trouble in starbreeze"},it="threat"},{q="Where does this quest lead next?",a="After you find Gaerolas Talvethren in Starbreeze Village, he sends you back to Athridas Bearmantle in Dolanaar with grave news: the nearby Gnarlpine furbolgs have succumbed to a spreading, unnatural corruption.",al={"next quest","a troubling breeze followup","what comes after a troubling breeze"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What is the pact with Ysera mentioned in the quest?",a="Night elf druids enter long meditative slumbers to walk the Emerald Dream alongside the Green Dragonflight and Ysera. They serve as custodians of nature's pristine blueprint.",al={"pact with ysera","ysera druid pact","druids of the talon sleep"},it="history"},{q="Why does Athridas Bearmantle send you to Gaerolas?",a="Athridas is deeply uneasy because regular word from Gaerolas Talvethren is overdue. Gaerolas stands watch over the hibernating Druids of the Talon resting within the Ban'ethil Barrow Den, ensuring their safety so they can uphold their sacred pact with Ysera in the Emerald Dream. With sinister portents stirring across the boughs of Teldrassil, Athridas needs someone to travel east to Starbreeze Village and confirm that the sleeping druids remain undisturbed.",al={"why send to starbreeze","athridas bearmantle motive","why a troubling breeze quest"},it="motive",add="3a7b456f"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, guarding the Druids of the Talon's sacred rest helps protect the delicate balance of your new home on Teldrassil.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you hold the Ban'ethil Barrow Den and its sleepers bound to Ysera in deep reverence. Any disturbance to their wardens is urgent."},kw={"athridas bearmantle","ban'ethil","druids of the talon","emerald dream","gaerolas talvethren","starbreeze village","teldrassil","troubling breeze","ysera"},rel={"npc:athridas-bearmantle","npc:gaerolas-talvethren","quest:476","subzone:starbreeze-village","subzone:ban-ethil-barrow-den","zone:teldrassil","topic:druid","topic:night-elf"},m={start="Athridas Bearmantle",["end"]="Gaerolas Talvethren",faction="Alliance",id=475},src={"A Troubling Breeze"}}
E["quest:476"] = {t="quest",n="Gnarlpine Corruption",z="teldrassil",s="Near Starbreeze Village, Gnarlpine Corruption threatens Teldrassil. Wounded Great Warden Gaerolas Talvethren sends word to the night elf leadership in Dolanaar: Gnarlpine furbolgs have overrun the village and fallen to demonic corruption. Their violence may reach the sleeping druids of Ban'ethil Barrow Den.",h="Near Starbreeze Village, Gnarlpine Corruption threatens Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Desperate Warning",b="Near the ruins of Starbreeze Village, Gaerolas Talvethren lies grievously wounded after an ambush by his former allies. The Gnarlpine furbolgs were long regarded as peaceful neighbors and stewards of the wild, but now they have turned feral. Too injured to carry the warning himself, Gaerolas entrusts you with bringing word to Athridas Bearmantle in Dolanaar before the madness spreads farther through Teldrassil.",sp=0},{t="The Scourge of Fel Moss",b="In Dolanaar, Athridas Bearmantle learns the Gnarlpine furbolgs are being subjected to fel magic. Their chieftain, Ursal the Mauler, has harnessed the corrupted Fel Moss festering within the World Tree, driving his people into a violent frenzy. The tribe threatens settlements such as Starbreeze, and Ban'ethil Barrow Den lies nearby, where sleeping druids remain defenseless.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What happened to Starbreeze Village?",a="Gnarlpine furbolgs overran and pillaged Starbreeze Village after fel magic corrupted them. Their sudden ambush drove out or slaughtered the inhabitants, leaving Gaerolas Talvethren trapped and wounded near the village ruins.",al={"why is starbreeze abandoned","starbreeze village attacked","who destroyed starbreeze"},it="ruin"},{q="Why have the Gnarlpine furbolgs turned violent?",a="The Gnarlpine furbolgs have turned violent under their chieftain, Ursal the Mauler, who wields the evil power of Fel Moss found on Teldrassil. Its dark magic has driven the tribe into an uncontrollable frenzy against their former night elf allies.",al={"why are gnarlpine mad","gnarlpine madness","why attack furbolgs"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Gaerolas Talvethren?",a="Gaerolas Talvethren is the night elf Great Warden of the sleeping Druids of the Talon. Gnarlpine furbolgs ambushed him while he traveled toward Ban'ethil Barrow Den, and his wounds leave him relying on travelers to carry news of the catastrophe to Dolanaar.",al={"gaerolas","injured night elf starbreeze"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Athridas Bearmantle?",a="Athridas Bearmantle is a prominent night elf authority stationed in Dolanaar. He oversees regional security and helps coordinate responses to threats against the World Tree and its inhabitants.",al={"athridas","athridas bearmantle dolanaar"},it="identity"},{q="Why are the night elves worried about Ban'ethil Barrow Den?",a="Ban'ethil Barrow Den holds many druids deep in the Emerald Dream. If the frenzied Gnarlpine furbolgs reach the barrows, the sleeping night elves will be defenseless against them.",al={"ban'ethil threat","why ban'ethil barrow den matters","sleeping druids danger"},it="danger"},{q="What is Fel Moss?",a="Fel Moss is a corrupted growth in Teldrassil, tainted by dark demonic energies. Its influence drives local wildlife and furbolgs mad when touched or wielded.",al={"what is fel moss","fel moss teldrassil"},it="item"},{q="Why does Gaerolas Talvethren want this done?",a="Gaerolas discovered firsthand that Ursal the Mauler is corrupting the Gnarlpine tribe with Fel Moss and driving them to rampage. With Starbreeze Village pillaged and the sacred Ban'ethil Barrow Den directly threatened, he knows Dolanaar must be warned immediately before the furbolgs cause even greater catastrophe.",al={"gaerolas motive","why send news to athridas","gaerolas quest reason"},it="motive",add="d35b6598"},{q="Why can't Gaerolas deliver the message himself?",a="Gaerolas was ambushed and severely wounded by the corrupted furbolgs as he departed for the Ban'ethil Barrow Den. Barely surviving the attack, his injuries leave him entirely unable to make the long trek back to Dolanaar, forcing him to rely on you to carry the urgent warning to Athridas Bearmantle.",al={"why does gaerolas need me","why cant gaerolas walk to dolanaar","why me gaerolas"},it="why_me",add="a846c6e3"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you face a tragic shock in Starbreeze Village's fall: even the newly grown World Tree is vulnerable to the demonic taint your people fought so hard to eradicate.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you face an urgent threat to Ban'ethil Barrow Den and the Cenarion Circle, with sleeping brothers vulnerable to the corrupted Gnarlpine tribe."},kw={"athridas bearmantle","ban'ethil barrow den","dolanaar","fel moss","furbolg","gaerolas talvethren","gnarlpine corruption","starbreeze village","ursal the mauler"},rel={"npc:gaerolas-talvethren","npc:athridas-bearmantle","subzone:starbreeze-village","subzone:ban-ethil-barrow-den","quest:475","quest:483","quest:486","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Gaerolas Talvethren",["end"]="Athridas Bearmantle",level="6",faction="Alliance",id=476},src={"Gnarlpine Corruption (Classic)"}}
E["quest:483"] = {t="quest",n="The Relics of Wakening",z="teldrassil",s="At Ban'ethil Barrow Den, an urgent effort is underway to save the sleeping Druids of the Talon. Corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs have overrun the sacred mounds, threatening the druids whose spirits wander the Emerald Dream. Four ritual relics are needed to bring the sleepers safely back to the waking world.",h="At Ban'ethil Barrow Den, an urgent effort is underway to save the sleeping Druids of the Talon.",sec={{t="A Sanctum Defiled",b="West of Dolanaar, a swarm of corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs has overrun the winding corridors of Ban'ethil Barrow Den. Barrow dens are secluded sanctuaries where night elf druids hibernate while their spirits walk the Emerald Dream. A foul taint spreading across Teldrassil has driven these former allies mad. They have desecrated the sanctum, leaving the sleepers unaware that danger threatens their physical bodies.",sp=0},{t="The Tools of Return",b="Athridas Bearmantle needs four sacred relics for the delicate ceremony that can safely awaken the Druids of the Talon. A druid's spirit needs an anchor when returning from the Dream; without one, a sudden awakening can shatter the mind or strand the spirit. The relics lie in chests across the den: the Raven Claw Talisman, the Black Feather Quill, the Sapphire of Sky, and the Rune of Nesting. They are the sleepers' only hope before the Gnarlpine butcher or abduct them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why can't the druids just be shaken awake?",a="Druidic hibernation is a delicate trance linking the mortal body with the Emerald Dream. Without the protective rites of the Relics of Wakening, an improper awakening can strand a druid's consciousness in the Dream, severed from the body.",al={"why need relics to wake druids","why wake ritual","why are relics necessary"}},{q="Who are the Druids of the Talon?",a="The Druids of the Talon are night elf druids attuned to the sky, able to take the form of storm crows and command the winds. Many entered the deep slumber of the Emerald Dream in Teldrassil's barrow dens.",al={"druids of the talon","talon druids","who sleeps in ban'ethil"},it="people"},{q="Why are the Gnarlpine furbolgs attacking the barrow den?",a="A dark corruption is steadily poisoning Teldrassil's wildlife and forests, driving the Gnarlpine tribe to attack. Once peaceful neighbors to the night elves, the corrupted furbolgs now swarm ancient sanctuaries such as Ban'ethil.",al={"why are furbolgs in the barrow den","gnarlpine attacks","why furbolgs aggressive"},it="hostile"},{q="What are the four relics being recovered?",a="The four relics are the Raven Claw Talisman, the Black Feather Quill, the Sapphire of Sky, and the Rune of Nesting. Athridas Bearmantle needs them from sacred chests inside Ban'ethil Barrow Den.",al={"which relics","relics needed","names of relics"},it="item"},{q="Who is Athridas Bearmantle?",a="Athridas Bearmantle is a night elf stationed at Dolanaar who watches over the surrounding wilds' spiritual health. He organizes efforts against the sudden corruption afflicting the Gnarlpine furbolgs and the barrow dens.",al={"athridas bearmantle","quest giver dolanaar"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Ban'ethil Barrow Den located?",a="Ban'ethil Barrow Den lies in the hills directly west of Dolanaar, on the boughs of Teldrassil.",al={"ban'ethil location","where is banethil","where is the den"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Athridas Bearmantle need the Relics of Wakening?",a="Athridas Bearmantle urgently needs the four relics to conduct the delicate awakening ritual for the Druids of the Talon. Gnarlpine furbolgs overran the Ban'ethil Barrow Den and abducted the slumberers. Because their spirits wander deep within the Emerald Dream, their hibernation cannot simply be broken by shaking them awake. Without these specific sacred artifacts, the sleeping druids will remain trapped in the Dream for eternity, utterly defenseless against their captors.",al={"why does athridas want relics","athridas bearmantle motive","relics of wakening purpose"},it="motive",add="64c9f1bc"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a young druid, you see the assault on Ban'ethil as a strike against your Cenarion kin. Securing the relics helps preserve the sacred bridge between mortal soil and the Emerald Dream.",["race:NightElf"]="On Teldrassil's boughs, the desecration of a barrow den shows how quickly corruption is warping the Gnarlpine tribe and disturbing the balance of your new home."},kw={"athridas bearmantle","ban'ethil barrow den","black feather quill","dolanaar","druids of the talon","emerald dream","gnarlpine","raven claw talisman","relics of wakening","rune of nesting","sapphire of sky"},rel={"npc:athridas-bearmantle","subzone:ban-ethil-barrow-den","subzone:dolanaar","quest:476","quest:486","quest:2541","topic:emerald-dream","topic:druid"},m={start="Athridas Bearmantle",faction="Alliance",id=483,ri={"Black Feather Quill","Raven Claw Talisman","Rune of Nesting","Sapphire of Sky"}},src={"The Relics of Wakening"}}
E["quest:486"] = {t="quest",n="Ursal the Mauler",z="teldrassil",s="In Teldrassil, Athridas Bearmantle seeks to wake the Druids of the Talon from their unnatural sleep. Their kin remain trapped in the Barrow Den, and the corrupted Gnarlpine chief behind the disturbance must be slain.",h="In Teldrassil, Athridas Bearmantle seeks to wake the Druids of the Talon from their unnatural sleep.",sec={{t="A Slumber Turned Nightmare",b="The Druids of the Talon withdrew to the Barrow Den of Ban'ethil to sleep and commune with the Emerald Dream. Their peaceful trance became a prison with no way back to waking. Athridas Bearmantle traced the trouble to the gnarlpine furbolgs, and to their vicious leader, Ursal the Mauler, who meddled with the druids' sacred ritual. The sleepers remain caught between waking and the Dream.",sp=0},{t="The Den in Gnarlpine Hold",b="Athridas needs more than the Relics of Wakening to reach the druids through the spiritual fog. The source of the interference must be ended. Ursal the Mauler makes his lair in Gnarlpine Hold, the tribe's home in far southwestern Teldrassil. Striking down the furbolg warlord breaks his hold on the sleepers' minds.",sp=0},{t="A Symptom of Deeper Rot",b="Athridas can perform the ritual and rescue the Druids of the Talon once Ursal is dead, but Teldrassil's sickness remains. The Gnarlpine tribe is still maddened by corruption, and no one knows what is spreading through the World Tree's boughs.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Ursal the Mauler?",a="Ursal the Mauler leads the corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs from Gnarlpine Hold in southwestern Teldrassil. His meddling with the Druids of the Talon's reverie trapped them in their Barrow Den slumber.",al={"who is ursal","ursal lore","who is the boss in gnarlpine hold"},it="target"},{q="Why must Ursal be killed to awaken the druids?",a="Athridas Bearmantle has the Relics of Wakening, but his ritual cannot reach the druids while Ursal lives. The furbolg's interference anchors them in slumber and keeps their spirits from returning to their bodies.",al={"why kill ursal","why does ursal need to die","relilcs of wakening purpose"},it="motive"},{q="Where can Ursal the Mauler be found?",a="Ursal makes his lair in Gnarlpine Hold, the Gnarlpine tribe's home in far southwestern Teldrassil.",al={"ursal location","where is gnarlpine hold","how to find ursal"},gp=true},{q="Does killing Ursal completely save the Gnarlpine furbolgs?",a="No. Ursal's death frees the sleeping druids, but the Gnarlpine furbolgs remain corrupted, and sickness continues to spread through Teldrassil's forests.",al={"are furbolgs cured","did we save the furbolgs","is teldrassil saved"},sp=1},{q="Who are the Druids of the Talon?",a="The Druids of the Talon are night elf druids devoted to the crow totem, and they can take the form of storm crows. They entered deep slumber in the Barrow Den to watch over the wilds from within the Emerald Dream.",al={"druids of the talon","who is sleeping","what druids were saved"},it="people"},{q="Who is Athridas Bearmantle?",a="Athridas Bearmantle is a night elf druid stationed in Dolanaar. He sends adventurers to recover stolen relics and slay Ursal so his brethren can wake safely.",al={"athridas bearmantle","quest giver athridas","who gives ursal quest"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Athridas Bearmantle need you to slay Ursal instead of doing it himself?",a="Athridas Bearmantle must remain behind to prepare the Relics of Wakening and conduct the delicate awakening ritual. If he were to leave his post to hunt down the beast himself, the ritual could not take place in time, leaving his fellow Druids of the Talon trapped forever in their deep, corrupted slumber.",al={"why me","why Athridas doesnt kill Ursal","why cant Athridas go"},it="why_me",add="3acbba65"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The Gnarlpine furbolgs were once ancient allies of the kaldorei. Slaying their maddened leader, Ursal, is a sorrowful necessity to protect your kin and the sleeping druids.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you know the sacred rites of the Emerald Dream must be preserved. Ursal's meddling with the Druids of the Talon profanes Cenarion communion.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help secure Teldrassil's interior roads and restore its circle of druids, strengthening the night elves' stronghold as they join the wider Alliance."},kw={"athridas","ban'ethil","bearmantle","druid","furbolg","gnarlpine","mauler","talon","teldrassil","ursal"},rel={"quest:483","npc:athridas-bearmantle","zone:teldrassil","topic:druid","quest:487","npc:moon-priestess-amara","zone:darnassus"},m={start="Athridas Bearmantle",faction="Alliance",id=486},src={"Ursal the Mauler (quest)"}}
E["quest:487"] = {t="quest",n="The Road to Darnassus",z="teldrassil",s="Along Teldrassil’s western road, corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs threaten the route from Dolanaar to Darnassus. Moon Priestess Amara coordinates scouts and travelers to keep this trade and messenger road clear of ambushes.",h="Along Teldrassil’s western road, corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs threaten the route from Dolanaar to Darnassus.",sec={{t="A Lifeline Under Siege",b="You travel west from Dolanaar toward Darnassus on Teldrassil’s main overland road. Trade goods, political messages, and travelers use it each day to stay connected with the capital and the boughs of the great tree. Teldrassil is young and wild, so safe roads matter to its kaldorei communities.",sp=0},{t="The Gnarlpine Menace",b="The Gnarlpine furbolgs of Teldrassil have fallen to a foul corruption. Driven mad by a sickness plaguing the boughs of the World Tree, they attack from hidden dens beneath the ridges. Gnarlpine ambushers stalk the tree line beside the road, preying on couriers and travelers and making the forest passage deadly.",sp=0},{t="The Sentinels' Vigil",b="Moon Priestess Amara watches over the road outside Dolanaar. She joins the spiritual authority of Elune’s priesthood with the Sentinels’ vigilance, directing capable travelers to strike at ambushers near their dens below the road. The safety of the route to Darnassus’s gates depends on keeping them at bay.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the road between Dolanaar and Darnassus so dangerous?",a="Corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs have made dens along the low ridges below the road. The corruption spreading through Teldrassil has driven them mad, and they attack travelers, couriers, and merchants from the underbrush.",al={"why are furbolgs attacking","gnarlpine road attacks","why is the road unsafe"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Moon Priestess Amara?",a="Moon Priestess Amara, also addressed by her full name, Sentinel Amara Nightwalker, is a night elf commander stationed on Dolanaar’s western outskirts. She oversees the road’s security and coordinates efforts against the nearby Gnarlpine.",al={"who gives the road to darnassus quest","amara nightwalker","who is amara"},it="identity"},{q="Why are the Gnarlpine furbolgs aggressive?",a="Furbolgs were once peaceful allies and neighbors of the kaldorei. On Teldrassil, a strange malady infecting the World Tree has twisted the Gnarlpine, making them violent and driving them to attack anyone entering the forest.",al={"why gnarlpine mad","furbolg corruption teldrassil","are gnarlpine evil"},it="origin"},{q="Where are the ambushers hiding?",a="The ambushers hide below the bluffs and vantage points just off the main road west of Dolanaar. Their dens let them leap upon travelers heading toward Darnassus.",al={"where are gnarlpine ambushers","find ambushers","ambusher den location"},gp=true},{q="Why doesn't Darnassus send a full Sentinel garrison to clear the road?",a="The Sentinels are spread thin across Teldrassil, facing grell infestations, corrupted timberlings, and threats along the coast. Officers like Amara rely on capable travelers and volunteers to keep the interior roads clear.",al={"where are the guards","why sentinels need help","darnassus patrol"},it="why_me"},{q="Why is Amara called both a Moon Priestess and a Sentinel?",a="In kaldorei society, Elune’s sisterhood and the Sentinel military are closely linked. Leaders in the priesthood often command Sentinel troops or have served as front-line warriors.",al={"amara rank","priestess or sentinel amara","amara nightwalker title"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Moon Priestess Amara want the Gnarlpine ambushers dealt with?",a="This road is the primary lifeline between Dolanaar and the night elf capital of Darnassus. Crucial news, travelers, and vital commerce journey along this path every day. With corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs relentlessly attacking travelers, Amara cannot tolerate a rogue band disrupting communication and trade or threatening innocent forest dwellers.",al={"why does amara want this done","amara road to darnassus reason","why clear the road to darnassus"},it="motive",add="4fcb3c8f"},{q="Who are the Gnarlpine ambushers?",a="They are members of the local Gnarlpine furbolg tribe who have succumbed to corruption spreading through Teldrassil. Lurking in the shadowed dens below the road's vantage, these rogue furbolgs lie in wait to launch ruthless, coordinated attacks on anyone journeying between Dolanaar and Darnassus.",al={"who are the ambushers","what are gnarlpine ambushers","why are gnarlpine attacking travelers"},it="target",add="68c15eec"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The Gnarlpine were once honorable kindred of the wild. Putting down corrupted ambushers on the road to Darnassus is a grim necessity born of Teldrassil’s sickness.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you aid Moon Priestess Amara and the Sisterhood of Elune, which gives spiritual leadership and martial defense to the young tree.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you help keep trade and messages moving safely along the main road to Darnassus, the heart of the Alliance presence in northern Kalimdor."},kw={"amara","ambusher","darnassus","dolanaar","furbolg","gnarlpine","nightwalker","road to darnassus","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:moon-priestess-amara","subzone:dolanaar","zone:darnassus","topic:furbolg","topic:sentinels","zone:teldrassil","quest:940"},m={start="Moon Priestess Amara",level="8",faction="Alliance",id=487},src={"The Road to Darnassus (Classic)"}}
E["quest:488"] = {t="quest",n="Zenn's Bidding",z="teldrassil",s="Zenn Foulhoof draws newcomers into his schemes north of the road from Shadowglen to Dolanaar. The solitary satyr asks them to gather animal parts, preying on their trust and naivety.",h="Zenn Foulhoof draws newcomers into his schemes north of the road from Shadowglen to Dolanaar.",sec={{t="A Dubious Bargain",b="Travelers on the path from Shadowglen to Dolanaar may find Zenn Foulhoof beneath the Great Tree. The satyr offers material rewards and secrets for simple work, asking for nightsaber fangs, strigid owl feathers, and webwood spider silk from the surrounding woods. He whispers conspiratorially, urging travelers to keep their bargain between themselves.",sp=0},{t="The Satyr's Joke",b="Satyrs have been ancient enemies of the kaldorei since demonic magic corrupted them during the War of the Ancients. Zenn’s presence on Teldrassil is an outrage. After the traveler completes his errand, Zenn laughs at their gullibility and offers no treasures or insights. He celebrates fooling a naive stranger into doing his dirty work.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Zenn Foulhoof?",a="Zenn Foulhoof is a sly satyr beside the path west of Shadowglen, on the way to Dolanaar. He uses smooth talk and false promises to manipulate naive travelers into doing chores for him, rather than attacking openly.",al={"who is zenn","zenn foulhoof lore","satyr questgiver"},it="identity"},{q="Why is a satyr giving quests in Teldrassil?",a="Zenn acts harmless to dupe newcomers who do not yet understand the treacherous, corrupt nature of satyrs. He exploits their eagerness for work and silver to gather reagents without drawing the Sentinels’ ire by hunting openly himself.",al={"why is a satyr friendly","why can i talk to zenn","satyr in teldrassil"},it="why_here"},{q="What does Zenn do with the fangs, feathers, and silk?",a="Zenn claims the fangs, feathers, and silk are reagents for his mysterious business in the forest. He relishes his influence over mortals, using their labor for his corrupt ends while privately mocking their gullibility.",al={"why does zenn want silk","zenn's reagents","what are the animal parts for"},it="motive"},{q="Why shouldn't night elves trust Zenn Foulhoof?",a="Satyrs were night elves transformed by the Burning Legion’s demonic power during the War of the Ancients. They are ancient enemies of the kaldorei and carriers of corruption, making any bargain with one dangerous and disgraceful.",al={"why hate satyrs","night elf satyr history","are satyrs evil"},it="danger"},{q="What happens after completing Zenn's Bidding?",a="After you hand over the items, Zenn openly mocks you for obeying a satyr. Adventurers realize they were deceived and feel the shame of aiding such a creature; they are then directed to seek redemption for their mistake.",al={"after zenn's bidding","seek redemption quest","what next after zenn"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Where is Zenn Foulhoof located?",a="Zenn Foulhoof stands in Teldrassil just north of the main road leading west from Shadowglen toward Dolanaar.",al={"zenn foulhoof location","where is zenn","zenn map location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Zenn Foulhoof need you to gather these reagents?",a="As a satyr skulking on the edges of night elf territory, Zenn cannot simply wander the boughs of Teldrassil or hunt openly without drawing the wrath of the Sentinels. He preys upon young, eager travelers who are willing to run errands without asking questions, exploiting your naivety to gather dangerous woodland reagents while keeping his own hands clean.",al={"why me zenn","why does zenn need my help","why recruit adventurers"},it="why_me",add="522e474d"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For a young night elf, taking orders from a satyr is deeply shameful. Satyrs are ancestral traitors corrupted by the Burning Legion, and aiding one among Teldrassil’s boughs offends nature and kaldorei heritage.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you are pledged to preserve nature’s balance. Poaching nightsabers, owls, and spiders for a twisted creature of corruption affronts Cenarion teachings."},kw={"dolanaar","foulhoof","nightsaber","satyr","shadowglen","strigid","teldrassil","webwood","zenn"},rel={"npc:zenn-foulhoof","quest:489","topic:satyr","subzone:dolanaar","subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf","topic:alliance"},m={start="Zenn Foulhoof",faction="Alliance",id=488,ri={"Nightsaber Fang","Strigid Owl Feather","Webwood Spider Silk"}},src={"Zenn's Bidding"}}
E["quest:489"] = {t="quest",n="Seek Redemption!",z="teldrassil",s="In Dolanaar, you face the Council of the Forest's demand for atonement. Adventurers were duped into doing Zenn Foulhoof's dirty work, and now the council sends you to trick the satyr into eating corrupted fel cones.",h="In Dolanaar, you face the Council of the Forest's demand for atonement.",sec={{t="A Fool's Errand Undone",b="Just outside Dolanaar, solitary satyr Zenn Foulhoof uses deceit to make passersby do his bidding. Adventurers who unwittingly slaughtered nightsabers, strigid owls, and webwood spiders to satisfy his twisted appetites draw the Council of the Forest's sharp disapproval. The council will not accept harm to nature, especially from its own allies.",sp=0},{t="The Price of Atonement",b="Syral Bladeleaf, Sentinel Kyra Starsong, or Sentinel Shayla Nightbreeze warns you that you must make amends to remain welcome in Teldrassil. Dolanaar's guardians tell you to turn Foulhoof's wicked gluttony against him instead of facing him with steel. Gather the billowing, corrupted fel cones from the forest floor, then offer the unsuspecting satyr a taste of his own foul medicine.",sp=0},{t="A Croaking Retribution",b="You hand Zenn Foulhoof the noxious cones, posing as a loyal errand-runner with a sweet snack. Unaware of the druidic snare, the satyr eagerly devours them and is promptly changed into a helpless frog, humbled before the wilderness he sought to taint.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is the Council of the Forest angry with me?",a="You followed Zenn Foulhoof's earlier bidding and unwittingly slaughtered nightsabers, strigid owls, and spiders. The Council of the Forest sees that needless killing as a defilement of Teldrassil and demands atonement.",al={"why council mad","seek redemption why","why do i need redemption"},it="motive"},{q="Who can give me this quest?",a="Syral Bladeleaf outside the northern dwelling, Sentinel Kyra Starsong inside the inn, or Sentinel Shayla Nightbreeze along the western road can offer it after you finish helping Foulhoof.",al={"quest givers","who starts seek redemption","where to get seek redemption"},gp=true},{q="What are fel cones?",a="Fel cones are corrupted pine seeds from the twisted branches around Teldrassil. Green vapors billow from their husks, and druids turn their foul magic against unsuspecting miscreants.",al={"fel cone","what is fel cone","where fel cones come from"},it="item"},{q="Why offer the fel cones to Zenn Foulhoof?",a="The Council expects you to teach Foulhoof a lesson. He takes the corrupted cones for a harmless snack from someone who once did his bidding.",al={"why give zenn cones","foulhoof snack","fel cone trick"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why is there a satyr living so close to Dolanaar?",a="Zenn Foulhoof keeps to a hollowed clearing just outside Dolanaar and hides his malice behind false pleasantries. Satyrs across Kalimdor are ancient servants of the Burning Legion, and his presence shows how far corruption reaches into the young World Tree.",al={"why is zenn near dolanaar","satyr in dolanaar","zenn foulhoof lore"},it="target"},{q="Can you skip or abandon this quest without ruining your standing?",a="Yes. The Council of the Forest scolds you for helping Foulhoof, but leaving this unfinished does not harm your standing or reputation with the night elves of Darnassus.",al={"reputation loss","can i abandon seek redemption","fail seek redemption"},gp=true},{q="Why do the Sentinels make me deal with Zenn Foulhoof instead of doing it themselves?",a="You brought this upon yourself by previously doing Zenn Foulhoof's bidding and defiling the forest. The Council of the Forest learned of your transgressions, and the local Sentinels expect you to right your own wrong. Because Zenn already trusts you to fetch items for him, you are uniquely positioned to approach the satyr with corrupted cones disguised as an innocent snack without raising his suspicions.",al={"why don't guards deal with zenn","why do i have to trick zenn","why do sentinels send me"},it="why_me",add="680beeda"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, aiding a satyr brings deep humiliation. The Burning Legion warped satyrs into ancient enemies during the War of the Ancients, so making amends before the Council of the Forest matters to cultural honor.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you hold Teldrassil's balance sacred. Hunting predators and scavengers for a demon-tainted outcast violates the Cenarion circle's tenets of guardianship."},kw={"dolanaar","fel cone","kyra starsong","satyr","seek redemption","shayla nightbreeze","syral bladeleaf","teldrassil","zenn foulhoof"},rel={"quest:488","npc:zenn-foulhoof","npc:syral-bladeleaf","subzone:dolanaar","topic:satyr","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf","topic:alliance"},m={start="Sentinel Kyra StarsongSyral BladeleafSentinel Shayla Nightbreeze",["end"]="Zenn Foulhoof",faction="Alliance",id=489,ri={"Fel Cone"}},src={"Seek Redemption!"}}
E["quest:5621"] = {t="quest",n="Garments of the Moon",z="teldrassil",s="Laurna Morninglight sends a young priest to aid a wounded Sentinel south of Dolanaar. The duty tests an initiate's devotion and brings formal recognition in the Sisterhood of Elune.",h="Laurna Morninglight sends a young priest to aid a wounded Sentinel south of Dolanaar.",sec={{t="A Sacred Calling",b="The Sisterhood of Elune guides kaldorei in worship and helps defend Teldrassil's borders. Sentinel Shaya is wounded while patrolling the wilderness south of Dolanaar, and priest trainer Laurna Morninglight cannot leave her post to help. She asks a newly trained initiate to tend Shaya's wounds and strengthen her with protective magic.",sp=0},{t="Vestments of the Sisterhood",b="After restoring Sentinel Shaya's vigor, a priest returns to Dolanaar to receive formal robes of office from Laurna Morninglight. The robes mark an acolyte's passage from classroom instruction to practical service that can save lives. For the kaldorei, aiding the Sentinels is both service to Elune and a duty to Teldrassil's safety.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers the quest Garments of the Moon?",a="Laurna Morninglight, the priest trainer in Dolanaar's northern building, offers Garments of the Moon.",al={"who gives garments of the moon","where to start garments of the moon","garments of the moon questgiver"},gp=true},{q="Who needs help during this task?",a="Sentinel Shaya needs help. Wounded while patrolling the wilderness, she waits just south of Dolanaar.",al={"who do i heal","injured sentinel location","where is sentinel shaya"},it="target"},{q="What magic is required to help Sentinel Shaya?",a="You use healing magic to tend Sentinel Shaya's wounds and protective wards to strengthen her before returning to Dolanaar.",al={"what spells to cast on shaya","how to complete garments of the moon","shaya objective"},gp=true},{q="Can any class take this quest?",a="No. Only night elf priests can receive Garments of the Moon, an early milestone in their spiritual training.",al={"is garments of the moon priest only","garments of the moon class requirement","can druids do garments of the moon"},gp=true},{q="What does the robe reward symbolize?",a="The robe awarded by Laurna Morninglight marks your service to Elune and your recognized place among the local priesthood.",al={"garments of the moon robe meaning","robe reward lore","significance of garments of the moon"}},{q="What is the relationship between this quest and In Favor of Elune?",a="In Favor of Elune is an introductory summons to visit the trainer in Dolanaar. It is not required for Garments of the Moon, but cannot be completed after Garments of the Moon is finished.",al={"in favor of elune prerequisite","in favor of elune missed","order of dolanaar priest quests"},gp=true},{q="Why does Laurna Morninglight want Sentinel Shaya healed?",a="Sentinel Shaya was wounded while patrolling the borders south of Dolanaar to safeguard the settlement. As a priest trainer dedicated to Elune, Laurna Morninglight considers it their sacred duty to tend to the protectors of Teldrassil. Tending Shaya's wounds and fortifying her spirit ensures that the Sentinels can endure the growing perils threatening the boughs of the World Tree.",al={"laurna morninglight motive","why heal sentinel shaya","garments of the moon motive"},it="motive",add="e07db161"},{q="Why does Laurna send you instead of helping Shaya herself?",a="Laurna Morninglight cannot abandon her post in Dolanaar, where she is tasked with instructing and guiding the novice acolytes of the priesthood. With her duties binding her to the village sanctuary, she entrusts you to venture into the field, put your training into practice, and fulfill your duty to Elune by aiding the wounded Sentinel.",al={"why send me","why doesn't laurna heal shaya","why can't laurna go"},it="why_me",add="6b18db0b"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you restore wounded allies through prayer and shield them from danger with divine wards.",["race:NightElf"]="As a kaldorei, you belong to a people whose Sisterhood of Elune and Sentinels have worked together for millennia to protect the forests and their people from encroaching darkness."},kw={"dolanaar","garments of the moon","in favor of elune","laurna morninglight","sentinel shaya","sisterhood of elune","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:laurna-morninglight","quest:5622","subzone:dolanaar","topic:elune","topic:sentinels","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf","topic:alliance"},m={start="Laurna Morninglight",level="4",faction="Alliance",id=5621},src={"Garments of the Moon"}}
E["quest:5622"] = {t="quest",n="In Favor of Elune",z="teldrassil",s="Young night elf priests leave Shadowglen for guidance and training in Dolanaar. Priestess Shanda sends them along the forest path to Laurna Morninglight.",h="Young night elf priests leave Shadowglen for guidance and training in Dolanaar.",sec={{t="Leaving the Glade",b="Priestess Shanda trains initiates serving Elune within Aldrassil's secluded shelter. Their learning begins with simple prayers and defensive invocations under her watchful eye. Shadowglen's cloistered life cannot prepare a priestess or priest for the turmoil gripping the wider world. Once an initiate shows steady faith and discipline, Shanda sends them down the shadowed forest path toward Dolanaar to continue their education.",sp=0},{t="A Step Into the Priesthood",b="Reaching Dolanaar marks an essential milestone in a night elf's divine vocation. There, respected priestess Laurna Morninglight prepares disciples for the trials facing Teldrassil. The acolyte can receive advanced instruction in moonlit spellcraft and claim their first formal vestments, marking their official standing within the Sisterhood of Elune.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends me on this journey?",a="Priestess Shanda, the night elf priest trainer in Aldrassil's boughs in Shadowglen, gives you this guidance once your initial training is complete.",al={"quest giver","who starts in favor of elune","where do i get this quest"},it="identity"},{q="Where do I need to go to find Laurna Morninglight?",a="Laurna Morninglight is in the northern building of Dolanaar, the first major settlement south of the Shadowglen gates in Teldrassil.",al={"laurna morninglight location","where is dolanaar","where is morninglight"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Can any class take this quest?",a="No. This is specifically for young night elf priests taking their first steps into the Sisterhood and the service of Elune.",al={"is this priest only","who can do in favor of elune","druid quest?"},gp=true},{q="What happens after I speak to Laurna Morninglight?",a="Laurna Morninglight greets you and offers the trial Garments of the Moon. It tests your ability to protect and heal wounded defenders before bestowing your first official clerical robes.",al={"what comes next","followup quest","garments of the moon quest"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Is this quest mandatory to continue priest training?",a="This is an optional breadcrumb. If you travel directly to Dolanaar, Laurna Morninglight still offers her training and subsequent tasks without this introduction.",al={"do i have to do in favor of elune","can i skip in favor of elune","optional breadcrumb"},gp=true},{q="Why is earning garments so important to the Sisterhood?",a="Vestments are sacred symbols in night elf culture, not merely cloth. They mark one's official station, devotion, and readiness to channel the Moon Goddess's blessings in service of their people.",al={"why robes matter","significance of garments","station of elune priestess"},it="item"},{q="Why does Shanda send you to Dolanaar?",a="Shanda has taught you the basic rites suited to a novice in Shadowglen, but your training in service to Elune must expand beyond this secluded glade. She directs you to Laurna Morninglight in Dolanaar so you can deepen your spiritual understanding and earn the ceremonial vestments appropriate to your growing station among the priesthood.",al={"why send to dolanaar","shanda motive","why see laurna morninglight"},it="motive",rc="Night Elf",add="012a62ea"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you leave simple novitiate studies for full service and begin the path toward earning your first consecrated clerical vestments.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you follow a traditional milestone for devotees: the Sisterhood of Elune forms the spiritual heart and historic leadership of kaldorei society."},kw={"dolanaar","garments of the moon","in favor of elune","laurna morninglight","priest","shadowglen","shanda","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:laurna-morninglight","npc:shanda","quest:5621","subzone:dolanaar","subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil","topic:elune","topic:night-elf"},m={start="Shanda",["end"]="Laurna Morninglight",level="4",faction="Alliance",id=5622},src={"In Favor of Elune"}}
E["quest:5636"] = {t="quest",n="Desperate Prayer",z="teldrassil",s="In Dolanaar, Laurna Morninglight sends human priests home to Stormwind for further training. A fellow priest has crossed continents to summon them to the Cathedral of Light.",h="In Dolanaar, Laurna Morninglight sends human priests home to Stormwind for further training.",sec={{t="A Message from Home",b="In Dolanaar, Priestess Laurna Morninglight brings you word from home. A fellow priest has crossed continents to find you, and Laurna urges you to return without delay. She offers Elune’s blessing and good wishes for your faith as you leave Teldrassil.",sp=0},{t="The Summons to Stormwind",b="Your path leads across the Great Sea to Stormwind City’s Cathedral of Light. High Priestess Laurena guides the Alliance faithful in their spiritual growth. She summons promising acolytes to deepen their devotion and learn Desperate Prayer, an emergency prayer that can save a life in a darkest hour.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who starts the quest Desperate Prayer in Teldrassil?",a="Laurna Morninglight, a night elf priest trainer in Dolanaar, sends you word from home. A visiting priest has left an urgent message for you.",al={"who gives desperate prayer","desperate prayer quest giver teldrassil","laurna morninglight quest"},it="identity",gp=true},{q="Where does this quest lead?",a="You travel to the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind City to speak with High Priestess Laurena.",al={"where do i go","turn in desperate prayer","where is laurena"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why is a night elf directing a priest to Stormwind?",a="Laurna Morninglight respects the faith of foreign priests who visit Teldrassil. She passes along messages from the religious leaders in their homelands, even though night elf priests revere Elune.",al={"why does a night elf send me to stormwind","night elf holy light"},it="why_here"},{q="What is the reward for completing this quest?",a="You gain access to spiritual mentorship and can learn Desperate Prayer, an instantaneous healing prayer from High Priestess Laurena.",al={"desperate prayer reward","what spell do i get"},gp=true},{q="Can night elf priests take this specific quest?",a="No. Night elf priests worship Elune and learn Starshards. This summons is for human priests exploring Kalimdor at early levels.",al={"can night elves do desperate prayer","night elf priest desperate prayer"},gp=true},{q="How do you travel back to Stormwind from Teldrassil?",a="Travel through Darnassus to Rut'theran Village, then take a boat to Auberdine in Darkshore. From there, board the ship across the sea to Stormwind Harbor.",al={"how to get to stormwind from dolanaar","teldrassil to stormwind route"},gp=true},{q="Why does Laurna Morninglight send you to Stormwind?",a="Laurna Morninglight has no personal stake or secret agenda; she is passing along an urgent summons. An emissary of the Holy Light visited Dolanaar seeking you specifically, instructing her that High Priestess Laurena requires your presence at the Cathedral of Light. Recognizing that your talents have drawn the notice of your leaders and that your people need you, Laurna urges you not to linger on Teldrassil when greater duties call you home.",al={"why send to stormwind","laurna morninglight motive","why desperate prayer quest"},it="motive",add="32b36d47"},{q="Why does Laurena need you instead of local priests in Stormwind?",a="You have advanced far enough in your communion with the Holy Light to warrant individual guidance from the church's highest elders. High Priestess Laurena seeks promising acolytes who demonstrate true devotion in the field, calling you back to Stormwind to undergo advanced instruction in sacred rites such as the Desperate Prayer. Your personal growth as a vessel of the Light is what commands her attention.",al={"why does laurena want me","why me desperate prayer","why summon me to stormwind"},it="why_me",add="5980c3c7"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you return to the Cathedral of Light at level ten to learn the blessings of faith tied to your race.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see night elf priestesses coordinate with the church leadership in Stormwind.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you revere Elune, and Priestess Laurna Morninglight still respects foreign followers of the Holy Light beneath Teldrassil’s boughs."},kw={"cathedral of light","desperate prayer","dolanaar","high priestess laurena","laurna morninglight","priest quest","stormwind","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:laurna-morninglight","npc:high-priestess-laurena","subzone:cathedral-of-light","zone:teldrassil","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:light","topic:elune"},m={start="Laurna Morninglight",["end"]="High Priestess Laurena",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=5636},src={"Desperate Prayer (Dolanaar)"}}
E["quest:6063"] = {t="quest",n="Taming the Beast",z="teldrassil",s="In Dolanaar, Taming the Beast begins a night elf hunter’s trials with a wild Webwood Lurker. Dazalar lends an enchanted taming rod, and the hunter must win the spider’s trust through a bond with nature.",h="In Dolanaar, Taming the Beast begins a night elf hunter’s trials with a wild Webwood Lurker.",sec={{t="A Sacred Bond",b="For the kaldorei, hunting means more than tracking prey or surviving in the wild. It binds a hunter to nature, which is greater than any mortal. Animals are independent creatures, not tools to bend to a hunter’s will. Dazalar teaches novice hunters to meet them with respect. Before gaining a lifelong beast companion, a hunter must master local wildlife through ancient techniques, never brute force.",sp=0},{t="The First Trial",b="Giant arachnids infest Teldrassil’s boughs, and Dazalar gives the hunter a taming rod. The hunter seeks a Webwood Lurker in the shadowed thickets, facing the venomous spider and its attacks while trying to reach it through empathy. A brief mental bond proves the hunter can commune with the World Tree’s eerie, skittering predators.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="The trial begins night elf hunters’ training to tame animal companions. Using a taming rod on local beasts tests whether a hunter has the calm and skill to commune with wild predators.",al={"why do this quest","pet quest purpose","what does taming the beast give"},it="purpose"},{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Dazalar, a hunter trainer in Dolanaar on Teldrassil, offers the trial to young night elf hunters with sufficient experience.",al={"quest giver","where to get taming quest","who starts taming the beast"},it="identity"},{q="What creature must be tamed in this trial?",a="You must tame a Webwood Lurker, a venomous giant spider from the wild thickets and woods outside Dolanaar.",al={"which pet to tame","webwood lurker target","what beast do i tame"},it="target"},{q="Do I keep the Webwood Lurker permanently?",a="No. The Webwood Lurker is a temporary companion for practicing basic beast handling. When you return to Dazalar, the bond ends as you prepare for the next trial.",al={"do i keep the spider","is the webwood lurker permanent","keep pet"},gp=true},{q="Why do night elves test hunters with spiders first?",a="Webwood Lurkers are predatory and aggressive, testing a novice hunter’s composure. Mastering an arachnid shows a hunter can bridge their consciousness with hostile forms of nature.",al={"why webwood lurker","why tame a spider","spider taming lore"}},{q="What comes after returning to Dazalar?",a="After you return to Dazalar, he sends you to test your bond with a Nightsaber Stalker and a Strigid Screecher, both native to Teldrassil. Then he grants permanent taming abilities.",al={"what next","after taming the beast","next trial"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Dazalar want this done?",a="Dazalar believes that nature is not a force to be bent to a mortal's whim, but a power that demands deep reverence and respect. Before he entrusts you with the enduring art of taming wild beasts, he must ensure you grasp this sacred duty. The trial tests whether you possess the patience and humility required of a true kaldorei hunter rather than treating wild creatures as mere tools.",al={"why does dazalar test you","dazalar motive","purpose of dazalar trial"},it="motive",add="641cd576"},{q="Why does Dazalar send you instead of doing this himself?",a="This is an essential rite of passage for your own growth as a hunter. Dazalar has already mastered the wild; his role is to guide and evaluate your progress. The trial requires you to forge a bond under your own will and prove that you have learned the discipline necessary to walk alongside Teldrassil's creatures as a trusted guardian.",al={"why do i have to tame the spider","why me dazalar","why doesnt dazalar do it"},it="why_me",add="a645c3ca"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you pass from solitary archer to partner of the wilderness, bound to the beasts of the forest.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you learn to tame through communion and reverence for nature, rather than subjugation."},kw={"dazalar","dolanaar","hunter pet","kaldorei","taming","taming rod","teldrassil","webwood lurker"},rel={"npc:dazalar","subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf"},m={start="Dazalar",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=6063},src={"Taming the Beast (night elf)"}}
E["quest:6101"] = {t="quest",n="Taming the Beast",z="teldrassil",s="Dazalar guides a night elf hunter through a second trial in Dolanaar. With an enchanted taming rod, you subdue a nightsaber stalker and learn how wild beasts differ.",h="Dazalar guides a night elf hunter through a second trial in Dolanaar.",sec={{t="The Changing Nature of Beasts",b="Dazalar teaches you that the forest's creatures do not all behave alike. Each species has its own temperament, and a hunter must learn to meet it on its own terms. Beneath Teldrassil's canopy, the next test brings you against beasts more cunning and predatory than webspinners.",sp=0},{t="Subduing the Nightsaber",b="Kaldorei revere nightsabers as sacred predators, fierce guardians, and companions of the Sentinels. With the taming rod, you face a nightsaber stalker and must keep a steady nerve and calm authority. Winning its trust shows you can handle a predator, not only the more docile creatures of the woods.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="Dazalar sends you to tame a nightsaber stalker and learn how different predators behave. This is the second trial in the night elf hunter's training; the full three-part trial unlocks permanent beast taming.",al={"why do this quest","pet taming quest 2","nightsaber taming goal"},it="purpose"},{q="Where can nightsaber stalkers be found?",a="Nightsaber stalkers roam the wooded paths and undergrowth south of Dolanaar, in central Teldrassil.",al={"where are nightsaber stalkers","stalker location","where to find the cat"},gp=true},{q="Do I get to keep the nightsaber stalker as my permanent pet?",a="No. The rod tames the beast only for practice. After you finish all three trials and return the rod, you learn to tame beasts permanently and choose a companion.",al={"do i keep the pet","can i keep the nightsaber","is this my pet forever"},gp=true},{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Dazalar, the hunter trainer in Dolanaar, gives you this instruction after you complete your first taming test.",al={"quest giver","who starts this","dazalar location"},it="people"},{q="Why do night elves revere nightsabers so deeply?",a="Kaldorei have lived alongside nightsabers for millennia. Sentinels and Priestesses of Elune have used them as companions, scouts, and war mounts, and taming one marks a proud mastery of the woods.",al={"night elf cats lore","why nightsabers matter","lore on nightsabers"},it="origin"},{q="What comes after completing this task?",a="Dazalar gives you a final taming task involving another creature of Teldrassil. Afterward, he teaches you to tame, feed, and care for permanent companions across Azeroth.",al={"next quest","what is after nightsaber stalker","hunter trial next"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Dazalar want you to tame a nightsaber stalker?",a="Dazalar aims to teach you that nature's variance is ever-shifting yet dependable. By guiding you through diverse creatures, he wants you to perceive the unique temperament and spirit of each beast, ensuring you learn how to harmonize with different companions across Teldrassil.",al={"why tame nightsaber stalker","dazalar motive","why nightsaber stalker"},it="motive",add="878d77ca"},{q="What is a nightsaber stalker and why are you seeking it?",a="Nightsaber stalkers are predatory great cats native to the shadowed boughs and woods of Teldrassil. Dazalar sends you after one so you can master bonding with a cunning, agile hunter, learning to respect its instinct and balance within the wild.",al={"what is a nightsaber stalker","nightsaber stalkers teldrassil","why hunt nightsaber stalker"},it="target",add="a23887a1"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you learn to respect different animal temperaments before you earn a lifelong companion.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you meet a traditional milestone for woodland scouts: taming a nightsaber, a creature woven into kaldorei history and culture."},kw={"beast taming","dazalar","dolanaar","hunter","nightsaber stalker","taming rod","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:dazalar","subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","quest:6061","topic:night-elf"},m={start="Dazalar",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=6101},src={"Taming the Beast (night elf 2)"}}
E["quest:6102"] = {t="quest",n="Taming the Beast",z="teldrassil",s="In Dolanaar, Taming the Beast brings a young night elf hunter to the final trial of basic training. Under Dazalar’s direction, hunters tame a predatory owl of the skies before gaining the power to choose a lifelong companion.",h="In Dolanaar, Taming the Beast brings a young night elf hunter to the final trial of basic training.",sec={{t="Mastery of the Canopy",b="Night elf hunters must make peace with creatures across Teldrassil before their basic beastcraft is complete. After proving their will against beasts of the underbrush, they face the spirit of the skies, the Strigid Screecher. These watchful birds of prey roost high in the boughs west of Dolanaar. Patience and a steady nerve are needed to pacify one with the enchanted Taming Rod.",sp=0},{t="A Hunter's Bond",b="Taming the Strigid Screecher fulfills the ancient lessons of communion between kaldorei hunters and nature. When the apprentice returns the spent rod to Dazalar, the training exercises end. The apprentice earns the full art of calling, dismissing, and permanently taming beasts of their own choosing across Azeroth.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are Strigid Screechers found?",a="Strigid Screechers roost in the woods west of Dolanaar. Hunters seek these predatory birds among the canopy and roots outside the village to test their rod.",al={"screecher location","where is strigid screecher","owl location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Dazalar?",a="Dazalar is a night elf hunter trainer in Dolanaar. He guides young kaldorei who have gained basic skill in archery and tracking, testing them against land and sky beasts before bestowing the ability to bind a real animal companion.",al={"dazalar role","who teaches pet taming dolanaar","hunter trainer dolanaar"},it="identity"},{q="Do I get to keep the Strigid Screecher as my pet?",a="No. The screechers tamed during this trial are temporary subjects bound only by the Taming Rod’s magic. When the trial ends, the rod is surrendered, and the hunter is taught how to tame a permanent companion of their own choosing in the wild.",al={"keep owl","is screecher permanent","do i keep this pet"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What happens after completing this trial?",a="Dazalar permanently unlocks your ability to tame, call, and dismiss beasts. He points you toward further training in Darnassus, where you can learn to feed your companion and teach it to fight.",al={"what comes next","after taming the beast","hunter pet quest finish"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why do night elves tame owls specifically?",a="Birds of prey such as owls hold deep cultural significance among the kaldorei as vigilant hunters of the night and trusted scouts. Mastering a creature of the skies proves a hunter understands aerial predators as well as beasts that dwell on the ground.",al={"owl lore night elf","why owls","strigid screecher importance"},it="history"},{q="Can hunters choose any animal after this quest?",a="Yes. Once the permanent taming ability is unlocked, a hunter can seek any tameable beast of the land, water, or sky across Teldrassil and beyond.",al={"what pets can i get","choosing first pet","any beast tameable"},gp=true},{q="Why does Dazalar have you tame a Strigid Screecher?",a="This is your final trial as a novice hunter. Having proven your ability to handle two distinct creatures of the land, Dazalar requires you to master one that rules the skies. By taming a fierce Strigid Screecher, you demonstrate that your empathy and authority over beasts extend beyond the earth, proving you are ready to bond with a permanent companion of your own.",al={"why tame strigid screecher","dazalar motive","why owl trial"},it="motive",rc="Night Elf",add="fcfecb3c"},{q="What are Strigid Screechers?",a="Strigid Screechers are large, predatory owls native to the boughs of Teldrassil. Revered by night elf hunters for their keen sight and silent flight, they hunt throughout the woods west of Dolanaar. Their fierce nature and aerial grace make them an ideal test of a hunter's patience, focus, and command before undertaking a permanent beast bond.",al={"strigid screechers","strigid screecher lore","screecher owls teldrassil"},it="target",add="ebb229ae"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, this rite marks the passage from fighting alone to forging a lifetime partnership with a wild companion.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, taming Teldrassil’s native wildlife follows the kaldorei path of living in harmony with nature rather than bending it through force."},kw={"beast","dazalar","dolanaar","hunter pet","screecher","strigid screecher","taming","taming rod","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:dazalar","subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf","quest:6061"},m={start="Dazalar",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=6102},src={"Taming the Beast (night elf 3)"}}
E["quest:6103"] = {t="quest",n="Training the Beast",z="teldrassil",s="In Teldrassil, Training the Beast sends night elf hunters from the wilds to Darnassus. After taming beasts among the boughs, they learn pet care and discipline from Jocaste.",h="In Teldrassil, Training the Beast sends night elf hunters from the wilds to Darnassus.",sec={{t="A Hunter's Rite of Passage",b="Dazalar sends you from the wilds near Dolanaar to Darnassus once you prove you can tame a beast. Before you travel Kalimdor with a loyal companion, you need to learn more than how to use a taming rod. Subduing a wild creature tests your strength and will, but an untrained beast can still be unpredictable.",sp=0},{t="Guidance in the Cenarion Enclave",b="Jocaste teaches you the arts of caring for a companion in Darnassus's Cenarion Enclave. She shows you how to feed your pet, bring it back if tragedy strikes, and train it to fight. For night elves, this bond reflects reverence for nature, not simple control.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="You go to Darnassus to learn the skills needed to care for and train a lasting animal companion. This completes the first steps of a night elf hunter's training with a pet.",al={"why do this quest","pet training quest night elf","what does training the beast do"},it="purpose"},{q="Where do I find Jocaste?",a="Jocaste is in Darnassus, in the Cenarion Enclave among the trees and hunter lodges in the northwest of the city.",al={"where is jocaste","jocaste location","find jocaste"},gp=true},{q="Who starts the quest?",a="Dazalar, the hunter trainer in Dolanaar, sends you after you've completed all three taming trials across Teldrassil.",al={"quest giver","who gives training the beast","dazalar location"},gp=true},{q="What skills do you learn from Jocaste?",a="Jocaste teaches you to feed your companion, revive it if it falls in combat, and train it in new abilities.",al={"what abilities do i get","jocaste rewards","hunter pet spells"},gp=true},{q="Why does night elf culture emphasize pet training?",a="Night elf hunters treat their pets as partners, not tools to command. Their care reflects a belief in living with respect for nature.",al={"night elf hunter lore","why train beasts night elf"},it="origin"},{q="Is this quest available to other races?",a="This journey to Darnassus is for night elf hunters. Hunters of other races undergo similar training with mentors of their own race.",al={"can dwarves do this","can horde do training the beast"},gp=true},{q="Why does Dazalar send you to Jocaste?",a="Dazalar has taught you how to tame beasts of the wild, but capturing a creature's loyalty is only the first step. Without proper guidance in feeding, caring for, and instructing your companion, the bond between hunter and beast cannot flourish. He directs you to Darnassus because Jocaste is among the night elves' most revered hunters, possessing the ancient wisdom required to elevate a fledgling tracker into a true master of beasts.",al={"why does dazalar want this done","dazalar motive","why go to darnassus hunter"},it="motive",add="1a4b70d0"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you learn to train, feed, and revive your companion as you move beyond the novice's path.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you share a tradition of companionship with beasts built on respect and coexistence, taught in Darnassus and the Cenarion Enclave."},kw={"cenarion enclave","darnassus","dazalar","hunter pet","jocaste","teldrassil","training the beast"},rel={"npc:jocaste","npc:dazalar","subzone:cenarion-enclave","zone:darnassus","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf","quest:6081"},m={start="Dazalar",["end"]="Jocaste",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=6103},src={"Training the Beast (night elf)"}}
E["quest:8357"] = {t="quest",n="Dancing for Marzipan",z="teldrassil",s="During Hallow's End, travelers in Darnassus gather sweets for Jesper, a sick orphan in Stormwind. Innkeeper Saelienne keeps the trick-or-treat custom: a dance comes before her Darnassus Marzipan.",h="During Hallow's End, travelers in Darnassus gather sweets for Jesper, a sick orphan in Stormwind.",sec={{t="A Tradition Upheld",b="Hallow's End brings a lighter spirit to Darnassus, the sacred forest city of the long-lived night elves. You come seeking sweets for Jesper, a sick child recovering in Stormwind. Innkeeper Saelienne keeps the season's custom, even when the treat is meant for a child in need. First, she asks for a trick.",sp=0},{t="The Price of Marzipan",b="Saelienne asks you to dance on the inn floor before she gives you Darnassus Marzipan. The performance earns the sweet needed for the holiday care package bound for Jesper.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of Dancing for Marzipan?",a="Dancing for Marzipan lets you earn Darnassus Marzipan from Innkeeper Saelienne in Darnassus. The sweet is one of several Hallow's End treats gathered to cheer Jesper, a sick orphan in Stormwind.",al={"why dance for marzipan","what is this quest","marzipan quest"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Innkeeper Saelienne?",a="Innkeeper Saelienne manages an inn in Darnassus, where travelers find shelter and rest beneath Teldrassil's boughs. During Hallow's End, she gives local sweets to those who take part in the tradition.",al={"who is saelienne","saelienne lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Saelienne insist on a dance?",a="Saelienne follows Hallow's End's trick-or-treat custom. She asks for a dance before giving you a sweet intended for an ailing child.",al={"why dance","why does saelienne want me to dance"},it="motive"},{q="Where does the marzipan go after this?",a="The Darnassus Marzipan joins seasonal sweets from inns in Ironforge and Stormwind, along with sweets from Talvash del Kissel in Ironforge. Together, they are meant to bring holiday joy to young Jesper in Stormwind.",al={"who gets the marzipan","what to do with marzipan"},it="next_step"},{q="What is Darnassus Marzipan?",a="Darnassus Marzipan is a sugary confection made in the night elven capital. It is the city's festive treat for Hallow's End visitors.",al={"darnassus marzipan lore","what kind of candy is it"},it="item"},{q="Can Horde players complete this quest?",a="No. Dancing for Marzipan is for Alliance characters. Darnassus is an Alliance stronghold, and the marzipan is gathered for an Alliance orphan recovering in Stormwind City.",al={"is this quest alliance only","horde marzipan quest"},gp=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, this Hallow's End tradition brings sweets from distant Teldrassil to a young orphan in Stormwind, shared across the capitals.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you take part in the Alliance's Hallow's End customs, joining playful revelry with your woodland way of life."},kw={"dance","darnassus","hallow's end","innkeeper","jesper","marzipan","saelienne","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:saelienne","quest:8311","zone:darnassus","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Innkeeper Saelienne",faction="Alliance",id=8357},src={"Dancing for Marzipan (Alliance)"}}
E["quest:916"] = {t="quest",n="Webwood Venom",z="teldrassil",s="In Shadowglen, Gilshalan Windwalker studies the giant webwood spiders of Shadowthread Cave. He asks young night elves to gather venom sacs so he can learn how Teldrassil's growth has affected the forest's wildlife.",h="In Shadowglen, Gilshalan Windwalker studies the giant webwood spiders of Shadowthread Cave.",sec={{t="A Naturalist's Curiosity",b="Gilshalan Windwalker has come to Shadowglen to study the webwood spiders in Shadowthread Cave. They are far larger and more aggressive than their cousins elsewhere. He suspects Teldrassil's immense magical energies are changing the local wildlife. He asks for venom sacs to compare with those of ordinary spiders and learn what has changed.",sp=0},{t="The Looming Threat in Shadowglen",b="Webwood spiders live in and around Shadowthread Cave, where they threaten young night elves in the glen. Gathering their venom can help thin their numbers and give Darnassian researchers evidence of Teldrassil's effect on the wild.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gilshalan Windwalker?",a="Gilshalan Windwalker is a night elf researcher at Aldrassil in Shadowglen. He studies Teldrassil's wildlife to learn how the World Tree's rapid growth affects the local ecology.",al={"gilshalan","who gives webwood venom","quest giver webwood venom"},it="identity"},{q="Why are the webwood spiders so large?",a="Webwood spiders are cousins to much smaller varieties. Gilshalan Windwalker believes Teldrassil's rapid growth and latent magical forces have enlarged them and changed their behavior.",al={"giant spiders teldrassil","why are spiders big shadowglen","webwood mutations"},it="origin"},{q="Where is Shadowthread Cave?",a="Shadowthread Cave lies in northern Shadowglen, in the rocky ridges beyond Aldrassil's training grounds.",al={"shadowthread cave location","where find webwoods","webwood spider cave"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What will Gilshalan do with the venom sacs?",a="Gilshalan plans to take the venom to Darnassus and compare its chemical and magical properties with those of ordinary forest spiders. He hopes to find signs of changes caused by the World Tree.",al={"why venom sacs","gilshalan venom study","venom research darnassus"},it="item"},{q="Are there other quests in Shadowthread Cave?",a="Yes. Near Shadowthread Cave, Dirania Silvershine helps Iverron, an elf poisoned by the same spiders.",al={"other spider quests shadowglen","shadowthread cave quests","iverron quest"},gp=true},{q="What quest follows Webwood Venom?",a="After studying the venom, Gilshalan asks for a Webwood Egg from deep inside Shadowthread Cave so he can study the spiders' life cycle.",al={"next quest webwood venom","what comes after webwood venom","gilshalan followup"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Gilshalan Windwalker want Webwood venom sacs?",a="Gilshalan came to Shadowglen as a scholar intending to study the unnaturally large webwood spiders inhabiting Shadowthread Cave. He suspects that the rapid growth and latent magic of the new World Tree, Teldrassil, have altered the local wildlife. By examining venom samples from these beasts, he hopes to compare them to their smaller mainland cousins and prove Teldrassil's profound influence on nature.",al={"why does gilshalan want venom","gilshalan windwalker motive","why collect webwood venom"},it="motive",add="6f3b3a77"},{q="What are webwood spiders and why are they in Shadowglen?",a="Webwood spiders are arachnids that have nested in and around Shadowthread Cave on the northern edge of Shadowglen. While related to common woodland spiders, these creatures have grown monstrously large and aggressive under the strange energies radiating from the new World Tree. Their sudden proliferation threatens the sheltered groves of Aldrassil.",al={"what are webwood spiders","why are webwood spiders here","webwood spiders lore"},it="target",add="432bbacd"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For young night elves coming of age in Shadowglen, this work offers an early lesson in how fragile and unpredictable nature has become beneath Teldrassil's boughs.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you have reason to follow Gilshalan's findings. The Cenarion Circle watches closely to learn whether Teldrassil heals or warps the wildlife around it."},kw={"aldrassil","gilshalan","shadowglen","shadowthread","spiders","teldrassil","venom","webwood","windwalker"},rel={"npc:gilshalan-windwalker","subzone:shadowthread-cave","subzone:aldrassil","subzone:shadowglen","quest:3521","quest:4495","zone:teldrassil","zone:darnassus"},m={start="Gilshalan Windwalker",level="4",faction="Alliance",id=916,ri={"Webwood Venom Sac"}},src={"Webwood Venom"}}
E["quest:917"] = {t="quest",n="Webwood Egg",z="teldrassil",s="In Shadowglen, Gilshalan Windwalker seeks an unhatched Webwood Egg for his study of Teldrassil’s wildlife. After gathering venom samples, he needs a living specimen to examine the unnatural aggression afflicting the forest’s creatures. An egg can be studied safely without subduing a full-grown spider.",h="In Shadowglen, Gilshalan Windwalker seeks an unhatched Webwood Egg for his study of Teldrassil’s wildlife.",sec={{t="A Safe Specimen",b="Gilshalan Windwalker needs live subjects to understand the unnatural corruption affecting the Webwood spiders around Shadowglen. You have secured raw venom from the aggressive spiders, but carrying a thrashing giant out of the depths would be deadly for a novice. Gilshalan asks you to bring back an unhatched egg from the brooding clutches inside Shadowthread Cave.",sp=0},{t="The Road to the Capital",b="Webwood spiders brood in Shadowthread Cave, where the forest’s increasingly hostile arachnids make their nests. An intact egg gives scholars a controlled subject that can hatch under containment. Gilshalan plans to bundle it with his venom samples and send both to Darnassus for examination. With his local study complete, he directs recruits toward higher duties in the boughs of Aldrassil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Gilshalan want an egg instead of an adult spider?",a="Gilshalan wants an egg because capturing a live giant spider is too dangerous for an unproven recruit and too difficult for him to contain alone. Researchers can transport an intact egg safely and arrange containment before the brood emerges.",al={"why an egg","why not catch a live spider","why webwood egg"},it="item"},{q="Where is the Webwood egg found?",a="The egg lies in a webbed nest deep inside Shadowthread Cave, at the northern end of Shadowglen in Teldrassil, among the boughs and roots.",al={"egg location","where to find webwood egg","shadowthread cave nest"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Gilshalan Windwalker?",a="Gilshalan Windwalker is a night elf researcher stationed at Aldrassil in Shadowglen. He investigates the sudden corruption driving Teldrassil’s native creatures to violent behavior.",al={"who is gilshalan","gilshalan lore"},it="identity"},{q="What happens to the egg after it is turned in?",a="Gilshalan prepares the egg and his venom vials for shipment to Darnassus. Scholars and druids there can examine them under controlled conditions after his work in Shadowglen concludes.",al={"what does gilshalan do with the egg","where does the egg go"},it="next_step"},{q="What comes after completing this task?",a="After you secure the egg, Gilshalan directs you up Aldrassil to answer Tenaron's Summons and meet the elder druids guiding the heart of Shadowglen.",al={"next quest after webwood egg","what to do after egg"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why are the Webwood spiders so aggressive?",a="The Webwood spiders, like much of Teldrassil’s wildlife, have been succumbing to unnatural corruption taking root across the young World Tree. It turns once-docile or neutral beasts into aggressive predators.",al={"why are spiders mad","spider corruption"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Gilshalan Windwalker want this done?",a="Gilshalan seeks to thoroughly investigate the strange corruption unsettling Teldrassil's wildlife. Having already collected samples of Webwood venom, he needs living specimens to examine how the taint affects the spiders from birth. Studying an unhatched egg allows scholars in Darnassus to raise and observe captive hatchlings safely, hoping to uncover the source of the bough's creeping sickness.",al={"gilshalan egg motive","why does gilshalan want an egg","gilshalan windwalker quest reason"},it="motive",add="5fcc2c84"},{q="Why does Gilshalan send you into Shadowthread Cave instead of going himself?",a="Gilshalan is a researcher and scholar rather than a seasoned warrior. He openly admits that wrangling giant arachnids or venturing into their infested subterranean den exceeds his own physical capabilities. Entrusting a promising young adventurer to navigate the hazardous caverns allows him to remain safely at Aldrassil, preparing the necessary containment measures for the delicate specimen.",al={"why can't gilshalan get the egg","why send me webwood egg","gilshalan why me"},it="why_me",add="f82204fd"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For a young night elf, recovering the egg shows how corruption is taking hold on Teldrassil. Scholars now study their homeland’s wildlife as hostile threats.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you know that Cenarion researchers study eggs and venom to learn whether the corruption altering these beasts can be cleansed or whether the blight runs deeper."},kw={"aldrassil","gilshalan windwalker","shadowglen","shadowthread cave","spider egg","teldrassil","webwood","webwood egg"},rel={"npc:gilshalan-windwalker","subzone:shadowthread-cave","quest:916","quest:920","subzone:aldrassil","zone:teldrassil","zone:darnassus","quest:98397"},m={start="Gilshalan Windwalker",level="5",faction="Alliance",id=917,ri={"Webwood Egg"}},src={"Webwood Egg (quest)"}}
E["quest:918"] = {t="quest",n="Timberling Seeds",z="teldrassil",s="At Lake Al'Ameth, botanist Denalan studies the growing hostility of Teldrassil's nature elementals. He seeks to harvest Timberling Seeds and test whether enriched soil can help them grow calmer. His work is one quiet effort by night elf herbalists to understand the subtle afflictions troubling the World Tree.",h="At Lake Al'Ameth, botanist Denalan studies the growing hostility of Teldrassil's nature elementals.",sec={{t="Restless Nature",b="Timberlings are nature elementals native to Teldrassil's boughs, closely bound to the health and vitality of the surrounding flora. They are usually peaceful reflections of the forest's balance, but their recent hostility has alarmed the local night elves, and no cause is known. Botanist Denalan hopes to learn what has stirred them rather than simply cull them.",sp=0},{t="Seeds of a New Growth",b="Denalan suspects the blemish lies deep in the ground. He hopes to sprout fresh timberlings, a gentler generation of elementals, in enriched and carefully treated loam. By harvesting seeds from wandering timberlings near Lake Al'Ameth, he aims to learn whether the land's corruption can be countered from the roots up.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are timberlings?",a="Timberlings are small, plant-like nature elementals found on Teldrassil. They mirror the natural order and life cycle of the great tree's flora and fauna.",al={"timberling lore","what are timberlings","nature elementals teldrassil"},it="people"},{q="Why have the timberlings become aggressive?",a="Denalan suspects a flaw or contamination in Teldrassil's soil. As elemental manifestations of the tree's ecology, timberlings reflect the growing corruption spreading through the island.",al={"why are timberlings angry","timberling hostility","angry timberlings"},it="hostile"},{q="Who is Denalan?",a="Denalan is a night elf naturalist and botanist who tends a small garden retreat on Lake Al'Ameth's eastern shore. He studies Teldrassil's unusual flora and soils.",al={"denalan lore","who is denalan","lake al'ameth botanist"},it="identity"},{q="Where can timberling seeds be gathered?",a="Timberlings roam the shaded thickets, shores, and forest glades around Lake Al'Ameth in central Teldrassil.",al={"where to find timberling seeds","timberling locations","lake al'ameth seeds"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Denalan plan to do with the seeds?",a="Denalan plans to cultivate the seeds in special, purified soil mixtures he has developed. He hopes to grow docile timberlings free from the forest's agitation.",al={"what happens to seeds","denalan plan","planting timberling seeds"},it="item"},{q="How does this connect to Teldrassil's wider troubles?",a="The aggression of these basic nature spirits is an early sign that Teldrassil suffers from an unnatural taint. It leads researchers toward deeper investigations in Darnassus.",al={"teldrassil corruption","why is teldrassil sick","tree corruption"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Denalan want timberling seeds gathered?",a="Denalan has observed Teldrassil's nature elementals growing uncharacteristically violent, a worrying sign that something is amiss with the world tree itself. Believing the corruption stems from tainted soil, he hopes to nurture new seeds using specialized earth to cultivate calm, docile timberlings and prove the land can be healed.",al={"why denalan timberling seeds","denalan motive seeds","why does denalan need seeds"},it="motive",add="0bbca4e0"},{q="Why must you hunt down the timberlings around Lake Al'Ameth?",a="Timberlings are plant-like nature elementals that wander the shores of Lake Al'Ameth. Because they are intimately tied to the environment, they carry the seeds Denalan needs for his research. Unfortunately, their sudden fury makes gathering seeds peacefully impossible, forcing you to fight them to collect the samples.",al={"why kill timberlings","timberlings target","timberlings around lake al'ameth"},it="target",add="024ee5fc"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, timberlings are direct signs of Teldrassil's well-being. Seeing these gentle spirits turn feral is a chilling sign that their new home is unwell.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you have a deep affinity for nature spirits. Helping Denalan study them supports elemental balance without relying only on culling them.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As an herbalist, you can appreciate Denalan's botanical experiments on the delicate relationship between plant seeds and enriched soil."},kw={"botany","denalan","elementals","lake al'ameth","seeds","teldrassil","timberling"},rel={"npc:denalan","subzone:lake-al-ameth","zone:teldrassil","quest:940"},m={start="Denalan",level="9",faction="Alliance",id=918,ri={"Timberling Seed"}},src={"Timberling Seeds (Classic)"}}
E["quest:919"] = {t="quest",n="Timberling Sprouts",z="teldrassil",s="Around Lake Al'Ameth, Timberling Sprouts are spreading across Teldrassil. Denalan asks you to uproot them before they grow into hostile timberlings.",h="Around Lake Al'Ameth, Timberling Sprouts are spreading across Teldrassil.",sec={{t="Weeding Lake Al'Ameth",b="Corrupted sprouts are spreading along Lake Al'Ameth's banks. Denalan lives beside the lake and knows these young plants cannot be healed. Left alone, they quickly grow into aggressive, bark-covered timberlings that threaten wildlife and travelers. Uprooting the sprouts helps protect the grove.",sp=0},{t="Signs of a Deeper Taint",b="Denalan is troubled by how quickly new sprouts appear across Teldrassil. Their spread points to a sickness in the World Tree's roots and soil, and Denalan and the druids of Darnassus seek its cause.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are timberling sprouts?",a="Timberling sprouts are young forms of the elemental plant beings native to Teldrassil's boughs. Those growing along Lake Al'Ameth are tainted and quickly become hostile.",al={"what are timberlings","timberling sprout lore","what is a sprout"},it="item"},{q="Who is Denalan?",a="Denalan is an herbalist who lives in a camp near Lake Al'Ameth. He watches the bough's plants and studies changes and corruption on Teldrassil.",al={"who gives timberling sprouts","denalan lore","lake al'ameth questgiver"},it="identity"},{q="Why can't these sprouts simply be healed or purified?",a="Denalan finds the sprouts already tainted beyond healing when they surface. Uprooting them is the only practical way to keep them from becoming dangerous timberlings.",al={"can sprouts be saved","why destroy timberlings","are sprouts beyond help"},it="threat"},{q="Where are the sprouts found?",a="The sprouts grow along the muddy shores, shallows, and banks around Lake Al'Ameth in central Teldrassil.",al={"timberling sprout location","where to find sprouts","lake al'ameth sprouts"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What causes the timberlings to sprout so aggressively?",a="A corrupting influence in Teldrassil's soil and waters drives the unnatural spread of hostile timberlings. Young growth is tainted before it blooms, pointing to a blight in the World Tree.",al={"why are timberlings mad","what taints the sprouts","timberling corruption"},it="origin"},{q="What happens after clearing these sprouts?",a="Denalan investigates the sickness in the lake, examining soil, seeds, and water for the blight's source.",al={"next quest after sprouts","what follows timberling sprouts"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Denalan want the timberling sprouts cleared?",a="Denalan watches over Lake Al'Ameth and fears the sprouts are already too corrupt to save. If left alone, they will mature into violent, full-grown timberlings that endanger anyone walking the shores. By uprooting them while they are small, he hopes to keep the surrounding land clean and buy time to uncover the root cause of the taint spreading through Teldrassil's waters.",al={"denalan motive sprouts","why clear sprouts","why does denalan want sprouts"},it="motive",add="24c78c98"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a kaldorei, you know Teldrassil was meant to be a fresh sanctuary. Corruption near Lake Al'Ameth's sacred waters is a troubling omen.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you help guard nature's balance. Uprooting blighted sprouts is a sad duty that protects the wider ecosystem.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As an herbalist, you recognize how healthy plants should grow. These sprouts are diseased and twisted."},kw={"corruption","denalan","lake al'ameth","taint","teldrassil","timberling sprouts","timberlings","weeding"},rel={"npc:denalan","subzone:lake-al-ameth","quest:997","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Denalan",faction="Alliance",id=919,ri={"Timberling Sprout"}},src={"Timberling Sprouts"}}
E["quest:920"] = {t="quest",n="Tenaron's Summons",z="teldrassil",s="In Shadowglen, Tenaron's Summons calls you to Aldrassil. After helping Gilshalan Windwalker with woodland dangers, you are asked to meet Tenaron Stormgrip high in the great tree. The call draws you from local troubles toward the spiritual afflictions touching Teldrassil.",h="In Shadowglen, Tenaron's Summons calls you to Aldrassil.",sec={{t="A Call to the Boughs",b="Your work against the venomous spiders and corrupted wildlife in the glen has reached Tenaron Stormgrip. Gilshalan Windwalker tells you the elder has asked for your presence. Even night elves, with their long lives, know better than to keep an elder waiting atop Aldrassil.",sp=0},{t="Ascending Aldrassil",b="Tenaron waits in Aldrassil's highest chamber, looking across Shadowglen's boughs. Meeting him brings you into wider concerns of stewardship, including the cleansing of Teldrassil's moonwells and the corruption spreading through the young World Tree's ecosystem.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tenaron Stormgrip?",a="Tenaron Stormgrip is a night elf who lives in Aldrassil's highest chamber in Shadowglen. He oversees the glen's spiritual care and efforts to watch over and cleanse Teldrassil's sacred waters.",al={"who is tenaron","tenaron stormgrip lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where do I find Tenaron Stormgrip?",a="Tenaron Stormgrip waits in the highest room of Aldrassil, the great hollow tree in Shadowglen. Climb the winding ramps inside to reach his chamber near the crown.",al={"find tenaron","tenaron location","where is tenaron"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Tenaron summon me?",a="After you prove yourself against the blighted wildlife below, Tenaron gives you greater responsibilities. He asks you to investigate the sacred moonwells and test their waters for corruption.",al={"why summons","what does tenaron want"},it="purpose"},{q="What happens after this quest?",a="Meeting Tenaron leads into the Crown of the Earth storyline. He asks you to collect water samples from moonwells across Teldrassil and check the tree's health.",al={"next quest","what comes after tenaron's summons"},it="next_step"},{q="Who sends you to Tenaron?",a="Gilshalan Windwalker sends you to Tenaron after you help him with the venom-crazed Webwood spiders threatening Shadowglen's lower hollows.",al={"who gives the quest","gilshalan windwalker"},it="origin"},{q="What is Aldrassil?",a="Aldrassil is a great tree in Shadowglen, with a hollow trunk that holds the central settlement and training sanctuary for young night elves on Teldrassil.",al={"aldrassil lore","what is aldrassil"},it="place"},{q="Why does Gilshalan Windwalker send you to Tenaron?",a="Gilshalan is simply relaying a message from higher up. Having watched your progress and deeds resolving troubles in Shadowglen, he knows Tenaron Stormgrip has taken note of your capabilities and urgently requires your aid atop Aldrassil.",al={"gilshalan motive","why send me to tenaron","gilshalan windwalker summons"},it="motive",add="494cb76b"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, this call marks your coming of age among the kaldorei. You move from defending the woods to serving the elders who tend the World Tree.",["class:Druid"]="Meeting Tenaron Stormgrip helps you learn how druids watch over and maintain Teldrassil's balance."},kw={"aldrassil","gilshalan","shadowglen","stormgrip","summons","teldrassil","tenaron","windwalker"},rel={"npc:tenaron-stormgrip","subzone:aldrassil","quest:921","npc:gilshalan-windwalker","subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Gilshalan Windwalker",["end"]="Tenaron Stormgrip",level="5",faction="Alliance",id=920},src={"Tenaron's Summons"}}
E["quest:921"] = {t="quest",n="Crown of the Earth",z="teldrassil",s="At Aldrassil, Tenaron Stormgrip asks young night elves to draw sacred water before they leave Shadowglen. The rite recalls Mount Hyjal and the immortality their people gave up there.",h="At Aldrassil, Tenaron Stormgrip asks young night elves to draw sacred water before they leave Shadowglen.",sec={{t="A Lesson in Recent History",b="Before young night elves leave Shadowglen, their elders teach them what their people lost. At the Battle of Mount Hyjal, the kaldorei sacrificed the World Tree Nordrassil to defeat Archimonde and banish the Burning Legion. The blast cost them their ageless immortality and sacred shield. Tenaron Stormgrip teaches this history as he gives novices a rite, preparing them with humility and purpose for a changing world.",sp=0},{t="Waters of the Well",b="To complete the rite, you draw water from the moonwell north of Aldrassil with a crystal phial. Moonwell waters carry remnants of the ancient Well of Eternity. Druids channel their restorative power into the wild, while Sentinels honor the wells as tranquil shrines to Elune. The kaldorei remain wary: arcane sorcery is forbidden, and the wellspring that sustains their land recalls the reckless magic that nearly broke the world.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tenaron Stormgrip?",a="Tenaron Stormgrip is a night elf high in the upper boughs of Aldrassil in Shadowglen. He mentors young night elves nearing the end of basic training, giving them rites that teach their people's solemn history before they travel onward into Teldrassil.",al={"tenaron stormgrip","who gives crown of the earth","aldrassil druid npc"},it="identity"},{q="What is the purpose of collecting moonwell water?",a="Filling the crystal phial begins a journey that is both practical and ceremonial. Moonwell waters hold ancient magic that druids use to nourish the land, and the rite teaches young kaldorei their society's sacred obligations.",al={"why get moonwell water","filled crystal phial use","moonwell purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Why did the night elves lose their immortality?",a="During the Third War, the night elves unleashed the ancestral power woven into the World Tree Nordrassil to destroy Archimonde atop Mount Hyjal. The sacrifice destroyed the Legion's vanguard, but cost the night elves their eternal youth and immunity to disease.",al={"why are night elves mortal","what happened to immortality","nordrassil destruction"},it="history"},{q="Are moonwells considered dangerous?",a="Moonwells hold diluted essences linked to the Well of Eternity. Druids and priestesses channel their energies for healing, blessing, and communion with nature, while the kaldorei forbid arcane sorcery because of the catastrophes reckless magic caused in ancient history.",al={"are moonwells arcane","is moonwell water safe","well of eternity danger"},it="danger"},{q="Where does this quest chain lead next?",a="Returning the filled phial completes the opening lesson in the Crown of the Earth series. Tenaron sends you to Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar, who has you fill phials at other moonwells across Teldrassil for the druids of Darnassus and, in the end, Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm.",al={"what comes after crown of the earth","crown of the earth questline","next quest after tenaron"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Where is the moonwell for this quest located?",a="The moonwell lies a short walk north of Aldrassil's great boughs, among the woods of Shadowglen.",al={"where is the moonwell","shadowglen moonwell location","find crystal phial well"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Tenaron Stormgrip send you on this task?",a="Tenaron believes you cannot properly step into the wider world without understanding the recent, painful history of the kaldorei. The sacrifice at the Battle of Mount Hyjal shattered Nordrassil and cost the night elves their immortality, reshaping their entire existence. By sending you to the sacred moonwells to gather their waters, Tenaron uses each step of the journey to teach you how your people arrived at their current state on Teldrassil.",al={"tenaron stormgrip motive","why does tenaron want moonwell water","tenaron motive crown of the earth"},it="motive",add="b29aebae"},{q="What is the Filled Crystal Phial used for?",a="The Filled Crystal Phial holds water drawn directly from the moonwell north of Aldrassil. These waters contain traces of the ancient Well of Eternity, sacred to the Sentinels and utilized carefully by druids. Tenaron requires you to bring the filled phial back to him atop Aldrassil as a symbolic first step in a larger ritual duty that will guide your path across Teldrassil.",al={"filled crystal phial use","what is filled crystal phial for","purpose of filled crystal phial"},it="item",add="e84820be"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, this rite marks your passage out of Shadowglen. It ties your path to the sacrifice atop Mount Hyjal and your duty to safeguard Teldrassil.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you know moonwells as essential tools of the Cenarion circle, offering purified conduits of nature's energy to tend the forest's balance.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you honor Elune at moonwells, reflective shrines where the waters are consecrated beneath the Mother Moon's gaze."},kw={"aldrassil","crown of the earth","crystal phial","hyjal","moonwell","nordrassil","shadowglen","teldrassil","tenaron stormgrip"},rel={"npc:tenaron-stormgrip","subzone:aldrassil","quest:920","zone:teldrassil","topic:nordrassil","topic:druid","topic:elune","topic:burning-legion"},m={start="Tenaron Stormgrip",level="5",faction="Alliance",id=921,ri={"Filled Crystal Phial"}},src={"Crown of the Earth"}}
E["quest:927"] = {t="quest",n="The Moss-twined Heart",z="teldrassil",s="Near Lake Al'Ameth, Denalan studies a strange heart taken from Blackmoss the Fetid. Dark, oily moss covers the core, yet it keeps beating after being cut from the timberling.",h="Near Lake Al'Ameth, Denalan studies a strange heart taken from Blackmoss the Fetid.",sec={{t="A Beating Core",b="Blackmoss the Fetid's heart still pulses after being cut from the timberling. Dark, oily moss hides nearly all of the timberling's core, but a slow rhythm continues within it. That pulse points to a corruption reaching beyond ordinary rot in Teldrassil's wild plants.",sp=0},{t="Denalan's Examination",b="Denalan, a researcher of local flora near Lake Al'Ameth, takes a keen interest in the heart and recognizes its troubling corruption. Timberlings should be gentle beings tied to the boughs of the World Tree, yet this core bears a virulent blight. Troubled by what he sees and eager to understand it, Denalan plans to plant and study the organ, hoping to learn how foul moss takes root in the island's soil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the Moss-twined Heart come from?",a="The heart comes from Blackmoss the Fetid, a large, heavily corrupted timberling that wanders Teldrassil's wilderness.",al={"where do i get the heart","moss-twined heart drop","blackmoss the fetid heart"},it="origin"},{q="Why is the heart still beating?",a="Dark, oily moss appears to keep the heart alive with unnatural vitality. Though cut from the timberling, it continues a slow, steady beat.",al={"why does heart pulse","still beating heart","timberling heart beat"},it="power"},{q="Who is Denalan?",a="Denalan is a night elf naturalist who tends a nursery near Lake Al'Ameth. He devotes himself to studying Teldrassil's flora, its sproutings, and the creeping corruption affecting the island's timberlings.",al={"who is denalan","where is denalan","denalan location"},it="identity"},{q="What will Denalan do with the heart?",a="Denalan plans to plant the heart in an enchanted planter so it can sprout, isolating the foul moss and helping him uncover the cause of the blighted growth.",al={"what happens to the heart","planting the heart quest","denalan heart research"},it="purpose"},{q="What are timberlings supposed to be?",a="Timberlings are naturally peaceful plant elementals born of the forest. Dark forces and unnatural taint have driven many of them mad and aggressive across Teldrassil.",al={"what are timberlings","timberling lore","are timberlings evil"},it="people"},{q="Is the corruption on the heart magical or natural?",a="The oily, foul moss suggests an unnatural blight in Teldrassil's native plants, rather than ordinary decay in the wild.",al={"is the moss magic","source of foul moss","teldrassil moss blight"},it="danger"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a kaldorei, you see the young World Tree Teldrassil fostering tainted, aggressive timberlings like Blackmoss. Their blight is a sobering sign that your new home is troubled by a creeping sickness.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you take keen interest in a beating, blighted heart like this. You seek to learn whether its corruption can be purged or signals deeper rot.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As a student of plants, you can see the oily growth on this core is unnatural. It defies ordinary botanical traits by keeping a severed heart alive."},kw={"blackmoss the fetid","blight","corruption","denalan","lake al'ameth","moss-twined heart","teldrassil","timberling"},rel={"npc:denalan","quest:941","subzone:lake-al-ameth","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Moss-Twined Heart",["end"]="Denalan",faction="Alliance",id=927},src={"The Moss-twined Heart"}}
E["quest:928"] = {t="quest",n="Crown of the Earth",z="teldrassil",s="In Shadowglen, you set out with moonwell water for Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar. The journey carries you from secluded training into the wider work of protecting Teldrassil.",h="In Shadowglen, you set out with moonwell water for Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar.",sec={{t="Leaving the Glade",b="After tasting the enchanted water of Shadowglen's moonwell, you meet Tenaron Stormgrip at the crown of Aldrassil. He seals the gathered water in a larger vessel and sends you beyond the sheltered glade. The road runs south toward Dolanaar, through woods where danger has grown harder to predict.",sp=0},{t="The Road to Dolanaar",b="Dolanaar is the first major village beyond Shadowglen, along the cobblestone paths through central Teldrassil. Its own moonwell lies at the heart of the village. Corithras Moonrage, an elder who oversees preservation across the boughs, waits there. The vessel you bring places you in the wider effort to protect the World Tree.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What am I carrying to Dolanaar?",a="You carry the Partially Filled Vessel, holding sanctified water from Shadowglen's moonwell. Tenaron Stormgrip gathered your offering in it for Corithras Moonrage to use in ritual work across Teldrassil.",al={"what is the vessel","partially filled vessel lore","what water is this"},it="item"},{q="Who is Corithras Moonrage?",a="Corithras Moonrage is a night elf elder beside the moonwell in Dolanaar. He directs those who arrive in rites and investigations meant to sustain the World Tree.",al={"who is corithras","corithras moonrage role","where is corithras"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Tenaron send me away from Shadowglen?",a="Shadowglen gives you basic training, while Teldrassil's troubles reach across the boughs. After you prove yourself against local threats and honor the moonwells, Tenaron sends you to Dolanaar, where broader work awaits.",al={"why leave shadowglen","why go to dolanaar","tenaron sending me away"},it="motive"},{q="Where is the road to Dolanaar?",a="Follow the cobblestone path south from Aldrassil and through Shadowglen's gates. Keep to the road as it bends south and west, and it will bring you to Dolanaar.",al={"how to get to dolanaar","path to dolanaar","road out of shadowglen"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Tenaron warn about dangerous beasts?",a="Tenaron says dangerous beasts have roamed the forests of late. Wildlife has grown aggressive even within Teldrassil's sacred boughs, so leaving the paved trail puts you at risk.",al={"why are beasts dangerous","corrupted beasts teldrassil","stay on the road warning"},it="danger"},{q="What happens after reaching Dolanaar?",a="Corithras Moonrage takes the vessel and sends you to fill phials at other moonwells throughout Teldrassil. The work continues across the tree.",al={"what next after crown of the earth","dolanaar next quest","what does corithras do"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Tenaron Stormgrip send an adventurer instead of delivering the vessel himself?",a="Tenaron Stormgrip oversees the boughs of Aldrassil and tends to the sacred matters of Shadowglen, where young night elves first hone their arts. He cannot abandon his duties atop the great tree simply to carry couriered waters across Teldrassil. Dispatching promising initiates allows him to test your discipline and readiness for the wider world, while ensuring the sacred vessel reaches Corithras Moonrage without leaving Shadowglen unattended.",al={"why send me","why does tenaron need me","why not take vessel himself"},it="why_me",add="a4343de4"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a young Kaldorei, leaving Shadowglen is a rite of passage as you set out to serve your people.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, carrying the sanctified waters connects you to the effort to nurture and balance Teldrassil's growing ecosystem.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, carrying moonwell water consecrated by Elune's grace reflects your duty to tend to your community's spiritual health."},kw={"aldrassil","corithras moonrage","crown of the earth","dolanaar","moonwell","partially filled vessel","shadowglen","teldrassil","tenaron stormgrip"},rel={"quest:921","npc:corithras-moonrage","npc:tenaron-stormgrip","subzone:dolanaar","subzone:shadowglen","subzone:aldrassil","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf"},m={start="Tenaron Stormgrip",["end"]="Corithras Moonrage",level="5",faction="Alliance",id=928},src={"Crown of the Earth (2)"}}
E["quest:929"] = {t="quest",n="Crown of the Earth",z="teldrassil",s="Near Starbreeze Village, you draw sacred water for Darnassus. Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar asks young night elves to replenish the city's moonwell, and the work teaches the history behind their care for Teldrassil's great boughs.",h="Near Starbreeze Village, you draw sacred water for Darnassus.",sec={{t="Sustaining the Moonwells",b="You carry a jade phial made by druids to Starbreeze Village, where a lesser moonwell holds sanctified water. Its refined craft lets you draw and carry the luminous water without disturbing its purity. Darnassus's central moonwell depends on these scattered fonts, and the elders send initiates on foot so the city's fountains stay full of Elune's grace. The journey also teaches the young what it takes to nourish Teldrassil.",sp=0},{t="Echoes of the Third War",b="Corithras Moonrage tells you of the sorrow that followed the Battle of Mount Hyjal. The sacrifice of Nordrassil, the ancestral World Tree, cost the night elves their immortality. Illidan Stormrage was unleashed amid the ruin, while Shan'do Malfurion Stormrage disappeared. Grief and isolation marked the days that followed, as the kaldorei turned to Teldrassil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of drawing moonwell water?",a="Druids in Darnassus replenish the city's main moonwell with water from forest shrines, sustaining the sacred network across Teldrassil.",al={"why get moonwell water","moonwell water use","purpose of jade phial"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is the moonwell for this task located?",a="The moonwell lies just outside Starbreeze Village, east of Dolanaar along the forest path.",al={"where is the moonwell","starbreeze moonwell location","starbreeze village well"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Corithras Moonrage?",a="Corithras Moonrage is a night elf in Dolanaar who guides young adventurers through ritual duties and teaches the histories tied to Teldrassil's health.",al={"who gives the quest","corithras moonrage lore"},it="identity"},{q="What history does Corithras teach upon return?",a="Corithras recounts the aftermath of the Battle of Mount Hyjal: Nordrassil was sacrificed, kaldorei immortality ended, Illidan was unleashed, and Shan'do Malfurion Stormrage disappeared.",al={"what does corithras say","crown of the earth lore text"},it="history"},{q="Why do night elves feel lost after Mount Hyjal?",a="Nordrassil gave the night elves perpetual life and protection. They sacrificed its power to destroy Archimonde, losing their timeless existence and becoming mortal, directionless, and deeply vulnerable.",al={"why did elves lose immortality","what happened after hyjal"}},{q="What is a Shan'do?",a="Shan'do means “honored teacher” in Darnassian. It is an honorific for Malfurion Stormrage, the druids' supreme leader.",al={"what does shando mean","shando meaning"}},{q="Why does Corithras Moonrage want this done?",a="Corithras is carrying out vital duties for the Cenarion Circle while educating young night elves on their people's fragile state. Teldrassil's sacred waters require constant care and balance, and the druids in Darnassus depend on fresh water gathered from outlying moonwells across the boughs. In exchanging this service for history and guidance, Corithras ensures both that Darnassus's moonwell remains replenished and that you understand the heavy burdens your people bear following the Third War.",al={"corithras moonrage motive","why does corithras need water","corithras moonwell task"},it="motive",add="5a4296ad"},{q="What is the Filled Jade Phial for?",a="The Filled Jade Phial contains sacred water gathered from the moonwell near Starbreeze Village. Specially crafted to hold and preserve moonwell waters without diminishing their latent magical potency, it delivers replenishment to the druids of Darnassus, who draw upon the combined strength of Teldrassil's springs for their rituals and healing.",al={"filled jade phial purpose","what is the jade phial used for","filled jade phial"},it="item",add="0abe9d82"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you face the loss of immortality and the disappearance of Malfurion Stormrage. Drawing moonwell water is an essential lesson in your people's recent grief.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you know the moonwells as living reservoirs of nature and astral magic. Their waters bind your order's duties in Darnassus to Teldrassil's roots."},kw={"corithras moonrage","crown of the earth","dolanaar","jade phial","moonwell","nordrassil","starbreeze village","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:corithras-moonrage","subzone:dolanaar","subzone:starbreeze-village","zone:teldrassil","zone:darnassus","topic:nordrassil","topic:druid","topic:shan-do"},m={start="Corithras Moonrage",level="5",faction="Alliance",id=929,ri={"Filled Jade Phial"}},src={"Crown of the Earth (3)"}}
E["quest:930"] = {t="quest",n="The Glowing Fruit",z="teldrassil",s="The Glowing Fruit is a quest in Teldrassil initiated by discovering a strange fruited plant growing wild in the forest. Suspecting something unnatural, young adventurers deliver the luminescent specimen to the herbalist Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth for study.",h="The Glowing Fruit is a quest in Teldrassil initiated by discovering a strange fruited plant growing wild in...",sec={{t="An Unnatural Harvest",b="While traversing the misty boughs of Teldrassil, explorers occasionally stumble across curious, luminous flora bearing large, round fruit. Given the delicate balance of the World Tree and the recent strange behaviors among the island's wildlife, unusual botanical specimens demand careful investigation. Convinced that the strange growth should not be ignored, adventurers pluck the radiant harvest to bring to someone versed in the flora of the wild.",sp=0},{t="Denalan's Investigation",b="At Lake Al'Ameth, the knowledgeable gardener and herbalist Denalan receives the glowing fruit with both fascination and concern. He notes that the specimen appears exotic, speculating that its seeds might have arrived from distant lands across the sea, perhaps even the Eastern Kingdoms. More troubling to Denalan is how the foreign seed reacted with the soil of Teldrassil itself—and when he plants its seeds in his prepared soil, hostile boglings rise from the earth.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the Strange Fruited Plant found?",a="The Strange Fruited Plant grows wild out in the wilds of Teldrassil, tucked among the undergrowth away from the major settlements. Interacting with the plant yields the Glowing Fruit and begins the quest.",al={"where do i find the plant","strange fruited plant location","how to start the glowing fruit"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Denalan?",a="Denalan is a night elf herbalist and botanist stationed along the shores of Lake Al'Ameth. He spends his days tending the soil, studying regional flora, and monitoring the strange environmental disturbances affecting Teldrassil.",al={"where is denalan","denalan npc","who turns in glowing fruit"},it="identity"},{q="Why does the fruit glow?",a="The cause of the fruit's glow is not established. Denalan considers it an unusual specimen and plans to study it.",al={"why is the fruit glowing","what is wrong with the fruit"},it="origin"},{q="What happens when you hand the fruit to Denalan?",a="Bring the glowing fruit to Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth for examination. His findings and the result of the delivery are revealed when you return.",al={"what spawns after quest","bogling ambush"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Where does Denalan think this plant came from?",a="Denalan suspects the plant's seeds may have originated far away across the Great Sea, carried to Kalimdor from the distant eastern continent of Azeroth.",al={"where did seeds come from","fruit origin"},it="origin"},{q="Does this quest connect to other ecological problems on Teldrassil?",a="Yes. It ties into Denalan's broader research into why the boughs of Teldrassil and its local woodland creatures, like the timberlings, are becoming increasingly agitated and unnatural.",al={"teldrassil corruption","lake al'ameth problems"},it="threat"},{q="Why take the glowing fruit to Denalan?",a="The Strange Fruited Plant is mindless flora, but its eerie luminescence and bizarre appearance immediately stand out against Teldrassil's natural flora. Recognizing that such an unnatural anomaly warrants investigation, you take the initiative to deliver a specimen to Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth, knowing the botanist is actively studying the island's strange ecological disturbances.",al={"why denalan fruit","strange fruited plant motive","why pick glowing fruit"},it="motive",add="a8a1e1a2"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For druids dedicated to preserving nature's balance, discovering foreign, volatile flora thriving unnaturally in Teldrassil's sacred boughs is an immediate red flag.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Herbalists will appreciate Denalan's botanical insight into how foreign seeds can cross continents and mutate when exposed to enchanted soils.",["race:NightElf"]="Kaldorei youth learn through Denalan that even the young soil of their new home, Teldrassil, is susceptible to unpredictable foreign blights."},kw={"boglings","denalan","glowing fruit","herbalism","lake al'ameth","strange fruited plant","teldrassil","timberlings"},rel={"npc:denalan","subzone:lake-al-ameth","zone:teldrassil","quest:940"},m={start="Strange Fruited Plant",["end"]="Denalan",faction="Alliance",id=930},src={"The Glowing Fruit"}}
E["quest:931"] = {t="quest",n="The Shimmering Frond",z="teldrassil",s="Across Teldrassil, a curious plant shimmers among the roots and canopy. Travelers bring a cutting to Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth, hoping the botanist can explain its origin.",h="Across Teldrassil, a curious plant shimmers among the roots and canopy.",sec={{t="A Strange Glow",b="In Teldrassil's boughs, a strange plant catches the light. Its fronds twist with a pulsing shimmer unlike the island's usual foliage. The glow draws the eye amid Teldrassil's young forest life.",sp=0},{t="Denalan's Discovery",b="At Lake Al'Ameth, Denalan recognizes the cutting as a plant from beyond northern Kalimdor. He last saw one decades ago, during a journey to the Swamp of Sorrows in the Eastern Kingdoms. How its seed crossed the ocean and grew so large on the World Tree puzzles him. Denalan begins cultivating the sample and testing it.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does the strange plant originally come from?",a="Denalan says the plant comes from the Swamp of Sorrows in the Eastern Kingdoms. He last saw a living specimen in those marshes decades ago.",al={"frond origin","where is frond from","swamp plant"},it="origin"},{q="Who is Denalan?",a="Denalan is a night elf botanist and herbalist near Lake Al'Ameth on Teldrassil. He studies and tends the island's growing plant life, experimenting with foreign seeds and planters.",al={"denalan lore","who is denalan"},it="identity"},{q="Why is this plant growing on Teldrassil?",a="No one knows how the plant reached Teldrassil. Denalan wonders how a seed crossed the Great Sea from the Eastern Kingdoms, then took root and grew large in Teldrassil's soil.",al={"how did it get to teldrassil","why is frond here"},it="why_here"},{q="What happens after giving the frond to Denalan?",a="Denalan places the specimen in his planter at Lake Al'Ameth and begins testing it. Several fronds quickly sprout and blossom, giving him more to study.",al={"next quest","denalan test","sprouted fronds"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Does this plant cause corruption in Teldrassil?",a="No. The plant appears to be an unusual exotic breed in the wrong place, rather than a source of corruption.",al={"is frond corrupted","corrupted plant"},it="threat"},{q="Why take a frond from the Strange Fronded Plant to Denalan?",a="The plant itself has no conscious motive; it is merely an unusual, pulsating specimen growing wild in Teldrassil's boughs. You recognize its strange, shimmering aura as something exotic and potentially unnatural to the great tree, prompting you to harvest a cutting for Denalan, the resident botanist studying rare flora at Lake Al'Ameth.",al={"strange fronded plant motive","why bring frond to denalan","why take frond"},it="motive",add="add2b0dd"}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Herbalists and plant enthusiasts may wonder how a plant from the Swamp of Sorrows thrives so far from its native marshland.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you may watch how foreign plant life affects Teldrassil's young canopy.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf tending your new home, you can see how Denalan's experiments reveal the resilience of Teldrassil's soil."},kw={"botany","denalan","lake al'ameth","shimmering frond","sprouted fronds","strange fronded plant","swamp of sorrows","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:denalan","quest:2399","subzone:lake-al-ameth","zone:teldrassil","zone:swampofsorrows"},m={start="Strange Fronded Plant",["end"]="Denalan",faction="Alliance",id=931},src={"The Shimmering Frond"}}
E["quest:932"] = {t="quest",n="Twisted Hatred",z="teldrassil",s="Tallonkai Swiftroot sends trusted champions into Fel Rock to stop Lord Melenas. The satyr has rallied the cave’s grell into an organized force, threatening night elf settlements near Teldrassil.",h="Tallonkai Swiftroot sends trusted champions into Fel Rock to stop Lord Melenas.",sec={{t="A Bitter Disgrace",b="Satyrs recall an ancient betrayal that still stains kaldorei history. They were Highborne who gave themselves to the Burning Legion during the War of the Ancients. Now one has made a foothold on Teldrassil, the young World Tree meant to be a sanctuary. For defenders like Tallonkai Swiftroot, that presence is a bitter disgrace.",sp=0},{t="The Threat at Fel Rock",b="Fel Rock lies north of the nearby paths, its corrupted caverns crawling with feral grell. Lord Melenas has gathered the chaotic creatures into a hostile force under his will. Tallonkai fears what the satyr may unleash on the World Tree’s boughs, and demands a swift, quiet end. He wants Melenas eliminated and his severed head brought back.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lord Melenas?",a="Lord Melenas is a satyr who has claimed Fel Rock in northern Teldrassil. He commands aggressive grell warriors and schemes to spread corruption through the World Tree.",al={"lord melenas","who is melenas","fel rock boss"},it="target"},{q="Where can I find Lord Melenas?",a="Lord Melenas lurks deep within Fel Rock, north of Dolanaar in Teldrassil. Grell and other corrupted creatures surround him.",al={"melenas location","where is melenas","how to find fel rock"},gp=true},{q="Why does Tallonkai Swiftroot want this kept secret?",a="Satyrs recall the night elves’ ancient betrayal during the War of the Ancients. A satyr’s bold presence within the young World Tree is a disgrace, and Tallonkai wants to resolve it without widespread panic.",al={"why secret","why must this stay between us","tallonkai secret"},it="motive"},{q="What is the relationship between satyrs and grell?",a="Grell are small, mischievous, naturally corrupted wild creatures found across Teldrassil. Satyrs can bully or bend these lesser creatures to serve their ambitions.",al={"grell and satyrs","why are grell following melenas","satyr grell connection"},it="ties"},{q="Why are there satyrs on Teldrassil in the first place?",a="Teldrassil was grown only a few years ago, and corruption and dark beings quickly reached the island despite the druids’ hopes for a clean sanctuary. Satyrs slipped in and made footholds in shadowy places like Fel Rock.",al={"satyrs on teldrassil","how did satyrs get here","teldrassil corruption"},it="history"},{q="Who is Tallonkai Swiftroot?",a="Tallonkai Swiftroot is a night elf guardian stationed near Dolanaar. He watches for threats to Teldrassil and sends adventurers to deal with nearby pockets of corruption.",al={"tallonkai","who gives twisted hatred"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Tallonkai Swiftroot need Melenas' Head?",a="Tallonkai Swiftroot asks for the severed head of Lord Melenas as irrefutable proof that the satyr has truly been slain. With Lord Melenas dead and his head in hand, Tallonkai can rest assured that the foul threat lurking right beside Shadowglen has been eliminated in secret, allowing him to put the humiliating matter behind him without raising alarm among the elders.",al={"melenas head purpose","why bring back melenas head","what is melenas head for"},it="item",add="84ee0888"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you face an ancient reminder of your ancestors’ fall to demonic ambition. Defeating Lord Melenas is a duty to the World Tree and an act of ancestral penance.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you find Melenas and his corrupted grell poisoning the fragile balance of Teldrassil’s young wilderness."},kw={"fel rock","grell","lord melenas","satyr","tallonkai swiftroot","teldrassil","twisted hatred"},rel={"npc:tallonkai-swiftroot","subzone:fel-rock","topic:satyr","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Tallonkai Swiftroot",faction="Alliance",id=932,ri={"Melenas' Head"}},src={"Twisted Hatred"}}
E["quest:933"] = {t="quest",n="Crown of the Earth",z="teldrassil",s="Corithras Moonrage sends you to the Pools of Arlithrien for water as Gnarlpine furbolgs turn violent. His account of Teldrassil begins with Malfurion Stormrage's disappearance after the Third War.",h="Corithras Moonrage sends you to the Pools of Arlithrien for water as Gnarlpine furbolgs turn violent.",sec={{t="A Perilous Moonwell",b="Corithras Moonrage sends you with a tourmaline phial to a moonwell southeast of Darnassus's entrance, along the Pools of Arlithrien. The Gnarlpine furbolgs, once peaceful, now lash out with sudden violence. They ambush travelers and harry Sentinel patrols across the region. What seemed like isolated skirmishes has become a threat to the night elves' new home.",sp=0},{t="Fandral Staghelm's Ambition",b="When you return with the filled phial, Corithras tells you how Teldrassil came to be. After the Third War, Shan'do Malfurion Stormrage vanished, leaving the Cenarion druids without a leader and divided. Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm took the mantle of leadership in his absence. He urged the Circle of Ancients in Darkshore to set aside their mourning. The night elves, he argued, had to regain their lost immortality and heal their civilization by planting a vast new World Tree.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the moonwell for this quest?",a="The moonwell lies southeast of Darnassus's main entrance, along the southern shores of the Pools of Arlithrien.",al={"arlithrien moonwell","moonwell location","where to fill phial"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are the Gnarlpine furbolgs attacking?",a="The Gnarlpine furbolgs, once a peaceful kin of bear-men, have been consumed by a dark, mindless rage across Teldrassil. Sentinels first dismissed the attacks as isolated incidents, but they have spread into a constant danger to nearby settlements and patrols.",al={"furbolgs mad","gnarlpine aggressive","why furbolgs attack"},it="conflict"},{q="What happened to Malfurion Stormrage?",a="Shan'do Malfurion Stormrage vanished without explanation after the Third War. The Cenarion druids and night elf leaders do not know what became of him.",al={"where is malfurion","what happened to stormrage","malfurion missing"},it="history"},{q="Who decided to plant Teldrassil?",a="With Malfurion missing, Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm took the lead among the druids. He persuaded the Circle of Ancients in Darkshore to raise a new World Tree, saying the kaldorei needed it to rebuild and regain the immortality lost with Nordrassil's destruction.",al={"who made teldrassil","staghelm world tree","why was teldrassil grown"},it="leader"},{q="Why does Corithras Moonrage want this done?",a="Corithras Moonrage is investigating the sacred moonwells across Teldrassil to assess and tend to the health of the World Tree. While he guides you through these rituals, he is also sharing the fraught history of Teldrassil's planting—hoping you understand both the sacred duties of your people and the troubling signs spreading across their new home.",al={"why does corithras want moonwell water","corithras motive","why crown of the earth"},it="motive",add="f2628340"},{q="What is the Filled Tourmaline Phial for?",a="The phial holds pure water drawn from the moonwell near the Pools of Arlithrien. Corithras requires samples from Teldrassil's various moonwells to monitor the waters nourishing the World Tree and to conduct the rites needed to keep the land's spiritual balance intact amidst rising corruption.",al={"filled tourmaline phial purpose","why fill tourmaline phial","tourmaline phial moonwell"},it="item",add="21308da4"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you hear how Teldrassil came to be after Malfurion's sudden disappearance, and the political choice behind its planting.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you hear how Fandral Staghelm's leadership left the Cenarion Circle divided as he pressed to regain the night elves' ancient immortality."},kw={"corithras moonrage","dolanaar","fandral staghelm","gnarlpine","malfurion stormrage","pools of arlithrien","tourmaline phial"},rel={"npc:corithras-moonrage","subzone:pools-of-arlithrien","subzone:dolanaar","npc:fandral-staghelm","topic:furbolg","topic:druid","topic:sentinels","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Corithras Moonrage",level="9",faction="Alliance",id=933,ri={"Filled Tourmaline Phial"}},src={"Crown of the Earth (4)"}}
E["quest:934"] = {t="quest",n="Crown of the Earth",z="teldrassil",s="At the Oracle Glade, Corithras Moonrage sends you to gather water from Teldrassil’s sacred moonwell. The journey reveals the truth behind the World Tree’s creation.",h="At the Oracle Glade, Corithras Moonrage sends you to gather water from Teldrassil’s sacred moonwell.",sec={{t="The Oracle Glade",b="Corithras Moonrage sends you northwest across Teldrassil to the Oracle Glade. Beneath the Oracle Tree’s great boughs lies the first and most powerful moonwell raised on the island. You draw water into an Amethyst Phial from its sacred pool. The moonwell is the sanctuary where druids and the tree itself watch over the health of their new homeland.",sp=0},{t="The Denied Blessing",b="When you return the phial to Dolanaar, Corithras tells you what went wrong with Archdruid Fandral Staghelm’s design. After Nordrassil was sacrificed at Mount Hyjal, Staghelm planted Teldrassil to restore night elf immortality and asked the Dragon Aspects to bless it. Nozdormu the Timeless One refused, rebuking Staghelm for his arrogance. Queen Alexstrasza also withheld her blessing, the Aspect of Life’s gift. Without it, Teldrassil’s growth became volatile and imperfect, leaving the tree vulnerable to deep corruption.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the Oracle Glade moonwell located?",a="The Oracle Glade moonwell lies in northwestern Teldrassil, beneath the great boughs of the Oracle Tree and directly north of the main road to Darnassus.",al={"where is oracle glade","oracle glade moonwell location","oracle well"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Corithras Moonrage?",a="Corithras Moonrage is a night elf keeper stationed at Dolanaar. He guides young defenders across Teldrassil to sample its moonwells and teaches the history of the tree’s flawed beginnings.",al={"corithras","who is corithras moonrage"},it="identity"},{q="Did Teldrassil restore night elf immortality?",a="No. Teldrassil gave the night elves a new home, but their immortality was not restored after Nordrassil’s sacrifice during the Third War.",al={"are night elves immortal","teldrassil immortality","do elves live forever again"},it="power"},{q="What is the purpose of collecting water from the Oracle Glade?",a="The moonwell beneath the Oracle Tree is the island’s first and most powerful. Its water lets Corithras assess Teldrassil’s spiritual and natural health.",al={"why get oracle water","amethyst phial purpose"},it="item"},{q="Why does Corithras Moonrage want this done?",a="Corithras Moonrage is guiding you through the sacred moonwells of Teldrassil to impart the true history of the new World Tree. By sending you under the boughs of the Oracle Tree to draw water from Teldrassil's first and most powerful well, he ensures you commune with its deep wisdom firsthand before he reveals why the boughs remain troubled and barren of immortality.",al={"why does corithras want the water","corithras motive","why send to oracle glade"},it="motive",add="28d6c4e0"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you hear of your people’s hopes for Teldrassil after Nordrassil’s sacrifice during the Third War.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you see the divide between Fandral Staghelm’s forceful ambitions and the natural balance traditionally kept by Malfurion Stormrage.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you learn why blight and creature madness trouble Teldrassil, the Alliance’s newest capital territory."},kw={"alexstrasza","amethyst phial","corithras moonrage","fandral staghelm","immortality","moonwell","nozdormu","oracle glade","oracle tree","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:corithras-moonrage","subzone:oracle-glade","zone:teldrassil","subzone:dolanaar","topic:nordrassil","topic:druid","topic:night-elf","zone:darnassus"},m={start="Corithras Moonrage",level="11",faction="Alliance",id=934,ri={"Filled Amethyst Phial"}},src={"Crown of the Earth (5)"}}
E["quest:935"] = {t="quest",n="Crown of the Earth",z="teldrassil",s="In Teldrassil, moonwell waters are gathered to tend the World Tree’s sickness. The rites lead to Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm in Darnassus, where concern grows over a tree raised without blessings.",h="In Teldrassil, moonwell waters are gathered to tend the World Tree’s sickness.",sec={{t="A Flawed Genesis",b="Teldrassil rose after the Third War to give the night elves a new home and restore their lost immortality. The Great Aspects Alexstrasza and Nozdormu withheld their blessings and refused to sanction its creation. Without their divine protection, sickness spreads through the tree. Strange creatures emerge from its boughs, and once-peaceful furbolg tribes fall into madness.",sp=0},{t="Delivery to the Arch Druid",b="Corithras Moonrage sends young adventurers to gather water from moonwells across Teldrassil, hoping to study and soothe the tree’s ailments. He gathers the samples into one vessel and sends you deep into Darnassus, to the Cenarion Enclave. Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm, who shaped Teldrassil, sees the spreading corruption as a burden he alone must solve.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Fandral Staghelm want this moonwell water?",a="Fandral Staghelm wants the moonwell samples to study and address the corruption spreading through the World Tree. As the leader who championed Teldrassil’s planting, he bears responsibility for finding a remedy for the strange beasts and maddened furbolgs in its canopy.",al={"fandral water purpose","why does fandral need the vessel","what is the water for"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is Teldrassil plagued by corruption and crazed beasts?",a="Teldrassil suffers corruption and strange beasts because it was planted without the blessings of Alexstrasza the Life-Binder or Nozdormu the Timeless. Unlike the ancient World Tree Nordrassil, it lacks the protection of those primal dragon aspects, leaving its growth flawed and allowing malignancies to warp nearby wildlife and furbolgs.",al={"why is teldrassil sick","teldrassil corruption","why are furbolgs mad"},it="threat"},{q="Where is Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm located?",a="Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm is in the Cenarion Enclave in Darnassus. You can find him atop the central druid pavilion, overlooking the enclave’s sacred groves.",al={"where is fandral","fandral staghelm location","how to find fandral"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Corithras Moonrage?",a="Corithras Moonrage is a night elf stationed at Dolanaar who sends young adventurers to fill phials at Teldrassil’s moonwells. He pours their waters into one vessel and directs couriers to deliver it to Arch Druid Staghelm in Darnassus.",al={"who gives crown of the earth","corithras role","corithras moonrage"},it="identity"},{q="What happens after completing this quest?",a="You deliver the filled vessel to Fandral Staghelm, ending the main Crown of the Earth chain in Teldrassil. He accepts the water curtly and turns back to the wider threats facing the night elf homeland.",al={"crown of the earth follow up","what comes after crown of the earth 6","next quest after crown of the earth"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why is Fandral Staghelm so dismissive upon receiving the vessel?",a="Fandral Staghelm is proud and impatient, and he bears the burden of leading the Cenarion Circle while Malfurion Stormrage is absent. He disdains administrative setbacks and slow messengers, believing Teldrassil’s survival rests on his shoulders.",al={"why is fandral rude","fandral personality","is fandral always grumpy"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Corithras Moonrage want the vessel brought to Fandral?",a="Corithras is deeply worried about the growing sickness infecting Teldrassil. Because the World Tree grew without the vital blessings of the Aspects Alexstrasza and Nozdormu, strange beasts have risen from the soil and once-peaceful furbolgs have turned violently mad. Corithras believes Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm is actively researching a remedy to purge this spreading corruption, so he urgently combines the water samples you collected across the boughs and sends you to deliver them directly to Darnassus.",al={"corithras motive","why send moonwell water","why does corithras want this done"},it="motive",add="d62362b9"},{q="Why does Corithras Moonrage send you instead of going himself?",a="Corithras remains stationed at Dolanaar to oversee local matters and monitor the troubling anomalies disturbing Teldrassil's lower boughs. You have personally journeyed to the various moonwells to gather the water phials, proving your stamina and dedication. Entrusting you with the combined vessel allows Corithras to keep watch over Dolanaar while ensuring Fandral Staghelm receives the samples in Darnassus without further delay.",al={"why send player to fandral","why me corithras","why doesn't corithras deliver the vessel"},it="why_me",add="01febe86"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see the worry beneath your new home: Teldrassil was planted in pride without the Dragon Aspects’ blessings, and its sickness threatens your people’s fresh start.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, carrying moonwell waters brings you before Fandral Staghelm, Arch Druid of the Cenarion Circle. His presence reveals the fierce political and spiritual divide among druids while Malfurion is absent.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see Darnassus as a capital of ancient mystery, while the corrupted wilderness around it shows that peril reaches the night elves even on their sacred ground."},kw={"alexstrasza","cenarion enclave","corithras moonrage","crown of the earth","darnassus","fandral staghelm","moonwell","nozdormu","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:929","npc:fandral-staghelm","npc:corithras-moonrage","zone:teldrassil","zone:darnassus","subzone:cenarion-enclave","topic:druid","topic:night-elf"},m={start="Corithras Moonrage",["end"]="Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm",level="11",faction="Alliance",id=935},src={"Crown of the Earth (6)"}}
E["quest:937"] = {t="quest",n="The Enchanted Glade",z="teldrassil",s="Bloodfeather harpies threaten the Oracle Glade on northwestern Teldrassil, where Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak guards the ancient Oracle Tree. After harpies kill a runner bound for Darnassus, Arynia calls for their nests to be thinned and their belts brought back as proof.",h="Bloodfeather harpies threaten the Oracle Glade on northwestern Teldrassil, where Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak...",sec={{t="A Glade Under Siege",b="Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak watches over the Oracle Glade with an escort of warriors. The sacred retreat centers on the colossal Oracle Tree, an ancient rooted among Teldrassil's boughs. Bloodfeather harpies have spread through the surrounding canopy, nesting in the hollows and threatening anyone who comes near.",sp=0},{t="Severed Lines to Darnassus",b="A runner carrying an urgent report from the Oracle Tree never reaches Darnassus. Bloodfeather harpies ambush and kill the messenger before the runner can leave the glade. Arynia calls on you to thin their flock and bring back Bloodfeather belts as proof that their nests have been weakened.",sp=0},{t="A Summons from the Tree",b="The Oracle Tree sends a piece of its enchanted bark as its nearby nests are thinned. The ancient seeks an emissary to carry its message to the high leadership of the kaldorei.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why are harpies attacking the Oracle Glade?",a="The Bloodfeather clan nests across northern Teldrassil, and its harpies have surrounded the Oracle Tree. They guard their roosts fiercely and attack anyone traveling to or from the sacred glade.",al={"harpies in oracle glade","why bloodfeather attack","oracle tree harpies"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak?",a="Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak is an officer stationed with a modest vanguard in the Oracle Glade. She guards the Oracle Tree from nearby harpies and works to restore contact with Darnassus.",al={"arynia cloudsbreak","who gives the enchanted glade","cloudsbreak lore"},it="identity"},{q="What happened to the runner sent to Darnassus?",a="Bloodfeather harpies ambushed and killed the runner carrying a report from the Oracle Tree to Darnassus along the glade paths, before the messenger reached safety.",al={"oracle tree messenger","dead runner darnassus"},it="history"},{q="What is the Oracle Tree?",a="The Oracle Tree is a massive, sentient ancient rooted in the Oracle Glade. It watches over the boughs of the World Tree and sends wisdom and warnings to the night elf leadership.",al={"oracle tree teldrassil","who is the oracle tree"},it="place"},{q="What proof does Sentinel Cloudsbreak require?",a="Sentinel Cloudsbreak asks you to bring back six Bloodfeather belts from slain harpies as proof that their roosts around the glade have been thinned.",al={"bloodfeather belt quest","how many belts","quest proof"},it="item"},{q="What happens after culling the harpies?",a="After the nearby harpies are thinned, the Oracle Tree sheds a piece of its bark. You can carry the ancient's long-delayed message toward Darnassus.",al={"next quest after enchanted glade","what does oracle tree do next"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak want this done?",a="Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak was dispatched with a small detachment of Sentinels to defend the sacred Oracle Tree. Harpies have nested throughout the glade, hemming in the defenders and even slaughtering a courier sent to Darnassus with vital reports. Arynia cannot leave her defensive post unguarded, so she needs an adventurer to strike directly at the nests and push back the flock before the glade is overwhelmed.",al={"why kill the harpies","arynia cloudsbreak motive","why protect the oracle tree"},it="motive",add="2b035f45"},{q="Who are the Bloodfeather harpies threatening the glade?",a="The Bloodfeather harpies are vicious, avian predators that have roosted across the northwestern reaches of Teldrassil. Aggressive and territorial, they have built nests encircling the Oracle Glade, cutting off communication with Darnassus and seeking to drive away or slaughter the night elf protectors guarding the ancient tree.",al={"who are the harpies","bloodfeather harpies teldrassil","why are harpies here"},it="target",add="164cdda3"},{q="Why can't Sentinel Cloudsbreak deal with the harpies herself?",a="Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak leads only a small contingent of Sentinels stationed at the Oracle Tree. With their messenger already dead and harpies encircling the position, her remaining troops must stay grounded to guard the sacred tree from ambush. Taking the offensive into the harpy rookeries requires capable, unattached travelers willing to venture into hostile nests.",al={"why does arynia need my help","why can't the sentinels kill the harpies","why me enchanted glade"},it="why_me",add="3f052dc4"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, defending the World Tree's ancient spirits and protecting the Sentinels from harpy attacks is a solemn duty.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, helping the Sentinels secure Teldrassil's sacred groves strengthens ties with the night elf leadership in nearby Darnassus.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you hold sentient ancients in great reverence. Clearing harpies that threaten the Oracle Tree helps protect the glade's natural balance."},kw={"arynia cloudsbreak","bloodfeather","darnassus","harpies","oracle glade","oracle tree","sentinel","teldrassil","the enchanted glade"},rel={"subzone:oracle-glade","npc:sentinel-arynia-cloudsbreak","quest:940","quest:952","zone:teldrassil","topic:sentinels","zone:darnassus"},m={start="Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak",level="11",faction="Alliance",id=937,ri={"Bloodfeather Belt"}},src={"The Enchanted Glade (Classic)"}}
E["quest:938"] = {t="quest",n="Mist",z="teldrassil",s="In Teldrassil's shaded boughs, Mist lies wounded and separated from her companion. She needs a safe path back to Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak at a nearby moon well.",h="In Teldrassil's shaded boughs, Mist lies wounded and separated from her companion.",sec={{t="A Wounded Companion",b="A gray sabercat named Mist lies wounded among Teldrassil's undergrowth. Deep slashes mark her back and belly. Her blue eyes are bright, and she stays calm rather than acting like a feral beast. She looks to friendly travelers for guidance and protection.",sp=0},{t="The Price of Ambush",b="Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak and Mist were patrolling near the Oracle Tree when witches ambushed them and drove them apart. Arynia believed her beloved companion had died. Grieving, she withdrew to a nearby moon well and hoped Mist had survived.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Mist?",a="Mist is the loyal gray sabercat companion of Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak. She lies injured in Teldrassil's forests after an ambush separated her from Arynia.",al={"mist cat","what is mist","who is the sabercat"},it="identity"},{q="Who injured Mist?",a="Witches in Teldrassil's woods ambushed Mist and Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak, separating them and slashing Mist's back and belly.",al={"who hurt mist","why is mist bleeding","witches ambush mist"},it="threat"},{q="Where should Mist be escorted?",a="Bring Mist safely to Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak, who waits beside a moon well near the Oracle Tree.",al={"where do i take mist","mist turn in","mist destination"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Who is Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak?",a="Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak is a night elf Sentinel and Mist's companion. She waits at the moon well near the Oracle Tree.",al={"arynia cloudsbreak","cloudsbreak","mist owner"},it="people"},{q="Why are night elf Sentinels bonded with sabercats?",a="For millennia, night elf Sentinels have fought beside Kalimdor's great cats. The sabercats serve as fierce partners in skirmishes, scouts among shadowed boughs, and trusted lifelong companions.",al={"night elf cat companions","sentinel sabercats","why sabercats"},it="ties"},{q="Where is the Oracle Tree in relation to this rescue?",a="The Oracle Tree stands in northwestern Teldrassil. A nearby moon well provides holy waters, and Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak tends to her duties there.",al={"oracle tree location","moon well mist"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Mist need your help?",a="Mist is badly wounded with deep lacerations across her back and stomach, separated from her companion Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak. Weakened and stranded alone in the forest, she cannot safely navigate the perils of Teldrassil on her own to reach the safety of the moon well without your protection.",al={"why help mist","mist motive","why does mist need an escort"},it="motive",add="1795c253"},{q="Why does Mist rely on you instead of saving herself?",a="Mist is too gravely injured to fight through the hostile woods or make the long journey back unassisted. Being a beast separated from her Sentinel, she has no nearby allies or guards to turn to; when you happen upon her, she recognizes you as a friendly presence and places her trust in your ability to guide and shield her.",al={"why me mist","why cant mist escape alone","why does mist follow you"},it="why_me",add="94db0917"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know the bond between Sentinels and sabercats is central to your warfare and forest lore. Bringing Mist home honors that ancient companionship.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you recognize the fierce devotion and bright gaze in Mist's eyes. Her safe return to her companion is a matter of pride.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can aid the Sentinels in Teldrassil and build goodwill between the young Alliance and the kaldorei who defend the world tree."},kw={"arynia cloudsbreak","mist","moon well","oracle tree","sabercat","sentinel","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:sentinel-arynia-cloudsbreak","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Mist",["end"]="Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak",faction="Alliance",id=938},src={"Mist (quest)"}}
E["quest:940"] = {t="quest",n="Teldrassil",z="teldrassil",s="After the harpies are driven back, Arynia Cloudsbreak sends you with a report to Darnassus. The inscribed bark tells Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm about the boughs and the corruption still troubling the World Tree.",h="After the harpies are driven back, Arynia Cloudsbreak sends you with a report to Darnassus.",sec={{t="A Messenger to the Stone City",b="Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak entrusts you with a piece of inscribed bark after you clear the harpies from their nests in the Oracle Glade. The Oracle Tree watches over the forest, and with the harpies gone, Arynia can send word to the kaldorei leadership. You carry her report through the wilderness to Darnassus, the great forest of stone, and deliver it to Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm.",sp=0},{t="Staghelm's Ambition and Frustration",b="Fandral Staghelm receives the report with mixed feelings. He is grateful to hear that the harpies have been pushed back, but the report shows how one threat gives way to another across Teldrassil. Staghelm championed the planting of the new World Tree to reclaim the night elves' lost immortality. The afflictions in its boughs remind him that his work remains far from finished.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the quest 'Teldrassil'?",a="You carry Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak's report from the Oracle Tree to Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm in Darnassus. The inscribed bark bears news of the tree after you drive back the harpies.",al={"teldrassil quest objective","what does this quest do","teldrassil delivery"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak?",a="Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak is a night elf Sentinel stationed near the Oracle Tree in Teldrassil's wilds. She watches regional threats, including the Bloodfeather harpies, and coordinates forest defenses with Darnassus.",al={"arynia cloudsbreak lore","who starts teldrassil quest"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Arynia call Darnassus a 'forest of stone'?",a="Darnassus is called a forest of stone because its temples, bridges, and pavilions are built of marble and stone. The night elves live within the World Tree's canopy, while the city rises among these structures.",al={"forest of stone meaning","why forest of stone"},it="place"},{q="Why is Fandral Staghelm so concerned about the Oracle Tree's report?",a="Fandral Staghelm is concerned because the report describes corruption and turmoil among the wildlife on Teldrassil. He championed the tree's planting in hopes of restoring kaldorei immortality after Nordrassil was damaged in the Third War, and these afflictions threaten that ambition.",al={"fandral staghelm reaction","why is staghelm worried"}},{q="What quest leads into this, and what follows it?",a="You arrive after dealing with the harpies threatening the Oracle Tree in The Enchanted Glade. After you deliver the report to Arch Druid Staghelm, he sends you to Darkshore with Grove of the Ancients.",al={"teldrassil quest chain","what quest next"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Where can Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm be found?",a="Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm resides in Darnassus, at the summit of the Cenarion Enclave. There he oversees the druids of the Cenarion Circle and guides kaldorei governance.",al={"where is fandral","fandral staghelm location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak want this report delivered?",a="Arynia needs Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm to receive the Oracle Tree's report so Darnassus remains informed on the bough's condition. The woods have suffered under harpy infestations and unnatural corruption, and past messengers failed to make the trek safely. With calm restored to the Oracle Tree's glade, the news must reach the Arch Druid so the leadership can assess the state of the world tree.",al={"why send report to fandral","arynia cloudsbreak motive","why does arynia want report delivered"},it="motive",add="d4229979"},{q="Why does Arynia Cloudsbreak send you instead of another messenger?",a="Previous messengers sent along the forest trails failed to reach Darnassus or were lost along the way, making Arynia hesitant to risk another ordinary runner. Having proven your courage and battle prowess by cleansing the harpies from the Oracle Glade, you have earned the forest's favor and demonstrated that you can defend yourself and the message along the perilous roads to the city.",al={"why send me to darnassus","why not send another messenger","why arynia needs you"},it="why_me",add="174bd7d2"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you bring the report to Arch Druid Staghelm and learn of his drive to restore kaldorei immortality through Teldrassil's troubled boughs.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you carry word from the Oracle Tree to the leader of the Cenarion Circle, where the struggle to cleanse Teldrassil's natural balance is plain.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion, you receive a formal introduction to the night elf capital and its stern leadership."},kw={"arynia cloudsbreak","cenarion enclave","darnassus","fandral staghelm","immortality","inscribed bark","kaldorei","oracle tree","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:fandral-staghelm","npc:sentinel-arynia-cloudsbreak","quest:937","quest:952","zone:darnassus","zone:teldrassil","topic:druid"},m={start="Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak",["end"]="Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm",level="11",faction="Alliance",id=940},src={"Teldrassil (quest)"}}
E["quest:941"] = {t="quest",n="Planting the Heart",z="teldrassil",s="At Lake Al'Ameth, you help Denalan tend a wooden heart taken from a corrupted timberling. After clearing away its moss, he asks you to place it in his planter and see whether it can be healed.",h="At Lake Al'Ameth, you help Denalan tend a wooden heart taken from a corrupted timberling.",sec={{t="A Second Chance at Life",b="Denalan has scraped the foul moss from the wooden heart taken from Blackmoss the Fetid, a corrupted timberling. Yet an unnatural taint still pulses within the wood. Trusting his years of botany and soil tending, the herbalist asks you to bury the heart directly in his personal planter. He hopes the rich nutrients he blended can draw its remaining natural vitality back toward health.",sp=0},{t="The Miracle of Enriched Earth",b="The heart burrows into the soil as soon as it touches the earth, as if moved by primal instinct. Moments later, it rises cleansed of corruption, warm with a gentle, companionable glow. The heart of a fallen, tainted creature has been purified. Its change shows that careful nurturing and sacred earth can restore harmony, even when unnatural blights strike Teldrassil's wild denizens.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does this tainted heart come from?",a="The heart came from Blackmoss the Fetid, a corrupted timberling along Lake Al'Ameth's shores. It was choked with foul moss when recovered, before Denalan scraped it clean.",al={"heart origin","where did the heart come from","blackmoss heart"},it="origin"},{q="Who is Denalan?",a="Denalan is a night elf botanist and herbalist with an isolated camp on Lake Al'Ameth's eastern edge. He spends his days studying Teldrassil's plant life, investigating the strange corruption spreading through its boughs, and mixing enriched soils.",al={"who is denalan","denalan lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why put the heart in a planter instead of destroying it?",a="Denalan believes nature should be understood and healed rather than simply destroyed. He hopes his nutritive soil can purge the taint and restore the heart's original vitality.",al={"why plant the heart","why heal the heart"},it="motive"},{q="What happens when you bury the heart?",a="On touching the soil, the heart burrows into it. Seconds later, it wriggles back to the surface cleansed of its taint, pulsing gently as an animated companion.",al={"what happens in the planter","heart burrows"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Does this cure the corruption of the timberlings?",a="Only this single salvaged heart is cured. The change shows that individual botanical spirits can be cleansed with care and rich soil, while corruption still spreads across Teldrassil.",al={"are timberlings cured","curing timberlings"},it="power"},{q="Why is the soil in Denalan's planter special?",a="Denalan has spent considerable time experimenting with compost and nutritive soil blends around Lake Al'Ameth. He designed the soil to revitalize sickly flora and purge creeping decay.",al={"denalan soil","planter soil"},it="item"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you see a corrupted timberling's core cleansed through rich earth. It is a reassuring sign that natural care can turn back the unnatural taint afflicting the World Tree's boughs.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Denalan's command of nutrient-rich soil and botanical renewal shows how studying the earth can help mend damaged plant life.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see the kaldorei commitment to stewarding nature in the restoration of living wood and the coaxing of life from fallen forest spirits, even as Teldrassil suffers troubling ailments."},kw={"blackmoss the fetid","cleansed heart","denalan","lake al'ameth","planter","tainted heart","teldrassil","timberling"},rel={"npc:denalan","quest:927","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Denalan",["end"]="Denalan's Planter",faction="Alliance",id=941},src={"Planting the Heart"}}
E["quest:96630"] = {t="quest",n="The Adventurer",z="teldrassil",s="In Teldrassil, a lost journal waits to be carried to Lyreena Duskblade near Dolanaar. Its pages record an unknown traveler's simple journeys and camping outings.",h="In Teldrassil, a lost journal waits to be carried to Lyreena Duskblade near Dolanaar.",sec={{t="A Wanderer's Journal",b="You find a journal among Teldrassil's boughs and roots. Its nameless writer records modest wanderings and the simple pleasure of making camp beneath the twilight canopy.",sp=0},{t="Delivery to Dolanaar",b="The journal can be carried toward Dolanaar instead of left in the wilderness. Lyreena Duskblade waits near the night elf settlement to receive the lost pages.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the journal mentioned in the quest?",a="The journal is a plain notebook found in Teldrassil's wilds. Its entries tell of an unknown traveler's quiet journeys and fondness for camping outdoors.",al={"lost journal","what is the book","the adventurer journal"},it="item"},{q="Who is Lyreena Duskblade?",a="Lyreena Duskblade is a night elf near Dolanaar, and the lost journal is meant for her.",al={"lyreena","where is lyreena duskblade","turn in npc"},it="people"},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="The story takes place in Teldrassil, in the wilderness around Dolanaar.",al={"where is the adventurer quest","quest zone"},it="place"},{q="Does the journal describe dangerous monsters or battles?",a="No. The journal tells of an unknown person's ordinary wanderings and enjoyment of camping, not dangerous monsters or battles.",al={"journal lore","what is in the journal","what does it say"}},{q="Who can complete this task?",a="Alliance members exploring Teldrassil, especially novice night elves near Dolanaar, can complete it.",al={"can horde do this","alliance quest"},gp=true},{q="Why turn the journal in to Dolanaar?",a="Dolanaar is a central gathering place and crossroads in this part of Teldrassil. Lyreena Duskblade waits nearby to receive the journal.",al={"why dolanaar","why lyreena"},it="purpose"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a young night elf patrolling Teldrassil, you may find signs of travelers and carry lost keepsakes to wanderers like Lyreena Duskblade.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance novice beneath the World Tree, you help keep the groves in order by returning lost belongings to fellow travelers."},kw={"camping","dolanaar","journal","lost journal","lyreena duskblade","teldrassil","the adventurer"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Object #654846",["end"]="Lyreena Duskblade",level="6",faction="Alliance",id=96630},src={"The Adventurer (Teldrassil)"},fv=true}
E["quest:997"] = {t="quest",n="Denalan's Earth",z="teldrassil",s="In Dolanaar, Syral Bladeleaf sends a late shipment of rare earth south to Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth. The night elf researcher studies Teldrassil's young plants.",h="In Dolanaar, Syral Bladeleaf sends a late shipment of rare earth south to Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth.",sec={{t="A Courier for Dolanaar",b="Syral Bladeleaf stops travelers in Dolanaar with a special shipment of rare earth for Denalan. The soil came from Darnassus to support his botanical studies, but delays kept it from reaching Dolanaar until now. Syral seeks a courier to carry the parcel south along the forest trail to Denalan's campsite by Lake Al'Ameth.",sp=0},{t="Cultivating Teldrassil",b="Denalan works alone at a station on Lake Al'Ameth's eastern shore, watching Teldrassil's young ecosystem take root. The tree grew quickly after the Battle of Mount Hyjal, and its plants behave in unexpected ways. Denalan tests the vitality and behavior of timberlings and native plants with unique soil mixtures and specimens. The rare earth shipment will support those experiments.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Denalan?",a="Denalan is a night elf researcher and herbalist who camps on Lake Al'Ameth's eastern shore. He studies, cultivates, and experiments on Teldrassil's distinctive plant life.",al={"denalan lore","who is denalan","denalan npc"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Syral Bladeleaf located?",a="Syral Bladeleaf is in Dolanaar, the main night elf outpost in central Teldrassil. She coordinates research supplies and helps travelers crossing the boughs.",al={"syral bladeleaf location","where is syral"},gp=true},{q="What is the rare earth used for?",a="The shipment is specially enriched soil from Darnassus. Denalan uses it to nurture experimental plantings and test how native saplings, including timberlings, respond to different growing conditions.",al={"what does denalan need the earth for","rare earth purpose"},it="item"},{q="Where is Lake Al'Ameth?",a="Lake Al'Ameth lies south of Dolanaar among Teldrassil's southern roots.",al={"lake al'ameth location","how to get to lake al'ameth"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why was the shipment late?",a="The package traveled from Darnassus and faced unspecified delays on Teldrassil's winding roads before reaching Dolanaar.",al={"why was the earth late","delayed parcel"}},{q="What does delivering this earth lead to?",a="After receiving the rare soil, Denalan asks the courier to gather timberling sprouts and seeds along the lake shore, opening a wider study of the plants there.",al={"denalan earth follow up","what comes next"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Syral Bladeleaf want the rare earth delivered?",a="Denalan has been eagerly awaiting this shipment from Darnassus to continue his experiments on Teldrassil's local flora. Because the rare earth was delayed in transit and only recently arrived in Dolanaar, Syral wants it brought to his lakeside camp without further delay before the material loses its potency.",al={"why deliver rare earth","syral bladeleaf motive","why send earth to denalan"},it="motive",add="77a156f9"},{q="Why does Syral ask you to make the delivery?",a="Syral Bladeleaf stays in Dolanaar tending to her duties, and she simply spots you as an able traveler heading south toward Lake Al'Ameth. Since the shipment has already suffered lengthy delays, entrusting it to someone already journeying toward Denalan's retreat is the quickest way to get it into his hands.",al={"why does syral need me","why not send a courier","why me denalan's earth"},it="why_me",add="2b5476f7"}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="If you practice herbalism, Denalan's lakeside retreat may interest you. His experiments seek to understand the fragile plant life unique to the newly grown World Tree.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you share an affinity with Denalan's work. Following Teldrassil's plant growth and balance helps protect nature on the new bough.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf from Shadowglen, helping Syral and Denalan introduces you to the wider care needed to sustain Teldrassil."},kw={"darnassus","denalan","dolanaar","lake al'ameth","rare earth","syral bladeleaf","teldrassil","timberling"},rel={"npc:denalan","npc:syral-bladeleaf","subzone:lake-al-ameth","subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","zone:darnassus","topic:night-elf","topic:alliance"},m={start="Syral Bladeleaf",["end"]="Denalan",faction="Alliance",id=997},src={"Denalan's Earth"}}
E["subzone:aldrassil"] = {t="subzone",n="Aldrassil",z="teldrassil",s="Young kaldorei gather beneath Aldrassil’s vast boughs in Shadowglen. The settlement shelters trainers, merchants, and local leaders in hollows carved through the great tree.",h="Young kaldorei gather beneath Aldrassil’s vast boughs in Shadowglen.",sec={{t="Heart of Shadowglen",b="Aldrassil shelters young night elves in Shadowglen. Ramps wind through its immense trunk, passing trainers and artisans on the way to the high roost. Tenaron Stormgrip watches over the glade’s protection from there. Beyond the tree, Teldrassil stretches across the horizon, while novices learn their arts beneath Aldrassil’s canopy before venturing into Kalimdor’s troubled wilds.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Aldrassil?",a="Aldrassil shelters young night elves at the heart of Shadowglen, in northeastern Teldrassil. Its hollowed trunk holds a settlement where they find training, goods, and guidance.",al={"aldrassil tree","what is aldrassil","shadowglen big tree"},it="place"},{q="Who leads the settlement at Aldrassil?",a="Tenaron Stormgrip oversees Shadowglen from his roost atop Aldrassil. He coordinates the vale’s defense and guides newly awakened kaldorei.",al={"who leads aldrassil","aldrassil leader","tenaron stormgrip location"},it="in_charge"},{q="What services can be found here?",a="Aldrassil’s trainers teach young night elf warriors, rogues, druids, hunters, and priests. Supply merchants and armorers also serve the glade’s immediate needs.",al={"trainers in aldrassil","vendors aldrassil","what is in aldrassil"},gp=true},{q="Who lives in Aldrassil?",a="Aldrassil is home to the night elf guardians, trainers, and caretakers who watch over Shadowglen. Priests of Elune, druids, rogues, and warriors maintain quarters throughout its carved trunk and surrounding platforms, while Tenaron Stormgrip, the leader of the glen, dwells at its very boughs.",al={"who lives here","aldrassil residents","aldrassil population"},it="residents",add="f93f81e4"},{q="Is Aldrassil dangerous?",a="The tree itself is a safe haven and the bustling heart of Shadowglen, protected by watchful night elf sentinels. However, the surrounding boughs and woodland are under growing threat from encroaching Grell, diseased nightsabers, and corrupted woodland beasts lurking just beyond its shade.",al={"is aldrassil safe","aldrassil danger","danger at aldrassil"},it="danger",add="1582ff91"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For many young kaldorei, Aldrassil’s carved hollows and ramps are their first memory of civic life and the start of their training.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can see the kaldorei affinity for living architecture in Aldrassil, shaped from living wood while keeping the forest’s balance."},kw={"aldrassil","great tree","kaldorei","night elf starting","shadowglen","teldrassil","tenaron stormgrip"},rel={"subzone:shadowglen","npc:tenaron-stormgrip","zone:teldrassil","quest:940"},src={"Aldrassil"}}
E["subzone:ban-ethil-barrow-den"] = {t="subzone",n="Ban'ethil Barrow Den",z="teldrassil",s="Gnarlpine furbolgs have overrun Ban'ethil Barrow Den beneath Teldrassil's roots. The sacred chambers were made for the sleeping Druids of the Talon, whose spirits commune with the Emerald Dream. Now the den is a dangerous warren, and the druids within are at risk.",h="Gnarlpine furbolgs have overrun Ban'ethil Barrow Den beneath Teldrassil's roots.",sec={{t="A Defiled Sanctuary",b="Ban'ethil Barrow Den lies beneath Teldrassil's roots, with upper and lower chambers. Barrow dens shelter night elf druids as they sleep and send their spirits into the Emerald Dream. This den was made for the Druids of the Talon to commune with nature. Its halls once held quiet meditation, but the corruption spreading through Teldrassil's wildlife reached the Gnarlpine furbolgs. They invaded the den and made its hollowed chambers a fortified warren.",sp=0},{t="The Gnarlpine Incursion",b="The Gnarlpine tribe has gone mad under a mysterious corruption spreading across the World Tree. Its furbolgs drove out or endangered the sleeping druids, and now guard the winding tunnels fiercely, attacking any night elf who approaches. Teldrassil's defenders must drive them back to protect the vulnerable druids and the sacred relics trapped in the den's lower depths.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Ban'ethil Barrow Den?",a="Ban'ethil Barrow Den is a hollow beneath Teldrassil, made by night elves to shelter the sleeping Druids of the Talon. Their spirits roam the Emerald Dream while they sleep.",al={"what is ban'ethil","ban'ethil barrow den purpose","what is this cave"},it="place"},{q="Why are there furbolgs inside Ban'ethil Barrow Den?",a="The Gnarlpine furbolgs fell to a spreading corruption among Teldrassil's creatures. They turned hostile, invaded the den, displaced its keepers, and threaten the sleeping druids.",al={"why are gnarlpine in ban'ethil","furbolgs in barrow den","who took over ban'ethil"},it="residents"},{q="What are the sections of the barrow den?",a="The den has two connected tiers, the Upper Den near the entrance passages and the Lower Den deeper among the subterranean roots.",al={"ban'ethil layout","upper den lower den","ban'ethil levels"}},{q="Why are barrow dens so important to druids?",a="Barrow dens shelter druids whose deep sleep lets their consciousness enter the Emerald Dream. Their waking bodies lie helpless for years or decades, so they need safe, secure shelter.",al={"why do druids sleep in barrows","druid barrow dens lore","emerald dream barrow den"},it="purpose"},{q="What happened at Ban'ethil Barrow Den?",a="Constructed by the night elves as a sacred refuge to house sleeping Druids of the Talon, Ban'ethil Barrow Den was meant to be a quiet sanctuary. Recently, however, corruption took hold of the native Gnarlpine furbolgs. Driven to madness, the tribe stormed the barrows and claimed them as their own den, driving out the night elves and desecrating the sacred hollows.",al={"ban'ethil barrow den history","what happened at banethil","banethil barrow den story"},it="history",add="129d8c28"},{q="Why was Ban'ethil Barrow Den abandoned?",a="The barrow den was not willingly abandoned by the night elves; it was violently overrun. When the Gnarlpine tribe succumbed to corruption, they invaded the sanctuary in force. The sleeping druids and their caretakers could not maintain control, leaving the upper and lower dens entirely in the hands of the hostile furbolgs.",al={"why is ban'ethil abandoned","why did druids leave ban'ethil","banethil barrow den overrun"},it="ruin",add="698c9749"},{q="Is Ban'ethil Barrow Den dangerous?",a="It is extremely hazardous to enter alone. The winding tunnels of both the Upper and Lower Dens are packed with aggressive, corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs. Between the cramped subterranean layout and the fierce territorial instincts of the crazed beasts, an unwary traveler can easily become surrounded and overwhelmed.",al={"is ban'ethil barrow den dangerous","how dangerous is ban'ethil","banethil danger"},it="danger",add="9b622bd1"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can see Ban'ethil as sacred ground for the Cenarion Circle, built to protect the Druids of the Talon as they commune with the Emerald Dream.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you can see the Gnarlpine occupation of Ban'ethil as a warning of the sickness spreading through your new home, Teldrassil."},kw={"ban'ethil","barrow den","druids of the talon","emerald dream","furbolg","gnarlpine","teldrassil"},rel={"zone:teldrassil","topic:druid","topic:furbolg","topic:night-elf","quest:940"},src={"Ban'ethil Barrow Den"}}
E["subzone:ban-ethil-hollow"] = {t="subzone",n="Ban'ethil Hollow",z="teldrassil",s="South of the road between Dolanaar and Darnassus, furbolgs threaten travelers in Ban'ethil Hollow. The ravine also hides the entrance to Ban'ethil Barrow Den.",h="South of the road between Dolanaar and Darnassus, furbolgs threaten travelers in Ban'ethil Hollow.",sec={{t="A Perilous Ravine",b="Furbolgs roam the rocky descent into Ban'ethil Hollow. Their strange affliction has driven them mad, and they stalk the nearby road, ambushing couriers and wandering sentinels. The hollow lies just south of the road between Dolanaar and Darnassus, a reminder that Teldrassil's woodland is not wholly safe. At the ravine's back stands the entrance to Ban'ethil Barrow Den. Slumbering druids and ancient tunnels lie within, threatened by the maddened beasts outside.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Ban'ethil Hollow located?",a="Ban'ethil Hollow is a ravine in central Teldrassil, just south of the main road between Dolanaar and Darnassus.",al={"banethil hollow location","where is ban'ethil hollow","find banethil hollow"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are the furbolgs here hostile?",a="A spreading corruption and madness grips the World Tree's wildlife, turning the furbolgs across Teldrassil fiercely territorial and violent. They once lived peacefully alongside the night elves.",al={"why are furbolgs mad","hostile furbolgs banethil","banethil furbolg attack"},it="hostile"},{q="What is inside the Ban'ethil Barrow Den at the back of the hollow?",a="Ban'ethil Barrow Den is an underground complex where night elven druids have long entered deep hibernation and communed with the Emerald Dream. Rising corruption in the hollow has made the den dangerous ground.",al={"what is in the barrow den","banethil barrow den","den in banethil hollow"}},{q="Is the road above the hollow safe to travel?",a="Night elf sentinels patrol the main road, but furbolgs from Ban'ethil Hollow often climb up to ambush travelers. Stay alert on the road between Dolanaar and Darnassus.",al={"is the road safe","furbolg ambushes","road to darnassus safe"},it="danger",gp=true},{q="What is Ban'ethil Hollow?",a="Ban'ethil Hollow is a secluded, sunken ravine carved into central Teldrassil, resting just south of the primary roadway connecting Dolanaar to Darnassus. Dominated by dense foliage and rugged slopes, the hollow serves as an encampment for corrupted furbolgs, and at its deepest recess lies the entrance to the vast Ban'ethil Barrow Den.",al={"banethil hollow","what is this place","ban'ethil hollow overview"},it="place",add="fa7d6d41"},{q="Who lives in Ban'ethil Hollow?",a="The ravine is overrun by aggressive, corrupted furbolgs. Once peaceful neighbors to the night elves, these creatures have fallen into madness and hostility, claiming the hollow as their territory and threatening anyone traveling nearby.",al={"who lives here","ban'ethil hollow residents","who inhabits ban'ethil hollow"},it="residents",add="5004ddfb"},{q="Is Ban'ethil Hollow dangerous?",a="It is extremely hazardous. The hollow is packed with hostile furbolgs who guard the ravine fiercely. Travelers on the main road just above frequently fall victim to ambushes launched from the ravine's edges, making the area perilous even for passersby who do not venture down.",al={"how dangerous is ban'ethil hollow","is banethil hollow safe","danger in ban'ethil hollow"},it="danger",add="f75c8a95"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see furbolgs falling to madness near the road between Dolanaar and Darnassus, a grim sign of Teldrassil's growing sickness. Young sentinels and druids must step in.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you know Ban'ethil Hollow hides the entrance to Ban'ethil Barrow Den, sacred ground where druids rest and commune with the Emerald Dream. Rabid wildlife now threatens it."},kw={"ambush","ban'ethil barrow den","ban'ethil hollow","darnassus","dolanaar","furbolg","ravine","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:ban-ethil-barrow-den","subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","zone:darnassus","topic:furbolg"},src={"Ban'ethil Hollow"}}
E["subzone:cleft"] = {t="subzone",n="Cleft",z="teldrassil",s="Gnarlpine furbolgs ambush travelers in the Cleft, northwest of Dolanaar.",h="Gnarlpine furbolgs ambush travelers in the Cleft, northwest of Dolanaar.",sec={{t="A Den of Corruption",b="The Cleft lies off the road between Dolanaar and Darnassus, where Gnarlpine furbolgs have made their den. Teldrassil’s spreading corruption has driven them mad, and they have fortified the hollow. From there, they threaten travelers on the main road and risk cutting Dolanaar off from Darnassus.",sp=0},{t="The Roadway Ambushers",b="Moon Priestess Amara and her sentinels keep watch outside the Cleft’s entrance. Their defense guards the main road linking Teldrassil’s villages with Darnassus, but the Gnarlpine still threaten its passage.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Cleft?",a="The Cleft is a furbolg den northwest of Dolanaar, beside the main road to Darnassus.",al={"what is the cleft","the cleft teldrassil","cleft location"},it="place"},{q="Who controls the Cleft?",a="Hostile Gnarlpine furbolgs occupy the Cleft, driven mad by Teldrassil’s spreading corruption.",al={"who lives in the cleft","cleft enemies","who rules the cleft"},it="residents"},{q="Why are the night elves fighting here?",a="The Gnarlpine ambush travelers on the road to Darnassus, so Moon Priestess Amara and the Sentinels work to keep the road safe.",al={"why attack the cleft","cleft night elf quests","road to darnassus"},it="conflict"},{q="Is the Cleft related to the Cleft of Shadow?",a="No. The Cleft is a furbolg cave in Teldrassil; the Cleft of Shadow is a dark cavern beneath Orgrimmar.",al={"cleft of shadow connection","cleft vs cleft of shadow"}},{q="What happened at the Cleft?",a="The Gnarlpine furbolgs took refuge within the cave, but foul corruption quickly overcame their minds. Falling into madness, they began raiding the nearby roadway leading toward Darnassus, attacking unwary travelers and threatening commerce with the capital.",al={"history of the cleft","what happened at the cleft","cleft history"},it="history",add="3e19e4c1"},{q="Is the Cleft dangerous?",a="The Cleft is very dangerous. Hostile, corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs pack the dark den. They fiercely defend their hollow, having already ambushed supply lines and threatened travelers. Moon Priestess Amara and her sentinels must guard the road just outside to hold them back.",al={"cleft danger","is the cleft safe","threats in the cleft"},it="danger",add="de17fe22"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see longtime furbolg allies driven mad and attacking travelers.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you know the corrupted Gnarlpine threaten travelers on the road to Darnassus."},kw={"cleft","darnassus","dolanaar","furbolg","gnarlpine","moon priestess amara"},rel={"quest:487","npc:moon-priestess-amara","topic:furbolg","subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","topic:druid","subzone:cleft-of-shadow"},src={"Cleft"}}
E["subzone:darnassus"] = {t="subzone",n="Darnassus",z="teldrassil",s="Darnassus rises among Teldrassil’s high boughs as the kaldorei capital and refuge. Its tranquil waters and groves make it the night elves’ spiritual heart and the Alliance’s primary bastion on northern Kalimdor. High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind and Archdruid Fandral Staghelm guide their people through the trials of newfound mortality.",h="Darnassus rises among Teldrassil’s high boughs as the kaldorei capital and refuge.",sec={{t="Sanctuary in the Boughs",b="Darnassus took shape after the Third War, honoring the night elves’ survival after they lost the immortality granted by their sacred World Tree, Nordrassil. Unlike the stone cities of Ironforge and Stormwind, it is an open, tranquil settlement of wood-crafted lodges, glowing shrines, and arched bridges over crystalline lakes. Vigilant Sentinels, towering ancients of war, and druids who shape trees watch the paths and preserve nature’s quiet within the city.",sp=0},{t="A Divided Leadership",b="Darnassus speaks of kaldorei unity, though its leadership is divided between different duties. High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind handles civil and military matters from the radiant Temple of the Moon, with the Sisters of Elune around her. Archdruid Fandral Staghelm leads the Cenarion Circle’s affairs and championed planting Teldrassil to restore the elves’ lost immortality. Malfurion Stormrage is lost in a mysterious slumber deep within the Emerald Dream, and Staghelm’s aggressive vision for the future often clashes with the more patient priesthood.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who rules Darnassus?",a="High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind leads night elf society from the Temple of the Moon and commands the Sentinels. Archdruid Fandral Staghelm leads the Cenarion Circle in Malfurion Stormrage’s absence.",al={"darnassus leader","who is in charge of darnassus","night elf leader"},it="in_charge"},{q="How do travelers reach Darnassus from outside Teldrassil?",a="Darnassus sits atop the massive boughs of a World Tree island, so ships and flight paths reach only Rut'theran Village at the tree’s base. From there, a magical portal carries visitors up into the city.",al={"how to get to darnassus","darnassus entrance","getting into darnassus"},it="arrival"},{q="Why was Darnassus founded so recently?",a="After the destruction at Mount Hyjal during the Third War, the night elves lost their immortality and ancient way of life. Fandral Staghelm and his allies planted Teldrassil off the coast of Kalimdor, and Darnassus took root on its branches as a fresh sanctuary for their people.",al={"why is darnassus new","when was darnassus built","darnassus age"},it="history"},{q="Where is Malfurion Stormrage?",a="Archdruid Malfurion Stormrage is missing, his spirit trapped in a deep, unexplained slumber within the Emerald Dream. In his absence, Fandral Staghelm leads the Cenarion Circle in Darnassus.",al={"where is malfurion","is malfurion in darnassus","malfurion status"}},{q="What is Darnassus?",a="Darnassus is the capital city of the night elves, nestled high within the colossal boughs of the newly grown World Tree, Teldrassil. Built around a serene lake and open to the twilight skies, it serves as the spiritual and cultural heart of their civilization following the Third War. Graceful bridges, living wood lodges, and sacred groves define its layout, anchored by the shining Temple of the Moon. It stands as an Alliance sanctuary and a living testament to the kaldorei's reverence for nature.",al={"what is this place","tell me about darnassus","darnassus city overview"},it="place",add="24a1a5b0"},{q="Who lives in Darnassus?",a="The city is predominantly home to the night elves, welcoming druids, hunters, priests, and warriors alike. High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind presides from the grand Temple of the Moon alongside her Sisters of Elune, while Archdruid Fandral Staghelm directs the Cenarion Circle from the Cenarion Enclave. The vigilant Sentinels patrol the avenues, and ancient protectors wander the pathways. Visitors will also encounter emissaries from fellow Alliance races, along with representatives of neutral orders such as the Argent Dawn.",al={"who lives here","darnassus residents","inhabitants of darnassus"},it="residents",add="3a9c78e5"},{q="Is Darnassus dangerous?",a="For members of the Alliance, Darnassus is an exceptionally peaceful refuge, shielded from Kalimdor's harsher perils by the ocean and Teldrassil's towering height. It is closely protected by armed Sentinels and formidable Ancient Protectors. However, agents of the Horde will find it fiercely hostile, facing immediate attack by the city's stalwart defenders upon entry.",al={"is darnassus safe","threats in darnassus","any danger in darnassus"},it="danger",add="0325f465"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a kaldorei, Darnassus is your people’s cultural and political capital, a fresh start and sovereign refuge after the harrowing sacrifices of the Third War.",["faction:Alliance"]="For travelers from the Eastern Kingdoms, Darnassus is a secluded, serene haven and the Alliance’s essential anchor on the continent of Kalimdor."},kw={"capital","darnassus","kaldorei","staghelm","teldrassil","temple of the moon","tyrande"},rel={"zone:teldrassil","subzone:temple-of-the-moon","subzone:rut-theran-village","npc:tyrande-whisperwind","npc:fandral-staghelm","npc:malfurion-stormrage","topic:alliance","topic:sentinels"},src={"Darnassus"}}
E["subzone:dolanaar"] = {t="subzone",n="Dolanaar",z="teldrassil",s="Dolanaar gathers travelers and guides beneath Teldrassil’s boughs. Southwest of Shadowglen, the town is the first place young night elves find after leaving their sheltered training grounds. Rangers, druids, and craftsmen help newcomers while strange afflictions spread through the World Tree.",h="Dolanaar gathers travelers and guides beneath Teldrassil’s boughs.",sec={{t="A Crossroads of Boughs",b="Dolanaar is a crossroads for travelers crossing Teldrassil. Beneath the canopy southwest of Shadowglen, its homes and platforms follow the traditional night elven way, woven into the woodland. Young night elves come here for their first broad training in trades, martial arts, and nature crafts. The road west leads toward Darnassus, the capital. From the surrounding boughs come reports of corrupted wildlife, aggressive furbolgs, and foul mosses, all brought before Dolanaar’s council.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of Dolanaar?",a="Dolanaar is the main hub and outpost for young night elves leaving Shadowglen’s novice grounds. Tradesfolk and trainers in martial and magical arts are gathered here, and the town links travelers to the capital.",al={"what is dolanaar","dolanaar purpose","why dolanaar matters"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is Dolanaar located?",a="Dolanaar lies in central-eastern Teldrassil, a short walk down the trail southwest of Shadowglen and east of Darnassus.",al={"dolanaar location","where is dolanaar","dolanaar directions"},gp=true},{q="How can travelers reach Darnassus from here?",a="Follow the forest road west through Teldrassil to reach the gates of Darnassus on foot. Dolanaar has no flight path of its own.",al={"travel to darnassus","flight master dolanaar","dolanaar to darnassus"},gp=true},{q="What threats affect Dolanaar?",a="A strange corruption is spreading through the woodland around Dolanaar. Diseased beasts, crazed timberlings, and hostile furbolg tribes threaten the area.",al={"trouble in dolanaar","dolanaar problems","dolanaar quests"},it="threat"},{q="What is Dolanaar?",a="Dolanaar is a bustling night elven village nestled in the central-eastern boughs of Teldrassil, just southwest of the training grounds of Shadowglen. Serving as the heart of regional trade and affairs on the great world tree, it is typically the very first major settlement young night elves encounter when stepping out into the wider realm.",al={"what is dolanaar","dolanaar town","dolanaar village"},it="place",add="d9d46a9a"},{q="Is Dolanaar dangerous?",a="Within the village itself you are safe among sentinel guards, druids, and merchants. However, the surrounding woodlands harbor growing unrest. Corrupted wildlife, restless gnarlpine furbolgs, and sinister harpy clutches threaten travelers venturing just beyond the perimeter of the settlement.",al={"is dolanaar dangerous","dolanaar safety","dolanaar safe"},it="danger",add="6bb1c128"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a young night elf, you take your first steps into the wider world at Dolanaar, where the growing corruption of the World Tree tests your vow to preserve nature.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid initiate, you can seek guidance at Dolanaar on Teldrassil’s ailments and learn to attune your spirit to nature’s balance."},kw={"darnassus","dolanaar","kaldorei","night elf town","shadowglen","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil","zone:darnassus","topic:night-elf"},src={"Dolanaar"}}
E["subzone:fel-rock"] = {t="subzone",n="Fel Rock",z="teldrassil",s="North of Dolanaar, Fel Rock has fallen under a spreading corruption. Lord Melenas and his grells have turned the once-tranquil cavern into a threat within Teldrassil’s woods.",h="North of Dolanaar, Fel Rock has fallen under a spreading corruption.",sec={{t="A Den of Corruption",b="North of Dolanaar, Fel Rock lies among Teldrassil’s forested hills. Once a peaceful cavern in wood and stone, it is now overtaken by twisted roots, unnatural shadows, wild grells and grellkin. The taint reaches into the world tree’s boughs.",sp=0},{t="The Satyr's Hold",b="Lord Melenas, a satyr, has claimed Fel Rock as his stronghold. From within the cavern, he spreads corruption beneath the watch of the night elf sentinels. Druids in Dolanaar, including Tallonkai Swiftroot, seek defenders to cleanse the cave and slay Melenas before the blight reaches farther into the surrounding woodlands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Fel Rock located?",a="Fel Rock lies in the hills directly north of Dolanaar, in central Teldrassil.",al={"fel rock location","where is fel rock","find fel rock"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who rules Fel Rock?",a="Lord Melenas, a satyr, commands Fel Rock and has gathered grells to do his bidding.",al={"who is in fel rock","boss of fel rock","lord melenas location"},it="leader"},{q="Why are druids concerned about Fel Rock?",a="A satyr and fel-tainted grells threaten Teldrassil’s natural balance. Druids such as Tallonkai Swiftroot send defenders to slay Lord Melenas and stem the corruption.",al={"why clean fel rock","fel rock quest","tallonkai swiftroot quest"},it="danger"},{q="What creatures dwell inside the cavern?",a="Fel Rock is home to aggressive grells, grellkin and their master, the satyr Lord Melenas.",al={"fel rock mobs","what is inside fel rock","fel rock enemies"},it="residents"},{q="What is Fel Rock?",a="Fel Rock is a dark, corrupted cavern carved into the boughs of Teldrassil, located just north of Dolanaar. While it was once a natural and pristine cave, vile demonic corruption has settled deep within its hollows, turning it into a foul nesting ground for wicked grells and satyrs.",al={"what is fel rock","fel rock overview","fel rock lore"},it="place",add="32acb48e"},{q="Why is it called Fel Rock?",a="The cavern takes its name from the foul, demonic corruption that has tainted its stone and hollows. Once a pristine, natural grotto on Teldrassil, the arrival of satyrs and the spreading influence of dark fel magic earned it the grim title of Fel Rock.",al={"why fel rock","fel rock name origin","why is it called fel rock"},it="name",add="3eaad617"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the Kaldorei, Lord Melenas and his hold so close to Dolanaar threaten Teldrassil and call for swift retribution.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid of the Cenarion Circle, you see Fel Rock’s corruption as a wound in the young world tree, one that must be purged before the blight spreads."},kw={"dolanaar","fel rock","grell","lord melenas","satyr","tallonkai swiftroot","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:932","subzone:dolanaar","npc:tallonkai-swiftroot","topic:satyr","zone:teldrassil","topic:druid","topic:night-elf","quest:940"},src={"Fel Rock"}}
E["subzone:lake-al-ameth"] = {t="subzone",n="Lake Al'Ameth",z="teldrassil",s="South of Dolanaar, Lake Al'Ameth's shores have turned perilous as the local plant life grows violent. Once a quiet haven with little more than a wooden jetty, the lake is one of Teldrassil's largest freshwater bodies.",h="South of Dolanaar, Lake Al'Ameth's shores have turned perilous as the local plant life grows violent.",sec={{t="A Troubled Shoreline",b="At Lake Al'Ameth, swarms of timberlings and timberling sprouts prowl the water's edge. The lake lies just south of Dolanaar, where its calm waters and sparse settlement offer little sign of the danger ashore. An unnatural sickness spreading through Teldrassil has driven the plant life into a frenzy. Druids and researchers from Dolanaar send travelers to gather seeds and kill the aggressive creatures before the corruption spreads deeper into the forest.",sp=0},{t="The Roots of Wrath",b="Oakenscowl, once a noble timberling, spreads corruption from a cave on Lake Al'Ameth's southern bank. A gargantuan tumor has swollen his body, and other timberlings lash out at anyone who approaches. The woodland spirits have lost their balance, and the Cenarion Circle faces an urgent test: can the rot around the lake be diagnosed and treated, and can Teldrassil's unblessed creation be sustained?",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Lake Al'Ameth located?",a="Lake Al'Ameth lies directly south of Dolanaar, the night elf settlement in eastern Teldrassil.",al={"lake alameth location","where is lake al'ameth","find lake al'ameth"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are the creatures around Lake Al'Ameth hostile?",a="A corrupting sickness afflicts Teldrassil's timberlings and other plant life along the shore, driving previously harmless woodland spriggans and treants into a territorial rage.",al={"why timberlings angry","lake alameth enemies","aggressive timberlings"},it="threat"},{q="What structures or landmarks are on the lake?",a="The lake is largely wild and undeveloped. A simple wooden fishing jetty stands on its northern bank near the path from Dolanaar.",al={"lake alameth pier","dock at lake alameth"},it="place"},{q="Who is Oakenscowl?",a="Oakenscowl is a corrupted timberling in a cave on Lake Al'Ameth's southern bank. Once a grand leader among his kind, he is poisoned by a gargantuan tumor and spreads corruption to the creatures that call the lake home.",al={"what is oakenscowl","oakenscowl lake al'ameth"},it="identity"},{q="What is Lake Al'Ameth?",a="Lake Al'Ameth is one of the largest bodies of fresh water cradled within the boughs of Teldrassil. Situated just south of Dolanaar, its tranquil waters and forested banks were once a serene natural haven, marked only by a modest wooden jetty along its shore. Recently, however, its quiet beauty has been overshadowed by mounting turmoil.",al={"what is lake al'ameth","about lake al'ameth","lake al'ameth lore"},it="place",add="a360f287"},{q="Is Lake Al'Ameth dangerous?",a="It is no longer safe to wander its banks unprepared. The shorelines have become overrun by agitated timberlings and virulent sprouts driven to violent frenzy. Between these aggressive woodland spirits and the presence of corrupted behemoths like Oakenscowl lurking nearby, any traveler visiting the water's edge must remain vigilant.",al={"is lake al'ameth safe","lake al'ameth danger","dangers at lake al'ameth"},it="danger",add="3493d075"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a kaldorei of Dolanaar, you see Lake Al'Ameth's sickness as a warning about the troubles facing your newly raised home. Young defenders must protect the surrounding road.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can study the unnatural corruption undermining Teldrassil's flora and fauna in the wild timberlings around the lake."},kw={"dolanaar","kaldorei","lake al'ameth","oakenscowl","teldrassil","timberling","timberling seeds"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","quest:918","quest:919","quest:2499","quest:922","quest:941","quest:940"},src={"Lake Al'Ameth"}}
E["subzone:oracle-glade"] = {t="subzone",n="Oracle Glade",z="teldrassil",s="Bloodfeather harpies harry Oracle Glade in northwestern Teldrassil. The sacred woodland holds the ancient Oracle Tree and Teldrassil’s first and most potent moonwell.",h="Bloodfeather harpies harry Oracle Glade in northwestern Teldrassil.",sec={{t="Heart of the Woodland",b="Between Darnassus and Wellspring Lake, the Oracle Glade shelters a place of communion with nature. At its heart stands the ancient Oracle Tree, magically nurtured, its great boughs shaped like an eagle perched atop a bear. Nearby lies the first and most potent of Teldrassil’s sacred moonwells, bright with Elune’s grace. The Circle of the Ancients and the Oracle Tree watch over the island boughs. The tree sheds bark marked with messages for Archdruid Fandral Staghelm about the World Tree’s health.",sp=0},{t="A Bough Besieged",b="Bloodfeather harpies have made roosts in the glade’s high branches. The aggressive avian scavengers threaten the sacred tree and harass traveling druids, disturbing the moonwell’s quiet. Sentinels from Darnassus struggle to drive them out. As you pass through the northern boughs, tread carefully; harpies strike swiftly near their roosts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Oracle Tree?",a="The Oracle Tree is an ancient, magically nurtured tree shaped like an eagle resting on a bear. It watches Teldrassil’s growth and health, shedding bark marked with reports that druids carry to Archdruid Fandral Staghelm in Darnassus.",al={"who is the oracle tree","oracle tree lore","talking tree teldrassil"},it="identity"},{q="Why are harpies attacking the Oracle Glade?",a="Bloodfeather harpies have nested in the glade’s high canopies, where they defend their roosts and harass the Oracle Tree. Local Sentinels work to contain them.",al={"bloodfeather harpies","why harpies here","oracle glade enemies"},it="conflict"},{q="What is the importance of the moonwell in this glade?",a="The Oracle Glade’s moonwell was the first and most powerful established on Teldrassil. Its sacred waters channel Elune’s energies to nourish the forest and sustain kaldorei druids and priestesses who draw upon them.",al={"oracle glade moonwell","first moonwell","teldrassil first moonwell"},it="power"},{q="Where is the Oracle Glade located?",a="Oracle Glade lies in northwestern Teldrassil, just west of Wellspring Lake. A road south connects it to the main path circling outside Darnassus’s gates.",al={"oracle glade location","where is oracle glade","how to get to oracle glade"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Oracle Glade?",a="Oracle Glade is a sacred sanctuary nestled in northwestern Teldrassil, north of Darnassus. It serves as the home to the ancient Oracle Tree and houses the first and most powerful of Teldrassil's moonwells. The glade is deeply revered by the night elves, who treat it as a peaceful place of reverence and natural communion where druids and priestesses monitor the great World Tree's health.",al={"what is oracle glade","oracle glade lore","oracle glade teldrassil"},it="place",add="3401eeb2"},{q="Why is it called Oracle Glade?",a="The glade takes its name from the mystical Oracle Tree standing at its heart. Grown by potent nature magic, this unique entity possesses deep wisdom and constantly monitors Teldrassil's vitality. By shedding inscribed bark containing supernatural reports, the tree communicates its insights to Archdruid Fandral Staghelm, acting as a living oracle for the Kaldorei.",al={"why oracle glade","oracle glade name origin","oracle glade name meaning"},it="name",add="808cde15"},{q="Is Oracle Glade dangerous?",a="While consecrated as a serene shrine, the glade has become perilous due to an infestation of Bloodfeather harpies. These aggressive creatures have established nests throughout the trees and boughs, threatening the sacred moonwell and the Oracle Tree itself. A contingent of night elf Sentinels has been dispatched here to hold the harpies at bay and defend travelers.",al={"is oracle glade safe","oracle glade threats","oracle glade enemies"},it="danger",add="80458d5a"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For a night elf, Oracle Glade shows the care needed to bring Teldrassil to fruition. It holds the crown’s most potent moonwell and a silent watcher that sends word to Cenarion leadership.",["class:Druid"]="For a druid of the wild, the Oracle Tree is a living partner in stewardship. Its bark bears written records of the land’s health."},kw={"bloodfeather","fandral staghelm","harpies","moonwell","oracle glade","oracle tree","teldrassil","wellspring lake"},rel={"zone:teldrassil","quest:940","quest:937","subzone:wellspring-lake","npc:fandral-staghelm","topic:sentinels","zone:darnassus"},src={"Oracle Glade"}}
E["subzone:pools-of-arlithrien"] = {t="subzone",n="Pools of Arlithrien",z="teldrassil",s="South of Darnassus, the Pools of Arlithrien have grown dangerous and neglected. Their moonwell once drew night elves to a quiet sanctuary, but beasts and nearby Gnarlpine furbolgs now threaten the springs.",h="South of Darnassus, the Pools of Arlithrien have grown dangerous and neglected.",sec={{t="A Troubled Sanctuary",b="The Pools of Arlithrien lie beneath Teldrassil’s shaded boughs, south of Darnassus. A stone moonwell rests at their heart, holding waters touched by Elune’s grace. Though the sanctuary lies near the night elven capital, danger has driven the night elves to leave it untended. Agitated beasts roam the shallows, and the Gnarlpine furbolgs nearby remain hostile. What was meant to be a peaceful retreat now reflects the growing troubles across the island.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are the Pools of Arlithrien located?",a="The Pools of Arlithrien lie in western Teldrassil, just south of the main bridge and entrance to Darnassus.",al={"pools of arlithrien location","where is arlithrien","arlithrien map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why was the moonwell here abandoned?",a="The night elves stopped tending the moonwell as danger mounted. Hostile Gnarlpine furbolgs settled nearby, while aggressive forest wildlife overran the surrounding waters.",al={"why abandoned","arlithrien moonwell abandoned","empty moonwell"},it="ruin"},{q="What threats can travelers find at the pools?",a="Aggressive woodland creatures roam the waters, and nearby territorial Gnarlpine furbolgs pose a threat to travelers.",al={"arlithrien monsters","pools of arlithrien mobs","enemies at pools"},it="danger"},{q="Can players still use the moonwell at the Pools of Arlithrien?",a="Yes. Though the priesthood and druids have left the moonwell untended because of local dangers, its sacred waters remain a functional source of lunar essence.",al={"use arlithrien moonwell","is moonwell active","water at pools"},gp=true},{q="What are the Pools of Arlithrien?",a="The Pools of Arlithrien are a collection of tranquil ponds nestled in western Teldrassil, just south of the gates to Darnassus. Though built as a serene sanctuary centered around a sacred moonwell, the area has fallen into neglect and disorder.",al={"pools of arlithrien lore","what is pools of arlithrien","about pools of arlithrien"},it="place",add="66076687"},{q="What happened to the Pools of Arlithrien?",a="Once a peaceful haven for reflection and worship, the sanctuary could not be maintained against the rising aggression of the local wildlife and the creeping threat of the Gnarlpine furbolgs. Night elf caretakers were eventually forced to withdraw, leaving the waters untended.",al={"pools of arlithrien history","what happened at pools of arlithrien"},it="history",add="3cd7c020"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, a holy moonwell left untended so close to Darnassus is a troubling sign of corruption and disruption spreading across Teldrassil.",["class:Druid"]="Druids studying Teldrassil’s imbalances see the unruly wildlife and neglected moonwell as signs that the Great Tree lacks nature’s true blessing."},kw={"arlithrien","darnassus","furbolg","gnarlpine","moonwell","pools of arlithrien","teldrassil"},rel={"zone:teldrassil","zone:darnassus","topic:furbolg"},src={"Pools of Arlithrien"}}
E["subzone:rut-theran-village"] = {t="subzone",n="Rut'theran Village",z="teldrassil",s="At Teldrassil's southern shore, Rut'theran Village links Darnassus to Kalimdor by sea and sky. Ferries and hippogryphs carry travelers between the World Tree and the mainland.",h="At Teldrassil's southern shore, Rut'theran Village links Darnassus to Kalimdor by sea and sky.",sec={{t="Gateway to the World Tree",b="Rut'theran Village meets the water below Teldrassil's towering heights. Darnassus rests in the boughs above, while the village handles its needs beyond the tree. A mystical portal beneath the trees carries travelers between the shore and Darnassus in an instant. Ferries leave the docks for Auberdine on the mainland coast of Darkshore, and flight masters tend roosts of trained hippogryphs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How do I get to Darnassus from here?",a="From the docks, walk up the slope toward the giant pavilion tent. Step into the glowing purple portal on its platform to reach the Temple Gardens inside Darnassus.",al={"get to darnassus","portal to darnassus","how to reach darnassus"},gp=true},{q="Where does the boat from the dock go?",a="The Moonspray sails from Rut'theran Village across the Veiled Sea to Auberdine, on the coast of Darkshore.",al={"where does boat go","rut'theran ferry","ruttheran ship route"},gp=true},{q="Why is this village down at sea level instead of up in the tree?",a="Teldrassil's canopy rises too high for sailing ships and sea trade. Rut'theran Village sits at the roots as a sea-level port and hippogryph roost, linked to the heights by a permanent teleportation gateway.",al={"why is ruttheran at sea level","why bottom of teldrassil"},it="purpose"},{q="Can I fly anywhere from here?",a="Yes. A hippogryph handler offers flights across the water to Auberdine in Darkshore. Druids returning from Moonglade also land here on the Cenarion Circle's hippogryphs from Nighthaven.",al={"rut'theran flight path","where can hippogryph fly"},gp=true},{q="What is Rut'theran Village?",a="Rut'theran Village is the coastal port settlement nestled at the base of Teldrassil. Because the capital city of Darnassus sits far above upon the boughs of the World Tree, this seaside haven serves as the vital maritime threshold connecting the night elves to the mainland of Kalimdor and the wider world beyond.",al={"what is this place","ruttheran village","ruttheran overview"},it="place",add="4018ea8f"},{q="What happened at Rut'theran Village?",a="Rut'theran was founded alongside the growth of Teldrassil in the wake of the Third War. Established to provide the secluded kaldorei an accessible harbor at sea level, it has grown peacefully into a bustling entry point, tended by boatmen, hippogryph handlers, and guards defending the foot of the great tree.",al={"ruttheran history","past of ruttheran","what happened here"},it="history",add="b57f91d4"},{q="Who lives in Rut'theran Village?",a="The settlement is populated by night elf caretakers, fishers, and sentinels tasked with securing the base of Teldrassil. It is also home to dedicated handlers who nurture hippogryphs and ferry travelers across the sea, keeping the boughs of Darnassus closely tied to the mainland shores of Darkshore.",al={"who lives here","ruttheran residents","ruttheran population"},it="residents",add="2418ef2b"},{q="Is Rut'theran Village dangerous?",a="No, the village is an entirely peaceful and heavily guarded sanctuary of the Alliance. Sheltered beneath the canopy of Teldrassil and watched over by kaldorei sentinels, visitors can rest and travel freely without fear of hostile wildlife or lurking enemies within the village grounds.",al={"is ruttheran dangerous","threats in ruttheran","is it safe here"},it="danger",add="854f3298"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Druids returning from Moonglade's sacred sanctuary can ride a Cenarion hippogryph from Nighthaven across northern Kalimdor to Rut'theran Village.",["race:NightElf"]="As a young night elf leaving Teldrassil to aid the Alliance, you say farewell to the World Tree's crown at Rut'theran Village before sailing to mainland Kalimdor."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","darnassus","docks","hippogryph","moonspray","port","rut'theran","teldrassil"},rel={"zone:teldrassil","zone:darnassus","subzone:auberdine","subzone:moonspray","zone:darkshore","topic:night-elf","topic:druid","quest:5921"},src={"Rut'theran Village"}}
E["subzone:shadowglen"] = {t="subzone",n="Shadowglen",z="teldrassil",s="Young night elves begin their training in Shadowglen, beneath the boughs of Teldrassil. The vale gathers around Aldrassil, where elders, priestesses, and mentors guide them before they travel farther into the world.",h="Young night elves begin their training in Shadowglen, beneath the boughs of Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Sheltered Cradle",b="Shadowglen lies beneath the northeastern boughs of Teldrassil, ringed by high ridges that shelter it from the rest of the world. Eternal dusk falls over the vale, where Aldrassil rises as a massive barrow-tree. Its hollowed trunk houses elders, priestesses, and mentors who guide young night elves beginning their training. A narrow mountain pass leads south toward Starbreeze Village and Dolanaar. This single route out leaves the sanctuary sheltered and peaceful.",sp=0},{t="Creeping Shadows",b="Danger reaches even this sheltered vale. Shadowthread Cave lies in the extreme northwest, where venomous spiders threaten the glade. Young defenders drive back the encroaching vermin and untamed wildlife before venturing farther among Teldrassil's boughs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Shadowglen?",a="Shadowglen is where young night elves begin their training in northeastern Teldrassil. In the vale, elders, priestesses, and mentors guide them beneath the great barrow-tree Aldrassil.",al={"what is this place","shadowglen lore","about shadowglen"},it="place"},{q="What is the massive tree at the center of the glen?",a="Aldrassil is the barrow-tree at the heart of Shadowglen. Its hollowed trunk houses elders, priestesses, and mentors who guide young night elves in training.",al={"big tree in shadowglen","aldrassil","shadowglen tree"},it="place",nx={8,9}},{q="What threats exist in Shadowglen?",a="Venomous spiders in Shadowthread Cave threaten Shadowglen from the extreme northwest. Young defenders also face untamed wildlife in the glade.",al={"why are there spiders here","shadowglen dangers","shadowthread cave"},it="threat"},{q="How do you leave Shadowglen?",a="A narrow mountain pass leads south out of Shadowglen toward Starbreeze Village and Dolanaar.",al={"exit shadowglen","where does the path lead","way out of shadowglen"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What is Teldrassil?",a="Teldrassil is an immense World Tree grown off the northwestern coast of Kalimdor. Its name means \"Crown of the Earth\" in Darnassian. Raised by the Circle of Ancients and powerful druids following the Third War, Teldrassil serves as the new homeland of the kaldorei. Its gargantuan limbs rise straight from the sea, bearing an entire forested landmass and the capital city of Darnassus in its boughs.",al={"what is this giant tree","teldrassil world tree","about teldrassil"},it="place",add="ceaa8c71",nx={6,7}},{q="Who grew Teldrassil?",a="After Malfurion Stormrage vanished, Archdruid Fandral Staghelm convinced the Circle of Ancients to plant a new World Tree. Powerful druids channeled their magic to raise it from the sea, hoping to restore the kaldorei's lost immortality. However, the Dragon Aspects—notably Nozdormu, who granted their ancient eternal life—refused to bless the boughs, leaving its growth flawed.",al={"who made teldrassil","who planted teldrassil","who created the world tree"},it="origin",add="c8ee90fe"},{q="Why do the night elves live in a tree now?",a="The devastation of the Third War stripped the night elves of their ancestral immortality when Nordrassil was sacrificed at Mount Hyjal. Seeking to regain their eternal life and a safe haven away from mainland threats, the kaldorei raised Teldrassil to serve as their sanctuary and established their gleaming capital of Darnassus high within its towering branches.",al={"why live in a tree","why night elves on teldrassil","why live in teldrassil"},it="history",add="8fe22cbd"},{q="Who lives at the top of Aldrassil?",a="Tenaron Stormgrip, the leader of Shadowglen, makes his home inside the very crown of Aldrassil. From high within the boughs of the great tree, he oversees the training and initiation of fledgling night elf protectors.",al={"top of aldrassil","who is in aldrassil","tenaron stormgrip aldrassil"},it="residents",add="5b09454b"},{q="Is Aldrassil the same as Teldrassil?",a="No. Teldrassil is the colossal World Tree that rises out of the ocean, supporting an entire island-sized land of forests, mountains, and cities upon its upper boughs. Aldrassil is simply a singular, massive ancient tree rooted in the soil of Shadowglen, sitting atop Teldrassil itself.",al={"aldrassil vs teldrassil","is aldrassil teldrassil","difference aldrassil teldrassil"},it="place",add="27b05a0e"},{q="Who's in charge around here?",a="Tenaron Stormgrip oversees Shadowglen from his chamber atop Aldrassil. He guides the valley's defense, coordinating local druids, Sentinels, and mentors as they instruct new arrivals and address the growing corruption among the local wildlife.",al={"who leads shadowglen","leader of shadowglen","in charge shadowglen"},it="in_charge",add="0792cbea",nx={11}},{q="Who leads the night elves overall?",a="High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind leads the kaldorei through the Sisterhood of Elune, while Archdruid Fandral Staghelm currently directs the Cenarion Circle in the absence of Malfurion Stormrage. Together, the priesthood and the druids guide the night elf nation from their capital in Darnassus.",al={"leader of night elves","who rules the night elves","kaldorei leader"},it="leader",add="3fc160d4"},{q="What are the Webwood spiders and why are they here?",a="The Webwood spiders are giant arachnids that have nested in Shadowthread Cave within the young World Tree. While they once kept largely to themselves, a dark taint over Teldrassil has driven them into a vicious frenzy, pushing them out of their hollows to attack anyone wandering the northern reaches.",al={"webwood spiders teldrassil","why spiders in shadowglen","spiders shadowglen"},it="threat",add="003c713a",nx={13}},{q="Were the Webwood spiders always in that cave?",a="Yes. Shadowthread Cave in the northwest is the natural home of Teldrassil's giant spiders. However, their hostility has surged dramatically in recent days under the broodmother Githyiss the Vile, turning the cavern into a deadly hazard for novice wanderers.",al={"spiders always in shadowthread","shadowthread cave history","were spiders always here"},it="history",add="19b22b7f"},{q="Who is Elune?",a="Elune is the revered moon goddess of the night elves, associated with peace, starlight, and healing. The kaldorei have worshipped her since ancient times, and her high priestesses—led by Tyrande Whisperwind—channel her celestial power to protect their people and smite their foes.",al={"moon goddess elune","elune night elves","goddess elune"},it="other",add="b0a66f5b"},{q="What's Dolanaar and why does everyone keep pointing me there?",a="Dolanaar is the nearest major settlement, situated just southwest of Shadowglen through the southern mountain pass. Once your mentors in the glen have tested your abilities, you are sent to Dolanaar to further your training, learn trades, and assist with regional crises across Teldrassil.",al={"what is dolanaar","why go to dolanaar","dolanaar village"},it="next_step",add="2f0ec344"},{q="Why did the night elves lose their immortality?",a="During the Third War, the Burning Legion marched on Mount Hyjal to consume the original World Tree, Nordrassil. Malfurion Stormrage channeled the spirits of the forest and the ancient tree's power to obliterate the demon lord Archimonde. Sacrificing Nordrassil destroyed the enchantment granted by the Dragon Aspects, stripping the kaldorei of their agelessness.",al={"lost immortality night elves","why are night elves mortal","night elf immortality loss"},it="history",add="94588242"},{q="How did I end up in Shadowglen?",a="You are in a secluded glade high in the northeastern boughs of Teldrassil, the young World Tree grown off the coast of northern Kalimdor. Sheltered from the wider world beneath the great tree Aldrassil, this tranquil forest serves as a safe haven and training ground for newly aspiring kaldorei. You came here to answer the call of your elders, honing your abilities in peaceful seclusion before stepping out onto the larger branches of your people's new homeland.",al={"how did i get here","how did i arrive here","why am i here"},it="arrival",add="b6ffca43"},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Shadowglen?",a="Your task is to aid the guardians and elders of Aldrassil with the growing problems disturbing the glade. A foul corruption has recently begun upsetting the local wildlife, causing the native Webwood spiders and woodland beasts to turn hostile. Speak with the trainers and leaders around the great tree, root out the sickness festering in Shadowthread Cave, and restore balance to the forest before continuing south down the path to Dolanaar.",al={"what should i do here","what is my purpose here","what am i doing in shadowglen"},it="purpose",add="e332bd9f"},{q="Why does a new Night Elf start here, in Shadowglen?",a="Following the Third War and the sacrifice of Nordrassil, the night elves relocated across the sea to Teldrassil to begin anew. Shadowglen is the most protected and secluded pocket of the crown, insulated behind ringed mountain ridges and guarded by veteran Sentinels. Because you are taking your first steps in the arts of druidism, warfare, or Elune's grace, your people cultivate your training here in the safety of Aldrassil before sending you into the wider, more perilous world.",al={"why do night elves start here","why does my night elf begin in shadowglen","why start in shadowglen"},it="arrival",rc="Night Elf",add="3011769b"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you begin your training in Shadowglen beneath Aldrassil, then face the wider world beyond the vale.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you find Shadowglen high among Teldrassil's boughs, sheltered behind guarded ports."},kw={"aldrassil","kaldorei","night elf starting area","shadowglen","shadowthread cave","teldrassil"},rel={"zone:teldrassil","subzone:aldrassil","subzone:shadowthread-cave","subzone:dolanaar","subzone:starbreeze-village","topic:night-elf","zone:darnassus","subzone:rut-theran-village"},src={"Shadowglen"}}
E["subzone:shadowthread-cave"] = {t="subzone",n="Shadowthread Cave",z="teldrassil",s="Shadowthread Cave lies beneath the northwest cliffs of Shadowglen, where its spiders have grown dangerous. Their brood now threatens young kaldorei near Aldrassil.",h="Shadowthread Cave lies beneath the northwest cliffs of Shadowglen, where its spiders have grown dangerous.",sec={{t="A Brood Growing Restless",b="Shadowthread Cave opens in Shadowglen’s shaded northwest, a lair for Teldrassil’s giant spiders. In earlier years, the spiders lived quietly alongside the World Tree’s young boughs. Now they guard their territory fiercely. Webwood silk chokes the stone corridors, and the brood threatens young kaldorei venturing beyond Aldrassil.",sp=0},{t="Githyiss the Vile",b="Githyiss the Vile rules the deepest recesses of Shadowthread Cave. The monstrous broodmother is far more ferocious than the common webwood crawlers. Young night elf sentinels and druids go into the cave to curb the infestation and slay Githyiss, keeping the corruption touching Teldrassil’s wildlife from overrunning Shadowglen’s sanctuary.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Shadowthread Cave located?",a="Shadowthread Cave lies in Shadowglen’s northwest corner, against the rocky hillside bordering Teldrassil’s night elf starting valley.",al={"shadowthread cave location","where is shadowthread cave","find shadowthread cave"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are the spiders in the cave so aggressive?",a="Spiders have always dwelled in Shadowthread Cave, but a foul sickness and growing imbalance across Teldrassil have driven local wildlife mad. The webwood spiders have become exceptionally violent.",al={"why are spiders hostile","spider corruption shadowthread","why spiders attacking"},it="danger"},{q="Who is Githyiss the Vile?",a="Githyiss the Vile is a massive, venomous webwood spider matriarch in the deepest part of Shadowthread Cave. She is the mother of the aggressive brood threatening young kaldorei in Shadowglen.",al={"githyiss","who is githyiss","shadowthread spider boss"},it="threat"},{q="What makes the cave valuable despite the danger?",a="Dense layers of naturally spun webwood silk fill the cave. The arachnids in its dark chambers weave this valuable, resilient crafting material in great numbers.",al={"shadowthread silk","spider silk shadowglen"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Shadowthread Cave?",a="Shadowthread Cave is a subterranean cavern tucked into the northwest bluffs of Shadowglen on Teldrassil. Traditionally the natural nesting ground of the island's webwood spiders, it serves as a secluded den where the arachnids spin their intricate webs and raise their broods away from the boughs of the World Tree.",al={"what is shadowthread cave","shadowthread cave lore","shadowthread cave"},it="place",add="3bee1b1c"},{q="Who lives in Shadowthread Cave?",a="The cavern is inhabited almost entirely by Teldrassil's native webwood spiders. At the heart of the nest rules their massive broodmother, Githyiss the Vile, who commands the swarms of arachnids that blanket the stone walls in dense webbing.",al={"who lives in shadowthread cave","shadowthread cave inhabitants","spiders in shadowthread cave"},it="residents",add="aa654c4e"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a young night elf, you face one of your first trials in defending your sacred home from creeping corruption: clearing Shadowthread Cave and slaying Githyiss the Vile.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can read the Webwood brood’s unchecked aggression as a troubling sign that Teldrassil’s natural harmony is deeply disturbed."},kw={"githyiss the vile","shadowglen","shadowthread cave","spider silk","teldrassil","webwood spider"},rel={"subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil","quest:940"},src={"Shadowthread Cave"}}
E["subzone:starbreeze-village"] = {t="subzone",n="Starbreeze Village",z="teldrassil",s="Gnarlpine furbolgs have overrun Starbreeze Village, east of Dolanaar in Teldrassil. Once a quiet night elf hamlet, it now lies in ruins beneath the spreading corruption of the World Tree.",h="Gnarlpine furbolgs have overrun Starbreeze Village, east of Dolanaar in Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Fallen Hamlet",b="Starbreeze Village lies southeast of Shadowglen, just down the road from Dolanaar. Peaceful night elf families once lived beneath Teldrassil’s boughs, but the village now lies in shambles. Aggressive Gnarlpine furbolgs have overrun its wooden homes. Driven wild by corruption afflicting the World Tree’s boughs, they drove out the elven residents and fiercely defend the ruined grounds.",sp=0},{t="The Threat of Ferocitas",b="Ferocitas the Dream Eater lurks on the settlement’s outskirts, where the Gnarlpine presence is more than an ordinary territorial raid. This enigmatic, corrupted entity suggests foul magic is driving the furbolgs mad. Hulking beasts like Uruson prowl the paths with them, making Starbreeze an active danger to travelers crossing eastern Teldrassil.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is Starbreeze Village abandoned?",a="Gnarlpine furbolgs overran the village after falling prey to a spreading corruption within Teldrassil. Driven mad and violent, they attacked the night elf inhabitants and forced them to flee their homes.",al={"what happened to starbreeze","why is starbreeze ruined","starbreeze empty"},it="ruin"},{q="Who lives in Starbreeze Village now?",a="Hostile Gnarlpine furbolgs occupy the village now. Among them are the wandering patrol Uruson and Ferocitas the Dream Eater, a corrupted figure.",al={"who is in starbreeze","starbreeze mobs","who took over starbreeze"},it="residents"},{q="Where is Starbreeze Village located?",a="Starbreeze Village lies in eastern Teldrassil, southeast of Shadowglen and east of Dolanaar.",al={"where is starbreeze","starbreeze map location","how to find starbreeze"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Ferocitas the Dream Eater?",a="Ferocitas the Dream Eater is a dangerous, corrupted creature on the outskirts of Starbreeze Village. The creature is associated with the dark forces driving the local Gnarlpine tribe into a frenzy.",al={"ferocitas lore","who is ferocitas","ferocitas starbreeze"}},{q="What is Starbreeze Village?",a="Starbreeze Village is a former night elf settlement nestled in the boughs of Teldrassil, located east of Dolanaar and southeast of Shadowglen. Once a peaceful enclave consisting of small elven dwellings, it has fallen into ruin and stands as a grim reminder of the corruption currently spreading across the World Tree.",al={"what is starbreeze village","starbreeze village overview","starbreeze lore"},it="place",add="3682bebf"},{q="What happened to Starbreeze Village?",a="Not long ago, Starbreeze was a quiet night elven community. However, a creeping corruption took hold of the local Gnarlpine furbolg tribe, driving them into a feral, violent frenzy. Overwhelmed by the sudden assault, the kaldorei inhabitants were driven out or slaughtered, and the furbolgs took complete control of the settlement.",al={"starbreeze village history","what happened at starbreeze","how did starbreeze fall"},it="history",add="71f9207c"},{q="Is Starbreeze Village dangerous?",a="Yes, it is very dangerous to enter unprepared. The ruins are swarming with hostile, corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs who attack any outsiders on sight. The hulking furbolg Uruson patrols the village paths, while the Gnarlpine leader Ferocitas the Dream Eater lurks on the settlement's outskirts.",al={"is starbreeze village safe","starbreeze danger","dangers of starbreeze village"},it="danger",add="678e5f4f"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, seeing a settlement so close to Dolanaar in ruins is a painful reminder of Teldrassil’s precarious state and the corruption gnawing at the World Tree.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, the madness consuming the Gnarlpine furbolgs and the defilement of Starbreeze Village challenge the Cenarion Circle’s charge to restore balance to Teldrassil’s wildlife."},kw={"dolanaar","ferocitas","furbolg","gnarlpine","starbreeze","teldrassil","uruson","village"},rel={"zone:teldrassil","topic:furbolg","subzone:dolanaar","quest:2459","subzone:shadowglen","quest:940","zone:darnassus"},src={"Starbreeze Village"}}
E["subzone:wellspring-lake"] = {t="subzone",n="Wellspring Lake",z="teldrassil",s="At Wellspring Lake, springs feed the river while corruption stirs the wildlife. The lake lies northeast of Darnassus, where night elf fishermen once found a quiet retreat.",h="At Wellspring Lake, springs feed the river while corruption stirs the wildlife.",sec={{t="A Tainted Refuge",b="Wellspring Lake lies between Darnassus and the Oracle Glade, beneath Teldrassil’s canopy. Night elves once came to its clear waters to fish and sit in quiet thought. Springs deep within the World Tree feed the lake, and its waters flow north through the Wellspring River. Now a blight troubles the surrounding wilds. Aggressive spiders, prowling nightsabers, and agitated timberlings roam the banks, making the shore dangerous for travelers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Wellspring Lake located?",a="Wellspring Lake lies in northern Teldrassil, northeast of Darnassus and just southeast of the Oracle Glade.",al={"where is wellspring lake","wellspring lake location","how to get to wellspring lake"},gp=true},{q="Where does the lake's water come from and go?",a="Natural springs deep within Teldrassil feed the lake. Its waters flow north into the Wellspring River, toward the edge of the tree.",al={"where does wellspring lake drain","wellspring river source","wellspring lake water source"},it="origin"},{q="Why is the area around Wellspring Lake dangerous?",a="Corruption across the World Tree has driven local beasts mad. Nightsabers, giant webwood spiders, and corrupted timberling bark-spirits stalk the shore.",al={"what lives at wellspring lake","wellspring lake mobs","why is wellspring lake hostile"},it="threat"},{q="Who used to gather at Wellspring Lake?",a="Local night elf fishermen once came to Wellspring Lake for quiet reflection and fishing. The recent blight has agitated the wildlife and made the shores dangerous.",al={"wellspring lake history","night elf fishermen lake"},it="history"},{q="What is Wellspring Lake?",a="Wellspring Lake is a small body of water nestled in the boughs of Teldrassil, northeast of Darnassus and southeast of the Oracle Glade. Fed by a natural spring buried deep within the World Tree itself, its fresh waters flow outward into the Wellspring River, nourishing the surrounding woodland.",al={"what is wellspring lake","wellspring lake teldrassil","about wellspring lake"},it="place",add="f7f79729"},{q="Why was Wellspring Lake abandoned?",a="Night elven fishermen once favored the lake's peaceful banks, but growing corruption across the World Tree drove them away. Corrupted timberlings now dwell within the waters, and aggressive nightsabers and spiders roam the surrounding wilderness, making peaceful visits impossible.",al={"why was wellspring lake abandoned","wellspring lake fishermen","why did fishermen leave wellspring lake"},it="ruin",add="ce819020"},{q="Is Wellspring Lake dangerous?",a="Yes. Though once a tranquil fishing retreat, the lake has been claimed by hostile, corrupted timberlings. The surrounding terrain offers no safety either, infested by predatory nightsabers and webwood spiders prowling the undergrowth.",al={"is wellspring lake dangerous","wellspring lake safe","wellspring lake dangers"},it="danger",add="0645470a"},{q="Why is it called Wellspring Lake?",a="The lake takes its name from its source: a natural spring fed from deep within the roots and soil of Teldrassil. In turn, it serves as the headwaters of the Wellspring River, giving life to the central waterways of the bough.",al={"why is it called wellspring lake","wellspring lake name origin","wellspring lake name meaning"},it="name",add="4ed9a160"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the Kaldorei, peaceful groves like Wellspring Lake turning into dangerous monster dens show how deeply something has gone wrong with their young World Tree.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can study the agitated timberlings and beasts near Wellspring Lake to understand the unnatural sickness spreading through Teldrassil’s waters and soil."},kw={"darnassus","kaldorei","nightsaber","oracle glade","teldrassil","timberlings","wellspring lake","wellspring river"},rel={"subzone:wellspring-river","zone:teldrassil","subzone:oracle-glade","zone:darnassus"},src={"Wellspring Lake"}}
E["subzone:wellspring-river"] = {t="subzone",n="Wellspring River",z="teldrassil",s="In Teldrassil, Wellspring River carries fresh water north from Wellspring Lake before plunging to the ocean below. Its banks have grown dangerous as the timberlings turn hostile.",h="In Teldrassil, Wellspring River carries fresh water north from Wellspring Lake before plunging to the ocean...",sec={{t="Waters of the World Tree",b="Wellspring River runs north from Wellspring Lake through Teldrassil's forest before falling from the great tree into the sea below. Its banks are no longer safe. The timberlings living there have grown crazed and attack travelers and druids who come near the water.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the Wellspring River lead?",a="Wellspring River flows north from Wellspring Lake, then reaches the edge of Teldrassil's canopy and plunges in a great waterfall to the ocean below.",al={"where does river flow","wellspring river destination","where does wellspring river go"}},{q="Why are the timberlings along the river attacking people?",a="The timberlings along Wellspring River have grown erratic and crazed, attacking anyone nearby. This unrest among Teldrassil's wildlife alarms the local night elven druids.",al={"why are timberlings aggressive","crazed timberlings wellspring","why timberlings hostile"},it="danger"},{q="Where does the water in the river come from?",a="Wellspring River flows from Wellspring Lake, which is fed by a natural freshwater spring deep within the living trunk and boughs of the World Tree.",al={"wellspring water source","where does wellspring water come from"},it="origin"},{q="What is Wellspring River?",a="Wellspring River is a vital freshwater stream flowing through Teldrassil. Originating from a natural spring deep within the boughs of the World Tree, it drains northward out of Wellspring Lake and carries its waters toward the northern cliffs, ultimately tumbling over the massive canopy's edge in a breathtaking waterfall down to the sea below.",al={"what is wellspring river","tell me about wellspring river","wellspring river lore"},it="place",add="cd3e3593"},{q="Why is it called Wellspring River?",a="The river takes its name from its origin: a natural spring and deep wellspring nestled high within Teldrassil's crown. Flowing directly out of Wellspring Lake, the clear waters serve as one of the primary arteries of moisture sustaining the surrounding forest before spilling off the edge of the great tree.",al={"why is it called wellspring river","wellspring river name meaning","wellspring name origin"},it="name",add="fd48f2c1"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The maddened timberlings along Wellspring River are an unsettling sign of sickness spreading through Teldrassil's ecosystem.",["race:NightElf"]="The freshwater waterways flowing from Teldrassil's heart represent the vitality of the Kaldorei's new home, so unrest along their banks is deeply concerning."},kw={"kaldorei","teldrassil","timberlings","waterfall","wellspring lake","wellspring river"},rel={"subzone:wellspring-lake","zone:teldrassil","quest:940"},src={"Wellspring River"}}
E["zone:teldrassil"] = {t="zone",n="Teldrassil",z="teldrassil",s="Teldrassil rises from the sea off Kalimdor's northwest coast, its crown sheltering Darnassus. Druids raised the World Tree after the Third War, but its growth is troubled.",h="Teldrassil rises from the sea off Kalimdor's northwest coast, its crown sheltering Darnassus.",sec={{t="A Canopy Upon the Sea",b="You stand beneath Teldrassil's vast limbs above the Veiled Sea. Hills, rivers fed by morning dew, misty lakes, and ancient glades spread across its boughs. Darnassus, the kaldorei capital, lies at the western edge. At the base of the trunk, Rut'theran Village is the island's harbor, linked to the crown by a mystical gateway.",sp=0},{t="The Refusal of the Aspects",b="After Nordrassil was sacrificed during the Third War, Shan'do Malfurion Stormrage vanished into the Emerald Dream. Archdruid Fandral Staghelm persuaded the Circle of Ancients to grow a replacement, hoping to restore the kaldorei's lost immortality. Nozdormu and the Dragon Aspects judged the effort hubristic and withheld their blessings. Without their warding, Teldrassil has grown with unnatural flaws.",sp=0},{t="A Creeping Malady",b="Violence has spread among Teldrassil's wildlife. Peaceful furbolg tribes have fallen into madness, twisted grells multiply in the barrows, and satyrs perform dark rites in places such as Fel Rock. On Darkshore's shores, sea giants, threshers, and turtles beach themselves to escape the tainted waters around the tree. Naturalists and sentinels search the boughs for the shadow slowly strangling their new home.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why was Teldrassil grown?",a="After Nordrassil was devastated at the end of the Third War, the night elves lost their immortality. Archdruid Fandral Staghelm urged the Circle of Ancients and Cenarion druids to plant a new World Tree in the sea, hoping to restore what their people had lost.",al={"why made","who made teldrassil","teldrassil origin"},it="origin"},{q="Why didn't Teldrassil restore night elf immortality?",a="Nozdormu, the Timeless One, blessed Nordrassil and granted the night elves immortality. When Teldrassil was raised, he judged their desire arrogant and refused to bless the new tree.",al={"immortality","why not immortal","nozdormu blessing"},it="power"},{q="How do you leave Teldrassil?",a="Go through Darnassus to the pink portal in the Temple Gardens, which carries you down to Rut'theran Village at the trunk's base. From there, take a ship across the sea to Auberdine on mainland Darkshore, or follow one of the available hippogryph routes.",al={"how to get out","leave tree","teldrassil boat"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why are there no mining nodes in Teldrassil?",a="Teldrassil grows from the living branches and wood of a colossal World Tree, not continental rock. Without stony subterranean crusts, the zone has no metal veins or ore deposits, though herbs grow in abundance.",al={"where is copper","no ore","teldrassil mining"},gp=true},{q="What is causing the furbolgs and beasts to turn mad?",a="A sinister presence is seeping into Teldrassil's unblessed roots, and sickness has tainted the local water and flora. It drives peaceful timberlings and the Gnarlpine furbolg tribe into aggression, while satyr remnants actively cultivate the taint.",al={"corrupted furbolgs","gnarlpine mad","what is the corruption"},it="threat"},{q="What is Shadowglen?",a="Shadowglen is a sheltered vale on Teldrassil's eastern boughs, surrounding the great tree Aldrassil. Young night elves begin their training in this peaceful sanctuary before venturing into the wider world.",al={"shadowglen","starting area","aldrassil zone"},it="place"},{q="What is Teldrassil?",a="Teldrassil is an immense World Tree grown upon an island off the northwestern coast of Kalimdor. Its gargantuan trunk rises out of the Veiled Sea, spreading out into boughs so vast they support an entire forested realm of lakes, rivers, and the capital city of Darnassus atop its canopy.",al={"what is this place","about teldrassil","tell me about teldrassil"},it="place",add="11a6d5e5"},{q="What happened at Teldrassil?",a="Following the Third War and the damage done to Mount Hyjal's Nordrassil, the druid Malfurion Stormrage went missing. In his absence, Archdruid Fandral Staghelm convinced the Circle of Ancients to grow a new World Tree to replace what was lost. Though grown successfully, a creeping corruption has since begun to taint its boughs.",al={"teldrassil history","how was teldrassil created","events of teldrassil"},it="history",add="313cd5a2"},{q="Who lives in or runs Teldrassil?",a="Teldrassil is the ancestral refuge and current homeland of the night elves. Spiritually and civically, High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind and Archdruid Fandral Staghelm guide their people from the capital of Darnassus, supported by the Sisterhood of Elune, Cenarion druids, and Sentinel warriors guarding the woodland settlements.",al={"who leads teldrassil","teldrassil leaders","who lives here"},it="residents",add="c5e34e84"},{q="Is Teldrassil dangerous?",a="While protected by Sentinels, Teldrassil is increasingly perilous. A dark affliction has maddened the native beasts and local furbolgs, while malicious satyrs, bloodthirsty harpies, and rampant timberlings threaten settlements beyond the patrolled highways.",al={"is it safe here","threats in teldrassil","dangers of teldrassil"},it="danger",add="b86e706e"},{q="Why is it called Teldrassil?",a="In the Darnassian language of the night elves, Teldrassil translates directly to 'crown of the earth.' It was named in honor of its role as a monumental World Tree meant to cradle and shield their civilization.",al={"what does teldrassil mean","teldrassil name meaning"},it="name",add="2863bed2"},{q="Who is Fandral Staghelm?",a="Fandral Staghelm is the Archdruid who stepped into leadership of the night elven druids following Malfurion Stormrage's disappearance into the Emerald Dream. Passionate, stubborn, and aggressive, Fandral championed the planting of Teldrassil and frequently clashes with High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind over policy.",al={"who is the archdruid","fandral staghelm lore","staghelm"},it="leader",add="514d23b0"},{q="Who is Tyrande Whisperwind?",a="Tyrande Whisperwind is the High Priestess of the goddess Elune and supreme leader of the night elven people. Having guided her kin for ten thousand years through the Long Vigil and the Third War, she now leads from the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus.",al={"who is tyrande","high priestess tyrande","who leads the night elves"},it="leader",add="52c333ac"},{q="How did I end up in Teldrassil?",a="If you are a night elf, this colossal World Tree is your people's new homeland. After sacrificing Nordrassil and your ancient immortality atop Mount Hyjal to defeat the Burning Legion, the kaldorei relocated off Kalimdor's northwest coast. Archdruid Fandral Staghelm and the Circle of Ancients grew Teldrassil in the Veiled Sea to give your race a renewed refuge, and you began your journey within its verdant boughs at Shadowglen. If you journeyed here from abroad, you likely sailed to the port of Rut'theran Village at the tree's base from Darkshore, then stepped through the glowing portal that carries travelers directly up into the crown.",al={"how did i get to teldrassil","how did i get here","why am i starting here"},it="arrival",add="29b1e9e4"},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Teldrassil?",a="You are called to protect the fledgling World Tree and uncover the dark malady unsettling its boughs. Despite its lush forests, a sinister corruption is taking hold: timberlings are turning aggressive, peaceful furbolgs of the Gnarlpine tribe are slipping into madness, and vile satyrs lurk in shadowy thickets like Fel Rock. Starting from Shadowglen and aiding settlements like Dolanaar, you must help the Sentinels and druids restore balance. You will replenish the sacred moonwells, root out corrupted vermin, and learn the history of your people before venturing out into the capital of Darnassus and across the sea to mainland Kalimdor.",al={"what do i do in teldrassil","why am i here","what is my mission here"},it="purpose",add="8381279f"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see Teldrassil as your people's new beginning after Mount Hyjal's devastation. Without the Aspects' blessings, defending it is urgent.",["class:Druid"]="With Malfurion trapped in the Emerald Dream, Archdruid Fandral Staghelm leads the Cenarion Circle here. Many druids worry Teldrassil was raised in haste.",["faction:Alliance"]="Teldrassil is the Alliance's northernmost stronghold in Kalimdor, supporting naval communication and trade between Darnassus and mainland kingdoms.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Teldrassil has no minerals or ore, but its canopy offers Peacebloom, Silverleaf, and Earthroot in abundance."},kw={"circle of ancients","crown of the earth","darnassus","dolanaar","fandral staghelm","rut'theran","shadowglen","teldrassil","world tree"},rel={"zone:darnassus","zone:darkshore","quest:929","quest:940","npc:fandral-staghelm","npc:tyrande-whisperwind","topic:nordrassil","subzone:rut-theran-village"},m={levels="1-10"},src={"Teldrassil (Classic)","Teldrassil"}}
